HELI_ES = {
  'The couple embracing in a summer meadow, the helicopter behind them': 'La pareja abrazada en un prado de verano, el helicóptero detrás',
  'The couple on a green summit with the helicopter and the Dolomites behind': 'La pareja en una cumbre verde con el helicóptero y los Dolomitas detrás',
  'The couple walking to the helicopter to board for the flight': 'La pareja caminando hacia el helicóptero para embarcar al vuelo',
  'The couple inside the helicopter cabin during the flight': 'La pareja dentro de la cabina del helicóptero durante el vuelo',
  'The couple with the helicopter on a snowy plateau at last light': 'La pareja con el helicóptero en un plateau nevado en la última luz',
  'The couple beside the helicopter on a ridge, veil in the wind': 'La pareja junto al helicóptero en una arista, el velo al viento',
  'The couple kissing in front of the helicopter in warm light': 'La pareja besándose frente al helicóptero con luz cálida',
  'A bride in a winter coat stepping out of the helicopter into the snow': 'Una novia con abrigo de invierno saliendo del helicóptero a la nieve',
  'The couple alone on a ridge with the helicopter and a Dolomite panorama': 'La pareja sola en una arista con el helicóptero y un panorama dolomítico',
  'A chef making fresh pizza on the mountain, the helicopter behind': 'Un cocinero preparando pizza fresca en la montaña, el helicóptero detrás',
  'What a helicopter elopement actually is': 'Qué es realmente un elopement en helicóptero',
  'A helicopter elopement is a very small mountain wedding with one difference: you reach your ceremony by air. A licensed alpine helicopter lifts the two of you (and, if you like, a witness or two) from a valley helipad, flies you over the peaks and sets down on an approved landing site &mdash; a ridge, a high meadow, a glacier plateau. You say your vows with the whole range beneath your feet, take portraits while the light is good, and fly back. The flight is not a transfer; it becomes half the story.': 'Un elopement en helicóptero es una boda de montaña muy pequeña con una diferencia: llegáis a vuestra ceremonia por aire. Un helicóptero alpino autorizado os eleva a los dos (y, si queréis, a uno o dos testigos) desde un helipuerto del valle, os lleva sobre las cumbres y aterriza en un lugar autorizado &mdash; una arista, un prado de altura, un plateau glaciar. Os dais el sí con toda la cordillera bajo vuestros pies, hacéis retratos mientras la luz acompaña y volvéis. El vuelo no es un traslado: se convierte en media historia.',
  'The machine carries up to <strong>six passengers plus the pilot</strong>, so bringing a witness or two &mdash; or even a few close guests &mdash; is no problem, and you still fly comfortably. Most of our couples keep it to just the two of them; some bring their witnesses up for the ceremony. Either way, there is room.': 'La máquina lleva hasta <strong>seis pasajeros más el piloto</strong>, así que traer a uno o dos testigos &mdash; o incluso a unos pocos invitados cercanos &mdash; no es problema, y voláis con comodidad. La mayoría de nuestras parejas se queda solo con los dos; algunos suben a sus testigos para la ceremonia. En cualquier caso, hay sitio.',
  'A helicopter over the Dolomite peaks at golden hour': 'Un helicóptero sobre las cumbres de los Dolomitas en la hora dorada',
  'Couples come to it for different reasons. Some cannot hike far &mdash; a knee, a pregnancy, a dress that was never built for scree &mdash; and a flight gives them a summit anyway. Some simply want the one thing money can still buy in a crowded range: a place, for an hour, with no one else in it. And some love the flight for itself, the door open, the valley dropping away, the first sight of the peaks from above. Whatever brings you, the result is the same &mdash; a day that feels less like a wedding you attended and more like an adventure you took together.': 'Las parejas llegan a esto por distintas razones. Algunas no pueden caminar mucho &mdash; una rodilla, un embarazo, un vestido que nunca se pensó para pedreras &mdash; y un vuelo les regala una cumbre igualmente. Otras simplemente quieren lo único que el dinero aún puede comprar en una cordillera concurrida: un lugar, durante una hora, sin nadie más en él. Y otras aman el vuelo en sí, la puerta abierta, el valle que se aleja, la primera visión de las cumbres desde arriba. Sea lo que os traiga, el resultado es el mismo &mdash; un día que se siente menos como una boda a la que asististeis y más como una aventura que vivisteis juntos.',
  'Exchanging rings on the mountain after the flight': 'Intercambio de anillos en la montaña tras el vuelo',
  'How the day unfolds, step by step': 'Cómo transcurre el día, paso a paso',
  '<strong>1. First call.</strong> We start with a video call to understand the day you picture &mdash; sunrise or golden hour, a bare summit or a lake, just the two of you or a few guests. <strong>2. Landing site &amp; operator.</strong> We match your vision to an approved landing site and book a licensed alpine operator; some sites need advance clearance. <strong>3. Timing &amp; weather window.</strong> We fix a date but keep a flexible window and a backup day &mdash; the flight only happens in safe conditions. <strong>4. Getting ready.</strong> Hair, make-up and dressing happen in the valley before the flight. <strong>5. The flight.</strong> A short set-down at the helipad, headsets on, and minutes later you step out onto the mountain. <strong>6. Ceremony &amp; portraits.</strong> Your words, then portraits &mdash; the pilot stays on the mountain with you, and you have up to a full hour on each landing before you fly on. <strong>7. Back down</strong> &mdash; often with time for a second landing, a hut lunch or a lakeside toast.': '<strong>1. Primera llamada.</strong> Empezamos con una videollamada para entender el día que imagináis &mdash; amanecer u hora dorada, una cumbre desnuda o un lago, solo vosotros dos o unos invitados. <strong>2. Lugar de aterrizaje y operador.</strong> Adaptamos vuestra idea a un lugar autorizado y reservamos un operador alpino con licencia; algunos sitios requieren permiso previo. <strong>3. Fecha y ventana meteorológica.</strong> Fijamos una fecha pero mantenemos una ventana flexible y un día de reserva &mdash; solo se vuela en condiciones seguras. <strong>4. Preparativos.</strong> Peinado, maquillaje y vestido se hacen en el valle antes del vuelo. <strong>5. El vuelo.</strong> Una breve toma en el helipuerto, cascos puestos, y minutos después salís a la montaña. <strong>6. Ceremonia y retratos.</strong> Vuestras palabras, luego retratos &mdash; el piloto se queda con vosotros en la montaña, y tenéis hasta una hora entera en cada aterrizaje antes de seguir. <strong>7. De vuelta abajo</strong> &mdash; a menudo con tiempo para un segundo aterrizaje, una comida en un refugio o un brindis junto al lago.',
  'That hour matters. Because the pilot waits with you rather than flying off and coming back, there is no clock-watching for a returning machine and no rush through your vows &mdash; you get a genuine, unhurried hour on each spot for the ceremony and portraits.': 'Esa hora importa. Como el piloto espera con vosotros en lugar de irse y volver, no hay que mirar el reloj por una máquina que regresa ni prisa en vuestros votos &mdash; tenéis una hora genuina y sin apuros en cada lugar para la ceremonia y los retratos.',
  'Bride with a headset inside the helicopter before take-off': 'Novia con casco dentro del helicóptero antes del despegue',
  'View across the cockpit as the helicopter climbs over the valley': 'Vista a través de la cabina mientras el helicóptero sube sobre el valle',
  'The flight itself is short and unforgettable. The rotor spins up, the machine goes light, and the valley simply falls away; a minute later the first peaks slide past the window at eye level, closer than you have ever seen them. Nobody speaks much &mdash; you just watch. Then the pilot picks the line in, the skids touch, the noise drops, and you step out into a silence so complete it rings. That contrast &mdash; from thunder to hush in thirty seconds &mdash; is a feeling couples talk about for years.': 'El vuelo en sí es breve e inolvidable. El rotor acelera, la máquina se aligera y el valle simplemente cae; un minuto después las primeras cumbres pasan a la altura de los ojos junto a la ventana, más cerca de lo que las habéis visto nunca. Nadie habla mucho &mdash; solo miráis. Luego el piloto elige la línea de entrada, los patines tocan, el ruido baja y salís a un silencio tan completo que resuena. Ese contraste &mdash; del trueno a la calma en treinta segundos &mdash; es una sensación de la que las parejas hablan durante años.',
  'A sharp ridge line seen from above during the flight': 'Una arista afilada vista desde arriba durante el vuelo',
  'Two example timelines': 'Dos ejemplos de cronograma',
  '<strong>A sunrise flight.</strong> 04:30 hair &amp; make-up in the valley &middot; 05:30 short drive to the helipad &middot; 06:00 lift-off as first light hits the peaks &middot; 06:15 set down on the ridge, ceremony as the rock turns pink &middot; 06:40 portraits in the still, empty light &middot; 07:15 fly back &middot; 08:00 breakfast at a mountain hut.': '<strong>Un vuelo al amanecer.</strong> 04:30 peinado y maquillaje en el valle &middot; 05:30 breve trayecto al helipuerto &middot; 06:00 despegue cuando la primera luz toca las cumbres &middot; 06:15 aterrizaje en la arista, ceremonia mientras la roca se vuelve rosa &middot; 06:40 retratos en la luz quieta y vacía &middot; 07:15 vuelo de regreso &middot; 08:00 desayuno en un refugio de montaña.',
  '<strong>A full golden-hour day.</strong> 15:00 getting ready &middot; 16:30 first flight to a high landing for portraits &middot; 17:30 ceremony at a second spot &middot; 18:30 the range glows at last light (enrosadira) &middot; 19:15 fly down &middot; 20:00 dinner on a hut terrace. Times shift with the season &mdash; we build the exact schedule around the sunrise and your landing site.': '<strong>Un día completo hasta la hora dorada.</strong> 15:00 preparativos &middot; 16:30 primer vuelo a un aterrizaje alto para retratos &middot; 17:30 ceremonia en un segundo lugar &middot; 18:30 la cordillera brilla en la última luz (enrosadira) &middot; 19:15 vuelo de bajada &middot; 20:00 cena en la terraza de un refugio. Los horarios cambian con la estación &mdash; construimos el plan exacto en torno al amanecer y a vuestro lugar de aterrizaje.',
  'One thing sets the outer limits of the day: the helicopter may lift off from <strong>half an hour before sunrise</strong> and must be back at its airport by <strong>half an hour after sunset</strong>. That is a generous window &mdash; wide enough for both a true first-light flight and a full golden-hour evening &mdash; and we build your exact times around the sunrise for your date, which shifts through the season.': 'Algo marca los límites del día: el helicóptero puede despegar desde <strong>media hora antes del amanecer</strong> y debe estar de vuelta en su aeropuerto <strong>media hora después de la puesta de sol</strong>. Es una ventana generosa &mdash; amplia para un vuelo de primera luz o para toda una tarde en la hora dorada &mdash; y ajustamos vuestros horarios exactos al amanecer de vuestra fecha, que varía con la estación.',
  'The Dolomite walls glowing pink at last light behind the couple': 'Las paredes de los Dolomitas brillando en rosa en la última luz tras la pareja',
  'Silhouetted peaks against a warm sunset sky': 'Cumbres en silueta contra un cálido cielo de atardecer',
  'What it costs': 'Cuánto cuesta',
  'The flight is booked as a charter, and the structure is simple. The minimum is a <strong>50-minute flight including one landing</strong> &mdash; enough for a ceremony and portraits at a single spot. You can add more landings to see more of the range; we usually recommend <strong>no more than three</strong>, so the day stays about being on the mountain rather than in and out of the machine. A few sought-after sites carry a surcharge (see below). The exact flight price depends on your date, your landings and the operator, so we confirm it in writing before anything is booked.': 'El vuelo se reserva como un chárter, y la estructura es sencilla. El mínimo es un <strong>vuelo de 50 minutos con un aterrizaje</strong> &mdash; suficiente para una ceremonia y retratos en un único lugar. Podéis añadir más aterrizajes para ver más de la cordillera; solemos recomendar <strong>no más de tres</strong>, para que el día trate de estar en la montaña y no de entrar y salir de la máquina. Unos pocos lugares muy solicitados tienen un suplemento (véase más abajo). El precio exacto del vuelo depende de la fecha, los aterrizajes y el operador, así que lo confirmamos por escrito antes de reservar nada.',
  'The helicopter waiting on the valley helipad': 'El helicóptero esperando en el helipuerto del valle',
  'It is worth being honest about what drives the number. The bigger levers are the total flight time, the number of landings you add beyond the first, and the landing point itself &mdash; a few premium sites carry a surcharge. Add-ons &mdash; a second location, film, flowers, a celebrant &mdash; sit on top, and we price them plainly so nothing is a surprise on the invoice. A helicopter day is not the cheapest way to elope, but it buys something specific: an hour on a summit that would otherwise cost you two days and a lot of luck.': 'Vale la pena ser honestos sobre qué determina el precio. Las palancas mayores son el tiempo total de vuelo, el número de aterrizajes que añadís tras el primero y el propio lugar de aterrizaje &mdash; unos pocos sitios premium tienen suplemento. Los extras &mdash; una segunda localización, vídeo, flores, un oficiante &mdash; se suman aparte, y los presupuestamos con claridad para que nada sorprenda en la factura. Un día en helicóptero no es la forma más barata de fugarse a casarse, pero compra algo concreto: una hora en una cumbre que de otro modo os costaría dos días y mucha suerte.',
  'Where a helicopter can land you': 'Dónde puede dejaros un helicóptero',
  'A flight opens ground a normal elopement never reaches: a remote rock ledge, a glacier plateau on the Marmolada, a summit that would otherwise be a two-day climb, a shoulder beneath the Cadini or Tre Cime spires. Landings are flown by licensed alpine operators onto approved sites only &mdash; not anywhere you like, and not inside every protected zone. We choose the spot together for the view, the light and what is actually permitted, and confirm it before we book.': 'Un vuelo abre terreno que un elopement normal nunca alcanza: un lejano lecho de roca, un plateau glaciar en la Marmolada, una cumbre que de otro modo sería una ascensión de dos días, un hombro bajo las agujas del Cadini o las Tre Cime. Los aterrizajes los realizan operadores alpinos con licencia, solo en lugares autorizados &mdash; no donde os apetezca, y no dentro de cada zona protegida. Elegimos el lugar juntos por la vista, la luz y lo que realmente está permitido, y lo confirmamos antes de reservar.',
  'Broadly there are three kinds of landing, and they feel different. A <strong>ridge or summit</strong> gives you exposure and a 360-degree horizon &mdash; the boldest frames, the most wind. A <strong>high meadow or shoulder</strong> is gentler underfoot, kinder to a dress and easy to move around on. A <strong>glacier plateau</strong> is the rarest and most otherworldly, a field of white with nothing human in sight. Not every one is available everywhere or in every season, and some sit inside protected zones that are off-limits; we work only where landings are permitted and safe.': 'A grandes rasgos hay tres tipos de aterrizaje, y se sienten distintos. Una <strong>arista o cumbre</strong> os da exposición y un horizonte de 360 grados &mdash; los encuadres más audaces, el mayor viento. Un <strong>prado o hombro de altura</strong> es más suave bajo los pies, más amable con el vestido y fácil de recorrer. Un <strong>plateau glaciar</strong> es el más raro y sobrenatural, un campo blanco sin nada humano a la vista. No todos están disponibles en todas partes ni en cada estación, y algunos quedan dentro de zonas protegidas vetadas; trabajamos solo donde los aterrizajes están permitidos y son seguros.',
  'You do not have to navigate the permissions yourself: the <strong>helicopter operator arranges the landing clearances</strong> for each site, which is exactly why we fly only with licensed local companies. A handful of the most iconic spots &mdash; the Seceda above Ortisei is the classic example &mdash; carry an extra landing fee, typically <strong>around &euro;300&ndash;500</strong>. We tell you upfront which of your dream landings is free to use and which comes with a surcharge, so the shortlist you fall in love with is one we can actually deliver.': 'No tenéis que ocuparos vosotros de los permisos: la <strong>empresa de helicópteros gestiona las autorizaciones de aterrizaje</strong> de cada lugar, y por eso volamos solo con compañías locales con licencia. Un puñado de los sitios más icónicos &mdash; la Seceda sobre Ortisei es el ejemplo clásico &mdash; tienen una tasa de aterrizaje adicional, normalmente <strong>de unos 300&ndash;500&nbsp;&euro;</strong>. Os decimos de antemano cuál de vuestros aterrizajes soñados es libre y cuál lleva suplemento, para que la lista de la que os enamoréis sea una que podamos cumplir de verdad.',
  'An aerial view of a jagged Dolomite peak from the helicopter': 'Vista aérea de una escarpada cumbre de los Dolomitas desde el helicóptero',
  'The couple stepping out onto the mountain beside the landed helicopter': 'La pareja saliendo a la montaña junto al helicóptero posado',
  'Getting there &amp; the helipad': 'Cómo llegar y el helipuerto',
  'Most couples fly into Venice, Verona or Innsbruck and drive the last stretch &mdash; roughly two to three hours to the heart of the Dolomites. Getting ready happens in the valley, then a short drive to the departure helipad. From there the flight is minutes, not hours. If you would rather not self-drive, we arrange transfers so the morning stays calm.': 'La mayoría de las parejas vuela a Venecia, Verona o Innsbruck y conduce el último tramo &mdash; unas dos o tres horas hasta el corazón de los Dolomitas. Los preparativos se hacen en el valle, luego un breve trayecto al helipuerto de salida. Desde allí el vuelo son minutos, no horas. Si preferís no conducir, organizamos traslados para que la mañana siga tranquila.',
  'There are <strong>two local operators</strong> we work with, each with its own base. <strong>Elikos</strong> flies from its airfield in <strong>Pontives</strong>, just below Ortisei in Val Gardena &mdash; about a 30-minute drive from Brixen. <strong>Kron Air</strong> departs from <strong>Olang</strong> in the Pustertal, roughly 20 minutes from Bruneck. Which one we choose depends on your landing site and where you are staying; both put the high Dolomites within a short flight. We match the base to your day and tell you exactly where to be and when.': 'Hay <strong>dos operadores locales</strong> con los que trabajamos, cada uno con su propia base. <strong>Elikos</strong> vuela desde su aeródromo en <strong>Pontives</strong>, justo debajo de Ortisei en Val Gardena &mdash; a unos 30 minutos en coche de Bressanone (Brixen). <strong>Kron Air</strong> despega desde <strong>Olang</strong> (Valdaora) en el Pustertal, a unos 20 minutos de Brunico. El que elijamos depende de vuestro lugar de aterrizaje y de dónde os alojéis; ambos ponen los altos Dolomitas a un vuelo corto. Adaptamos la base a vuestro día y os decimos exactamente dónde estar y cuándo.',
  'The Dolomite peaks seen from the helicopter window': 'Las cumbres de los Dolomitas vistas desde la ventana del helicóptero',
  'Weather &amp; Plan B': 'El tiempo y el plan B',
  'A helicopter flies only in safe conditions &mdash; good visibility, workable wind, no storm. Mountain weather turns fast, so we watch the forecast in the days before and keep a flexible window and, from our middle package up, a spare backup day. If the flight cannot go on your first morning, we move it; if a window never opens, we have a ground-based Plan B ready &mdash; a cable-car summit, a lake, a ridge you can reach on foot &mdash; so you are married beautifully either way. Fog and low cloud are not the enemy: some of the most atmospheric mountain photographs happen in exactly that light.': 'Un helicóptero vuela solo en condiciones seguras &mdash; buena visibilidad, viento manejable, sin tormenta. El tiempo de montaña cambia rápido, así que vigilamos la previsión los días previos y mantenemos una ventana flexible y, desde nuestro paquete intermedio, un día de reserva. Si el vuelo no puede salir la primera mañana, lo movemos; si nunca se abre una ventana, tenemos un plan B en tierra listo &mdash; una cumbre con teleférico, un lago, una arista accesible a pie &mdash; para que os caséis igual de bien de cualquier modo. La niebla y la nube baja no son el enemigo: algunas de las fotos de montaña más atmosféricas ocurren justo con esa luz.',
  'A peak breaking through cloud, seen from the air': 'Una cumbre asomando entre las nubes, vista desde el aire',
  'Summer or winter?': '¿Verano o invierno?',
  'A summer flight lands you on green shoulders and warm rock at first or last light; a winter flight lands you in a white world &mdash; snow to the horizon, the peaks stripped to black and white, your breath in the air. Winter is quieter, colder and more dramatic, and it opens something summer cannot: a ceremony on a snow ridge, and, for the bold, skis on and the first run down together in gown and black tie. It asks for warm layers, good edges and a flexible eye on the weather &mdash; we handle the flight, the timing and the light, so all you bring is the nerve. Both seasons are beautiful; we help you choose the one that matches the day in your head.': 'Un vuelo de verano os deja sobre hombros verdes y roca cálida en la primera o la última luz; un vuelo de invierno os deja en un mundo blanco &mdash; nieve hasta el horizonte, las cumbres reducidas a blanco y negro, vuestro aliento en el aire. El invierno es más silencioso, más frío y más dramático, y abre algo que el verano no puede: una ceremonia en una arista nevada y, para los atrevidos, los esquís puestos y la primera bajada juntos en vestido y frac. Pide capas de abrigo, buenos cantos y un ojo flexible al tiempo &mdash; nosotros nos ocupamos del vuelo, los tiempos y la luz, así que solo traéis el valor. Ambas estaciones son hermosas; os ayudamos a elegir la que encaja con el día que tenéis en la cabeza.',
  'A snow-covered Dolomite peak reached by helicopter in winter': 'Una cumbre nevada de los Dolomitas alcanzada en helicóptero en invierno',
  'What to wear up there': 'Qué llevar allá arriba',
  'It is cold at altitude, even in August &mdash; a summit at dawn can be near freezing while the valley is warm. Bring warm layers you can slip off for photos and back on between them, and a wrap or coat for the dress. Shoes matter: pack sturdy footwear for the landing site and change into the pretty ones for the frames. Rotor wash is real &mdash; hair, veils and loose petals move in the downdraught, which often looks wonderful, but secure anything you do not want to lose. We tell you exactly what to expect for your date and landing so nothing catches you out.': 'Hace frío en altura, incluso en agosto &mdash; una cumbre al amanecer puede rozar el punto de congelación mientras el valle está templado. Llevad capas de abrigo que podáis quitaros para las fotos y volver a poneros entre ellas, y un chal o abrigo para el vestido. El calzado importa: llevad zapatos resistentes para el lugar de aterrizaje y cambiaos a los bonitos para las imágenes. El viento del rotor es real &mdash; el pelo, los velos y los pétalos sueltos se mueven en la corriente descendente, lo que a menudo queda precioso, pero asegurad todo lo que no queráis perder. Os decimos exactamente qué esperar para vuestra fecha y aterrizaje para que nada os pille por sorpresa.',
  'The couple on a wind-scoured ridge, dress moving in the breeze': 'La pareja en una arista batida por el viento, el vestido moviéndose en la brisa',
  'A portrait on the summit with the Dolomites behind': 'Un retrato en la cumbre con los Dolomitas detrás',
  'Papers &amp; making it legal': 'Papeles y lo legal',
  'A helicopter flight is the setting, not the legal act &mdash; and there are two honest paths. <strong>A symbolic ceremony</strong> in the mountains with the legal marriage at home is what most of our couples choose: you sign the papers at your local registry before or after the trip, and up here you have the ceremony that actually matters. <strong>A legal civil marriage</strong> is also possible: in Italy for foreign nationals it means a certificate of no impediment (Nulla Osta / Ehefähigkeitszeugnis), international birth certificates, valid passports, usually an apostille and sworn translations, started months ahead; Austria offers civil ceremonies and, in some regions, approved outdoor locations. Couples from Germany, Austria, the USA and the UK all marry here &mdash; the paperwork differs by country, and we point you to the right path for yours.': 'Un vuelo en helicóptero es el marco, no el acto legal &mdash; y hay dos caminos honestos. <strong>Una ceremonia simbólica</strong> en la montaña con el matrimonio legal en casa es lo que eligen la mayoría de nuestras parejas: firmáis los papeles en vuestro registro civil antes o después del viaje, y aquí arriba tenéis la ceremonia que de verdad importa. <strong>Un matrimonio civil legal</strong> también es posible: en Italia, para extranjeros, significa un certificado de capacidad matrimonial (Nulla Osta / Ehefähigkeitszeugnis), partidas de nacimiento internacionales, pasaportes válidos, normalmente una apostilla y traducciones juradas, iniciadas con meses de antelación; Austria ofrece ceremonias civiles y, en algunas regiones, lugares al aire libre autorizados. Parejas de Alemania, Austria, EE. UU. y el Reino Unido se casan aquí &mdash; el papeleo cambia según el país, y os indicamos el camino correcto para el vuestro.',
  'One honest word on timing: the earlier you tell us, the more we can hold for you. The best summer dawn slots and every winter date fill first, and a legal marriage abroad needs its documents started months ahead. Reach out as soon as you have a rough season in mind &mdash; even before the exact date &mdash; and we will pencil in a window, sketch the day and tell you what to set in motion at home. Nothing is locked until you are ready; an early conversation simply keeps the good mornings open.': 'Una palabra honesta sobre los plazos: cuanto antes nos lo digáis, más podremos reservaros. Los mejores amaneceres de verano y todas las fechas de invierno se llenan primero, y un matrimonio legal en el extranjero necesita sus documentos iniciados con meses de antelación. Escribidnos en cuanto tengáis una estación aproximada en mente &mdash; incluso antes de la fecha exacta &mdash; y apuntaremos una ventana, esbozaremos el día y os diremos qué poner en marcha en casa. Nada queda fijado hasta que estéis listos; una conversación temprana simplemente mantiene abiertas las buenas mañanas.',
  'One point to be clear about: in Italy a <strong>legally binding marriage can only take place at a registry office (comune)</strong> &mdash; never at a landing site on the mountain. So the ceremony up on the peak is always a symbolic one, and it is every bit as moving for it: your vows, your words, the two of you and the range. The legal signature happens at a town hall &mdash; at home, or at an Italian comune before or after the flight &mdash; and we help you line up the paperwork either way.': 'Un punto que dejar claro: en Italia un <strong>matrimonio con validez legal solo puede celebrarse en un registro civil (comune)</strong> &mdash; nunca en un lugar de aterrizaje en la montaña. Por eso la ceremonia en la cumbre es siempre simbólica, y no por ello menos emocionante: vuestros votos, vuestras palabras, los dos y la cordillera. La firma legal ocurre en un ayuntamiento &mdash; en casa, o en un comune italiano antes o después del vuelo &mdash; y os ayudamos a preparar el papeleo en cualquier caso.',
  'Exchanging vows on the summit, the range spread below': 'Intercambio de votos en la cumbre, la cordillera extendida abajo',
  'Above the crowds': 'Por encima de las multitudes',
  'The Dolomites are the most photographed range in Europe, and the icons fill up. A flight is the cleanest way past that: you land where the day-trippers cannot follow and the summit is yours. Even so, we plan for the quiet hours &mdash; first light before the valleys wake, or last light after they empty &mdash; because empty light is always the better light.': 'Los Dolomitas son la cordillera más fotografiada de Europa, y los iconos se llenan. Un vuelo es la forma más limpia de dejar eso atrás: aterrizáis donde los excursionistas de un día no pueden seguir y la cumbre es vuestra. Aun así, planificamos para las horas tranquilas &mdash; la primera luz antes de que despierten los valles, o la última luz cuando se vacían &mdash; porque la luz vacía es siempre la mejor luz.',
  'The couple alone on a summit ridge with nobody else in sight': 'La pareja sola en una arista de cumbre sin nadie más a la vista',
  'Drones, protected zones &amp; flying responsibly': 'Drones, zonas protegidas y volar con responsabilidad',
  'A helicopter is not a drone. Licensed alpine flights land on approved sites under strict rules; private drones, by contrast, are banned across much of the Dolomites &mdash; Lago di Braies has prohibited them since 2026, patrolled by rangers and subject to fines &mdash; and inside nature-reserve zones generally. On the ground we stay on the landing site, off the meadows and out of protected vegetation, and we leave the mountain exactly as we found it. Respect is part of being allowed back.': 'Un helicóptero no es un dron. Los vuelos alpinos con licencia aterrizan en lugares autorizados bajo normas estrictas; los drones privados, en cambio, están prohibidos en gran parte de los Dolomitas &mdash; el Lago di Braies los tiene vetados desde 2026, con vigilancia de guardas y sujeto a multas &mdash; y dentro de las zonas de reserva natural en general. En tierra permanecemos en el lugar de aterrizaje, fuera de los prados y de la vegetación protegida, y dejamos la montaña exactamente como la encontramos. El respeto es parte de que os dejen volver.',
  'After the flight': 'Después del vuelo',
  'The flight does not have to be the whole day. Couples pair it with a slow lunch on a hut terrace, a swim in a cold alpine lake, a via ferrata or an easy hike, or simply a bottle opened somewhere with a view. The Dolomites make an easy honeymoon base too &mdash; Cortina, Val Gardena and the Alta Badia villages sit within an hour of everything, full of huts, spas and long dinners. We are happy to sketch the days around your elopement, not just the hour of it.': 'El vuelo no tiene por qué ser todo el día. Las parejas lo combinan con una comida sin prisas en la terraza de un refugio, un baño en un frío lago alpino, una vía ferrata o una caminata fácil, o simplemente una botella abierta en algún lugar con vistas. Los Dolomitas son además una base fácil para la luna de miel &mdash; Cortina, Val Gardena y los pueblos de la Alta Badia están a menos de una hora de todo, llenos de refugios, spas y cenas largas. Con gusto esbozamos los días alrededor de vuestro elopement, no solo su hora.',
  'The couple taking in the panorama after the ceremony': 'La pareja contemplando el panorama tras la ceremonia',
  'A favourite pairing is a lake to finish. After the summit, a landing or a short drive brings you to still water &mdash; a mirror of turquoise under the peaks &mdash; for the softest frames of the day and a first quiet moment as a married couple. Others want nothing planned at all after the flight: just a blanket, a view and the rest of the morning to themselves. There is no wrong way to spend the hours we are not photographing; we simply make sure they are yours.': 'Una combinación favorita es terminar en un lago. Tras la cumbre, un aterrizaje o un breve trayecto os lleva a aguas quietas &mdash; un espejo turquesa bajo las cumbres &mdash; para los encuadres más suaves del día y un primer momento tranquilo como pareja casada. Otros no quieren nada planeado después del vuelo: solo una manta, una vista y el resto de la mañana para ellos. No hay forma equivocada de pasar las horas que no fotografiamos; simplemente nos aseguramos de que sean vuestras.',
  'A turquoise Dolomite lake reached to finish the day': 'Un lago turquesa de los Dolomitas alcanzado para cerrar el día',
  'Helicopter, cable car or hike?': '¿Helicóptero, teleférico o caminata?',
  'A flight is the boldest way up, but not the only one. If you want the summit feeling without the price, a cable car to the Lagazuoi, Sass Pordoi or Seceda delivers an enormous view for the cost of a ticket &mdash; though the lifts open well after sunrise. If you want the day to feel earned, a hike gives you solitude and costs nothing but the early alarm. We often combine them: fly in for the drama, then walk a few minutes to a quieter ledge. Unsure? Tell us how you feel about heights, effort and budget, and we will tell you honestly which one fits.': 'Un vuelo es la forma más audaz de subir, pero no la única. Si queréis la sensación de cumbre sin el precio, un teleférico al Lagazuoi, el Sass Pordoi o la Seceda ofrece una vista enorme por el coste de un billete &mdash; aunque los remontes abren bastante después del amanecer. Si queréis que el día se sienta merecido, una caminata os da soledad y no cuesta nada salvo el despertador temprano. A menudo los combinamos: llegar en vuelo por el drama, luego caminar unos minutos a un rincón más tranquilo. ¿Dudáis? Decidnos cómo os sentís con las alturas, el esfuerzo y el presupuesto, y os diremos con honestidad cuál encaja.',
  'The couple walking a quiet ridge after landing': 'La pareja caminando por una arista tranquila tras el aterrizaje',
  'What it is': 'Qué es',
  'How the day unfolds': 'Cómo transcurre el día',
  'Where you can land': 'Dónde aterrizar',
  'Getting there': 'Cómo llegar',
  'Weather & Plan B': 'Tiempo y plan B',
  'What to wear': 'Qué llevar',
  'Papers & legal': 'Papeles y ley',
  'Drones & respect': 'Drones y respeto',
  'Heli, cable car or hike?': '¿Heli, teleférico o caminata?',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'Helicopter elopement FAQ': 'Preguntas frecuentes sobre el elopement en helicóptero',
  'A helicopter turns a two-day trek into a ten-minute flight and sets you down where almost no one else can stand &mdash; a remote ledge of rock, a glacier shoulder, a summit ringed by the pale towers of the Dolomites. It is the most direct way we know to the extraordinary: no long approach, no compromise on the view, just the two of you and a mountain kept entirely to yourselves. Here is everything we have learned planning helicopter elopements in the Dolomites &mdash; how the flight works, what it costs, where you can land, the paperwork, the weather, and how to make the day feel like yours.': 'Un helicóptero convierte una travesía de dos días en un vuelo de diez minutos y os deja donde casi nadie más puede estar &mdash; un lejano lecho de roca, un hombro glaciar, una cumbre rodeada por las pálidas torres de los Dolomitas. Es el camino más directo que conocemos a lo extraordinario: sin larga aproximación, sin compromisos con la vista, solo vosotros dos y una montaña enteramente para vosotros. Aquí está todo lo que hemos aprendido planificando elopements en helicóptero en los Dolomitas &mdash; cómo funciona el vuelo, cuánto cuesta, dónde podéis aterrizar, el papeleo, el tiempo, y cómo hacer que el día se sienta vuestro.',
  'On this page': 'En esta página',
}
HELI_IT = {
  'The couple embracing in a summer meadow, the helicopter behind them': "La coppia abbracciata in un prato estivo, l'elicottero dietro",
  'The couple on a green summit with the helicopter and the Dolomites behind': "La coppia su una vetta verde con l'elicottero e le Dolomiti dietro",
  'The couple walking to the helicopter to board for the flight': "La coppia che cammina verso l'elicottero per imbarcarsi per il volo",
  'The couple inside the helicopter cabin during the flight': "La coppia dentro la cabina dell'elicottero durante il volo",
  'The couple with the helicopter on a snowy plateau at last light': "La coppia con l'elicottero su un plateau innevato nell'ultima luce",
  'The couple beside the helicopter on a ridge, veil in the wind': "La coppia accanto all'elicottero su una cresta, il velo al vento",
  'The couple kissing in front of the helicopter in warm light': "La coppia che si bacia davanti all'elicottero nella luce calda",
  'A bride in a winter coat stepping out of the helicopter into the snow': "Una sposa con cappotto invernale che scende dall'elicottero sulla neve",
  'The couple alone on a ridge with the helicopter and a Dolomite panorama': "La coppia sola su una cresta con l'elicottero e un panorama dolomitico",
  'A chef making fresh pizza on the mountain, the helicopter behind': "Uno chef che prepara pizza fresca in montagna, l'elicottero dietro",
  'What a helicopter elopement actually is': "Cos'è davvero un elopement in elicottero",
  'A helicopter elopement is a very small mountain wedding with one difference: you reach your ceremony by air. A licensed alpine helicopter lifts the two of you (and, if you like, a witness or two) from a valley helipad, flies you over the peaks and sets down on an approved landing site &mdash; a ridge, a high meadow, a glacier plateau. You say your vows with the whole range beneath your feet, take portraits while the light is good, and fly back. The flight is not a transfer; it becomes half the story.': "Un elopement in elicottero è un matrimonio di montagna molto piccolo con una differenza: raggiungete la vostra cerimonia dall'alto. Un elicottero alpino autorizzato solleva voi due (e, se volete, uno o due testimoni) da un'elisuperficie a valle, vi porta sopra le cime e atterra su un sito approvato &mdash; una cresta, un prato d'alta quota, un plateau glaciale. Vi scambiate le promesse con l'intera catena sotto i piedi, fate i ritratti finché la luce è buona e rientrate. Il volo non è un trasferimento: diventa metà della storia.",
  'The machine carries up to <strong>six passengers plus the pilot</strong>, so bringing a witness or two &mdash; or even a few close guests &mdash; is no problem, and you still fly comfortably. Most of our couples keep it to just the two of them; some bring their witnesses up for the ceremony. Either way, there is room.': "La macchina porta fino a <strong>sei passeggeri più il pilota</strong>, quindi portare uno o due testimoni &mdash; o anche pochi invitati stretti &mdash; non è un problema, e volate comodi. La maggior parte delle nostre coppie resta solo in due; alcuni fanno salire i testimoni per la cerimonia. In ogni caso, c'è posto.",
  'A helicopter over the Dolomite peaks at golden hour': "Un elicottero sopra le cime delle Dolomiti nell'ora dorata",
  'Couples come to it for different reasons. Some cannot hike far &mdash; a knee, a pregnancy, a dress that was never built for scree &mdash; and a flight gives them a summit anyway. Some simply want the one thing money can still buy in a crowded range: a place, for an hour, with no one else in it. And some love the flight for itself, the door open, the valley dropping away, the first sight of the peaks from above. Whatever brings you, the result is the same &mdash; a day that feels less like a wedding you attended and more like an adventure you took together.': "Le coppie ci arrivano per motivi diversi. Alcune non possono camminare a lungo &mdash; un ginocchio, una gravidanza, un abito mai pensato per i ghiaioni &mdash; e un volo regala loro comunque una vetta. Altre vogliono semplicemente l'unica cosa che il denaro può ancora comprare in una catena affollata: un luogo, per un'ora, senza nessun altro. E altre amano il volo in sé, la porta aperta, la valle che si allontana, la prima vista delle cime dall'alto. Qualunque cosa vi porti, il risultato è lo stesso &mdash; una giornata che sembra meno un matrimonio a cui avete partecipato e più un'avventura vissuta insieme.",
  'Exchanging rings on the mountain after the flight': 'Scambio degli anelli in montagna dopo il volo',
  'How the day unfolds, step by step': 'Come si svolge la giornata, passo dopo passo',
  '<strong>1. First call.</strong> We start with a video call to understand the day you picture &mdash; sunrise or golden hour, a bare summit or a lake, just the two of you or a few guests. <strong>2. Landing site &amp; operator.</strong> We match your vision to an approved landing site and book a licensed alpine operator; some sites need advance clearance. <strong>3. Timing &amp; weather window.</strong> We fix a date but keep a flexible window and a backup day &mdash; the flight only happens in safe conditions. <strong>4. Getting ready.</strong> Hair, make-up and dressing happen in the valley before the flight. <strong>5. The flight.</strong> A short set-down at the helipad, headsets on, and minutes later you step out onto the mountain. <strong>6. Ceremony &amp; portraits.</strong> Your words, then portraits &mdash; the pilot stays on the mountain with you, and you have up to a full hour on each landing before you fly on. <strong>7. Back down</strong> &mdash; often with time for a second landing, a hut lunch or a lakeside toast.': "<strong>1. Prima chiamata.</strong> Iniziamo con una videochiamata per capire la giornata che immaginate &mdash; alba o ora dorata, una vetta spoglia o un lago, solo voi due o pochi invitati. <strong>2. Sito di atterraggio e operatore.</strong> Abbiniamo la vostra idea a un sito approvato e prenotiamo un operatore alpino autorizzato; alcuni siti richiedono un permesso anticipato. <strong>3. Data e finestra meteo.</strong> Fissiamo una data ma teniamo una finestra flessibile e un giorno di riserva &mdash; si vola solo in condizioni sicure. <strong>4. Preparativi.</strong> Capelli, trucco e vestizione avvengono a valle prima del volo. <strong>5. Il volo.</strong> Un breve appoggio all'elisuperficie, cuffie indossate, e minuti dopo scendete in montagna. <strong>6. Cerimonia e ritratti.</strong> Le vostre parole, poi i ritratti &mdash; il pilota resta con voi in montagna, e avete fino a un'ora intera a ogni atterraggio prima di proseguire. <strong>7. Rientro a valle</strong> &mdash; spesso con tempo per un secondo atterraggio, un pranzo in rifugio o un brindisi in riva al lago.",
  'That hour matters. Because the pilot waits with you rather than flying off and coming back, there is no clock-watching for a returning machine and no rush through your vows &mdash; you get a genuine, unhurried hour on each spot for the ceremony and portraits.': "Quell'ora conta. Poiché il pilota aspetta con voi invece di ripartire e tornare, non c'è da guardare l'orologio per una macchina che rientra né fretta nelle vostre promesse &mdash; avete un'ora autentica e senza fretta in ogni luogo per la cerimonia e i ritratti.",
  'Bride with a headset inside the helicopter before take-off': "Sposa con la cuffia dentro l'elicottero prima del decollo",
  'View across the cockpit as the helicopter climbs over the valley': "Vista attraverso la cabina mentre l'elicottero sale sopra la valle",
  'The flight itself is short and unforgettable. The rotor spins up, the machine goes light, and the valley simply falls away; a minute later the first peaks slide past the window at eye level, closer than you have ever seen them. Nobody speaks much &mdash; you just watch. Then the pilot picks the line in, the skids touch, the noise drops, and you step out into a silence so complete it rings. That contrast &mdash; from thunder to hush in thirty seconds &mdash; is a feeling couples talk about for years.': "Il volo in sé è breve e indimenticabile. Il rotore accelera, la macchina si alleggerisce e la valle semplicemente sprofonda; un minuto dopo le prime cime scorrono all'altezza degli occhi accanto al finestrino, più vicine di quanto le abbiate mai viste. Nessuno parla molto &mdash; guardate soltanto. Poi il pilota sceglie la linea d'ingresso, i pattini toccano, il rumore cala e scendete in un silenzio così pieno da risuonare. Quel contrasto &mdash; dal tuono alla quiete in trenta secondi &mdash; è una sensazione di cui le coppie parlano per anni.",
  'A sharp ridge line seen from above during the flight': "Una cresta affilata vista dall'alto durante il volo",
  'Two example timelines': 'Due esempi di programma',
  '<strong>A sunrise flight.</strong> 04:30 hair &amp; make-up in the valley &middot; 05:30 short drive to the helipad &middot; 06:00 lift-off as first light hits the peaks &middot; 06:15 set down on the ridge, ceremony as the rock turns pink &middot; 06:40 portraits in the still, empty light &middot; 07:15 fly back &middot; 08:00 breakfast at a mountain hut.': "<strong>Un volo all'alba.</strong> 04:30 capelli e trucco a valle &middot; 05:30 breve tragitto all'elisuperficie &middot; 06:00 decollo quando la prima luce colpisce le cime &middot; 06:15 atterraggio sulla cresta, cerimonia mentre la roccia si tinge di rosa &middot; 06:40 ritratti nella luce quieta e vuota &middot; 07:15 volo di rientro &middot; 08:00 colazione in un rifugio di montagna.",
  '<strong>A full golden-hour day.</strong> 15:00 getting ready &middot; 16:30 first flight to a high landing for portraits &middot; 17:30 ceremony at a second spot &middot; 18:30 the range glows at last light (enrosadira) &middot; 19:15 fly down &middot; 20:00 dinner on a hut terrace. Times shift with the season &mdash; we build the exact schedule around the sunrise and your landing site.': "<strong>Una giornata intera fino all'ora dorata.</strong> 15:00 preparativi &middot; 16:30 primo volo a un atterraggio alto per i ritratti &middot; 17:30 cerimonia in un secondo luogo &middot; 18:30 la catena si accende nell'ultima luce (enrosadira) &middot; 19:15 volo di discesa &middot; 20:00 cena sulla terrazza di un rifugio. Gli orari cambiano con la stagione &mdash; costruiamo il programma esatto attorno all'alba e al vostro sito di atterraggio.",
  'One thing sets the outer limits of the day: the helicopter may lift off from <strong>half an hour before sunrise</strong> and must be back at its airport by <strong>half an hour after sunset</strong>. That is a generous window &mdash; wide enough for both a true first-light flight and a full golden-hour evening &mdash; and we build your exact times around the sunrise for your date, which shifts through the season.': "Una cosa segna i limiti della giornata: l'elicottero può decollare da <strong>mezz'ora prima dell'alba</strong> e deve rientrare al suo aeroporto entro <strong>mezz'ora dopo il tramonto</strong>. È una finestra generosa &mdash; ampia sia per un vero volo di prima luce sia per un'intera serata nell'ora dorata &mdash; e adattiamo i vostri orari esatti all'alba della vostra data, che si sposta con la stagione.",
  'The Dolomite walls glowing pink at last light behind the couple': "Le pareti delle Dolomiti che brillano di rosa nell'ultima luce dietro la coppia",
  'Silhouetted peaks against a warm sunset sky': 'Cime in controluce contro un caldo cielo al tramonto',
  'What it costs': 'Quanto costa',
  'The flight is booked as a charter, and the structure is simple. The minimum is a <strong>50-minute flight including one landing</strong> &mdash; enough for a ceremony and portraits at a single spot. You can add more landings to see more of the range; we usually recommend <strong>no more than three</strong>, so the day stays about being on the mountain rather than in and out of the machine. A few sought-after sites carry a surcharge (see below). The exact flight price depends on your date, your landings and the operator, so we confirm it in writing before anything is booked.': "Il volo si prenota come charter, e la struttura è semplice. Il minimo è un <strong>volo di 50 minuti con un atterraggio</strong> &mdash; sufficiente per una cerimonia e i ritratti in un solo luogo. Potete aggiungere altri atterraggi per vedere di più della catena; di solito consigliamo <strong>non più di tre</strong>, così la giornata resta lo stare in montagna e non l'entrare e uscire dalla macchina. Alcuni siti molto richiesti hanno un supplemento (vedi sotto). Il prezzo esatto del volo dipende dalla data, dagli atterraggi e dall'operatore, quindi lo confermiamo per iscritto prima di prenotare qualsiasi cosa.",
  'The helicopter waiting on the valley helipad': "L'elicottero in attesa sull'elisuperficie a valle",
  'It is worth being honest about what drives the number. The bigger levers are the total flight time, the number of landings you add beyond the first, and the landing point itself &mdash; a few premium sites carry a surcharge. Add-ons &mdash; a second location, film, flowers, a celebrant &mdash; sit on top, and we price them plainly so nothing is a surprise on the invoice. A helicopter day is not the cheapest way to elope, but it buys something specific: an hour on a summit that would otherwise cost you two days and a lot of luck.': "Vale la pena essere onesti su cosa determina il prezzo. Le leve maggiori sono il tempo di volo totale, il numero di atterraggi che aggiungete oltre il primo e il sito di atterraggio stesso &mdash; alcuni siti premium hanno un supplemento. Gli extra &mdash; una seconda location, il video, i fiori, un celebrante &mdash; si aggiungono a parte, e li quotiamo con chiarezza così nulla sorprende in fattura. Una giornata in elicottero non è il modo più economico per sposarsi in fuga, ma compra qualcosa di preciso: un'ora su una vetta che altrimenti vi costerebbe due giorni e molta fortuna.",
  'Where a helicopter can land you': 'Dove un elicottero può portarvi',
  'A flight opens ground a normal elopement never reaches: a remote rock ledge, a glacier plateau on the Marmolada, a summit that would otherwise be a two-day climb, a shoulder beneath the Cadini or Tre Cime spires. Landings are flown by licensed alpine operators onto approved sites only &mdash; not anywhere you like, and not inside every protected zone. We choose the spot together for the view, the light and what is actually permitted, and confirm it before we book.': 'Un volo apre terreni che un elopement normale non raggiunge mai: un lembo di roccia remoto, un plateau glaciale sulla Marmolada, una vetta che altrimenti sarebbe una salita di due giorni, una spalla sotto le guglie dei Cadini o delle Tre Cime. Gli atterraggi sono effettuati da operatori alpini autorizzati solo su siti approvati &mdash; non ovunque vogliate, e non dentro ogni zona protetta. Scegliamo il luogo insieme per la vista, la luce e ciò che è davvero permesso, e lo confermiamo prima di prenotare.',
  'Broadly there are three kinds of landing, and they feel different. A <strong>ridge or summit</strong> gives you exposure and a 360-degree horizon &mdash; the boldest frames, the most wind. A <strong>high meadow or shoulder</strong> is gentler underfoot, kinder to a dress and easy to move around on. A <strong>glacier plateau</strong> is the rarest and most otherworldly, a field of white with nothing human in sight. Not every one is available everywhere or in every season, and some sit inside protected zones that are off-limits; we work only where landings are permitted and safe.': "In linea di massima ci sono tre tipi di atterraggio, e si percepiscono in modo diverso. Una <strong>cresta o vetta</strong> vi dà esposizione e un orizzonte a 360 gradi &mdash; le inquadrature più audaci, il vento maggiore. Un <strong>prato o una spalla d'alta quota</strong> è più dolce sotto i piedi, più gentile con l'abito e facile da percorrere. Un <strong>plateau glaciale</strong> è il più raro e ultraterreno, un campo bianco senza nulla di umano in vista. Non tutti sono disponibili ovunque o in ogni stagione, e alcuni si trovano dentro zone protette off-limits; lavoriamo solo dove gli atterraggi sono permessi e sicuri.",
  'You do not have to navigate the permissions yourself: the <strong>helicopter operator arranges the landing clearances</strong> for each site, which is exactly why we fly only with licensed local companies. A handful of the most iconic spots &mdash; the Seceda above Ortisei is the classic example &mdash; carry an extra landing fee, typically <strong>around &euro;300&ndash;500</strong>. We tell you upfront which of your dream landings is free to use and which comes with a surcharge, so the shortlist you fall in love with is one we can actually deliver.': "Non dovete occuparvi voi dei permessi: la <strong>società di elicotteri gestisce le autorizzazioni di atterraggio</strong> per ogni sito, ed è proprio per questo che voliamo solo con compagnie locali autorizzate. Una manciata dei luoghi più iconici &mdash; la Seceda sopra Ortisei è l'esempio classico &mdash; comporta una tariffa di atterraggio extra, di solito <strong>attorno ai 300&ndash;500&nbsp;&euro;</strong>. Vi diciamo in anticipo quale dei vostri atterraggi da sogno è libero e quale ha un supplemento, così la rosa di cui vi innamorate è una che possiamo davvero realizzare.",
  'An aerial view of a jagged Dolomite peak from the helicopter': "Veduta aerea di una frastagliata cima dolomitica dall'elicottero",
  'The couple stepping out onto the mountain beside the landed helicopter': "La coppia che scende in montagna accanto all'elicottero appena atterrato",
  'Getting there &amp; the helipad': "Come arrivare e l'elisuperficie",
  'Most couples fly into Venice, Verona or Innsbruck and drive the last stretch &mdash; roughly two to three hours to the heart of the Dolomites. Getting ready happens in the valley, then a short drive to the departure helipad. From there the flight is minutes, not hours. If you would rather not self-drive, we arrange transfers so the morning stays calm.': "La maggior parte delle coppie atterra a Venezia, Verona o Innsbruck e guida l'ultimo tratto &mdash; circa due o tre ore fino al cuore delle Dolomiti. I preparativi avvengono a valle, poi un breve tragitto all'elisuperficie di partenza. Da lì il volo è di minuti, non di ore. Se preferite non guidare, organizziamo i transfer così la mattina resta serena.",
  'There are <strong>two local operators</strong> we work with, each with its own base. <strong>Elikos</strong> flies from its airfield in <strong>Pontives</strong>, just below Ortisei in Val Gardena &mdash; about a 30-minute drive from Brixen. <strong>Kron Air</strong> departs from <strong>Olang</strong> in the Pustertal, roughly 20 minutes from Bruneck. Which one we choose depends on your landing site and where you are staying; both put the high Dolomites within a short flight. We match the base to your day and tell you exactly where to be and when.': "Ci sono <strong>due operatori locali</strong> con cui lavoriamo, ciascuno con la propria base. <strong>Elikos</strong> vola dal suo campo di volo a <strong>Pontives</strong>, appena sotto Ortisei in Val Gardena &mdash; a circa 30 minuti d'auto da Bressanone (Brixen). <strong>Kron Air</strong> parte da <strong>Valdaora (Olang)</strong> in Val Pusteria, a circa 20 minuti da Brunico. Quale scegliere dipende dal vostro sito di atterraggio e da dove alloggiate; entrambi mettono le alte Dolomiti a un breve volo. Abbiniamo la base alla vostra giornata e vi diciamo esattamente dove essere e quando.",
  'The Dolomite peaks seen from the helicopter window': "Le cime delle Dolomiti viste dal finestrino dell'elicottero",
  'Weather &amp; Plan B': 'Meteo e piano B',
  'A helicopter flies only in safe conditions &mdash; good visibility, workable wind, no storm. Mountain weather turns fast, so we watch the forecast in the days before and keep a flexible window and, from our middle package up, a spare backup day. If the flight cannot go on your first morning, we move it; if a window never opens, we have a ground-based Plan B ready &mdash; a cable-car summit, a lake, a ridge you can reach on foot &mdash; so you are married beautifully either way. Fog and low cloud are not the enemy: some of the most atmospheric mountain photographs happen in exactly that light.': 'Un elicottero vola solo in condizioni sicure &mdash; buona visibilità, vento gestibile, niente temporale. Il meteo di montagna cambia in fretta, così seguiamo le previsioni nei giorni prima e teniamo una finestra flessibile e, dal nostro pacchetto intermedio in su, un giorno di riserva. Se il volo non può partire la prima mattina, lo spostiamo; se una finestra non si apre mai, abbiamo pronto un piano B a terra &mdash; una vetta con funivia, un lago, una cresta raggiungibile a piedi &mdash; così vi sposate splendidamente in ogni caso. Nebbia e nubi basse non sono il nemico: alcune delle foto di montagna più suggestive nascono proprio con quella luce.',
  'A peak breaking through cloud, seen from the air': "Una cima che buca le nubi, vista dall'alto",
  'Summer or winter?': 'Estate o inverno?',
  'A summer flight lands you on green shoulders and warm rock at first or last light; a winter flight lands you in a white world &mdash; snow to the horizon, the peaks stripped to black and white, your breath in the air. Winter is quieter, colder and more dramatic, and it opens something summer cannot: a ceremony on a snow ridge, and, for the bold, skis on and the first run down together in gown and black tie. It asks for warm layers, good edges and a flexible eye on the weather &mdash; we handle the flight, the timing and the light, so all you bring is the nerve. Both seasons are beautiful; we help you choose the one that matches the day in your head.': "Un volo estivo vi posa su spalle verdi e roccia calda alla prima o all'ultima luce; un volo invernale vi posa in un mondo bianco &mdash; neve fino all'orizzonte, le cime ridotte al bianco e nero, il vostro fiato nell'aria. L'inverno è più silenzioso, più freddo e più drammatico, e apre qualcosa che l'estate non può: una cerimonia su una cresta innevata e, per i più audaci, gli sci ai piedi e la prima discesa insieme in abito e cravatta nera. Chiede strati caldi, buone lamine e un occhio flessibile sul meteo &mdash; noi gestiamo il volo, i tempi e la luce, così portate solo il coraggio. Entrambe le stagioni sono bellissime; vi aiutiamo a scegliere quella che corrisponde alla giornata che avete in testa.",
  'A snow-covered Dolomite peak reached by helicopter in winter': "Una cima dolomitica innevata raggiunta in elicottero d'inverno",
  'What to wear up there': 'Cosa indossare lassù',
  'It is cold at altitude, even in August &mdash; a summit at dawn can be near freezing while the valley is warm. Bring warm layers you can slip off for photos and back on between them, and a wrap or coat for the dress. Shoes matter: pack sturdy footwear for the landing site and change into the pretty ones for the frames. Rotor wash is real &mdash; hair, veils and loose petals move in the downdraught, which often looks wonderful, but secure anything you do not want to lose. We tell you exactly what to expect for your date and landing so nothing catches you out.': "In quota fa freddo, anche ad agosto &mdash; una vetta all'alba può essere vicina allo zero mentre la valle è calda. Portate strati caldi da togliere per le foto e rimettere tra una e l'altra, e una mantella o un cappotto per l'abito. Le scarpe contano: portate calzature robuste per il sito di atterraggio e cambiatele con quelle belle per gli scatti. Il vento del rotore è reale &mdash; capelli, veli e petali sciolti si muovono nella corrente discendente, cosa che spesso è splendida, ma fissate tutto ciò che non volete perdere. Vi diciamo esattamente cosa aspettarvi per la vostra data e il vostro atterraggio, così nulla vi coglie di sorpresa.",
  'The couple on a wind-scoured ridge, dress moving in the breeze': "La coppia su una cresta spazzata dal vento, l'abito che si muove nella brezza",
  'A portrait on the summit with the Dolomites behind': 'Un ritratto in vetta con le Dolomiti alle spalle',
  'Papers &amp; making it legal': 'Documenti e la parte legale',
  'A helicopter flight is the setting, not the legal act &mdash; and there are two honest paths. <strong>A symbolic ceremony</strong> in the mountains with the legal marriage at home is what most of our couples choose: you sign the papers at your local registry before or after the trip, and up here you have the ceremony that actually matters. <strong>A legal civil marriage</strong> is also possible: in Italy for foreign nationals it means a certificate of no impediment (Nulla Osta / Ehefähigkeitszeugnis), international birth certificates, valid passports, usually an apostille and sworn translations, started months ahead; Austria offers civil ceremonies and, in some regions, approved outdoor locations. Couples from Germany, Austria, the USA and the UK all marry here &mdash; the paperwork differs by country, and we point you to the right path for yours.': "Un volo in elicottero è la cornice, non l'atto legale &mdash; e ci sono due strade oneste. <strong>Una cerimonia simbolica</strong> in montagna con il matrimonio legale a casa è ciò che sceglie la maggior parte delle nostre coppie: firmate i documenti al vostro comune prima o dopo il viaggio, e quassù avete la cerimonia che conta davvero. <strong>Un matrimonio civile con valore legale</strong> è anch'esso possibile: in Italia per gli stranieri significa un nulla osta (Nulla Osta / Ehefähigkeitszeugnis), certificati di nascita internazionali, passaporti validi, di solito un'apostille e traduzioni giurate, avviati con mesi di anticipo; l'Austria offre cerimonie civili e, in alcune regioni, luoghi all'aperto autorizzati. Coppie da Germania, Austria, USA e Regno Unito si sposano qui &mdash; le pratiche cambiano da Paese a Paese, e vi indichiamo la strada giusta per la vostra.",
  'One honest word on timing: the earlier you tell us, the more we can hold for you. The best summer dawn slots and every winter date fill first, and a legal marriage abroad needs its documents started months ahead. Reach out as soon as you have a rough season in mind &mdash; even before the exact date &mdash; and we will pencil in a window, sketch the day and tell you what to set in motion at home. Nothing is locked until you are ready; an early conversation simply keeps the good mornings open.': "Una parola onesta sui tempi: prima ce lo dite, più possiamo tenervi. I migliori albori estivi e tutte le date invernali si riempiono per primi, e un matrimonio legale all'estero richiede documenti avviati con mesi di anticipo. Scriveteci appena avete in mente una stagione di massima &mdash; anche prima della data esatta &mdash; e segneremo una finestra, abbozzeremo la giornata e vi diremo cosa mettere in moto a casa. Nulla è bloccato finché non siete pronti; una conversazione anticipata tiene semplicemente aperte le mattine buone.",
  'One point to be clear about: in Italy a <strong>legally binding marriage can only take place at a registry office (comune)</strong> &mdash; never at a landing site on the mountain. So the ceremony up on the peak is always a symbolic one, and it is every bit as moving for it: your vows, your words, the two of you and the range. The legal signature happens at a town hall &mdash; at home, or at an Italian comune before or after the flight &mdash; and we help you line up the paperwork either way.': 'Un punto da chiarire: in Italia un <strong>matrimonio con valore legale può avvenire solo in comune</strong> &mdash; mai su un sito di atterraggio in montagna. Perciò la cerimonia in vetta è sempre simbolica, e non per questo meno commovente: le vostre promesse, le vostre parole, voi due e la catena. La firma legale avviene in municipio &mdash; a casa, o in un comune italiano prima o dopo il volo &mdash; e vi aiutiamo a preparare le pratiche in entrambi i casi.',
  'Exchanging vows on the summit, the range spread below': 'Scambio delle promesse in vetta, la catena distesa in basso',
  'Above the crowds': 'Sopra la folla',
  'The Dolomites are the most photographed range in Europe, and the icons fill up. A flight is the cleanest way past that: you land where the day-trippers cannot follow and the summit is yours. Even so, we plan for the quiet hours &mdash; first light before the valleys wake, or last light after they empty &mdash; because empty light is always the better light.': "Le Dolomiti sono la catena più fotografata d'Europa, e le icone si affollano. Un volo è il modo più netto per lasciarle indietro: atterrate dove i gitanti di giornata non possono seguirvi e la vetta è vostra. Anche così, pianifichiamo per le ore tranquille &mdash; la prima luce prima che le valli si sveglino, o l'ultima luce quando si svuotano &mdash; perché la luce vuota è sempre la luce migliore.",
  'The couple alone on a summit ridge with nobody else in sight': 'La coppia sola su una cresta di vetta senza nessun altro in vista',
  'Drones, protected zones &amp; flying responsibly': 'Droni, zone protette e volare responsabilmente',
  'A helicopter is not a drone. Licensed alpine flights land on approved sites under strict rules; private drones, by contrast, are banned across much of the Dolomites &mdash; Lago di Braies has prohibited them since 2026, patrolled by rangers and subject to fines &mdash; and inside nature-reserve zones generally. On the ground we stay on the landing site, off the meadows and out of protected vegetation, and we leave the mountain exactly as we found it. Respect is part of being allowed back.': "Un elicottero non è un drone. I voli alpini autorizzati atterrano su siti approvati secondo regole severe; i droni privati, al contrario, sono vietati in gran parte delle Dolomiti &mdash; il Lago di Braies li proibisce dal 2026, con controlli dei guardaparco e sanzioni &mdash; e in generale dentro le zone di riserva naturale. A terra restiamo sul sito di atterraggio, fuori dai prati e dalla vegetazione protetta, e lasciamo la montagna esattamente come l'abbiamo trovata. Il rispetto fa parte del poter tornare.",
  'After the flight': 'Dopo il volo',
  'The flight does not have to be the whole day. Couples pair it with a slow lunch on a hut terrace, a swim in a cold alpine lake, a via ferrata or an easy hike, or simply a bottle opened somewhere with a view. The Dolomites make an easy honeymoon base too &mdash; Cortina, Val Gardena and the Alta Badia villages sit within an hour of everything, full of huts, spas and long dinners. We are happy to sketch the days around your elopement, not just the hour of it.': "Il volo non deve essere tutta la giornata. Le coppie lo abbinano a un pranzo lento sulla terrazza di un rifugio, un tuffo in un freddo lago alpino, una via ferrata o una camminata facile, o semplicemente una bottiglia aperta in un posto con vista. Le Dolomiti sono anche una comoda base per la luna di miele &mdash; Cortina, la Val Gardena e i paesi dell'Alta Badia sono a meno di un'ora da tutto, pieni di rifugi, spa e cene lunghe. Con piacere abbozziamo i giorni attorno al vostro elopement, non solo la sua ora.",
  'The couple taking in the panorama after the ceremony': 'La coppia che ammira il panorama dopo la cerimonia',
  'A favourite pairing is a lake to finish. After the summit, a landing or a short drive brings you to still water &mdash; a mirror of turquoise under the peaks &mdash; for the softest frames of the day and a first quiet moment as a married couple. Others want nothing planned at all after the flight: just a blanket, a view and the rest of the morning to themselves. There is no wrong way to spend the hours we are not photographing; we simply make sure they are yours.': "Un abbinamento preferito è chiudere con un lago. Dopo la vetta, un atterraggio o un breve tragitto vi porta ad acque calme &mdash; uno specchio turchese sotto le cime &mdash; per le inquadrature più morbide della giornata e un primo momento di quiete da sposati. Altri non vogliono nulla di pianificato dopo il volo: solo una coperta, una vista e il resto della mattina per sé. Non c'è modo sbagliato di passare le ore in cui non fotografiamo; ci assicuriamo semplicemente che siano vostre.",
  'A turquoise Dolomite lake reached to finish the day': 'Un lago turchese delle Dolomiti raggiunto per chiudere la giornata',
  'Helicopter, cable car or hike?': 'Elicottero, funivia o escursione?',
  'A flight is the boldest way up, but not the only one. If you want the summit feeling without the price, a cable car to the Lagazuoi, Sass Pordoi or Seceda delivers an enormous view for the cost of a ticket &mdash; though the lifts open well after sunrise. If you want the day to feel earned, a hike gives you solitude and costs nothing but the early alarm. We often combine them: fly in for the drama, then walk a few minutes to a quieter ledge. Unsure? Tell us how you feel about heights, effort and budget, and we will tell you honestly which one fits.': "Un volo è il modo più audace per salire, ma non l'unico. Se volete la sensazione della vetta senza il prezzo, una funivia al Lagazuoi, al Sass Pordoi o al Seceda regala un panorama enorme al costo di un biglietto &mdash; anche se gli impianti aprono ben dopo l'alba. Se volete che la giornata sia conquistata, un'escursione dona solitudine e non costa nulla se non la sveglia presto. Spesso li combiniamo: arrivare in volo per l'effetto, poi camminare pochi minuti fino a un lembo più quieto. Indecisi? Diteci come vivete le altezze, la fatica e il budget, e vi diremo con onestà quale fa per voi.",
  'The couple walking a quiet ridge after landing': "La coppia che cammina su una cresta tranquilla dopo l'atterraggio",
  'What it is': "Cos'è",
  'How the day unfolds': 'Come si svolge la giornata',
  'Where you can land': 'Dove atterrare',
  'Getting there': 'Come arrivare',
  'Weather & Plan B': 'Meteo e piano B',
  'What to wear': 'Cosa indossare',
  'Papers & legal': 'Documenti e legge',
  'Drones & respect': 'Droni e rispetto',
  'Heli, cable car or hike?': 'Eli, funivia o escursione?',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'Helicopter elopement FAQ': "Domande frequenti sull'elopement in elicottero",
  'A helicopter turns a two-day trek into a ten-minute flight and sets you down where almost no one else can stand &mdash; a remote ledge of rock, a glacier shoulder, a summit ringed by the pale towers of the Dolomites. It is the most direct way we know to the extraordinary: no long approach, no compromise on the view, just the two of you and a mountain kept entirely to yourselves. Here is everything we have learned planning helicopter elopements in the Dolomites &mdash; how the flight works, what it costs, where you can land, the paperwork, the weather, and how to make the day feel like yours.': "Un elicottero trasforma un trekking di due giorni in un volo di dieci minuti e vi posa dove quasi nessun altro può stare &mdash; un lembo di roccia remoto, una spalla glaciale, una vetta cinta dalle pallide torri delle Dolomiti. È la via più diretta che conosciamo allo straordinario: nessun lungo avvicinamento, nessun compromesso sulla vista, solo voi due e una montagna tutta per voi. Qui c'è tutto ciò che abbiamo imparato pianificando elopement in elicottero nelle Dolomiti &mdash; come funziona il volo, quanto costa, dove potete atterrare, le pratiche, il meteo, e come far sentire la giornata vostra.",
  'On this page': 'In questa pagina',
}
HELI_FAQ_ES = {
  'How much does a helicopter elopement cost?': ('¿Cuánto cuesta un elopement en helicóptero?', 'El vuelo se reserva como un chárter &mdash; el mínimo es un vuelo de 50 minutos con un aterrizaje, y podéis añadir más (recomendamos hasta tres). Unos pocos sitios premium como la Seceda tienen un suplemento de unos 300&ndash;500&nbsp;&euro;. Confirmamos el precio exacto del vuelo por escrito, y la fotografía y el resto del día se presupuestan aparte.'),
  'How long are we actually in the air?': ('¿Cuánto tiempo estamos realmente en el aire?', 'Normalmente solo minutos por trayecto &mdash; los Dolomitas están cerca. El vuelo sustituye una caminata de horas, así que pasáis la mayor parte del tiempo en la montaña, no en tránsito.'),
  'Where can the helicopter land?': ('¿Dónde puede aterrizar el helicóptero?', 'Solo en lugares autorizados &mdash; una arista, un prado de altura o un plateau glaciar, no donde se quiera. El operador gestiona las autorizaciones de aterrizaje, y unos pocos sitios icónicos como la Seceda tienen una tasa extra. Confirmamos el lugar exacto antes de reservar.'),
  'Is it legal to get married after a helicopter flight?': ('¿Es legal casarse tras un vuelo en helicóptero?', 'La ceremonia en la montaña es simbólica &mdash; en Italia un matrimonio con validez legal solo puede celebrarse en un registro civil (comune), nunca en el lugar de aterrizaje. La mayoría de las parejas firma los papeles legales en casa; un matrimonio civil en un registro italiano o austriaco es posible con el papeleo iniciado con meses de antelación.'),
  'What happens if the weather is bad?': ('¿Qué pasa si hace mal tiempo?', 'Un helicóptero solo vuela en condiciones seguras. Mantenemos una ventana flexible, un día de reserva y un bonito plan B en tierra &mdash; así una mañana sin vuelo nunca significa un día perdido.'),
  'Can we combine the helicopter with other places?': ('¿Podemos combinar el helicóptero con otros lugares?', 'Sí &mdash; un segundo aterrizaje, una comida en un refugio, un brindis junto al lago o una caminata corta. Construimos todo el día en torno a vosotros, no solo el vuelo.'),
  'How many people can come along?': ('¿Cuántas personas pueden venir?', 'El helicóptero lleva hasta seis pasajeros más el piloto, así que uno o dos testigos &mdash; o unos pocos invitados cercanos &mdash; pueden venir. La mayoría de las parejas aun así elige volar solo los dos. Planificamos el número de personas con el operador.'),
}
HELI_FAQ_IT = {
  'How much does a helicopter elopement cost?': ('Quanto costa un elopement in elicottero?', 'Il volo si prenota come charter &mdash; il minimo è un volo di 50 minuti con un atterraggio, e potete aggiungerne altri (consigliamo fino a tre). Alcuni siti premium come la Seceda hanno un supplemento di circa 300&ndash;500&nbsp;&euro;. Confermiamo il prezzo esatto del volo per iscritto, e la fotografia e il resto della giornata si quotano a parte.'),
  'How long are we actually in the air?': ('Quanto tempo restiamo davvero in aria?', 'Di solito solo minuti a tratta &mdash; le Dolomiti sono vicine. Il volo sostituisce una camminata di ore, così passate la maggior parte del tempo in montagna, non in trasferimento.'),
  'Where can the helicopter land?': ("Dove può atterrare l'elicottero?", "Solo su siti approvati &mdash; una cresta, un prato d'alta quota o un plateau glaciale, non dove si vuole. L'operatore gestisce le autorizzazioni di atterraggio, e alcuni luoghi iconici come la Seceda hanno una tariffa extra. Confermiamo il luogo esatto prima di prenotare."),
  'Is it legal to get married after a helicopter flight?': ('È legale sposarsi dopo un volo in elicottero?', 'La cerimonia in montagna è simbolica &mdash; in Italia un matrimonio con valore legale può avvenire solo in comune, mai sul sito di atterraggio. La maggior parte delle coppie firma i documenti legali a casa; un matrimonio civile in un comune italiano o austriaco è possibile con le pratiche avviate con mesi di anticipo.'),
  'What happens if the weather is bad?': ('Cosa succede se il tempo è brutto?', 'Un elicottero vola solo in condizioni sicure. Teniamo una finestra flessibile, un giorno di riserva e un bel piano B a terra &mdash; così una mattina senza volo non è mai una giornata persa.'),
  'Can we combine the helicopter with other places?': ("Possiamo combinare l'elicottero con altri luoghi?", "Sì &mdash; un secondo atterraggio, un pranzo in rifugio, un brindisi in riva al lago o una breve camminata. Costruiamo l'intera giornata attorno a voi, non solo il volo."),
  'How many people can come along?': ('Quante persone possono venire?', "L'elicottero porta fino a sei passeggeri più il pilota, quindi uno o due testimoni &mdash; o pochi invitati stretti &mdash; possono venire. La maggior parte delle coppie sceglie comunque di volare solo in due. Pianifichiamo il numero di persone con l'operatore."),
}

def build_helicopter_guide(lang):
    slug='helicopter-elopement-dolomites-guide'
    g=next(x for x in GUIDES if x['slug']==slug); ex=GUIDE_EXTRA[slug]
    rel='how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/'+slug+'/'; P=prefix(lang,rel)
    DE=(lang=='de')
    def L(en,de):
        if lang=='de': return de
        if lang=='es': return HELI_ES.get(en,en)
        if lang=='it': return HELI_IT.get(en,en)
        return en
    def FQ(qen,aen,qde,ade):
        if lang=='de': return (qde,ade)
        if lang=='es': return HELI_FAQ_ES.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        if lang=='it': return HELI_FAQ_IT.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        return (qen,aen)
    GI=f'{P}img/guide-helicopter/'; GIREL='img/guide-helicopter/'; HERO_IMG='img/guide-helicopter/h06-landed-couple.webp'
    H2S='font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,3vw,36px);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:1.7em 0 .4em;scroll-margin-top:96px'
    def h2(i,en,de): return f'<h2 id="{i}" style="{H2S}">{L(en,de)}</h2>'
    def p(en,de): return f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2)">{L(en,de)}</p>'
    def fig(name,en,de): return '<figure class="guide-fig">'+bild(P,GIREL+name,L(en,de),sizes='(max-width:820px) 100vw, 820px')+'</figure>'
    toc=[('what',L('What it is','Was es ist')),('how',L('How the day unfolds','So läuft der Tag')),
         ('timelines',L('Two example timelines','Zwei Beispiel-Abläufe')),('cost',L('What it costs','Was es kostet')),
         ('where',L('Where you can land','Wo ihr landen könnt')),('getting-there',L('Getting there','Anreise')),
         ('weather',L('Weather & Plan B','Wetter & Plan B')),('season',L('Summer or winter?','Sommer oder Winter?')),('wear',L('What to wear','Was anziehen')),
         ('papers',L('Papers & legal','Papiere & Recht')),('crowds',L('Above the crowds','Über den Massen')),
         ('drones',L('Drones & respect','Drohnen & Respekt')),('after',L('After the flight','Danach')),
         ('compare',L('Heli, cable car or hike?','Heli, Bahn oder Wandern?')),('faq',L('FAQ','FAQ'))]
    toc_html=('<nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'"><div class="cap">'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'</div><ol>'
      +''.join(f'<li><a href="#{i}">{lbl}</a></li>' for i,lbl in toc)+'</ol></nav>')
    facts='<div class="facts">'+''.join(f'<div class="fct"><div class="fl">{LBL[k][lang]}</div><div class="fv">{val[lang]}</div></div>' for k,val in ex['facts'])+'</div>'
    C=[]
    C.append(f'<p class="lead">{L("A helicopter turns a two-day trek into a ten-minute flight and sets you down where almost no one else can stand &mdash; a remote ledge of rock, a glacier shoulder, a summit ringed by the pale towers of the Dolomites. It is the most direct way we know to the extraordinary: no long approach, no compromise on the view, just the two of you and a mountain kept entirely to yourselves. Here is everything we have learned planning helicopter elopements in the Dolomites &mdash; how the flight works, what it costs, where you can land, the paperwork, the weather, and how to make the day feel like yours.","Ein Helikopter macht aus einer Zweitagestour einen Zehn-Minuten-Flug und setzt euch dort ab, wo sonst kaum jemand stehen kann &mdash; ein einsames Felsband, eine Gletscherschulter, ein Gipfel im Kranz der bleichen Dolomitentürme. Es ist der direkteste Weg zum Außergewöhnlichen, den wir kennen: kein langer Zustieg, kein Kompromiss bei der Aussicht, nur ihr beide und ein Berg ganz für euch. Hier steht alles, was wir beim Planen von Helikopter-Elopements in den Dolomiten gelernt haben &mdash; wie der Flug abläuft, was er kostet, wo ihr landen könnt, die Papiere, das Wetter, und wie der Tag sich nach euch anfühlt.")}</p>')
    C.append(f'<div class="cap" style="margin:0 0 -14px">{t(lang,"quick_facts")}</div>{facts}')
    C.append(toc_html)
    C.append(h2('what','What a helicopter elopement actually is','Was ein Helikopter-Elopement wirklich ist'))
    C.append(p("A helicopter elopement is a very small mountain wedding with one difference: you reach your ceremony by air. A licensed alpine helicopter lifts the two of you (and, if you like, a witness or two) from a valley helipad, flies you over the peaks and sets down on an approved landing site &mdash; a ridge, a high meadow, a glacier plateau. You say your vows with the whole range beneath your feet, take portraits while the light is good, and fly back. The flight is not a transfer; it becomes half the story.","Ein Helikopter-Elopement ist eine sehr kleine Berghochzeit mit einem Unterschied: Ihr erreicht eure Zeremonie aus der Luft. Ein zugelassener Alpin-Helikopter hebt euch beide (und auf Wunsch ein bis zwei Trauzeugen) von einem Talhubschrauberlandeplatz ab, fliegt über die Gipfel und setzt auf einem genehmigten Landeplatz auf &mdash; einem Grat, einer Hochwiese, einem Gletscherplateau. Ihr gebt euch das Ja mit dem ganzen Massiv zu euren Füßen, macht Porträts, solange das Licht steht, und fliegt zurück. Der Flug ist kein Transfer &mdash; er wird zur halben Geschichte."))
    C.append(p("The machine carries up to <strong>six passengers plus the pilot</strong>, so bringing a witness or two &mdash; or even a few close guests &mdash; is no problem, and you still fly comfortably. Most of our couples keep it to just the two of them; some bring their witnesses up for the ceremony. Either way, there is room.","Die Maschine fasst <strong>bis zu sechs Passagiere plus Pilot</strong> &mdash; ein bis zwei Trauzeugen oder sogar ein paar enge Gäste sind also kein Problem, und ihr fliegt trotzdem bequem. Die meisten unserer Paare bleiben zu zweit; manche nehmen ihre Trauzeugen für die Zeremonie mit hinauf. So oder so ist Platz."))
    C.append(fig('h21-paar-vor-hubschrauber-dolomiten.webp',"The couple embracing in a summer meadow, the helicopter behind them","Das Paar umarmt sich auf einer Sommerwiese, der Helikopter dahinter"))
    C.append(p("Couples come to it for different reasons. Some cannot hike far &mdash; a knee, a pregnancy, a dress that was never built for scree &mdash; and a flight gives them a summit anyway. Some simply want the one thing money can still buy in a crowded range: a place, for an hour, with no one else in it. And some love the flight for itself, the door open, the valley dropping away, the first sight of the peaks from above. Whatever brings you, the result is the same &mdash; a day that feels less like a wedding you attended and more like an adventure you took together.","Paare kommen aus verschiedenen Gründen dazu. Manche können nicht weit wandern &mdash; ein Knie, eine Schwangerschaft, ein Kleid, das nie für Geröll gedacht war &mdash; und ein Flug schenkt ihnen trotzdem einen Gipfel. Manche wollen einfach das Eine, das man in einem überlaufenen Massiv noch kaufen kann: einen Ort, für eine Stunde, mit niemandem sonst darin. Und manche lieben den Flug um seiner selbst willen, die offene Tür, das Tal, das wegsackt, den ersten Blick auf die Gipfel von oben. Was auch immer euch bringt &mdash; das Ergebnis ist dasselbe: ein Tag, der sich weniger wie eine Hochzeit anfühlt, bei der ihr wart, und mehr wie ein Abenteuer, das ihr gemeinsam unternommen habt."))
    C.append(fig('h30-coldai-summit-couple.webp',"The couple on a green summit with the helicopter and the Dolomites behind","Das Paar auf einem grünen Gipfel mit Helikopter und Dolomiten dahinter"))
    C.append(h2('how','How the day unfolds, step by step','So läuft der Tag, Schritt für Schritt'))
    C.append(p("<strong>1. First call.</strong> We start with a video call to understand the day you picture &mdash; sunrise or golden hour, a bare summit or a lake, just the two of you or a few guests. <strong>2. Landing site &amp; operator.</strong> We match your vision to an approved landing site and book a licensed alpine operator; some sites need advance clearance. <strong>3. Timing &amp; weather window.</strong> We fix a date but keep a flexible window and a backup day &mdash; the flight only happens in safe conditions. <strong>4. Getting ready.</strong> Hair, make-up and dressing happen in the valley before the flight. <strong>5. The flight.</strong> A short set-down at the helipad, headsets on, and minutes later you step out onto the mountain. <strong>6. Ceremony &amp; portraits.</strong> Your words, then portraits &mdash; the pilot stays on the mountain with you, and you have up to a full hour on each landing before you fly on. <strong>7. Back down</strong> &mdash; often with time for a second landing, a hut lunch or a lakeside toast.","<strong>1. Erstes Gespräch.</strong> Wir starten mit einem Videocall, um euren Wunschtag zu verstehen &mdash; Sonnenaufgang oder goldene Stunde, kahler Gipfel oder See, nur ihr zwei oder ein paar Gäste. <strong>2. Landeplatz &amp; Anbieter.</strong> Wir bringen eure Vorstellung mit einem genehmigten Landeplatz zusammen und buchen einen zugelassenen Alpin-Anbieter; manche Plätze brauchen eine Voranmeldung. <strong>3. Timing &amp; Wetterfenster.</strong> Wir legen einen Termin fest, halten aber ein flexibles Fenster und einen Reservetag frei &mdash; geflogen wird nur bei sicheren Bedingungen. <strong>4. Getting Ready.</strong> Haare, Make-up und Ankleiden passieren im Tal vor dem Flug. <strong>5. Der Flug.</strong> Kurzes Aufsetzen am Helipad, Headsets auf, und Minuten später steigt ihr am Berg aus. <strong>6. Zeremonie &amp; Porträts.</strong> Eure Worte, dann Porträts &mdash; der Pilot bleibt mit euch am Berg, und ihr habt bis zu einer ganzen Stunde pro Landung, bevor es weitergeht. <strong>7. Zurück ins Tal</strong> &mdash; oft mit Zeit für eine zweite Landung, ein Hüttenessen oder einen Toast am See."))
    C.append(p("That hour matters. Because the pilot waits with you rather than flying off and coming back, there is no clock-watching for a returning machine and no rush through your vows &mdash; you get a genuine, unhurried hour on each spot for the ceremony and portraits.","Diese Stunde zählt. Weil der Pilot bei euch wartet, statt wegzufliegen und zurückzukommen, gibt es kein Schielen nach einer zurückkehrenden Maschine und keine Hetze durchs Ja-Wort &mdash; ihr habt eine echte, entspannte Stunde pro Ort für Zeremonie und Porträts."))
    C.append(fig('h01-flight-headset.webp',"Bride with a headset inside the helicopter before take-off","Braut mit Headset im Helikopter vor dem Abflug"))
    C.append(fig('h22-einstieg-braut-dolomiten.webp',"The couple walking to the helicopter to board for the flight","Das Paar geht zum Helikopter, um zum Flug einzusteigen"))
    C.append(p("The flight itself is short and unforgettable. The rotor spins up, the machine goes light, and the valley simply falls away; a minute later the first peaks slide past the window at eye level, closer than you have ever seen them. Nobody speaks much &mdash; you just watch. Then the pilot picks the line in, the skids touch, the noise drops, and you step out into a silence so complete it rings. That contrast &mdash; from thunder to hush in thirty seconds &mdash; is a feeling couples talk about for years.","Der Flug selbst ist kurz und unvergesslich. Der Rotor dreht auf, die Maschine wird leicht, und das Tal sackt einfach weg; eine Minute später ziehen die ersten Gipfel auf Augenhöhe am Fenster vorbei, näher, als ihr sie je gesehen habt. Man spricht kaum &mdash; man schaut nur. Dann sucht der Pilot die Linie hinein, die Kufen setzen auf, der Lärm fällt ab, und ihr steigt in eine Stille aus, die so vollständig ist, dass sie klingt. Dieser Kontrast &mdash; von Donner zu Stille in dreißig Sekunden &mdash; ist ein Gefühl, von dem Paare noch Jahre erzählen."))
    C.append(fig('h25-winter-blick-aus-kabine.webp',"The couple inside the helicopter cabin during the flight","Das Paar in der Helikopterkabine während des Flugs"))
    C.append(h2('timelines','Two example timelines','Zwei Beispiel-Tagesabläufe'))
    C.append(p("<strong>A sunrise flight.</strong> 04:30 hair &amp; make-up in the valley &middot; 05:30 short drive to the helipad &middot; 06:00 lift-off as first light hits the peaks &middot; 06:15 set down on the ridge, ceremony as the rock turns pink &middot; 06:40 portraits in the still, empty light &middot; 07:15 fly back &middot; 08:00 breakfast at a mountain hut.","<strong>Ein Sonnenaufgangsflug.</strong> 04:30 Haare &amp; Make-up im Tal &middot; 05:30 kurze Fahrt zum Helipad &middot; 06:00 Abheben, wenn das erste Licht die Gipfel trifft &middot; 06:15 Aufsetzen am Grat, Zeremonie, während der Fels rosa wird &middot; 06:40 Porträts im stillen, leeren Licht &middot; 07:15 Rückflug &middot; 08:00 Frühstück auf der Hütte."))
    C.append(p("<strong>A full golden-hour day.</strong> 15:00 getting ready &middot; 16:30 first flight to a high landing for portraits &middot; 17:30 ceremony at a second spot &middot; 18:30 the range glows at last light (enrosadira) &middot; 19:15 fly down &middot; 20:00 dinner on a hut terrace. Times shift with the season &mdash; we build the exact schedule around the sunrise and your landing site.","<strong>Ein ganzer Tag zur goldenen Stunde.</strong> 15:00 Getting Ready &middot; 16:30 erster Flug zu einer hohen Landung für Porträts &middot; 17:30 Zeremonie an einem zweiten Ort &middot; 18:30 das Massiv glüht im letzten Licht (Enrosadira) &middot; 19:15 Rückflug &middot; 20:00 Abendessen auf der Hüttenterrasse. Die Zeiten verschieben sich mit der Saison &mdash; den genauen Ablauf bauen wir um den Sonnenaufgang und euren Landeplatz."))
    C.append(p("One thing sets the outer limits of the day: the helicopter may lift off from <strong>half an hour before sunrise</strong> and must be back at its airport by <strong>half an hour after sunset</strong>. That is a generous window &mdash; wide enough for both a true first-light flight and a full golden-hour evening &mdash; and we build your exact times around the sunrise for your date, which shifts through the season.","Eines steckt die äußeren Grenzen des Tages ab: Der Helikopter darf <strong>ab einer halben Stunde vor Sonnenaufgang</strong> abheben und muss <strong>spätestens eine halbe Stunde nach Sonnenuntergang</strong> zurück am Airport sein. Das ist ein großzügiges Fenster &mdash; weit genug für einen echten Erstlicht-Flug ebenso wie für einen ganzen Abend zur goldenen Stunde &mdash;, und eure genauen Zeiten bauen wir um den Sonnenaufgang eures Datums, der sich mit der Saison verschiebt."))
    C.append(fig('h29-tre-cime-winter-paar.webp',"The couple with the helicopter on a snowy plateau at last light","Das Paar mit dem Helikopter auf einem verschneiten Plateau im letzten Licht"))
    C.append(h2('cost','What it costs','Was es kostet'))
    C.append(p("The flight is booked as a charter, and the structure is simple. The minimum is a <strong>50-minute flight including one landing</strong> &mdash; enough for a ceremony and portraits at a single spot. You can add more landings to see more of the range; we usually recommend <strong>no more than three</strong>, so the day stays about being on the mountain rather than in and out of the machine. A few sought-after sites carry a surcharge (see below). The exact flight price depends on your date, your landings and the operator, so we confirm it in writing before anything is booked.","Der Flug wird als Charter gebucht, und die Struktur ist einfach. Das Minimum ist ein <strong>50-Minuten-Flug inklusive einer Landung</strong> &mdash; genug für Zeremonie und Porträts an einem Ort. Ihr könnt weitere Landungen dazunehmen, um mehr vom Massiv zu sehen; wir empfehlen meist <strong>maximal drei</strong>, damit der Tag vom Sein am Berg handelt und nicht vom Ein- und Aussteigen. Einige begehrte Plätze haben einen Aufpreis (siehe unten). Der genaue Flugpreis hängt von Datum, Landungen und Anbieter ab &mdash; wir bestätigen ihn schriftlich, bevor etwas gebucht wird."))
    C.append(fig('h07-helipad.webp',"The helicopter waiting on the valley helipad","Der Helikopter wartet am Talhubschrauberlandeplatz"))
    C.append(p("It is worth being honest about what drives the number. The bigger levers are the total flight time, the number of landings you add beyond the first, and the landing point itself &mdash; a few premium sites carry a surcharge. Add-ons &mdash; a second location, film, flowers, a celebrant &mdash; sit on top, and we price them plainly so nothing is a surprise on the invoice. A helicopter day is not the cheapest way to elope, but it buys something specific: an hour on a summit that would otherwise cost you two days and a lot of luck.","Man sollte ehrlich sagen, was den Preis treibt. Die größeren Hebel sind die gesamte Flugzeit, die Zahl der Landungen über die erste hinaus und der Landeplatz selbst &mdash; einige Premium-Orte haben einen Aufpreis. Zusatzoptionen &mdash; eine zweite Location, Film, Blumen, eine freie Trauung &mdash; kommen obendrauf, und wir kalkulieren sie transparent, damit auf der Rechnung nichts überrascht. Ein Helikoptertag ist nicht der günstigste Weg zu heiraten, aber er kauft etwas Bestimmtes: eine Stunde auf einem Gipfel, der euch sonst zwei Tage und viel Glück kosten würde."))
    C.append(h2('where','Where a helicopter can land you','Wohin ein Helikopter euch bringt'))
    C.append(p("A flight opens ground a normal elopement never reaches: a remote rock ledge, a glacier plateau on the Marmolada, a summit that would otherwise be a two-day climb, a shoulder beneath the Cadini or Tre Cime spires. Landings are flown by licensed alpine operators onto approved sites only &mdash; not anywhere you like, and not inside every protected zone. We choose the spot together for the view, the light and what is actually permitted, and confirm it before we book.","Ein Flug öffnet Gelände, das ein normales Elopement nie erreicht: ein einsames Felsband, ein Gletscherplateau an der Marmolada, ein Gipfel, der sonst eine Zweitagestour wäre, eine Schulter unter den Cadini- oder Drei-Zinnen-Spitzen. Landungen fliegen zugelassene Alpin-Anbieter ausschließlich auf genehmigten Plätzen &mdash; nicht überall und nicht in jeder Schutzzone. Wir wählen den Ort gemeinsam nach Aussicht, Licht und dem, was tatsächlich erlaubt ist, und bestätigen ihn vor der Buchung."))
    C.append(p("Broadly there are three kinds of landing, and they feel different. A <strong>ridge or summit</strong> gives you exposure and a 360-degree horizon &mdash; the boldest frames, the most wind. A <strong>high meadow or shoulder</strong> is gentler underfoot, kinder to a dress and easy to move around on. A <strong>glacier plateau</strong> is the rarest and most otherworldly, a field of white with nothing human in sight. Not every one is available everywhere or in every season, and some sit inside protected zones that are off-limits; we work only where landings are permitted and safe.","Grob gibt es drei Arten von Landung, und sie fühlen sich verschieden an. Ein <strong>Grat oder Gipfel</strong> gibt euch Ausgesetztheit und einen 360-Grad-Horizont &mdash; die kühnsten Bilder, den meisten Wind. Eine <strong>Hochwiese oder Schulter</strong> ist sanfter unter den Füßen, freundlicher zum Kleid und leicht zu begehen. Ein <strong>Gletscherplateau</strong> ist das seltenste und unwirklichste &mdash; ein weißes Feld ohne etwas Menschliches in Sicht. Nicht jede ist überall oder in jeder Saison verfügbar, und manche liegen in gesperrten Schutzzonen; wir arbeiten nur dort, wo Landungen erlaubt und sicher sind."))
    C.append(p("You do not have to navigate the permissions yourself: the <strong>helicopter operator arranges the landing clearances</strong> for each site, which is exactly why we fly only with licensed local companies. A handful of the most iconic spots &mdash; the Seceda above Ortisei is the classic example &mdash; carry an extra landing fee, typically <strong>around &euro;300&ndash;500</strong>. We tell you upfront which of your dream landings is free to use and which comes with a surcharge, so the shortlist you fall in love with is one we can actually deliver.","Ihr müsst euch nicht selbst um Genehmigungen kümmern: Das <strong>Hubschrauber-Unternehmen holt die Landefreigaben</strong> für jeden Platz ein &mdash; genau deshalb fliegen wir nur mit zugelassenen lokalen Anbietern. Eine Handvoll der ikonischsten Orte &mdash; die Seceda über St.&nbsp;Ulrich ist das klassische Beispiel &mdash; kostet eine zusätzliche Landegebühr, meist <strong>rund 300&ndash;500&nbsp;&euro;</strong>. Wir sagen euch vorab, welche eurer Wunschlandungen frei nutzbar ist und welche einen Aufpreis hat, damit die Auswahl, in die ihr euch verliebt, auch eine ist, die wir wirklich umsetzen können."))
    C.append(fig('h31-kronair-ridge-veil.webp',"The couple beside the helicopter on a ridge, veil in the wind","Das Paar neben dem Helikopter auf einem Grat, Schleier im Wind"))
    C.append(h2('getting-there','Getting there &amp; the helipad','Anreise &amp; Helipad'))
    C.append(p("Most couples fly into Venice, Verona or Innsbruck and drive the last stretch &mdash; roughly two to three hours to the heart of the Dolomites. Getting ready happens in the valley, then a short drive to the departure helipad. From there the flight is minutes, not hours. If you would rather not self-drive, we arrange transfers so the morning stays calm.","Die meisten Paare fliegen nach Venedig, Verona oder Innsbruck und fahren das letzte Stück &mdash; etwa zwei bis drei Stunden ins Herz der Dolomiten. Das Getting Ready passiert im Tal, dann eine kurze Fahrt zum Start-Helipad. Von dort dauert der Flug Minuten, nicht Stunden. Wenn ihr nicht selbst fahren wollt, organisieren wir Transfers, damit der Morgen ruhig bleibt."))
    C.append(p("There are <strong>two local operators</strong> we work with, each with its own base. <strong>Elikos</strong> flies from its airfield in <strong>Pontives</strong>, just below Ortisei in Val Gardena &mdash; about a 30-minute drive from Brixen. <strong>Kron Air</strong> departs from <strong>Olang</strong> in the Pustertal, roughly 20 minutes from Bruneck. Which one we choose depends on your landing site and where you are staying; both put the high Dolomites within a short flight. We match the base to your day and tell you exactly where to be and when.","Es gibt <strong>zwei lokale Anbieter</strong>, mit denen wir arbeiten, jeder mit eigener Basis. <strong>Elikos</strong> fliegt von seinem Flugplatz in <strong>Pontives</strong> unterhalb von St.&nbsp;Ulrich im Grödnertal &mdash; rund 30&nbsp;Autominuten von Brixen. <strong>Kron Air</strong> startet von <strong>Olang</strong> im Pustertal, etwa 20&nbsp;Minuten von Bruneck. Welchen wir wählen, hängt von eurem Landeplatz und eurer Unterkunft ab; beide bringen euch mit einem kurzen Flug in die hohen Dolomiten. Wir stimmen die Basis auf euren Tag ab und sagen euch genau, wo ihr wann sein müsst."))
    C.append(fig('h33-heli-kiss.webp',"The couple kissing in front of the helicopter in warm light","Das Paar küsst sich vor dem Helikopter im warmen Licht"))
    C.append(h2('weather','Weather &amp; Plan B','Wetter &amp; Plan B'))
    C.append(p("A helicopter flies only in safe conditions &mdash; good visibility, workable wind, no storm. Mountain weather turns fast, so we watch the forecast in the days before and keep a flexible window and, from our middle package up, a spare backup day. If the flight cannot go on your first morning, we move it; if a window never opens, we have a ground-based Plan B ready &mdash; a cable-car summit, a lake, a ridge you can reach on foot &mdash; so you are married beautifully either way. Fog and low cloud are not the enemy: some of the most atmospheric mountain photographs happen in exactly that light.","Ein Helikopter fliegt nur bei sicheren Bedingungen &mdash; gute Sicht, machbarer Wind, kein Gewitter. Bergwetter kippt schnell, deshalb beobachten wir die Vorhersage in den Tagen davor und halten ein flexibles Fenster frei &mdash; ab unserem mittleren Paket zusätzlich einen Reservetag. Geht der Flug am ersten Morgen nicht, verschieben wir ihn; öffnet sich gar kein Fenster, haben wir einen Plan B am Boden bereit &mdash; ein Bergbahn-Gipfel, ein See, ein Grat zu Fuß &mdash;, damit ihr so oder so schön heiratet. Nebel und tiefe Wolken sind kein Feind: Manche der stimmungsvollsten Bergbilder entstehen genau in diesem Licht."))
    C.append(h2('season','Summer or winter?','Sommer oder Winter?'))
    C.append(p("A summer flight lands you on green shoulders and warm rock at first or last light; a winter flight lands you in a white world &mdash; snow to the horizon, the peaks stripped to black and white, your breath in the air. Winter is quieter, colder and more dramatic, and it opens something summer cannot: a ceremony on a snow ridge, and, for the bold, skis on and the first run down together in gown and black tie. It asks for warm layers, good edges and a flexible eye on the weather &mdash; we handle the flight, the timing and the light, so all you bring is the nerve. Both seasons are beautiful; we help you choose the one that matches the day in your head.","Ein Sommerflug setzt euch auf grüne Schultern und warmen Fels im ersten oder letzten Licht; ein Winterflug in eine weiße Welt &mdash; Schnee bis zum Horizont, die Gipfel auf Schwarzweiß reduziert, euer Atem in der Luft. Der Winter ist stiller, kälter und dramatischer und öffnet etwas, das der Sommer nicht kann: eine Zeremonie auf einem Schneegrat &mdash; und, für Mutige, Ski an und die erste Abfahrt gemeinsam in Kleid und Fliege. Er verlangt warme Schichten, griffige Kanten und ein flexibles Auge fürs Wetter &mdash; wir kümmern uns um Flug, Timing und Licht, ihr bringt nur den Mut mit. Beide Jahreszeiten sind schön; wir helfen euch, die zu wählen, die zu eurem Bild im Kopf passt."))
    C.append(fig('h18-winter-peak.webp',"A snow-covered Dolomite peak reached by helicopter in winter","Ein verschneiter Dolomitengipfel, im Winter per Helikopter erreicht"))
    C.append(h2('wear','What to wear up there','Was ihr da oben anzieht'))
    C.append(p("It is cold at altitude, even in August &mdash; a summit at dawn can be near freezing while the valley is warm. Bring warm layers you can slip off for photos and back on between them, and a wrap or coat for the dress. Shoes matter: pack sturdy footwear for the landing site and change into the pretty ones for the frames. Rotor wash is real &mdash; hair, veils and loose petals move in the downdraught, which often looks wonderful, but secure anything you do not want to lose. We tell you exactly what to expect for your date and landing so nothing catches you out.","In der Höhe ist es kalt, selbst im August &mdash; ein Gipfel im Morgengrauen kann nahe null Grad sein, während das Tal warm ist. Nehmt warme Schichten mit, die ihr für Fotos abstreift und dazwischen wieder anzieht, und ein Cape oder einen Mantel fürs Kleid. Schuhe zählen: feste Schuhe für den Landeplatz, die schönen für die Bilder. Der Rotorabwind ist real &mdash; Haare, Schleier und lose Blüten bewegen sich im Abwind, was oft herrlich aussieht &mdash; sichert aber, was ihr nicht verlieren wollt. Wir sagen euch für euren Termin und eure Landung genau, was euch erwartet, damit euch nichts überrascht."))
    C.append(fig('h24-winter-braut-ausstieg.webp',"A bride in a winter coat stepping out of the helicopter into the snow","Eine Braut im Wintermantel steigt in den Schnee aus dem Helikopter"))
    C.append(h2('papers','Papers &amp; making it legal','Papiere &amp; das Rechtliche'))
    C.append(p("A helicopter flight is the setting, not the legal act &mdash; and there are two honest paths. <strong>A symbolic ceremony</strong> in the mountains with the legal marriage at home is what most of our couples choose: you sign the papers at your local registry before or after the trip, and up here you have the ceremony that actually matters. <strong>A legal civil marriage</strong> is also possible: in Italy for foreign nationals it means a certificate of no impediment (Nulla Osta / Ehefähigkeitszeugnis), international birth certificates, valid passports, usually an apostille and sworn translations, started months ahead; Austria offers civil ceremonies and, in some regions, approved outdoor locations. Couples from Germany, Austria, the USA and the UK all marry here &mdash; the paperwork differs by country, and we point you to the right path for yours.","Ein Helikopterflug ist der Rahmen, nicht der Rechtsakt &mdash; und es gibt zwei ehrliche Wege. <strong>Eine symbolische Zeremonie</strong> in den Bergen mit der rechtsgültigen Trauung zu Hause wählen die meisten unserer Paare: Ihr unterschreibt vor oder nach der Reise auf dem heimischen Standesamt, und hier oben habt ihr die Zeremonie, die wirklich zählt. <strong>Eine standesamtliche Trauung</strong> ist ebenso möglich: In Italien bedeutet das für Ausländer ein Ehefähigkeitszeugnis (Nulla Osta), internationale Geburtsurkunden, gültige Reisepässe, meist eine Apostille und beglaubigte Übersetzungen &mdash; Monate im Voraus begonnen; Österreich bietet standesamtliche Trauungen und in manchen Regionen genehmigte Orte im Freien. Paare aus Deutschland, Österreich, den USA und Großbritannien heiraten hier &mdash; die Papiere unterscheiden sich je Land, und wir weisen euch den richtigen Weg für eures."))
    C.append(p("One honest word on timing: the earlier you tell us, the more we can hold for you. The best summer dawn slots and every winter date fill first, and a legal marriage abroad needs its documents started months ahead. Reach out as soon as you have a rough season in mind &mdash; even before the exact date &mdash; and we will pencil in a window, sketch the day and tell you what to set in motion at home. Nothing is locked until you are ready; an early conversation simply keeps the good mornings open.","Ein ehrliches Wort zum Timing: Je früher ihr euch meldet, desto mehr können wir für euch freihalten. Die besten Sommer-Morgenfenster und alle Wintertermine sind zuerst weg, und eine rechtsgültige Trauung im Ausland braucht ihre Dokumente Monate vorher. Meldet euch, sobald ihr eine grobe Jahreszeit im Kopf habt &mdash; auch vor dem genauen Datum &mdash;, und wir reservieren ein Fenster, skizzieren den Tag und sagen euch, was ihr zu Hause in Gang setzen solltet. Nichts ist fix, bevor ihr bereit seid; ein frühes Gespräch hält einfach die guten Morgen offen."))
    C.append(p("One point to be clear about: in Italy a <strong>legally binding marriage can only take place at a registry office (comune)</strong> &mdash; never at a landing site on the mountain. So the ceremony up on the peak is always a symbolic one, and it is every bit as moving for it: your vows, your words, the two of you and the range. The legal signature happens at a town hall &mdash; at home, or at an Italian comune before or after the flight &mdash; and we help you line up the paperwork either way.","Ein Punkt zur Klarheit: In Italien kann eine <strong>rechtsgültige Trauung nur am Standesamt (comune)</strong> stattfinden &mdash; nie an einem Landeplatz am Berg. Die Zeremonie oben am Gipfel ist deshalb immer eine symbolische &mdash; und genau so berührend: euer Ja, eure Worte, ihr beide und das Massiv. Die rechtsgültige Unterschrift erfolgt am Standesamt &mdash; zu Hause oder an einem italienischen comune vor oder nach dem Flug &mdash;, und wir helfen euch in beiden Fällen, die Papiere zu ordnen."))
    C.append(h2('crowds','Above the crowds','Über den Massen'))
    C.append(p("The Dolomites are the most photographed range in Europe, and the icons fill up. A flight is the cleanest way past that: you land where the day-trippers cannot follow and the summit is yours. Even so, we plan for the quiet hours &mdash; first light before the valleys wake, or last light after they empty &mdash; because empty light is always the better light.","Die Dolomiten sind das meistfotografierte Massiv Europas, und die Ikonen füllen sich. Ein Flug ist der sauberste Weg daran vorbei: Ihr landet, wohin Tagesgäste nicht folgen können, und der Gipfel gehört euch. Trotzdem planen wir die stillen Stunden &mdash; erstes Licht, ehe die Täler erwachen, oder letztes Licht, wenn sie sich leeren &mdash;, denn leeres Licht ist immer das bessere Licht."))
    C.append(fig('h32-ridge-panorama-heli.webp',"The couple alone on a ridge with the helicopter and a Dolomite panorama","Das Paar allein auf einem Grat mit Helikopter und Dolomiten-Panorama"))
    C.append(h2('drones','Drones, protected zones &amp; flying responsibly','Drohnen, Schutzzonen &amp; verantwortungsvoll fliegen'))
    C.append(p("A helicopter is not a drone. Licensed alpine flights land on approved sites under strict rules; private drones, by contrast, are banned across much of the Dolomites &mdash; Lago di Braies has prohibited them since 2026, patrolled by rangers and subject to fines &mdash; and inside nature-reserve zones generally. On the ground we stay on the landing site, off the meadows and out of protected vegetation, and we leave the mountain exactly as we found it. Respect is part of being allowed back.","Ein Helikopter ist keine Drohne. Zugelassene Alpinflüge landen unter strengen Regeln auf genehmigten Plätzen; private Drohnen dagegen sind in weiten Teilen der Dolomiten verboten &mdash; am Pragser Wildsee seit 2026, von Rangern überwacht und mit Bußgeldern belegt &mdash; und in Naturschutzzonen generell. Am Boden bleiben wir auf dem Landeplatz, weg von den Wiesen und aus der geschützten Vegetation, und wir lassen den Berg genau so zurück, wie wir ihn vorgefunden haben. Respekt ist Teil davon, wiederkommen zu dürfen."))
    C.append(h2('after','After the flight','Nach dem Flug'))
    C.append(p("The flight does not have to be the whole day. Couples pair it with a slow lunch on a hut terrace, a swim in a cold alpine lake, a via ferrata or an easy hike, or simply a bottle opened somewhere with a view. The Dolomites make an easy honeymoon base too &mdash; Cortina, Val Gardena and the Alta Badia villages sit within an hour of everything, full of huts, spas and long dinners. We are happy to sketch the days around your elopement, not just the hour of it.","Der Flug muss nicht der ganze Tag sein. Paare verbinden ihn mit einem langen Mittagessen auf der Hüttenterrasse, einem Bad im kalten Bergsee, einem Klettersteig oder einer leichten Wanderung &mdash; oder einfach einer Flasche, die irgendwo mit Aussicht geöffnet wird. Die Dolomiten sind auch eine leichte Flitterwochen-Basis &mdash; Cortina, Gröden und die Dörfer der Alta Badia liegen eine Stunde von allem, voller Hütten, Spas und langer Abende. Wir skizzieren gern die Tage rund um euer Elopement, nicht nur die eine Stunde."))
    C.append(fig('h28-pizza-am-berg.webp',"A chef making fresh pizza on the mountain, the helicopter behind","Ein Koch macht frische Pizza am Berg, der Helikopter dahinter"))
    C.append(p("A favourite pairing is a lake to finish. After the summit, a landing or a short drive brings you to still water &mdash; a mirror of turquoise under the peaks &mdash; for the softest frames of the day and a first quiet moment as a married couple. Others want nothing planned at all after the flight: just a blanket, a view and the rest of the morning to themselves. There is no wrong way to spend the hours we are not photographing; we simply make sure they are yours.","Eine liebste Kombination ist ein See zum Abschluss. Nach dem Gipfel bringt euch eine Landung oder eine kurze Fahrt an stilles Wasser &mdash; einen türkisen Spiegel unter den Gipfeln &mdash; für die weichsten Bilder des Tages und einen ersten ruhigen Moment als Ehepaar. Andere wollen nach dem Flug gar nichts Geplantes: nur eine Decke, eine Aussicht und den Rest des Morgens für sich. Es gibt keinen falschen Weg, die Stunden zu verbringen, die wir nicht fotografieren; wir sorgen nur dafür, dass sie euch gehören."))
    C.append(fig('h19-lago-heli.webp',"A turquoise Dolomite lake reached to finish the day","Ein türkiser Dolomitensee zum Abschluss des Tages"))
    C.append(h2('compare','Helicopter, cable car or hike?','Helikopter, Bergbahn oder Wandern?'))
    C.append(p("A flight is the boldest way up, but not the only one. If you want the summit feeling without the price, a cable car to the Lagazuoi, Sass Pordoi or Seceda delivers an enormous view for the cost of a ticket &mdash; though the lifts open well after sunrise. If you want the day to feel earned, a hike gives you solitude and costs nothing but the early alarm. We often combine them: fly in for the drama, then walk a few minutes to a quieter ledge. Unsure? Tell us how you feel about heights, effort and budget, and we will tell you honestly which one fits.","Der Flug ist der kühnste Weg nach oben, aber nicht der einzige. Wollt ihr das Gipfelgefühl ohne den Preis, liefert eine Bergbahn zum Lagazuoi, Sass Pordoi oder zur Seceda einen gewaltigen Blick zum Ticketpreis &mdash; die Bahnen öffnen allerdings deutlich nach Sonnenaufgang. Soll sich der Tag verdient anfühlen, schenkt eine Wanderung Einsamkeit und kostet nur den frühen Wecker. Oft kombinieren wir: einfliegen für die Dramatik, dann ein paar Minuten zu einem stilleren Band gehen. Unsicher? Sagt uns, wie ihr zu Höhe, Aufwand und Budget steht &mdash; wir sagen euch ehrlich, was passt."))
    faq_html='<h2 id="faq" style="'+H2S+'">'+L('Helicopter elopement FAQ','FAQ zum Helikopter-Elopement')+'</h2>'
    FAQL=[FQ(*x) for x in HELI_FAQ]
    faq_html+=''.join('<div style="margin:1.3em 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:1.1em">'
      f'<h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:20px;margin:0 0 .3em">{q}</h3>'
      f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2);margin:0">{a}</p></div>' for q,a in FAQL)
    faq_ld={"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
      {"@type":"Question","name":_plain(q),"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":_plain(a)}} for q,a in FAQL]}
    related=''.join(story_card(lang,P,STORYBY[sl]) for sl in ex['stories'])
    more=''.join(guide_card(lang,P,x) for x in GUIDES if x['slug']!=slug)
    body=(nav(lang,rel,'howto')+
      f'<section class="page-hero" style="padding:0">{herobg(P,HERO_IMG,g["title"][lang])}'
      f'<div class="content"><div class="wrap"><div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"guide_kick")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h1>{g["title"][lang]}</h1></div></div></section>'
      '<section><div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">'+''.join(C)+faq_html+
      f'<p style="margin-top:2.4em"><a href="{u(P,lang,"how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/")}" class="arrow-link">&larr; {T["nav"]["howto"][lang]}</a></p></div></section>'
      '<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"related_stories")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"related_stories")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{related}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="stories" style="padding-top:clamp(40px,6vw,80px)"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"more_guides")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"more_guides")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{more}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="cta"><div class="wrap row reveal"><div>'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"cta_k")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2 style="margin-top:20px">{t(lang,"cta_h")}</h2></div>'
      f'<a href="{u(P,lang,"get-in-touch/")}" class="btn light">{t(lang,"start_planning")}</a></div></section>'
      +footer(lang,rel))
    write(lang,rel,head(lang,rel,g['title'][lang]+' — Mountain Elopement',g['excerpt'][lang],ld_extra=faq_ld,pre=herolink(P,HERO_IMG))+body+scripts(P))

REGION_FAQ=[
 ("Do we need a permit to get married in the Dolomites?",
  "For a small symbolic ceremony with two people and a photographer, you generally do not need a special permit in open terrain. Restrictions apply to protected nature reserve zones, to commercial set-ups (arches, chairs, drones), and to some municipalities. We check the specific spot before we book it &mdash; and we will tell you if a place we love is not permitted."),
 ("How many people can come?",
  "An elopement is usually just the two of you, sometimes with a handful of witnesses. Above roughly ten guests the logistics change: transport, huts and permits all become more complicated. We are happy to plan either, but we will be honest about what changes."),
 ("What if the weather is bad?",
  "It will be, at some point &mdash; this is the high Alps. We build flexibility into the schedule, watch the forecast in the days before, and can move the ceremony to a different valley or another morning. Fog and rain also make some of the most atmospheric photographs we have ever taken."),
 ("Can we get married on the Seceda ridge or at Lago di Braies?",
  "Yes to both, with planning. Seceda means either an early hike or an overnight stay nearby, since the cable car starts after sunrise. Braies means arriving before 09:00 or after 16:00 between 1 July and 15 September, or coming outside the high season. Both are among our favourite places on earth."),
 ("Can you fly a drone at Lago di Braies?",
  "No. Since 2026 drones are strictly prohibited at the lake, patrolled by rangers and subject to fines. We plan without aerial footage there &mdash; and honestly, the pictures from the shoreline are the ones you will hang on your wall."),
 ("Do we need a reservation to drive to Lago di Braies?",
  "Between 1 July and 15 September, yes &mdash; driving to the lake from 09:00 to 16:00 requires an advance online reservation. For sunrise or late-afternoon sessions outside those hours it is not needed, which is another reason we plan around that light."),
 ("How far do we have to walk?",
  "That is entirely your choice. Some of our locations are a two-minute stroll from the car; others are a two-hour hike. Tell us how you feel about walking in a wedding dress and we will build the day around your answer."),
 ("How far in advance should we book?",
  "For July to September, six to twelve months is comfortable &mdash; huts, planners and the good mornings fill up. Off-season we have occasionally made something beautiful happen in a few weeks."),
]

# Elopement explainer FAQs (DACH SEO) — bilingual; appended in the page language (DE→German, else English).
ELOPE_FAQ = {
 'en': [
  ("What is an elopement?",
   "An elopement is a small, intimate wedding &mdash; usually just the two of you, sometimes with a handful of your closest people. Instead of a big reception and a long guest list, the day is about the moment together, often in a place that means something to you. Originally &lsquo;to elope&rsquo; meant running away to marry in secret; today it is a deliberate, modern way to wed: less organising, more real experience."),
  ("What is an elopement shoot?",
   "An elopement shoot is the photography of exactly that day: we capture the ceremony for two, your vows and the hours around them at your chosen place &mdash; from sunrise on a summit to portraits by an alpine lake. Unlike a plain engagement or couple session, it documents the actual wedding, not just posed pictures."),
  ("What does the word &lsquo;elopement&rsquo; mean?",
   "&lsquo;Elope&rsquo; comes from the idea of running away to marry &mdash; historically, in secret. Today an elopement simply means a small, private wedding without a large gathering: just the couple, their vows, and a place they love."),
  ("Why are elopements a wedding trend?",
   "As a wedding trend, eloping is a conscious choice against the big celebration &mdash; in favour of experience, place and time together. More and more couples want an honest day somewhere that matters to them rather than the stress of a large guest list: in the Dolomites, on a summit or by a mountain lake. The budget goes into the experience and the photographs instead of a venue and a menu."),
  ("How much does an elopement wedding cost?",
   "Our elopement packages start at &euro;6,000 and include photography, location scouting, a planning call and your private online gallery. Larger packages add hair and make-up, flowers and full coordination, up to the whole day with accommodation and transfers. An elopement is usually far less expensive than a big wedding &mdash; the budget goes into the experience and the images rather than a hall and a headcount."),
  ("How do you make an elopement special?",
   "The magic comes from place, light and real moments &mdash; not decoration. We often start at sunrise, when a summit or lake is yours alone, plan personal vows, and add small touches where they fit: a celebrant, flowers, a picnic or dinner in a mountain hut, a helicopter flight to a remote ridge. Less programme, more time for each other."),
  ("Is eloping legal in Austria?",
   "Yes. In Austria you can marry in a civil ceremony &mdash; in some regions even at selected outdoor locations &mdash; and we coordinate the date and paperwork. Alternatively you hold a free, symbolic ceremony in the mountains and complete the legal part at home. For a legally binding ceremony in the mountains we connect you with the right people."),
 ],
 'de': [
  ("Was ist ein Elopement?",
   "Ein Elopement ist eine kleine, intime Hochzeit &mdash; meist nur das Paar, manchmal mit den wenigen engsten Menschen. Statt gro&szlig;er Feier und langer G&auml;steliste steht der Moment zu zweit im Mittelpunkt, oft an einem besonderen Ort in den Bergen. Urspr&uuml;nglich bedeutete &bdquo;to elope&ldquo; das heimliche Durchbrennen; heute ist es eine bewusste, moderne Art zu heiraten: weniger Organisation, mehr echtes Erlebnis."),
  ("Was ist ein Elopement-Shooting?",
   "Ein Elopement-Shooting ist die fotografische Begleitung genau dieses Tages: Wir halten die Trauung zu zweit, euer Ja und die Stunden danach an eurem Wunschort fest &mdash; vom Sonnenaufgang am Gipfel bis zum Paarshooting am Bergsee. Anders als ein reines Verlobungs- oder Paarshooting dokumentiert es die tats&auml;chliche Hochzeit, nicht nur gestellte Bilder."),
  ("Was bedeutet &bdquo;Elopement&ldquo; auf Deutsch?",
   "&bdquo;Elopement&ldquo; kommt aus dem Englischen (von &bdquo;to elope&ldquo; &mdash; durchbrennen, entfliehen) und hat kein exaktes deutsches Wort. Am n&auml;chsten kommen &bdquo;Hochzeit zu zweit&ldquo;, &bdquo;Mikrohochzeit&ldquo; oder &bdquo;heimlich heiraten&ldquo;. Gemeint ist immer eine kleine, private Trauung ohne gro&szlig;e Gesellschaft."),
  ("Was bedeutet der Hochzeitstrend Elopement?",
   "Als Hochzeitstrend steht Elopement f&uuml;r die bewusste Entscheidung gegen die gro&szlig;e Feier &mdash; und f&uuml;r Erlebnis, Ort und Zweisamkeit. Immer mehr Paare wollen keinen Stress mit vielen G&auml;sten, sondern einen ehrlichen Tag an einem Ort, der ihnen etwas bedeutet: in den Dolomiten, auf einem Gipfel oder an einem Bergsee. Budget und Energie flie&szlig;en in Erlebnis und Bilder statt in Saal und Men&uuml;."),
  ("Was kostet eine Elopement-Hochzeit?",
   "Bei uns beginnen Elopement-Pakete bei 6.000&nbsp;&euro; und umfassen Fotografie, Locationscouting, ein Planungsgespr&auml;ch und eure private Online-Galerie. Gr&ouml;&szlig;ere Pakete erg&auml;nzen Haare und Make-up, Blumen und volle Koordination bis hin zum ganzen Tag mit Unterkunft und Transfers. Ein Elopement ist meist deutlich g&uuml;nstiger als eine gro&szlig;e Hochzeit &mdash; das Budget flie&szlig;t in Erlebnis und Bilder statt in Saal und G&auml;stezahl."),
  ("Wie macht man ein Elopement besonders?",
   "Das Besondere entsteht aus Ort, Licht und echten Momenten &mdash; nicht aus Deko. Wir starten oft zum Sonnenaufgang, wenn ihr einen Gipfel oder See f&uuml;r euch allein habt, planen pers&ouml;nliche Gel&uuml;bde und erg&auml;nzen, wo es passt, kleine Details: freie Trauung, Blumen, ein Picknick oder Abendessen auf der H&uuml;tte, ein Helikopterflug auf einen einsamen Grat. Weniger Programm, mehr Zeit f&uuml;reinander."),
  ("Ist ein Elopement in &Ouml;sterreich erlaubt?",
   "Ja. In &Ouml;sterreich k&ouml;nnt ihr standesamtlich heiraten &mdash; in manchen Regionen sogar an ausgew&auml;hlten Orten im Freien &mdash; und wir koordinieren Termin und Papiere. Alternativ feiert ihr eine freie, symbolische Zeremonie in den Bergen und erledigt das Standesamtliche zu Hause. F&uuml;r eine rechtsg&uuml;ltige Trauung am Berg bringen wir euch mit den passenden Ansprechpartnern zusammen."),
 ],
 'es': [
  ("&iquest;Qu&eacute; es un elopement?",
   "Un elopement es una boda peque&ntilde;a e &iacute;ntima &mdash; normalmente solo los dos, a veces con vuestras personas m&aacute;s cercanas. En lugar de una gran celebraci&oacute;n y una larga lista de invitados, el d&iacute;a gira en torno al momento a solas, a menudo en un lugar que significa algo para vosotros. Originalmente &lsquo;to elope&rsquo; significaba fugarse para casarse en secreto; hoy es una forma consciente y moderna de casarse: menos organizaci&oacute;n, m&aacute;s experiencia real."),
  ("&iquest;Qu&eacute; es una sesi&oacute;n de elopement?",
   "Una sesi&oacute;n de elopement es la fotograf&iacute;a de ese d&iacute;a concreto: capturamos la ceremonia para dos, vuestros votos y las horas alrededor en el lugar que elij&aacute;is &mdash; desde el amanecer en una cima hasta los retratos junto a un lago alpino. A diferencia de una sesi&oacute;n de pareja o de compromiso, documenta la boda real, no solo fotos posadas."),
  ("&iquest;Qu&eacute; significa la palabra &lsquo;elopement&rsquo;?",
   "&lsquo;Elope&rsquo; viene de la idea de fugarse para casarse &mdash; hist&oacute;ricamente, en secreto. Hoy un elopement significa simplemente una boda peque&ntilde;a y privada sin una gran reuni&oacute;n: solo la pareja, sus votos y un lugar que aman."),
  ("&iquest;Por qu&eacute; el elopement es una tendencia de boda?",
   "Como tendencia de boda, fugarse es una decisi&oacute;n consciente contra la gran celebraci&oacute;n &mdash; a favor de la experiencia, el lugar y el tiempo juntos. Cada vez m&aacute;s parejas quieren un d&iacute;a sincero en un sitio que les importa en lugar del estr&eacute;s de una larga lista de invitados: en los Dolomitas, en una cima o junto a un lago de monta&ntilde;a. El presupuesto se destina a la experiencia y las fotos en lugar de a un sal&oacute;n y un men&uacute;."),
  ("&iquest;Cu&aacute;nto cuesta una boda elopement?",
   "Nuestros paquetes de elopement empiezan en 6.000&nbsp;&euro; e incluyen fotograf&iacute;a, b&uacute;squeda de localizaci&oacute;n, una llamada de planificaci&oacute;n y vuestra galer&iacute;a online privada. Los paquetes mayores a&ntilde;aden peluquer&iacute;a y maquillaje, flores y coordinaci&oacute;n completa, hasta el d&iacute;a entero con alojamiento y traslados. Un elopement suele ser mucho m&aacute;s econ&oacute;mico que una gran boda &mdash; el presupuesto se destina a la experiencia y las im&aacute;genes en lugar de a un sal&oacute;n y al n&uacute;mero de invitados."),
  ("&iquest;C&oacute;mo se hace especial un elopement?",
   "La magia surge del lugar, la luz y los momentos reales &mdash; no de la decoraci&oacute;n. Solemos empezar al amanecer, cuando una cima o un lago son solo vuestros, planeamos votos personales y a&ntilde;adimos peque&ntilde;os detalles donde encajan: un oficiante, flores, un picnic o una cena en un refugio, un vuelo en helic&oacute;ptero a una cresta remota. Menos programa, m&aacute;s tiempo el uno para el otro."),
  ("&iquest;Es legal fugarse para casarse en Austria?",
   "S&iacute;. En Austria pod&eacute;is casaros por lo civil &mdash; en algunas regiones incluso en lugares al aire libre seleccionados &mdash; y coordinamos la fecha y los tr&aacute;mites. Como alternativa, celebr&aacute;is una ceremonia libre y simb&oacute;lica en la monta&ntilde;a y complet&aacute;is la parte legal en casa. Para una ceremonia legalmente vinculante en la monta&ntilde;a os ponemos en contacto con las personas adecuadas."),
 ],
 'it': [
  ("Che cos&rsquo;&egrave; un elopement?",
   "Un elopement &egrave; un matrimonio piccolo e intimo &mdash; di solito solo voi due, a volte con le persone pi&ugrave; care. Invece di una grande festa e di una lunga lista di invitati, la giornata ruota attorno al momento a due, spesso in un luogo che ha un significato per voi. In origine &lsquo;to elope&rsquo; significava fuggire per sposarsi in segreto; oggi &egrave; un modo consapevole e moderno di sposarsi: meno organizzazione, pi&ugrave; esperienza autentica."),
  ("Che cos&rsquo;&egrave; un servizio elopement?",
   "Un servizio elopement &egrave; la fotografia di quella giornata: catturiamo la cerimonia a due, le vostre promesse e le ore attorno nel luogo che scegliete &mdash; dall&rsquo;alba su una vetta ai ritratti in riva a un lago alpino. A differenza di un servizio di coppia o di fidanzamento, documenta il matrimonio vero, non solo foto in posa."),
  ("Che cosa significa la parola &lsquo;elopement&rsquo;?",
   "&lsquo;Elope&rsquo; nasce dall&rsquo;idea di fuggire per sposarsi &mdash; storicamente, in segreto. Oggi un elopement significa semplicemente un matrimonio piccolo e privato senza un grande raduno: solo la coppia, le loro promesse e un luogo che amano."),
  ("Perch&eacute; l&rsquo;elopement &egrave; una tendenza nozze?",
   "Come tendenza nozze, l&rsquo;elopement &egrave; una scelta consapevole contro la grande festa &mdash; a favore dell&rsquo;esperienza, del luogo e del tempo insieme. Sempre pi&ugrave; coppie vogliono una giornata autentica in un posto che conta per loro invece dello stress di una lunga lista di invitati: nelle Dolomiti, su una vetta o in riva a un lago di montagna. Il budget va nell&rsquo;esperienza e nelle foto invece che in una sala e un men&ugrave;."),
  ("Quanto costa un matrimonio elopement?",
   "I nostri pacchetti elopement partono da 6.000&nbsp;&euro; e comprendono fotografia, sopralluogo, una call di pianificazione e la vostra galleria online privata. I pacchetti pi&ugrave; grandi aggiungono trucco e acconciatura, fiori e coordinazione completa, fino all&rsquo;intera giornata con alloggio e trasferimenti. Un elopement &egrave; di solito molto meno costoso di un grande matrimonio &mdash; il budget va nell&rsquo;esperienza e nelle immagini invece che in una sala e nel numero di invitati."),
  ("Come si rende speciale un elopement?",
   "La magia nasce dal luogo, dalla luce e dai momenti veri &mdash; non dalle decorazioni. Spesso iniziamo all&rsquo;alba, quando una vetta o un lago sono solo vostri, pianifichiamo promesse personali e aggiungiamo piccoli dettagli dove servono: un celebrante, fiori, un picnic o una cena in rifugio, un volo in elicottero verso una cresta remota. Meno programma, pi&ugrave; tempo l&rsquo;uno per l&rsquo;altro."),
  ("Un elopement &egrave; legale in Austria?",
   "S&igrave;. In Austria potete sposarvi civilmente &mdash; in alcune regioni anche in location all&rsquo;aperto selezionate &mdash; e coordiniamo data e pratiche. In alternativa celebrate una cerimonia libera e simbolica in montagna e completate la parte legale a casa. Per una cerimonia legalmente valida in montagna vi mettiamo in contatto con le persone giuste."),
 ],
}

PROP_FAQ=[
 ("How far ahead should we plan a mountain proposal?",
  "Two to eight weeks is comfortable. We need enough time to pick the spot, watch the forecast and hold a backup morning, but proposals are nimble &mdash; we have put beautiful ones together on a week's notice when the weather lined up.",
  "Wie lange im Voraus sollten wir einen Bergantrag planen?",
  "Zwei bis acht Wochen sind angenehm. Wir brauchen genug Zeit, um den Ort zu wählen, die Vorhersage zu beobachten und einen Reservemorgen freizuhalten &mdash; aber Anträge sind flink; wir haben schöne mit einer Woche Vorlauf hinbekommen, wenn das Wetter passte."),
 ("How do you photograph it without giving it away?",
  "We plan everything by message with the person proposing, arrive early and pass for ordinary hikers, then shoot from a distance with a long lens. Your partner usually only realises there was a photographer after the yes &mdash; which is when we step in for a proper session.",
  "Wie fotografiert ihr, ohne es zu verraten?",
  "Wir planen alles per Nachricht mit der antragenden Person, kommen früh an, geben uns als gewöhnliche Wanderer aus und fotografieren aus der Distanz mit Teleobjektiv. Euer Gegenüber merkt meist erst nach dem Ja, dass jemand da war &mdash; dann kommen wir für ein richtiges Shooting dazu."),
 ("Where is the easiest place to propose in the Dolomites?",
  "A roadside lake or a cable-car viewpoint, because neither needs a long hike that gives the surprise away. Lago di Braies and little Lago d'Antorno are favourites at first light; so is the Alpe di Siusi meadow and the Nordkette above Innsbruck. We match the spot to your fitness, the season and the light.",
  "Wo lässt sich in den Dolomiten am leichtesten ein Antrag machen?",
  "Ein See am Straßenrand oder eine Bergbahn-Aussicht, weil beide keine lange Wanderung brauchen, die die Überraschung verrät. Der Pragser Wildsee und der kleine Lago d'Antorno sind bei erstem Licht Favoriten; ebenso die Seiser Alm und die Nordkette über Innsbruck. Wir stimmen den Ort auf Fitness, Saison und Licht ab."),
 ("What if the weather is bad?",
  "Mountain weather turns fast, so we always hold a backup spot and a spare morning. Low cloud and a little rain are not the enemy either &mdash; some of the most atmospheric proposal images we have taken happened in exactly that soft, moody light.",
  "Was, wenn das Wetter schlecht ist?",
  "Bergwetter kippt schnell, deshalb halten wir immer einen Ausweichort und einen Reservemorgen bereit. Tiefe Wolken und etwas Regen sind auch kein Feind &mdash; einige der stimmungsvollsten Antragsbilder entstanden genau in diesem weichen, dramatischen Licht."),
 ("Can we turn the proposal into a full session?",
  "Yes, and most couples do. After the yes we keep shooting for a relaxed couples session to celebrate, and can send you a few images the same day to share with family. Many couples later come back to us to photograph the wedding itself.",
  "Können wir aus dem Antrag ein ganzes Shooting machen?",
  "Ja, und die meisten Paare tun das. Nach dem Ja fotografieren wir weiter für ein entspanntes Paar-Shooting zum Feiern und schicken euch noch am selben Tag ein paar Bilder für die Familie. Viele Paare kommen später für die Hochzeit zurück zu uns."),
 ("Is a sunrise proposal really worth the early start?",
  "Almost always. First light gives you empty viewpoints, soft colour and the mountain nearly to yourselves &mdash; the same spot at midday can be busy and harsh. We handle the timing; you just set the alarm.",
  "Lohnt sich ein Sonnenaufgangs-Antrag trotz frühem Aufstehen?",
  "Fast immer. Das erste Licht schenkt leere Aussichtspunkte, weiche Farben und den Berg fast für euch allein &mdash; derselbe Ort ist mittags oft voll und hart im Licht. Um das Timing kümmern wir uns, ihr stellt nur den Wecker."),
]

# --- Proposal guide ES/IT translations (auto-generated, keyed by exact EN string) ---
PROP_ES = {
  'Ready to book a surprise proposal shoot': 'Listos para reservar una sesión de pedida sorpresa',
  'What a mountain proposal really is': 'Qué es realmente una pedida en la montaña',
  'A mountain proposal is a small, precise piece of theatre: one person knows the plan, the other has no idea, and a photographer is hidden in plain sight to catch the moment it all lands. The setting does half the work &mdash; a lakeshore at first light, a viewpoint above the clouds, a meadow under jagged peaks &mdash; but the magic is the surprise, and protecting it is our whole job until you kneel. After that it turns into a celebration, and we keep photographing while you float.': 'Una pedida en la montaña es una pieza de teatro pequeña y precisa: una persona conoce el plan, la otra no tiene ni idea, y un fotógrafo está escondido a plena vista para capturar el momento en que todo encaja. El lugar hace la mitad del trabajo &mdash; la orilla de un lago con la primera luz, un mirador sobre las nubes, un prado bajo cumbres escarpadas &mdash;, pero la magia es la sorpresa, y protegerla es toda nuestra tarea hasta que os arrodilláis. Después se convierte en celebración, y seguimos fotografiando mientras flotáis.',
  'A proposal on the Lago di Braies boardwalk among the wooden boats': 'Una pedida en la pasarela del Lago di Braies entre las barcas de madera',
  'Couples come to us for it from all over &mdash; some already live for the mountains, some just want somewhere that will never feel ordinary to remember. It works for the fit and the not-so-fit, in deep summer and deep snow, at a lake you can drive to or a summit you have to earn. Whatever you picture, the shape is the same: a quiet approach, a natural pause, the question, and then the loudest, happiest hour of your trip.': 'Las parejas nos buscan desde todas partes &mdash; algunas ya viven por la montaña, otras solo quieren un lugar que nunca se sienta ordinario para recordar. Funciona para los en forma y los no tanto, en pleno verano y en plena nieve, en un lago al que se llega en coche o una cumbre que hay que ganarse. Sea lo que imaginéis, la forma es la misma: una aproximación tranquila, una pausa natural, la pregunta, y luego la hora más ruidosa y feliz de vuestro viaje.',
  'Foreheads together after the yes, the new ring visible': 'Frente con frente tras el sí, el nuevo anillo a la vista',
  'How we pull off the surprise, step by step': 'Cómo logramos la sorpresa, paso a paso',
  '<strong>1. First message.</strong> Everything runs through the person planning it &mdash; never a shared chat. We learn the story, the fitness level and the vibe. <strong>2. Spot &amp; time.</strong> We pick a location that gives a natural reason to pause and the best light, usually sunrise. <strong>3. The cover story.</strong> We agree on a believable reason to be up there early &mdash; "a sunrise hike," "a photographer friend meeting us." <strong>4. The signal.</strong> You give us a small, invisible cue &mdash; a hand on the back, taking off a hat &mdash; so we know the second is coming. <strong>5. From a distance.</strong> We shoot long, quiet and unnoticed. <strong>6. The reveal.</strong> After the yes we walk over, introduce ourselves properly, and turn it into a relaxed couples session.': '<strong>1. Primer mensaje.</strong> Todo pasa por la persona que lo planea &mdash; nunca un chat compartido. Conocemos la historia, el nivel de forma y el ambiente. <strong>2. Lugar y hora.</strong> Elegimos una ubicación con un motivo natural para parar y la mejor luz, normalmente el amanecer. <strong>3. La coartada.</strong> Acordamos un motivo creíble para estar arriba temprano &mdash; "una caminata al amanecer", "un amigo fotógrafo que nos acompaña". <strong>4. La señal.</strong> Nos dais una pista pequeña e invisible &mdash; una mano en la espalda, quitarse un gorro &mdash; para saber que llega el momento. <strong>5. Desde la distancia.</strong> Fotografiamos con teleobjetivo, en silencio y sin que nos noten. <strong>6. La revelación.</strong> Tras el sí nos acercamos, nos presentamos como es debido y lo convertimos en una sesión de pareja relajada.',
  'Hands to her face in the first second of surprise': 'Las manos en el rostro en el primer segundo de sorpresa',
  'Choosing the moment &amp; the light': 'Elegir el momento y la luz',
  'First light is our favourite, and not only for the colour. At sunrise the viewpoints are empty, the air is still, and the person being surprised has no crowd to feel self-conscious in front of. We look for a spot with a built-in reason to stop &mdash; a railing, a bench, a summit cross, the end of a jetty &mdash; so that pausing there feels like the most natural thing in the world rather than a staged halt. Then we let the place do the talking.': 'La primera luz es nuestra favorita, y no solo por el color. Al amanecer los miradores están vacíos, el aire está quieto y la persona sorprendida no tiene público ante el que sentirse cohibida. Buscamos un lugar con un motivo incorporado para detenerse &mdash; una baranda, un banco, una cruz de cumbre, el final de un pantalán &mdash; para que pararse allí sea lo más natural del mundo y no un alto ensayado. Luego dejamos que el lugar hable.',
  'Kneeling in the snow at sunrise, backlit by first light': 'El momento de arrodillarse en la nieve al amanecer, a contraluz de la primera luz',
  'Golden hour in the evening works too, and is kinder to non-morning people &mdash; but it is busier, so we choose the spot more carefully. Exact times swing by nearly three hours across the year, so the plan always starts with your date: in high summer the sun clears the peaks around 05:15&ndash;06:00 and sets near 21:00, in spring and autumn sunrise falls between about 06:00 and 07:30, and in winter it is a civilised 07:45&ndash;08:00 with the light gone again by 16:30&ndash;17:15.': 'La hora dorada del atardecer también funciona y es más amable con quienes no son de mañana &mdash; pero hay más gente, así que elegimos el lugar con más cuidado. Las horas exactas varían casi tres horas a lo largo del año, así que el plan siempre empieza por vuestra fecha: en pleno verano el sol asoma sobre las cumbres hacia las 05:15&ndash;06:00 y se pone cerca de las 21:00, en primavera y otoño el amanecer cae entre las 06:00 y las 07:30 aprox., y en invierno es a unas civilizadas 07:45&ndash;08:00 con la luz ya ida hacia las 16:30&ndash;17:15.',
  'Kneeling to propose on the Alpe di Siusi, the Sassolungo behind': 'El momento de arrodillarse en el Alpe di Siusi, el Sassolungo detrás',
  'Keeping it a secret': 'Guardar el secreto',
  'The whole plan lives in one thread between us and the person proposing &mdash; we never message you both, and we never tag the location. On the morning we are simply there first, cameras looking like they are pointed at the mountains, not at you. A long lens lets us stand far enough away that we read as another early hiker with a tripod. The only people who ever spot us are the ones already in on it. That distance is also why the photos feel so unguarded: nobody is performing for a camera they can see.': 'Todo el plan vive en un único hilo entre nosotros y la persona que propone &mdash; nunca os escribimos a los dos, y nunca etiquetamos el lugar. Por la mañana simplemente estamos allí antes, las cámaras aparentando apuntar a las montañas, no a vosotros. Un teleobjetivo nos deja lo bastante lejos como para parecer otro senderista madrugador con trípode. Los únicos que nos detectan son los que ya están en el ajo. Esa distancia es también la razón de que las fotos se sientan tan sinceras: nadie posa para una cámara que puede ver.',
  'Kneeling to propose beneath jagged Dolomite spires, shot from a distance': 'El momento de arrodillarse bajo escarpadas agujas dolomíticas, fotografiado desde la distancia',
  'Often there are accomplices. A friend who suggests the sunrise walk, a parent kept in the loop for the phone call afterwards, a hotel that lets us in early &mdash; we coordinate all of it quietly so the story holds together. And if your partner is the suspicious type, we lean into the cover: we are happy to be introduced as friends of a friend who just happen to love photographing mountains at dawn. The more ordinary we seem, the bigger the surprise lands.': 'A menudo hay cómplices. Una amiga que propone la caminata al amanecer, un padre al tanto para la llamada de después, un hotel que nos deja entrar temprano &mdash; lo coordinamos todo en silencio para que la historia se sostenga. Y si vuestra pareja es del tipo desconfiado, jugamos con la coartada: encantados de que nos presenten como amigos de un amigo a quienes casualmente les encanta fotografiar montañas al alba. Cuanto más normales parezcamos, mayor es la sorpresa.',
  'Where to do it: lakes, viewpoints &amp; meadows': 'Dónde hacerlo: lagos, miradores y prados',
  "The best proposal spots share one thing: a natural reason to pause and little effort to get there &mdash; a long, sweaty hike tends to give the game away. <strong>Roadside lakes</strong> are perfect. The Lago di Braies boardwalk or little Lago d'Antorno give you a railing and a mirror of water before anyone arrives. <strong>Cable-car viewpoints</strong> are just as easy &mdash; Sass Pordoi's terrace, or the Nordkette minutes above Innsbruck &mdash; but the lifts open well after sunrise &mdash; the Nordkette runs its first car around 08:00 and the Seceda not until about 08:30 &mdash; so for a true first-light proposal these are daytime or golden-hour spots unless you stay overnight on the mountain or walk up. Where a cable car is part of the plan, we build the morning around the timetable.": "Los mejores lugares para la pedida comparten una cosa: un motivo natural para parar y poco esfuerzo para llegar &mdash; una caminata larga y sudorosa suele delatar el plan. Los <strong>lagos junto a la carretera</strong> son perfectos. La pasarela del Lago di Braies o el pequeño Lago d'Antorno os dan una baranda y un espejo de agua antes de que llegue nadie. Los <strong>miradores de teleférico</strong> son igual de cómodos &mdash; la terraza del Sass Pordoi o la Nordkette a minutos de Innsbruck &mdash;, pero los remontes abren bastante después del amanecer &mdash; la Nordkette hace su primer viaje hacia las 08:00 y el Seceda no hasta las 08:30 aprox. &mdash;, así que para una pedida de verdad con la primera luz son lugares de día o de hora dorada, salvo que paséis la noche en la montaña o subáis a pie. Cuando un teleférico es parte del plan, construimos la mañana según el horario.",
  'Dancing on the Alpe di Siusi meadow, the Sassolungo behind': 'Baile en el prado del Alpe di Siusi, el Sassolungo detrás',
  '<strong>Open meadows</strong> like the Alpe di Siusi give you space, soft grass and the great tooth of the Sassolungo as a backdrop &mdash; gentle underfoot and endlessly photogenic. And if you do want a <strong>summit</strong>, we pick one with a short walk from a lift or a road, so the effort never signals what is coming. We match the spot to your fitness, the season and the light, and we always scout a second option in case the first is busy or socked in.': 'Los <strong>prados abiertos</strong> como el Alpe di Siusi os dan espacio, hierba blanda y el gran diente del Sassolungo como fondo &mdash; suave bajo los pies e infinitamente fotogénico. Y si de verdad queréis una <strong>cumbre</strong>, elegimos una con una caminata corta desde un remonte o una carretera, para que el esfuerzo nunca delate lo que viene. Ajustamos el lugar a vuestra forma, la estación y la luz, y siempre exploramos una segunda opción por si la primera está llena o cubierta de nubes.',
  'The Nordkette cable car rising over a snowy forest above Innsbruck': 'El teleférico de la Nordkette ascendiendo sobre un bosque nevado por encima de Innsbruck',
  'The ring &amp; the reveal': 'El anillo y la revelación',
  'Carry the ring somewhere zipped and secure on the walk up &mdash; a closed pocket, not a coat you might hand over or a bag you might set down. If you are nervous about the box being spotted, take it out of the box and keep it loose in a small pouch; a bulky box is the classic tell. Tell us if you want a specific hand or angle for the moment, and we will position ourselves for it without ever crowding you.': 'Llevad el anillo en algo cerrado y seguro durante la subida &mdash; un bolsillo con cremallera, no un abrigo que podríais dar ni una bolsa que podríais dejar. Si os preocupa que se vea la cajita, sacad el anillo y llevadlo suelto en una bolsita; una cajita voluminosa es el delator clásico. Decidnos si queréis una mano o un ángulo concretos para el momento, y nos colocaremos para ello sin agobiaros nunca.',
  'A close-up of the new engagement ring in warm light': 'Un primer plano del nuevo anillo de compromiso con luz cálida',
  'Once the yes is out, the ring becomes its own little series &mdash; the hand on a chest, the first look down at it, the shot against the peaks. These are the frames families zoom into, so we take a couple of minutes for them while you are still glowing, then let you go back to being giddy.': 'Una vez fuera el sí, el anillo se vuelve su propia pequeña serie &mdash; la mano sobre el pecho, la primera mirada hacia él, la foto contra las cumbres. Son los fotogramas en los que las familias hacen zoom, así que les dedicamos un par de minutos mientras seguís radiantes, y luego os dejamos volver a vuestro vértigo de felicidad.',
  'The new ring resting on his shoulder during an embrace': 'El nuevo anillo apoyado en su hombro durante un abrazo',
  'Weather &amp; a Plan B': 'El tiempo y un plan B',
  'Mountain weather turns fast, so a proposal plan is never a single point &mdash; it is a window. We watch the forecast in the days before, hold a backup spot that works in worse light, and keep a spare morning where we can. If your first choice is fogged in, we move; if it clears an hour late, we wait. And do not fear a grey sky: low cloud drifting through the peaks, or a little rain on a lake, gives some of the most cinematic, tender frames we ever take. The only weather we truly avoid is the unsafe kind.': 'El tiempo de montaña cambia rápido, así que un plan de pedida nunca es un punto único &mdash; es una ventana. Vigilamos la previsión los días previos, mantenemos un lugar de reserva que funcione con peor luz y guardamos una mañana extra cuando podemos. Si vuestra primera elección se cubre de niebla, cambiamos; si despeja una hora tarde, esperamos. Y no temáis un cielo gris: nubes bajas deslizándose entre las cumbres, o algo de lluvia sobre un lago, dan algunos de los fotogramas más cinematográficos y tiernos que hacemos. El único tiempo que de verdad evitamos es el inseguro.',
  'A kiss under a moody, dramatic Dolomite sky': 'Un beso bajo un cielo dolomítico dramático y encapotado',
  'This is why we never sell a proposal as a single fixed slot. We build in a little give &mdash; an earlier alarm than strictly needed, a second spot ten minutes away, a backup morning if your trip allows it. Nine times out of ten the first plan works perfectly; the tenth time, that flexibility is the difference between a soggy compromise and a morning you could not have dreamed up. Nervous energy is enough to carry on the day &mdash; the weather is our job to worry about, not yours.': 'Por eso nunca vendemos una pedida como un único horario fijo. Metemos un poco de margen &mdash; una alarma más temprana de lo estrictamente necesario, un segundo lugar a diez minutos, una mañana de reserva si vuestro viaje lo permite. Nueve de cada diez veces el primer plan funciona a la perfección; la décima, ese margen es la diferencia entre un compromiso empapado y una mañana que no habríais podido soñar. La energía nerviosa basta para llevar el día &mdash; preocuparse por el tiempo es nuestro trabajo, no el vuestro.',
  'When to go: snow or meadows': 'Cuándo ir: nieve o prados',
  'A proposal works year-round, and the season changes the whole feeling. <strong>Summer</strong> gives you green meadows, cotton grass and long light &mdash; the easiest logistics and the warmest mornings. <strong>Autumn</strong> brings larches turning gold and the first quiet after the crowds. <strong>Winter</strong> is our secret favourite: snow to the horizon, a hush over everything, and a kneel in fresh powder that looks like the inside of a snow globe &mdash; you just need warm layers and good boots. We help you pick the season that matches the picture in your head, then build the morning around it.': 'Una pedida funciona todo el año, y la estación cambia toda la sensación. El <strong>verano</strong> os da prados verdes, algodón de pantano y luz larga &mdash; la logística más fácil y las mañanas más cálidas. El <strong>otoño</strong> trae los alerces volviéndose dorados y la primera calma tras las multitudes. El <strong>invierno</strong> es nuestro favorito secreto: nieve hasta el horizonte, un silencio sobre todo y un arrodillarse en nieve fresca que parece el interior de una bola de nieve &mdash; solo necesitáis capas de abrigo y buenas botas. Os ayudamos a elegir la estación que encaja con la imagen de vuestra cabeza y construimos la mañana en torno a ella.',
  'Arriving at a snowy mountain station in winter light': 'Llegando a una estación de montaña nevada con luz de invierno',
  'What to wear': 'Qué llevar',
  'Dress like the best version of a normal day out &mdash; nice enough that you will love the photos, plausible enough that it does not tip your partner off. Solid, muted colours read beautifully against rock and snow; busy logos and neon do not. Bring warm layers you can peel for the frames and pull back on between them, and real shoes for the ground you will actually be standing on. If it is a surprise, the person being proposed to should just be told "we\'re doing sunrise photos, wear something you feel good in" &mdash; enough to look lovely, not enough to guess.': 'Vestíos como la mejor versión de un día normal &mdash; bastante bien como para amar las fotos, bastante plausible como para no dar pistas a vuestra pareja. Los colores sólidos y apagados quedan preciosos contra la roca y la nieve; los logos recargados y el neón no. Llevad capas de abrigo que podáis quitaros para las fotos y volver a poneros entre ellas, y zapatos de verdad para el suelo en el que estaréis realmente. Si es sorpresa, a la persona a la que se le propone basta con decirle "vamos a hacer fotos al amanecer, ponte algo con lo que te sientas bien" &mdash; suficiente para verse preciosa, no para adivinarlo.',
  'Sitting together in the cotton grass as the peaks glow at last light': 'Sentados juntos en el algodón de pantano mientras las cumbres brillan en la última luz',
  'A few small things make a big difference in the pictures. Loose hair moves beautifully in a summit breeze, so skip the tight updo unless you love it. Bring a warm layer you can hide until the walk down, and think about your hands &mdash; they are the stars of every ring photo, so a little care there pays off. And whatever you wear, wear it in beforehand: new boots on a cold dawn are the one thing guaranteed to distract from the moment.': 'Unas pocas cosas pequeñas marcan una gran diferencia en las fotos. El pelo suelto se mueve precioso en una brisa de cumbre, así que dejad el moño tirante salvo que os encante. Llevad una capa de abrigo que podáis esconder hasta la bajada, y pensad en vuestras manos &mdash; son las estrellas de toda foto de anillo, así que cuidarlas un poco compensa. Y llevéis lo que llevéis, estrenadlo antes: unas botas nuevas en un amanecer frío son lo único que garantiza distraer del momento.',
  'Getting there &amp; the logistics': 'Cómo llegar y la logística',
  'Most couples fly into Venice, Verona or Innsbruck and drive the last stretch &mdash; roughly two to three hours to the heart of the Dolomites, and Innsbruck is right at the foot of the Nordkette. Where cable cars are part of the plan, the first departure sets the morning: many lifts open only after sunrise, so a true first-light proposal often means a roadside lake or a spot you can reach on foot instead. We tell you exactly where to be, when, and how to get there, and can meet you at the trailhead so you are never navigating on the big morning.': 'La mayoría de las parejas vuela a Venecia, Verona o Innsbruck y conduce el último tramo &mdash; unas dos o tres horas hasta el corazón de los Dolomitas, e Innsbruck está justo al pie de la Nordkette. Cuando los teleféricos son parte del plan, la primera salida marca la mañana: muchos remontes abren solo después del amanecer, así que una pedida de verdad con la primera luz suele significar un lago junto a la carretera o un lugar que podáis alcanzar a pie. Os decimos exactamente dónde estar, cuándo y cómo llegar, y podemos veros en el inicio del sendero para que nunca tengáis que orientaros en la gran mañana.',
  'A signpost at the Hafelekar station high above Innsbruck': 'Un cartel indicador en la estación del Hafelekar muy por encima de Innsbruck',
  'Beating the crowds': 'Esquivar las multitudes',
  'The famous spots fill up &mdash; Braies in particular is a different place at 06:00 than at 11:00. First light is the cleanest way past that: you get the railing, the reflection and the silence before the tour buses. Where driving access is limited we plan around it &mdash; the road to Lago di Braies, for example, needs an advance reservation from 09:00 to 16:00 between 1 July and 15 September, which is another reason we love being there for sunrise instead. Empty light is always the better light, and an empty viewpoint makes the surprise feel like it is yours alone.': 'Los lugares famosos se llenan &mdash; Braies en particular es otro sitio a las 06:00 que a las 11:00. La primera luz es la forma más limpia de dejar eso atrás: tenéis la baranda, el reflejo y el silencio antes de los autobuses turísticos. Donde el acceso en coche está limitado, planificamos en torno a ello &mdash; la carretera al Lago di Braies, por ejemplo, necesita una reserva anticipada de 09:00 a 16:00 entre el 1 de julio y el 15 de septiembre, otra razón por la que preferimos estar allí al amanecer. La luz vacía es siempre la mejor luz, y un mirador vacío hace que la sorpresa se sienta solo vuestra.',
  'The shadow of the cable-car cabin cast on the snow below': 'La sombra de la cabina del teleférico proyectada sobre la nieve',
  'It helps to think in half-hours. A viewpoint that is serene at 06:15 can have a queue for the same railing by 07:30, so we build the morning backwards from the light and stay a step ahead of the first arrivals. If a spot is simply too popular to guarantee privacy, we will say so and offer a quieter twin nearby &mdash; there is almost always a lesser-known ledge or shoreline with the same peaks behind it and none of the crowd in front.': 'Ayuda pensar en medias horas. Un mirador sereno a las 06:15 puede tener cola en la misma baranda a las 07:30, así que construimos la mañana hacia atrás desde la luz y nos mantenemos un paso por delante de los primeros en llegar. Si un lugar es sencillamente demasiado popular para garantizar intimidad, lo diremos y ofreceremos un gemelo más tranquilo cerca &mdash; casi siempre hay un saliente o una orilla menos conocidos con las mismas cumbres detrás y sin la multitud delante.',
  'After the yes': 'Tras el sí',
  'The moment is over in seconds; the celebration is the rest of the morning. Once we have introduced ourselves properly, we keep shooting a relaxed couples session while you are still buzzing &mdash; the laughing, the disbelief, the first phone call home. This is when the pictures get loose and joyful, and it is often the part couples treasure most. We can turn a few images around the same day so you can share the news before you are even back down in the valley.': 'El momento se acaba en segundos; la celebración es el resto de la mañana. Una vez que nos hemos presentado como es debido, seguimos fotografiando una sesión de pareja relajada mientras seguís vibrando &mdash; las risas, la incredulidad, la primera llamada a casa. Es cuando las fotos se sueltan y se llenan de alegría, y a menudo es la parte que las parejas más atesoran. Podemos entregaros unas imágenes el mismo día para que compartáis la noticia antes incluso de haber bajado al valle.',
  'He lifts her in joy, the Cadini spires behind': 'Él la levanta de alegría, las agujas del Cadini detrás',
  'Make a day of it, too. The Dolomites reward a slow morning after: a hut breakfast, a swim in a cold lake, a quiet drive through the passes while it all sinks in. Cortina, Val Gardena and the villages of the Alta Badia sit within an hour of everything, full of terraces made for exactly this kind of celebrating. We are happy to point you to the good ones.': 'Haced un día de ello, además. Los Dolomitas premian una mañana lenta después: un desayuno en un refugio, un baño en un lago frío, un tranquilo recorrido por los puertos mientras todo cala. Cortina, Val Gardena y los pueblos de la Alta Badia están a menos de una hora de todo, llenos de terrazas hechas para exactamente este tipo de celebración. Encantados de indicaros las buenas.',
  'The couple playing in the last evening light after the yes': 'La pareja jugando en la última luz de la tarde tras el sí',
  'From proposal to wedding': 'De la pedida a la boda',
  'A surprising number of our couples propose here and then come back to marry here &mdash; the mountains that held the question turn out to be exactly where they want to say the vows. If that thought is already flickering, we can plant the seed on the same trip: show you the spot that would make a perfect elopement, talk through how the legal side works in Italy and Austria, and hand you a plan for later with zero pressure now. The proposal is the beginning of the story; sometimes we get to photograph the whole thing.': 'Un número sorprendente de nuestras parejas se propone aquí y luego vuelve a casarse aquí &mdash; las montañas que sostuvieron la pregunta resultan ser justo donde quieren decir el sí. Si ese pensamiento ya titila, podemos plantar la semilla en el mismo viaje: enseñaros el lugar que sería un elopement perfecto, explicaros cómo funciona la parte legal en Italia y Austria y entregaros un plan para más adelante sin ninguna presión ahora. La pedida es el comienzo de la historia; a veces podemos fotografiarla entera.',
  'A first kiss as she shows the new ring to the camera': 'Un primer beso mientras ella muestra el nuevo anillo a la cámara',
  'What it is': 'Qué es',
  'How we pull it off': 'Cómo lo logramos',
  'Choosing the moment': 'Elegir el momento',
  'Keeping the secret': 'Guardar el secreto',
  'Where to do it': 'Dónde hacerlo',
  'The ring': 'El anillo',
  'Weather & Plan B': 'El tiempo y plan B',
  'When to go': 'Cuándo ir',
  'Getting there': 'Cómo llegar',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'Mountain proposal FAQ': 'Preguntas frecuentes sobre la pedida en la montaña',
  'A proposal in the mountains is equal parts logistics and nerve. Get it right and you have the best surprise of your life in the best light on earth &mdash; the question asked with a whole range of peaks as your witness, and every second of it quietly photographed. This is everything we have learned helping people propose in the Dolomites and the wider Alps: how to keep the secret, where to kneel, how to read the weather, and what happens after the yes.': 'Una pedida en la montaña es logística y nervios a partes iguales. Si sale bien, tenéis la mejor sorpresa de vuestra vida en la mejor luz de la tierra &mdash; la pregunta hecha con toda una cordillera de cumbres como testigo, y cada segundo fotografiado en silencio. Esto es todo lo que hemos aprendido ayudando a la gente a proponerse en los Dolomitas y en los Alpes en general: cómo guardar el secreto, dónde arrodillarse, cómo leer el tiempo y qué pasa tras el sí.',
  'On this page': 'En esta página',
}
PROP_IT = {
  'Ready to book a surprise proposal shoot': 'Pronti a prenotare un servizio di proposta a sorpresa',
  'What a mountain proposal really is': "Cos'è davvero una proposta in montagna",
  'A mountain proposal is a small, precise piece of theatre: one person knows the plan, the other has no idea, and a photographer is hidden in plain sight to catch the moment it all lands. The setting does half the work &mdash; a lakeshore at first light, a viewpoint above the clouds, a meadow under jagged peaks &mdash; but the magic is the surprise, and protecting it is our whole job until you kneel. After that it turns into a celebration, and we keep photographing while you float.': "Una proposta in montagna è un piccolo e preciso pezzo di teatro: una persona conosce il piano, l'altra non ne ha idea, e un fotografo è nascosto in piena vista per cogliere il momento in cui tutto accade. Il luogo fa metà del lavoro &mdash; la riva di un lago alla prima luce, un punto panoramico sopra le nuvole, un prato sotto cime frastagliate &mdash;, ma la magia è la sorpresa, e proteggerla è tutto il nostro compito finché non vi inginocchiate. Dopo diventa una festa, e continuiamo a fotografare mentre fluttuate.",
  'A proposal on the Lago di Braies boardwalk among the wooden boats': 'Una proposta sulla passerella del Lago di Braies tra le barche di legno',
  'Couples come to us for it from all over &mdash; some already live for the mountains, some just want somewhere that will never feel ordinary to remember. It works for the fit and the not-so-fit, in deep summer and deep snow, at a lake you can drive to or a summit you have to earn. Whatever you picture, the shape is the same: a quiet approach, a natural pause, the question, and then the loudest, happiest hour of your trip.': "Le coppie ci cercano da ogni dove &mdash; alcune vivono già per la montagna, altre vogliono solo un luogo che non sembrerà mai ordinario da ricordare. Funziona per gli allenati e i meno allenati, in piena estate e in piena neve, a un lago raggiungibile in auto o a una vetta da guadagnarsi. Qualunque cosa immaginiate, la forma è la stessa: un avvicinamento tranquillo, una pausa naturale, la domanda, e poi l'ora più rumorosa e felice del vostro viaggio.",
  'Foreheads together after the yes, the new ring visible': 'Fronte contro fronte dopo il sì, il nuovo anello in vista',
  'How we pull off the surprise, step by step': 'Come realizziamo la sorpresa, passo dopo passo',
  '<strong>1. First message.</strong> Everything runs through the person planning it &mdash; never a shared chat. We learn the story, the fitness level and the vibe. <strong>2. Spot &amp; time.</strong> We pick a location that gives a natural reason to pause and the best light, usually sunrise. <strong>3. The cover story.</strong> We agree on a believable reason to be up there early &mdash; "a sunrise hike," "a photographer friend meeting us." <strong>4. The signal.</strong> You give us a small, invisible cue &mdash; a hand on the back, taking off a hat &mdash; so we know the second is coming. <strong>5. From a distance.</strong> We shoot long, quiet and unnoticed. <strong>6. The reveal.</strong> After the yes we walk over, introduce ourselves properly, and turn it into a relaxed couples session.': '<strong>1. Primo messaggio.</strong> Tutto passa dalla persona che organizza &mdash; mai una chat condivisa. Conosciamo la storia, il livello di forma e l\'atmosfera. <strong>2. Luogo e orario.</strong> Scegliamo una location con un motivo naturale per fermarsi e la luce migliore, di solito l\'alba. <strong>3. La copertura.</strong> Concordiamo un motivo credibile per essere lassù presto &mdash; "un\'escursione all\'alba", "un amico fotografo che ci raggiunge". <strong>4. Il segnale.</strong> Ci date un cenno piccolo e invisibile &mdash; una mano sulla schiena, togliersi il cappello &mdash; così sappiamo che il momento arriva. <strong>5. Dalla distanza.</strong> Fotografiamo con il teleobiettivo, in silenzio e senza farci notare. <strong>6. La rivelazione.</strong> Dopo il sì ci avviciniamo, ci presentiamo come si deve e trasformiamo il tutto in un rilassato servizio di coppia.',
  'Hands to her face in the first second of surprise': 'Le mani sul viso nel primo secondo di sorpresa',
  'Choosing the moment &amp; the light': 'Scegliere il momento e la luce',
  'First light is our favourite, and not only for the colour. At sunrise the viewpoints are empty, the air is still, and the person being surprised has no crowd to feel self-conscious in front of. We look for a spot with a built-in reason to stop &mdash; a railing, a bench, a summit cross, the end of a jetty &mdash; so that pausing there feels like the most natural thing in the world rather than a staged halt. Then we let the place do the talking.': "La prima luce è la nostra preferita, e non solo per il colore. All'alba i punti panoramici sono vuoti, l'aria è ferma e la persona sorpresa non ha un pubblico davanti a cui sentirsi in imbarazzo. Cerchiamo un luogo con un motivo incorporato per fermarsi &mdash; una ringhiera, una panchina, una croce di vetta, la fine di un pontile &mdash; così che sostare lì sembri la cosa più naturale del mondo e non una sosta preparata. Poi lasciamo parlare il luogo.",
  'Kneeling in the snow at sunrise, backlit by first light': "L'inginocchiarsi nella neve all'alba, in controluce nella prima luce",
  'Golden hour in the evening works too, and is kinder to non-morning people &mdash; but it is busier, so we choose the spot more carefully. Exact times swing by nearly three hours across the year, so the plan always starts with your date: in high summer the sun clears the peaks around 05:15&ndash;06:00 and sets near 21:00, in spring and autumn sunrise falls between about 06:00 and 07:30, and in winter it is a civilised 07:45&ndash;08:00 with the light gone again by 16:30&ndash;17:15.': "Anche l'ora dorata della sera funziona ed è più gentile con chi non è mattiniero &mdash; ma c'è più gente, quindi scegliamo il luogo con più cura. Gli orari esatti variano di quasi tre ore nell'arco dell'anno, perciò il piano parte sempre dalla vostra data: in piena estate il sole spunta sulle cime verso le 05:15&ndash;06:00 e tramonta attorno alle 21:00, in primavera e autunno l'alba cade tra circa le 06:00 e le 07:30, e in inverno è a civili 07:45&ndash;08:00 con la luce già andata verso le 16:30&ndash;17:15.",
  'Kneeling to propose on the Alpe di Siusi, the Sassolungo behind': "L'inginocchiarsi sull'Alpe di Siusi, il Sassolungo dietro",
  'Keeping it a secret': 'Mantenere il segreto',
  'The whole plan lives in one thread between us and the person proposing &mdash; we never message you both, and we never tag the location. On the morning we are simply there first, cameras looking like they are pointed at the mountains, not at you. A long lens lets us stand far enough away that we read as another early hiker with a tripod. The only people who ever spot us are the ones already in on it. That distance is also why the photos feel so unguarded: nobody is performing for a camera they can see.': 'Tutto il piano vive in un unico filo tra noi e la persona che propone &mdash; non scriviamo mai a entrambi, e non taggiamo mai il luogo. Al mattino siamo semplicemente lì per primi, le fotocamere che sembrano puntate sulle montagne, non su di voi. Un teleobiettivo ci fa stare abbastanza lontani da sembrare un altro escursionista mattiniero con il treppiede. Gli unici che ci notano sono quelli già a conoscenza. Quella distanza è anche il motivo per cui le foto sembrano così spontanee: nessuno posa per una fotocamera che può vedere.',
  'Kneeling to propose beneath jagged Dolomite spires, shot from a distance': "L'inginocchiarsi sotto frastagliate guglie dolomitiche, fotografato dalla distanza",
  'Often there are accomplices. A friend who suggests the sunrise walk, a parent kept in the loop for the phone call afterwards, a hotel that lets us in early &mdash; we coordinate all of it quietly so the story holds together. And if your partner is the suspicious type, we lean into the cover: we are happy to be introduced as friends of a friend who just happen to love photographing mountains at dawn. The more ordinary we seem, the bigger the surprise lands.': "Spesso ci sono complici. Un'amica che propone la camminata all'alba, un genitore informato per la telefonata dopo, un hotel che ci fa entrare presto &mdash; coordiniamo tutto in silenzio così la storia regge. E se il vostro partner è del tipo sospettoso, giochiamo sulla copertura: felici di essere presentati come amici di un amico che per caso adorano fotografare le montagne all'alba. Più sembriamo ordinari, più grande è la sorpresa.",
  'Where to do it: lakes, viewpoints &amp; meadows': 'Dove farlo: laghi, punti panoramici e prati',
  "The best proposal spots share one thing: a natural reason to pause and little effort to get there &mdash; a long, sweaty hike tends to give the game away. <strong>Roadside lakes</strong> are perfect. The Lago di Braies boardwalk or little Lago d'Antorno give you a railing and a mirror of water before anyone arrives. <strong>Cable-car viewpoints</strong> are just as easy &mdash; Sass Pordoi's terrace, or the Nordkette minutes above Innsbruck &mdash; but the lifts open well after sunrise &mdash; the Nordkette runs its first car around 08:00 and the Seceda not until about 08:30 &mdash; so for a true first-light proposal these are daytime or golden-hour spots unless you stay overnight on the mountain or walk up. Where a cable car is part of the plan, we build the morning around the timetable.": "I migliori luoghi per la proposta hanno una cosa in comune: un motivo naturale per fermarsi e poca fatica per arrivarci &mdash; una lunga camminata sudata tende a tradire il piano. I <strong>laghi sul ciglio della strada</strong> sono perfetti. La passerella del Lago di Braies o il piccolo Lago d'Antorno vi danno una ringhiera e uno specchio d'acqua prima che arrivi qualcuno. I <strong>punti panoramici con funivia</strong> sono altrettanto comodi &mdash; la terrazza del Sass Pordoi o la Nordkette a pochi minuti da Innsbruck &mdash;, ma gli impianti aprono ben dopo l'alba &mdash; la Nordkette fa la prima corsa verso le 08:00 e il Seceda non prima delle 08:30 circa &mdash;, perciò per una vera proposta alla prima luce sono luoghi da giorno o da ora dorata, a meno che non pernottiate in montagna o saliate a piedi. Dove una funivia fa parte del piano, costruiamo la mattina attorno agli orari.",
  'Dancing on the Alpe di Siusi meadow, the Sassolungo behind': "Ballo sul prato dell'Alpe di Siusi, il Sassolungo dietro",
  '<strong>Open meadows</strong> like the Alpe di Siusi give you space, soft grass and the great tooth of the Sassolungo as a backdrop &mdash; gentle underfoot and endlessly photogenic. And if you do want a <strong>summit</strong>, we pick one with a short walk from a lift or a road, so the effort never signals what is coming. We match the spot to your fitness, the season and the light, and we always scout a second option in case the first is busy or socked in.': "I <strong>prati aperti</strong> come l'Alpe di Siusi vi danno spazio, erba morbida e il grande dente del Sassolungo come sfondo &mdash; dolce sotto i piedi e infinitamente fotogenico. E se volete davvero una <strong>vetta</strong>, ne scegliamo una con una breve camminata da un impianto o da una strada, così la fatica non tradisce mai ciò che sta per arrivare. Adattiamo il luogo alla vostra forma, alla stagione e alla luce, e cerchiamo sempre una seconda opzione nel caso la prima sia affollata o coperta.",
  'The Nordkette cable car rising over a snowy forest above Innsbruck': 'La funivia della Nordkette che sale sopra un bosco innevato sopra Innsbruck',
  'The ring &amp; the reveal': "L'anello e la rivelazione",
  'Carry the ring somewhere zipped and secure on the walk up &mdash; a closed pocket, not a coat you might hand over or a bag you might set down. If you are nervous about the box being spotted, take it out of the box and keep it loose in a small pouch; a bulky box is the classic tell. Tell us if you want a specific hand or angle for the moment, and we will position ourselves for it without ever crowding you.': "Portate l'anello in qualcosa di chiuso e sicuro durante la salita &mdash; una tasca con cerniera, non una giacca che potreste consegnare né una borsa che potreste posare. Se temete che la scatola venga notata, togliete l'anello e tenetelo sciolto in un sacchettino; una scatola voluminosa è il classico indizio. Diteci se volete una mano o un'angolazione precisa per il momento, e ci posizioneremo per questo senza mai starvi addosso.",
  'A close-up of the new engagement ring in warm light': 'Un primo piano del nuovo anello di fidanzamento nella luce calda',
  'Once the yes is out, the ring becomes its own little series &mdash; the hand on a chest, the first look down at it, the shot against the peaks. These are the frames families zoom into, so we take a couple of minutes for them while you are still glowing, then let you go back to being giddy.': "Una volta uscito il sì, l'anello diventa una sua piccola serie &mdash; la mano sul petto, il primo sguardo verso il basso, lo scatto contro le cime. Sono i fotogrammi su cui le famiglie fanno zoom, quindi dedichiamo un paio di minuti mentre siete ancora raggianti, e poi vi lasciamo tornare alla vostra euforia.",
  'The new ring resting on his shoulder during an embrace': 'Il nuovo anello appoggiato sulla sua spalla durante un abbraccio',
  'Weather &amp; a Plan B': 'Meteo e un piano B',
  'Mountain weather turns fast, so a proposal plan is never a single point &mdash; it is a window. We watch the forecast in the days before, hold a backup spot that works in worse light, and keep a spare morning where we can. If your first choice is fogged in, we move; if it clears an hour late, we wait. And do not fear a grey sky: low cloud drifting through the peaks, or a little rain on a lake, gives some of the most cinematic, tender frames we ever take. The only weather we truly avoid is the unsafe kind.': "Il meteo di montagna cambia in fretta, quindi un piano di proposta non è mai un punto singolo &mdash; è una finestra. Seguiamo le previsioni nei giorni prima, teniamo un luogo di riserva che funzioni con luce peggiore e teniamo una mattina in più quando possiamo. Se la vostra prima scelta è nella nebbia, ci spostiamo; se schiarisce un'ora dopo, aspettiamo. E non temete un cielo grigio: nubi basse che scorrono tra le cime, o un po' di pioggia su un lago, regalano alcuni dei fotogrammi più cinematografici e teneri che facciamo. L'unico tempo che evitiamo davvero è quello non sicuro.",
  'A kiss under a moody, dramatic Dolomite sky': 'Un bacio sotto un cielo dolomitico cupo e drammatico',
  'This is why we never sell a proposal as a single fixed slot. We build in a little give &mdash; an earlier alarm than strictly needed, a second spot ten minutes away, a backup morning if your trip allows it. Nine times out of ten the first plan works perfectly; the tenth time, that flexibility is the difference between a soggy compromise and a morning you could not have dreamed up. Nervous energy is enough to carry on the day &mdash; the weather is our job to worry about, not yours.': "Ecco perché non vendiamo mai una proposta come un unico orario fisso. Inseriamo un po' di margine &mdash; una sveglia più presto del necessario, un secondo luogo a dieci minuti, una mattina di riserva se il vostro viaggio lo consente. Nove volte su dieci il primo piano funziona alla perfezione; la decima, quel margine è la differenza tra un compromesso fradicio e una mattina che non avreste potuto sognare. L'energia nervosa basta a reggere la giornata &mdash; preoccuparsi del meteo è compito nostro, non vostro.",
  'When to go: snow or meadows': 'Quando andare: neve o prati',
  'A proposal works year-round, and the season changes the whole feeling. <strong>Summer</strong> gives you green meadows, cotton grass and long light &mdash; the easiest logistics and the warmest mornings. <strong>Autumn</strong> brings larches turning gold and the first quiet after the crowds. <strong>Winter</strong> is our secret favourite: snow to the horizon, a hush over everything, and a kneel in fresh powder that looks like the inside of a snow globe &mdash; you just need warm layers and good boots. We help you pick the season that matches the picture in your head, then build the morning around it.': "Una proposta funziona tutto l'anno, e la stagione cambia l'intera sensazione. L'<strong>estate</strong> vi dà prati verdi, erioforo e luce lunga &mdash; la logistica più facile e le mattine più calde. L'<strong>autunno</strong> porta i larici che diventano dorati e la prima quiete dopo la folla. L'<strong>inverno</strong> è il nostro preferito segreto: neve fino all'orizzonte, un silenzio su tutto e un inginocchiarsi nella neve fresca che sembra l'interno di una palla di neve &mdash; vi servono solo strati caldi e buoni scarponi. Vi aiutiamo a scegliere la stagione che corrisponde all'immagine nella vostra testa e costruiamo la mattina attorno a essa.",
  'Arriving at a snowy mountain station in winter light': 'Arrivo a una stazione di montagna innevata nella luce invernale',
  'What to wear': 'Cosa indossare',
  'Dress like the best version of a normal day out &mdash; nice enough that you will love the photos, plausible enough that it does not tip your partner off. Solid, muted colours read beautifully against rock and snow; busy logos and neon do not. Bring warm layers you can peel for the frames and pull back on between them, and real shoes for the ground you will actually be standing on. If it is a surprise, the person being proposed to should just be told "we\'re doing sunrise photos, wear something you feel good in" &mdash; enough to look lovely, not enough to guess.': 'Vestitevi come la versione migliore di una normale giornata fuori &mdash; abbastanza belli da amare le foto, abbastanza plausibili da non insospettire il partner. I colori pieni e tenui rendono benissimo su roccia e neve; loghi vistosi e neon no. Portate strati caldi da togliere per le foto e rimettere tra una e l\'altra, e scarpe vere per il terreno su cui starete davvero. Se è una sorpresa, alla persona a cui si propone basta dire "facciamo foto all\'alba, metti qualcosa in cui ti senti bene" &mdash; abbastanza per essere splendida, non abbastanza per indovinare.',
  'Sitting together in the cotton grass as the peaks glow at last light': "Seduti insieme nell'erioforo mentre le cime si accendono nell'ultima luce",
  'A few small things make a big difference in the pictures. Loose hair moves beautifully in a summit breeze, so skip the tight updo unless you love it. Bring a warm layer you can hide until the walk down, and think about your hands &mdash; they are the stars of every ring photo, so a little care there pays off. And whatever you wear, wear it in beforehand: new boots on a cold dawn are the one thing guaranteed to distract from the moment.': "Poche piccole cose fanno una grande differenza nelle foto. I capelli sciolti si muovono benissimo in una brezza di vetta, quindi lasciate perdere lo chignon stretto se non lo amate. Portate uno strato caldo da nascondere fino alla discesa, e pensate alle mani &mdash; sono le star di ogni foto dell'anello, quindi un po' di cura lì ripaga. E qualunque cosa indossiate, indossatela prima: scarponi nuovi in un'alba fredda sono l'unica cosa che di sicuro distrae dal momento.",
  'Getting there &amp; the logistics': 'Come arrivare e la logistica',
  'Most couples fly into Venice, Verona or Innsbruck and drive the last stretch &mdash; roughly two to three hours to the heart of the Dolomites, and Innsbruck is right at the foot of the Nordkette. Where cable cars are part of the plan, the first departure sets the morning: many lifts open only after sunrise, so a true first-light proposal often means a roadside lake or a spot you can reach on foot instead. We tell you exactly where to be, when, and how to get there, and can meet you at the trailhead so you are never navigating on the big morning.': "La maggior parte delle coppie atterra a Venezia, Verona o Innsbruck e guida l'ultimo tratto &mdash; circa due o tre ore fino al cuore delle Dolomiti, e Innsbruck è proprio ai piedi della Nordkette. Dove le funivie fanno parte del piano, la prima corsa detta la mattina: molti impianti aprono solo dopo l'alba, quindi una vera proposta alla prima luce spesso significa un lago sul ciglio della strada o un luogo raggiungibile a piedi. Vi diciamo esattamente dove essere, quando e come arrivare, e possiamo incontrarvi all'inizio del sentiero così non dovete mai orientarvi nella grande mattina.",
  'A signpost at the Hafelekar station high above Innsbruck': "Un cartello indicatore alla stazione dell'Hafelekar in alto sopra Innsbruck",
  'Beating the crowds': 'Battere la folla',
  'The famous spots fill up &mdash; Braies in particular is a different place at 06:00 than at 11:00. First light is the cleanest way past that: you get the railing, the reflection and the silence before the tour buses. Where driving access is limited we plan around it &mdash; the road to Lago di Braies, for example, needs an advance reservation from 09:00 to 16:00 between 1 July and 15 September, which is another reason we love being there for sunrise instead. Empty light is always the better light, and an empty viewpoint makes the surprise feel like it is yours alone.': "I luoghi famosi si riempiono &mdash; Braies in particolare è un posto diverso alle 06:00 rispetto alle 11:00. La prima luce è il modo più netto per lasciarla indietro: avete la ringhiera, il riflesso e il silenzio prima dei pullman turistici. Dove l'accesso in auto è limitato, pianifichiamo di conseguenza &mdash; la strada per il Lago di Braies, ad esempio, richiede una prenotazione anticipata dalle 09:00 alle 16:00 tra il 1° luglio e il 15 settembre, un altro motivo per cui amiamo esserci all'alba. La luce vuota è sempre la luce migliore, e un punto panoramico vuoto fa sentire la sorpresa solo vostra.",
  'The shadow of the cable-car cabin cast on the snow below': "L'ombra della cabina della funivia proiettata sulla neve sottostante",
  'It helps to think in half-hours. A viewpoint that is serene at 06:15 can have a queue for the same railing by 07:30, so we build the morning backwards from the light and stay a step ahead of the first arrivals. If a spot is simply too popular to guarantee privacy, we will say so and offer a quieter twin nearby &mdash; there is almost always a lesser-known ledge or shoreline with the same peaks behind it and none of the crowd in front.': "Aiuta pensare in mezze ore. Un punto panoramico sereno alle 06:15 può avere la coda alla stessa ringhiera per le 07:30, quindi costruiamo la mattina a ritroso dalla luce e restiamo un passo avanti ai primi arrivi. Se un luogo è semplicemente troppo popolare per garantire privacy, lo diciamo e proponiamo un gemello più tranquillo nelle vicinanze &mdash; c'è quasi sempre un lembo o una riva meno noti con le stesse cime dietro e nessuna folla davanti.",
  'After the yes': 'Dopo il sì',
  'The moment is over in seconds; the celebration is the rest of the morning. Once we have introduced ourselves properly, we keep shooting a relaxed couples session while you are still buzzing &mdash; the laughing, the disbelief, the first phone call home. This is when the pictures get loose and joyful, and it is often the part couples treasure most. We can turn a few images around the same day so you can share the news before you are even back down in the valley.': "Il momento finisce in pochi secondi; la festa è il resto della mattina. Una volta presentati come si deve, continuiamo a fotografare un rilassato servizio di coppia mentre siete ancora in fibrillazione &mdash; le risate, l'incredulità, la prima telefonata a casa. È quando le foto diventano sciolte e gioiose, ed è spesso la parte che le coppie custodiscono di più. Possiamo consegnarvi qualche immagine lo stesso giorno così condividete la notizia prima ancora di essere tornati a valle.",
  'He lifts her in joy, the Cadini spires behind': 'Lui la solleva di gioia, le guglie dei Cadini dietro',
  'Make a day of it, too. The Dolomites reward a slow morning after: a hut breakfast, a swim in a cold lake, a quiet drive through the passes while it all sinks in. Cortina, Val Gardena and the villages of the Alta Badia sit within an hour of everything, full of terraces made for exactly this kind of celebrating. We are happy to point you to the good ones.': "Fatene anche una giornata. Le Dolomiti premiano una mattina lenta dopo: una colazione in rifugio, un tuffo in un lago freddo, un tranquillo giro tra i passi mentre tutto si sedimenta. Cortina, la Val Gardena e i paesi dell'Alta Badia sono a meno di un'ora da tutto, pieni di terrazze fatte esattamente per questo tipo di festa. Con piacere vi indichiamo quelle buone.",
  'The couple playing in the last evening light after the yes': "La coppia che gioca nell'ultima luce della sera dopo il sì",
  'From proposal to wedding': 'Dalla proposta al matrimonio',
  'A surprising number of our couples propose here and then come back to marry here &mdash; the mountains that held the question turn out to be exactly where they want to say the vows. If that thought is already flickering, we can plant the seed on the same trip: show you the spot that would make a perfect elopement, talk through how the legal side works in Italy and Austria, and hand you a plan for later with zero pressure now. The proposal is the beginning of the story; sometimes we get to photograph the whole thing.': "Un numero sorprendente delle nostre coppie fa la proposta qui e poi torna a sposarsi qui &mdash; le montagne che hanno tenuto la domanda si rivelano proprio dove vogliono dire il sì. Se quel pensiero già balugina, possiamo piantare il seme nello stesso viaggio: mostrarvi il luogo che sarebbe un elopement perfetto, spiegarvi come funziona la parte legale in Italia e Austria e consegnarvi un piano per dopo senza alcuna pressione ora. La proposta è l'inizio della storia; a volte ci tocca fotografarla tutta.",
  'A first kiss as she shows the new ring to the camera': 'Un primo bacio mentre lei mostra il nuovo anello alla fotocamera',
  'What it is': "Cos'è",
  'How we pull it off': 'Come lo realizziamo',
  'Choosing the moment': 'Scegliere il momento',
  'Keeping the secret': 'Mantenere il segreto',
  'Where to do it': 'Dove farlo',
  'The ring': "L'anello",
  'Weather & Plan B': 'Meteo e piano B',
  'When to go': 'Quando andare',
  'Getting there': 'Come arrivare',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'Mountain proposal FAQ': 'Domande frequenti sulla proposta in montagna',
  'A proposal in the mountains is equal parts logistics and nerve. Get it right and you have the best surprise of your life in the best light on earth &mdash; the question asked with a whole range of peaks as your witness, and every second of it quietly photographed. This is everything we have learned helping people propose in the Dolomites and the wider Alps: how to keep the secret, where to kneel, how to read the weather, and what happens after the yes.': "Una proposta in montagna è logistica e nervi in parti uguali. Se la fate bene, avete la sorpresa più bella della vita nella luce più bella della terra &mdash; la domanda posta con un'intera catena di cime come testimone, e ogni secondo fotografato in silenzio. Questo è tutto ciò che abbiamo imparato aiutando le persone a fare la proposta nelle Dolomiti e nelle Alpi in generale: come mantenere il segreto, dove inginocchiarsi, come leggere il meteo e cosa succede dopo il sì.",
  'On this page': 'In questa pagina',
}
PROP_FAQ_ES = {
  'How far ahead should we plan a mountain proposal?': ('¿Con cuánta antelación deberíamos planear una pedida en la montaña?', 'De dos a ocho semanas está bien. Necesitamos tiempo suficiente para elegir el lugar, vigilar la previsión y guardar una mañana de reserva, pero las pedidas son ágiles &mdash; hemos montado algunas preciosas con una semana de aviso cuando el tiempo acompañó.'),
  'How do you photograph it without giving it away?': ('¿Cómo lo fotografiáis sin que se note?', 'Lo planeamos todo por mensaje con la persona que propone, llegamos temprano y pasamos por senderistas normales, y luego fotografiamos de lejos con un teleobjetivo. Vuestra pareja suele darse cuenta de que había un fotógrafo solo tras el sí &mdash; que es cuando entramos para una sesión en condiciones.'),
  'Where is the easiest place to propose in the Dolomites?': ('¿Cuál es el lugar más fácil para una pedida en los Dolomitas?', "Un lago junto a la carretera o un mirador de teleférico, porque ninguno necesita una caminata larga que delate la sorpresa. El Lago di Braies y el pequeño Lago d'Antorno son favoritos con la primera luz; también el prado del Alpe di Siusi y la Nordkette sobre Innsbruck. Ajustamos el lugar a vuestra forma, la estación y la luz."),
  'What if the weather is bad?': ('¿Y si hace mal tiempo?', 'El tiempo de montaña cambia rápido, así que siempre mantenemos un lugar de reserva y una mañana extra. Las nubes bajas y algo de lluvia tampoco son el enemigo &mdash; algunas de las imágenes de pedida más atmosféricas que hemos hecho ocurrieron justo con esa luz suave y dramática.'),
  'Can we turn the proposal into a full session?': ('¿Podemos convertir la pedida en una sesión completa?', 'Sí, y la mayoría de las parejas lo hace. Tras el sí seguimos fotografiando una sesión de pareja relajada para celebrarlo, y podemos enviaros unas imágenes el mismo día para compartir con la familia. Muchas parejas vuelven luego a nosotros para fotografiar la boda misma.'),
  'Is a sunrise proposal really worth the early start?': ('¿Merece la pena madrugar para una pedida al amanecer?', 'Casi siempre. La primera luz os da miradores vacíos, color suave y la montaña casi para vosotros &mdash; el mismo lugar a mediodía puede estar lleno y duro de luz. Del timing nos ocupamos nosotros; vosotros solo ponéis la alarma.'),
}
PROP_FAQ_IT = {
  'How far ahead should we plan a mountain proposal?': ('Con quanto anticipo dovremmo pianificare una proposta in montagna?', 'Da due a otto settimane va bene. Ci serve tempo a sufficienza per scegliere il luogo, seguire le previsioni e tenere una mattina di riserva, ma le proposte sono agili &mdash; ne abbiamo organizzate di bellissime con una settimana di preavviso quando il meteo si è allineato.'),
  'How do you photograph it without giving it away?': ('Come la fotografate senza farla scoprire?', "Pianifichiamo tutto via messaggio con la persona che propone, arriviamo presto e passiamo per escursionisti normali, poi fotografiamo dalla distanza con un teleobiettivo. Il vostro partner di solito si accorge che c'era un fotografo solo dopo il sì &mdash; ed è allora che entriamo per un servizio come si deve."),
  'Where is the easiest place to propose in the Dolomites?': ('Qual è il luogo più facile per una proposta nelle Dolomiti?', "Un lago sul ciglio della strada o un punto panoramico con funivia, perché nessuno dei due richiede una lunga camminata che tradisce la sorpresa. Il Lago di Braies e il piccolo Lago d'Antorno sono favoriti alla prima luce; così l'Alpe di Siusi e la Nordkette sopra Innsbruck. Adattiamo il luogo alla vostra forma, alla stagione e alla luce."),
  'What if the weather is bad?': ('E se il tempo è brutto?', "Il meteo di montagna cambia in fretta, quindi teniamo sempre un luogo di riserva e una mattina in più. Nubi basse e un po' di pioggia non sono nemmeno il nemico &mdash; alcune delle immagini di proposta più suggestive che abbiamo fatto sono nate proprio con quella luce morbida e drammatica."),
  'Can we turn the proposal into a full session?': ('Possiamo trasformare la proposta in un servizio completo?', 'Sì, e la maggior parte delle coppie lo fa. Dopo il sì continuiamo a fotografare un rilassato servizio di coppia per festeggiare, e possiamo inviarvi qualche immagine lo stesso giorno da condividere con la famiglia. Molte coppie tornano poi da noi per fotografare il matrimonio stesso.'),
  'Is a sunrise proposal really worth the early start?': ("Vale davvero la pena alzarsi presto per una proposta all'alba?", 'Quasi sempre. La prima luce vi dà punti panoramici vuoti, colore morbido e la montagna quasi per voi &mdash; lo stesso luogo a mezzogiorno può essere affollato e duro. Del timing ci occupiamo noi; voi mettete solo la sveglia.'),
}

def build_proposal_guide(lang):
    slug='mountain-proposal-guide'
    g=next(x for x in GUIDES if x['slug']==slug); ex=GUIDE_EXTRA[slug]
    rel='how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/'+slug+'/'; P=prefix(lang,rel)
    DE=(lang=='de')
    def L(en,de):
        if lang=='de': return de
        if lang=='es': return PROP_ES.get(en,en)
        if lang=='it': return PROP_IT.get(en,en)
        return en
    def FQ(qen,aen,qde,ade):
        if lang=='de': return (qde,ade)
        if lang=='es': return PROP_FAQ_ES.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        if lang=='it': return PROP_FAQ_IT.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        return (qen,aen)
    GI=f'{P}img/guide-mountain-proposal/'; GIREL='img/guide-mountain-proposal/'; HERO_IMG='img/guide-mountain-proposal/p-cadini-kneel.webp'
    H2S='font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,3vw,36px);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:1.7em 0 .4em;scroll-margin-top:96px'
    def h2(i,en,de): return f'<h2 id="{i}" style="{H2S}">{L(en,de)}</h2>'
    def p(en,de): return f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2)">{L(en,de)}</p>'
    def fig(name,en,de): return '<figure class="guide-fig">'+bild(P,GIREL+name,L(en,de),sizes='(max-width:820px) 100vw, 820px')+'</figure>'
    toc=[('what',L('What it is','Worum es geht')),('how',L('How we pull it off','So gelingt es')),
         ('moment',L('Choosing the moment','Den Moment wählen')),('secret',L('Keeping the secret','Das Geheimnis wahren')),
         ('spots',L('Where to do it','Wo ihr es macht')),('ring',L('The ring','Der Ring')),
         ('weather',L('Weather & Plan B','Wetter & Plan B')),('season',L('When to go','Wann')),('wear',L('What to wear','Was anziehen')),
         ('getting-there',L('Getting there','Anreise')),('crowds',L('Beating the crowds','Den Massen entkommen')),
         ('after',L('After the yes','Nach dem Ja')),('elope',L('From proposal to wedding','Vom Antrag zur Hochzeit')),('faq',L('FAQ','FAQ'))]
    toc_html=('<nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'"><div class="cap">'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'</div><ol>'
      +''.join(f'<li><a href="#{i}">{lbl}</a></li>' for i,lbl in toc)+'</ol></nav>')
    facts='<div class="facts">'+''.join(f'<div class="fct"><div class="fl">{LBL[k][lang]}</div><div class="fv">{val[lang]}</div></div>' for k,val in ex['facts'])+'</div>'
    C=[]
    C.append(f'<p class="lead">{L("A proposal in the mountains is equal parts logistics and nerve. Get it right and you have the best surprise of your life in the best light on earth &mdash; the question asked with a whole range of peaks as your witness, and every second of it quietly photographed. This is everything we have learned helping people propose in the Dolomites and the wider Alps: how to keep the secret, where to kneel, how to read the weather, and what happens after the yes.","Ein Antrag in den Bergen ist Logistik und Nerven zugleich. Macht ihr es richtig, habt ihr die beste Überraschung eures Lebens im schönsten Licht der Welt &mdash; die Frage gestellt mit einem ganzen Gipfelkranz als Zeuge, und jede Sekunde davon leise fotografiert. Hier steht alles, was wir beim Begleiten von Anträgen in den Dolomiten und den weiteren Alpen gelernt haben: wie ihr das Geheimnis wahrt, wo ihr niederkniet, wie ihr das Wetter lest, und was nach dem Ja passiert.")}</p>')
    C.append(f'<p style="margin:.1em 0 1.3em"><a href="{u(P,lang,"dolomites-proposal/")}" class="arrow-link">{L("Ready to book a surprise proposal shoot","Bereit, ein Überraschungs-Antragsshooting zu buchen")} &rarr;</a></p>')
    C.append(f'<div class="cap" style="margin:0 0 -14px">{t(lang,"quick_facts")}</div>{facts}')
    C.append(toc_html)

    C.append(h2('what','What a mountain proposal really is','Was ein Bergantrag wirklich ist'))
    C.append(p("A mountain proposal is a small, precise piece of theatre: one person knows the plan, the other has no idea, and a photographer is hidden in plain sight to catch the moment it all lands. The setting does half the work &mdash; a lakeshore at first light, a viewpoint above the clouds, a meadow under jagged peaks &mdash; but the magic is the surprise, and protecting it is our whole job until you kneel. After that it turns into a celebration, and we keep photographing while you float.","Ein Bergantrag ist ein kleines, präzises Stück Theater: Eine Person kennt den Plan, die andere ahnt nichts, und ein Fotograf ist unsichtbar in Sichtweite, um den Moment zu fangen, in dem alles zusammenkommt. Der Ort erledigt die halbe Arbeit &mdash; ein Seeufer bei erstem Licht, eine Aussicht über den Wolken, eine Wiese unter schroffen Gipfeln &mdash;, doch der Zauber ist die Überraschung, und sie zu schützen ist bis zum Kniefall unsere ganze Aufgabe. Danach wird es eine Feier, und wir fotografieren weiter, während ihr schwebt."))
    C.append(fig('p-lago-braies.webp',"A proposal on the Lago di Braies boardwalk among the wooden boats","Ein Antrag auf dem Steg am Pragser Wildsee zwischen den Holzbooten"))
    C.append(p("Couples come to us for it from all over &mdash; some already live for the mountains, some just want somewhere that will never feel ordinary to remember. It works for the fit and the not-so-fit, in deep summer and deep snow, at a lake you can drive to or a summit you have to earn. Whatever you picture, the shape is the same: a quiet approach, a natural pause, the question, and then the loudest, happiest hour of your trip.","Paare kommen von überall dafür zu uns &mdash; manche leben ohnehin für die Berge, manche wollen einfach einen Ort, der nie gewöhnlich wirken wird. Es funktioniert für Sportliche und weniger Sportliche, im Hochsommer und im tiefen Schnee, an einem See, zu dem man fahren kann, oder auf einem Gipfel, den man sich verdienen muss. Was auch immer ihr euch vorstellt &mdash; der Ablauf ist gleich: ein leiser Zustieg, eine natürliche Pause, die Frage, und dann die lauteste, glücklichste Stunde eurer Reise."))
    C.append(fig('p-foreheads.webp',"Foreheads together after the yes, the new ring visible","Stirn an Stirn nach dem Ja, der neue Ring sichtbar"))

    C.append(h2('how','How we pull off the surprise, step by step','So gelingt die Überraschung, Schritt für Schritt'))
    C.append(p("<strong>1. First message.</strong> Everything runs through the person planning it &mdash; never a shared chat. We learn the story, the fitness level and the vibe. <strong>2. Spot &amp; time.</strong> We pick a location that gives a natural reason to pause and the best light, usually sunrise. <strong>3. The cover story.</strong> We agree on a believable reason to be up there early &mdash; \"a sunrise hike,\" \"a photographer friend meeting us.\" <strong>4. The signal.</strong> You give us a small, invisible cue &mdash; a hand on the back, taking off a hat &mdash; so we know the second is coming. <strong>5. From a distance.</strong> We shoot long, quiet and unnoticed. <strong>6. The reveal.</strong> After the yes we walk over, introduce ourselves properly, and turn it into a relaxed couples session.","<strong>1. Erste Nachricht.</strong> Alles läuft über die planende Person &mdash; nie ein gemeinsamer Chat. Wir lernen die Geschichte, das Fitnesslevel und die Stimmung kennen. <strong>2. Ort &amp; Zeit.</strong> Wir wählen einen Ort mit natürlichem Grund für eine Pause und dem besten Licht, meist Sonnenaufgang. <strong>3. Die Tarngeschichte.</strong> Wir vereinbaren einen glaubhaften Grund, früh oben zu sein &mdash; „eine Sonnenaufgangswanderung“, „ein Fotografen-Freund trifft uns“. <strong>4. Das Signal.</strong> Ihr gebt uns einen kleinen, unsichtbaren Hinweis &mdash; eine Hand am Rücken, das Absetzen einer Mütze &mdash;, damit wir wissen, dass es gleich soweit ist. <strong>5. Aus der Distanz.</strong> Wir fotografieren mit langer Brennweite, leise und unbemerkt. <strong>6. Die Auflösung.</strong> Nach dem Ja kommen wir herüber, stellen uns richtig vor und machen ein entspanntes Paar-Shooting daraus."))
    C.append(fig('p-reaction.webp',"Hands to her face in the first second of surprise","Hände vors Gesicht in der ersten Sekunde der Überraschung"))

    C.append(h2('moment','Choosing the moment &amp; the light','Den Moment und das Licht wählen'))
    C.append(p("First light is our favourite, and not only for the colour. At sunrise the viewpoints are empty, the air is still, and the person being surprised has no crowd to feel self-conscious in front of. We look for a spot with a built-in reason to stop &mdash; a railing, a bench, a summit cross, the end of a jetty &mdash; so that pausing there feels like the most natural thing in the world rather than a staged halt. Then we let the place do the talking.","Das erste Licht ist unser Favorit, und nicht nur wegen der Farbe. Bei Sonnenaufgang sind die Aussichtspunkte leer, die Luft ist ruhig, und die überraschte Person hat kein Publikum, vor dem sie sich befangen fühlt. Wir suchen einen Ort mit eingebautem Grund zum Anhalten &mdash; ein Geländer, eine Bank, ein Gipfelkreuz, das Ende eines Stegs &mdash;, damit das Innehalten das Natürlichste der Welt wirkt und kein inszeniertes Stoppen. Dann lassen wir den Ort sprechen."))
    C.append(fig('05-antrag-kniefall-im-schnee.webp',"Kneeling in the snow at sunrise, backlit by first light","Der Kniefall im Schnee bei Sonnenaufgang, vom ersten Licht durchleuchtet"))
    C.append(p("Golden hour in the evening works too, and is kinder to non-morning people &mdash; but it is busier, so we choose the spot more carefully. Exact times swing by nearly three hours across the year, so the plan always starts with your date: in high summer the sun clears the peaks around 05:15&ndash;06:00 and sets near 21:00, in spring and autumn sunrise falls between about 06:00 and 07:30, and in winter it is a civilised 07:45&ndash;08:00 with the light gone again by 16:30&ndash;17:15.","Auch die goldene Stunde am Abend funktioniert und ist freundlicher zu Morgenmuffeln &mdash; aber es ist voller, also wählen wir den Ort sorgfältiger. Die genauen Zeiten schwanken übers Jahr um fast drei Stunden, deshalb beginnt der Plan immer mit eurem Datum: im Hochsommer steigt die Sonne gegen 05:15&ndash;06:00 Uhr über die Gipfel und geht erst gegen 21:00 Uhr unter, in Frühling und Herbst liegt der Sonnenaufgang etwa zwischen 06:00 und 07:30 Uhr, und im Winter ist er zivilisierte 07:45&ndash;08:00 Uhr, während das Licht schon gegen 16:30&ndash;17:15 Uhr wieder weg ist."))
    C.append(fig('p-seiseralm-kneel.webp',"Kneeling to propose on the Alpe di Siusi, the Sassolungo behind","Der Kniefall auf der Seiser Alm, der Langkofel dahinter"))

    C.append(h2('secret','Keeping it a secret','Das Geheimnis wahren'))
    C.append(p("The whole plan lives in one thread between us and the person proposing &mdash; we never message you both, and we never tag the location. On the morning we are simply there first, cameras looking like they are pointed at the mountains, not at you. A long lens lets us stand far enough away that we read as another early hiker with a tripod. The only people who ever spot us are the ones already in on it. That distance is also why the photos feel so unguarded: nobody is performing for a camera they can see.","Der ganze Plan lebt in einem einzigen Nachrichtenstrang zwischen uns und der antragenden Person &mdash; wir schreiben nie euch beiden, und wir markieren nie den Ort. Am Morgen sind wir einfach zuerst da, die Kameras scheinbar auf die Berge gerichtet, nicht auf euch. Ein Teleobjektiv lässt uns weit genug entfernt stehen, dass wir wie ein weiterer früher Wanderer mit Stativ wirken. Die Einzigen, die uns je bemerken, sind die Eingeweihten. Diese Distanz ist auch der Grund, warum die Bilder so unbefangen sind: Niemand spielt für eine Kamera, die er sieht."))
    C.append(fig('p-kneel-spires.webp',"Kneeling to propose beneath jagged Dolomite spires, shot from a distance","Der Kniefall unter schroffen Dolomitentürmen, aus der Distanz fotografiert"))

    C.append(p("Often there are accomplices. A friend who suggests the sunrise walk, a parent kept in the loop for the phone call afterwards, a hotel that lets us in early &mdash; we coordinate all of it quietly so the story holds together. And if your partner is the suspicious type, we lean into the cover: we are happy to be introduced as friends of a friend who just happen to love photographing mountains at dawn. The more ordinary we seem, the bigger the surprise lands.","Oft gibt es Mitwisser. Eine Freundin, die die Sonnenaufgangswanderung vorschl\u00e4gt, ein Elternteil, das f\u00fcr den Anruf danach eingeweiht ist, ein Hotel, das uns fr\u00fch hineinl\u00e4sst &mdash; wir stimmen das alles leise ab, damit die Geschichte tr\u00e4gt. Und ist euer Gegen\u00fcber der misstrauische Typ, spielen wir die Tarnung aus: Wir lassen uns gern als Freunde eines Freundes vorstellen, die zuf\u00e4llig Berge im Morgengrauen fotografieren. Je gew\u00f6hnlicher wir wirken, desto gr\u00f6\u00dfer die \u00dcberraschung."))
    C.append(h2('spots','Where to do it: lakes, viewpoints &amp; meadows','Wo ihr es macht: Seen, Aussichten &amp; Wiesen'))
    C.append(p("The best proposal spots share one thing: a natural reason to pause and little effort to get there &mdash; a long, sweaty hike tends to give the game away. <strong>Roadside lakes</strong> are perfect. The Lago di Braies boardwalk or little Lago d'Antorno give you a railing and a mirror of water before anyone arrives. <strong>Cable-car viewpoints</strong> are just as easy &mdash; Sass Pordoi's terrace, or the Nordkette minutes above Innsbruck &mdash; but the lifts open well after sunrise &mdash; the Nordkette runs its first car around 08:00 and the Seceda not until about 08:30 &mdash; so for a true first-light proposal these are daytime or golden-hour spots unless you stay overnight on the mountain or walk up. Where a cable car is part of the plan, we build the morning around the timetable.","Die besten Antragsorte teilen eines: einen natürlichen Grund für eine Pause und wenig Aufwand beim Hinkommen &mdash; eine lange, schweißtreibende Wanderung verrät oft alles. <strong>Seen am Straßenrand</strong> sind perfekt. Der Steg am Pragser Wildsee oder der kleine Lago d'Antorno schenken euch ein Geländer und einen Wasserspiegel, ehe jemand kommt. <strong>Bergbahn-Aussichten</strong> sind ebenso bequem &mdash; die Terrasse des Sass Pordoi oder die Nordkette wenige Minuten über Innsbruck &mdash;, doch die Bahnen öffnen deutlich nach Sonnenaufgang &mdash; die Nordkette fährt die erste Gondel gegen 08:00 Uhr, die Seceda erst gegen 08:30 Uhr &mdash;, für einen echten Erstlicht-Antrag sind das also eher Tages- oder Golden-Hour-Orte, außer ihr übernachtet oben oder steigt zu Fuß auf. Wo eine Bahn zum Plan gehört, bauen wir den Morgen nach dem Fahrplan."))
    C.append(fig('p-seiseralm-dance.webp',"Dancing on the Alpe di Siusi meadow, the Sassolungo behind","Tanz auf der Seiser Alm, der Langkofel dahinter"))
    C.append(p("<strong>Open meadows</strong> like the Alpe di Siusi give you space, soft grass and the great tooth of the Sassolungo as a backdrop &mdash; gentle underfoot and endlessly photogenic. And if you do want a <strong>summit</strong>, we pick one with a short walk from a lift or a road, so the effort never signals what is coming. We match the spot to your fitness, the season and the light, and we always scout a second option in case the first is busy or socked in.","<strong>Offene Wiesen</strong> wie die Seiser Alm schenken euch Raum, weiches Gras und den großen Zahn des Langkofels als Kulisse &mdash; sanft unter den Füßen und endlos fotogen. Und wenn ihr doch einen <strong>Gipfel</strong> wollt, wählen wir einen mit kurzem Weg von Bahn oder Straße, damit die Anstrengung nie verrät, was kommt. Wir stimmen den Ort auf Fitness, Saison und Licht ab und suchen immer eine zweite Option aus, falls die erste voll oder zugezogen ist."))
    C.append(fig('01-antrag-nordkette-seilbahn-blick.webp',"The Nordkette cable car rising over a snowy forest above Innsbruck","Die Nordkettenbahn steigt über verschneitem Wald über Innsbruck"))

    C.append(h2('ring','The ring &amp; the reveal','Der Ring &amp; die Auflösung'))
    C.append(p("Carry the ring somewhere zipped and secure on the walk up &mdash; a closed pocket, not a coat you might hand over or a bag you might set down. If you are nervous about the box being spotted, take it out of the box and keep it loose in a small pouch; a bulky box is the classic tell. Tell us if you want a specific hand or angle for the moment, and we will position ourselves for it without ever crowding you.","Tragt den Ring auf dem Weg nach oben in etwas Verschlossenem, Sicherem &mdash; einer zugezogenen Tasche, nicht in einer Jacke, die ihr weggebt, oder einem Beutel, den ihr absetzt. Wenn ihr fürchtet, die Schachtel könnte auffallen, nehmt den Ring heraus und tragt ihn lose in einem kleinen Säckchen; eine klobige Schachtel ist der klassische Verräter. Sagt uns, ob ihr eine bestimmte Hand oder einen Winkel für den Moment wollt, und wir positionieren uns dafür, ohne euch je zu bedrängen."))
    C.append(fig('p-ring-detail.webp',"A close-up of the new engagement ring in warm light","Nahaufnahme des neuen Verlobungsrings im warmen Licht"))
    C.append(p("Once the yes is out, the ring becomes its own little series &mdash; the hand on a chest, the first look down at it, the shot against the peaks. These are the frames families zoom into, so we take a couple of minutes for them while you are still glowing, then let you go back to being giddy.","Ist das Ja erst raus, wird der Ring zu einer eigenen kleinen Serie &mdash; die Hand auf der Brust, der erste Blick darauf, das Bild vor den Gipfeln. Das sind die Aufnahmen, in die Familien hineinzoomen, deshalb nehmen wir uns ein paar Minuten dafür, solange ihr noch strahlt, und lassen euch dann wieder einfach selig sein."))
    C.append(fig('p-ring-embrace.webp',"The new ring resting on his shoulder during an embrace","Der neue Ring auf seiner Schulter während einer Umarmung"))

    C.append(h2('weather','Weather &amp; a Plan B','Wetter &amp; ein Plan B'))
    C.append(p("Mountain weather turns fast, so a proposal plan is never a single point &mdash; it is a window. We watch the forecast in the days before, hold a backup spot that works in worse light, and keep a spare morning where we can. If your first choice is fogged in, we move; if it clears an hour late, we wait. And do not fear a grey sky: low cloud drifting through the peaks, or a little rain on a lake, gives some of the most cinematic, tender frames we ever take. The only weather we truly avoid is the unsafe kind.","Bergwetter kippt schnell, deshalb ist ein Antragsplan nie ein einzelner Punkt &mdash; er ist ein Fenster. Wir beobachten die Vorhersage in den Tagen davor, halten einen Ausweichort bereit, der bei schlechterem Licht funktioniert, und, wo möglich, einen Reservemorgen. Ist eure erste Wahl im Nebel, ziehen wir um; klart es eine Stunde später auf, warten wir. Und fürchtet den grauen Himmel nicht: tiefe Wolken, die durch die Gipfel treiben, oder etwas Regen an einem See schenken einige der filmreifsten, zärtlichsten Bilder, die wir je machen. Das einzige Wetter, das wir wirklich meiden, ist das unsichere."))
    C.append(fig('p-kiss-sky.webp',"A kiss under a moody, dramatic Dolomite sky","Ein Kuss unter einem dramatischen Dolomitenhimmel"))

    C.append(p("This is why we never sell a proposal as a single fixed slot. We build in a little give &mdash; an earlier alarm than strictly needed, a second spot ten minutes away, a backup morning if your trip allows it. Nine times out of ten the first plan works perfectly; the tenth time, that flexibility is the difference between a soggy compromise and a morning you could not have dreamed up. Nervous energy is enough to carry on the day &mdash; the weather is our job to worry about, not yours.","Deshalb verkaufen wir einen Antrag nie als einen einzigen fixen Termin. Wir bauen etwas Spielraum ein &mdash; einen fr\u00fcheren Wecker als n\u00f6tig, einen zweiten Ort zehn Minuten entfernt, einen Reservemorgen, wenn eure Reise es zul\u00e4sst. Neun von zehn Malen klappt der erste Plan perfekt; beim zehnten Mal ist genau dieser Spielraum der Unterschied zwischen einem nassen Kompromiss und einem Morgen, den ihr euch nicht h\u00e4ttet ausdenken k\u00f6nnen. Nerv\u00f6se Energie reicht f\u00fcr den Tag &mdash; ums Wetter k\u00fcmmern wir uns, nicht ihr."))
    C.append(h2('season','When to go: snow or meadows','Wann: Schnee oder Wiesen'))
    C.append(p("A proposal works year-round, and the season changes the whole feeling. <strong>Summer</strong> gives you green meadows, cotton grass and long light &mdash; the easiest logistics and the warmest mornings. <strong>Autumn</strong> brings larches turning gold and the first quiet after the crowds. <strong>Winter</strong> is our secret favourite: snow to the horizon, a hush over everything, and a kneel in fresh powder that looks like the inside of a snow globe &mdash; you just need warm layers and good boots. We help you pick the season that matches the picture in your head, then build the morning around it.","Ein Antrag funktioniert das ganze Jahr, und die Saison verändert das ganze Gefühl. <strong>Sommer</strong> schenkt grüne Wiesen, Wollgras und langes Licht &mdash; die einfachste Logistik und die wärmsten Morgen. <strong>Herbst</strong> bringt goldene Lärchen und die erste Ruhe nach dem Andrang. <strong>Winter</strong> ist unser heimlicher Favorit: Schnee bis zum Horizont, eine Stille über allem und ein Kniefall im frischen Pulver, der aussieht wie das Innere einer Schneekugel &mdash; ihr braucht nur warme Schichten und gute Schuhe. Wir helfen euch, die Saison zum Bild in eurem Kopf zu wählen, und bauen den Morgen darum."))
    C.append(fig('04-antrag-ankunft-bergstation.webp',"Arriving at a snowy mountain station in winter light","Ankunft an einer verschneiten Bergstation im Winterlicht"))

    C.append(h2('wear','What to wear','Was ihr anzieht'))
    C.append(p("Dress like the best version of a normal day out &mdash; nice enough that you will love the photos, plausible enough that it does not tip your partner off. Solid, muted colours read beautifully against rock and snow; busy logos and neon do not. Bring warm layers you can peel for the frames and pull back on between them, and real shoes for the ground you will actually be standing on. If it is a surprise, the person being proposed to should just be told \"we're doing sunrise photos, wear something you feel good in\" &mdash; enough to look lovely, not enough to guess.","Zieht euch an wie die beste Version eines normalen Ausflugs &mdash; schön genug, dass ihr die Bilder liebt, plausibel genug, dass es euer Gegenüber nicht misstrauisch macht. Ruhige, gedeckte Farben wirken wunderbar vor Fels und Schnee; wilde Logos und Neon nicht. Nehmt warme Schichten mit, die ihr für die Bilder ablegt und dazwischen wieder anzieht, und echte Schuhe für den Boden, auf dem ihr wirklich steht. Ist es eine Überraschung, sagt der überraschten Person einfach: „Wir machen Sonnenaufgangsfotos, zieh etwas an, in dem du dich wohlfühlst“ &mdash; genug, um schön auszusehen, nicht genug, um es zu erraten."))
    C.append(fig('p-seiseralm-glow.webp',"Sitting together in the cotton grass as the peaks glow at last light","Gemeinsam im Wollgras, während die Gipfel im letzten Licht glühen"))

    C.append(p("A few small things make a big difference in the pictures. Loose hair moves beautifully in a summit breeze, so skip the tight updo unless you love it. Bring a warm layer you can hide until the walk down, and think about your hands &mdash; they are the stars of every ring photo, so a little care there pays off. And whatever you wear, wear it in beforehand: new boots on a cold dawn are the one thing guaranteed to distract from the moment.","Ein paar Kleinigkeiten machen in den Bildern viel aus. Offenes Haar bewegt sich wunderbar in einer Gipfelbrise, spart euch also den strengen Dutt, au\u00dfer ihr liebt ihn. Nehmt eine warme Schicht mit, die ihr bis zum Abstieg verstecken k\u00f6nnt, und denkt an eure H\u00e4nde &mdash; sie sind die Stars jedes Ringfotos, ein wenig Pflege lohnt sich dort. Und was ihr auch tragt, tragt es vorher ein: neue Schuhe an einem kalten Morgen sind das Einzige, das garantiert vom Moment ablenkt."))
    C.append(h2('getting-there','Getting there &amp; the logistics','Anreise &amp; Logistik'))
    C.append(p("Most couples fly into Venice, Verona or Innsbruck and drive the last stretch &mdash; roughly two to three hours to the heart of the Dolomites, and Innsbruck is right at the foot of the Nordkette. Where cable cars are part of the plan, the first departure sets the morning: many lifts open only after sunrise, so a true first-light proposal often means a roadside lake or a spot you can reach on foot instead. We tell you exactly where to be, when, and how to get there, and can meet you at the trailhead so you are never navigating on the big morning.","Die meisten Paare fliegen nach Venedig, Verona oder Innsbruck und fahren das letzte Stück &mdash; etwa zwei bis drei Stunden ins Herz der Dolomiten, und Innsbruck liegt direkt am Fuß der Nordkette. Wo Bergbahnen zum Plan gehören, gibt die erste Fahrt den Morgen vor: Viele Bahnen öffnen erst nach Sonnenaufgang, ein echter Erstlicht-Antrag heißt daher oft ein Straßensee oder ein zu Fuß erreichbarer Ort. Wir sagen euch genau, wo ihr wann sein müsst und wie ihr hinkommt, und treffen euch am Ausgangspunkt, damit ihr am großen Morgen nie navigieren müsst."))
    C.append(fig('03-antrag-wegweiser-hafelekar.webp',"A signpost at the Hafelekar station high above Innsbruck","Ein Wegweiser an der Station Hafelekar hoch über Innsbruck"))

    C.append(h2('crowds','Beating the crowds','Den Massen entkommen'))
    C.append(p("The famous spots fill up &mdash; Braies in particular is a different place at 06:00 than at 11:00. First light is the cleanest way past that: you get the railing, the reflection and the silence before the tour buses. Where driving access is limited we plan around it &mdash; the road to Lago di Braies, for example, needs an advance reservation from 09:00 to 16:00 between 1 July and 15 September, which is another reason we love being there for sunrise instead. Empty light is always the better light, and an empty viewpoint makes the surprise feel like it is yours alone.","Die berühmten Orte füllen sich &mdash; Braies ist um 06:00 Uhr ein anderer Ort als um 11:00 Uhr. Das erste Licht ist der sauberste Weg daran vorbei: Ihr habt das Geländer, die Spiegelung und die Stille vor den Reisebussen. Wo die Zufahrt begrenzt ist, planen wir darum herum &mdash; die Straße zum Pragser Wildsee etwa braucht von 09:00 bis 16:00 Uhr zwischen 1. Juli und 15. September eine Voranmeldung, ein weiterer Grund, warum wir lieber zum Sonnenaufgang dort sind. Leeres Licht ist immer das bessere Licht, und ein leerer Aussichtspunkt lässt die Überraschung wie euren ganz eigenen Moment wirken."))
    C.append(fig('02-antrag-seilbahn-schatten-im-schnee.webp',"The shadow of the cable-car cabin cast on the snow below","Der Schatten der Seilbahnkabine auf dem Schnee darunter"))

    C.append(p("It helps to think in half-hours. A viewpoint that is serene at 06:15 can have a queue for the same railing by 07:30, so we build the morning backwards from the light and stay a step ahead of the first arrivals. If a spot is simply too popular to guarantee privacy, we will say so and offer a quieter twin nearby &mdash; there is almost always a lesser-known ledge or shoreline with the same peaks behind it and none of the crowd in front.","Es hilft, in halben Stunden zu denken. Ein Aussichtspunkt, der um 06:15 Uhr still ist, kann um 07:30 Uhr eine Schlange am selben Gel\u00e4nder haben, deshalb bauen wir den Morgen vom Licht her r\u00fcckw\u00e4rts und bleiben den ersten Ankommenden einen Schritt voraus. Ist ein Ort schlicht zu beliebt, um Privatsph\u00e4re zu garantieren, sagen wir das und bieten einen ruhigeren Zwilling in der N\u00e4he &mdash; fast immer gibt es ein weniger bekanntes Felsband oder Ufer mit denselben Gipfeln dahinter und ohne die Menge davor."))
    C.append(h2('after','After the yes','Nach dem Ja'))
    C.append(p("The moment is over in seconds; the celebration is the rest of the morning. Once we have introduced ourselves properly, we keep shooting a relaxed couples session while you are still buzzing &mdash; the laughing, the disbelief, the first phone call home. This is when the pictures get loose and joyful, and it is often the part couples treasure most. We can turn a few images around the same day so you can share the news before you are even back down in the valley.","Der Moment ist in Sekunden vorbei; die Feier ist der Rest des Morgens. Sobald wir uns richtig vorgestellt haben, fotografieren wir ein entspanntes Paar-Shooting weiter, solange ihr noch vibriert &mdash; das Lachen, das Ungläubige, der erste Anruf nach Hause. Dann werden die Bilder locker und freudig, und oft ist genau das der Teil, den Paare am meisten schätzen. Ein paar Bilder liefern wir noch am selben Tag, damit ihr die Neuigkeit teilen könnt, ehe ihr überhaupt wieder im Tal seid."))
    C.append(fig('p-cadini-lift.webp',"He lifts her in joy, the Cadini spires behind","Er hebt sie vor Freude hoch, die Cadini-Türme dahinter"))
    C.append(p("Make a day of it, too. The Dolomites reward a slow morning after: a hut breakfast, a swim in a cold lake, a quiet drive through the passes while it all sinks in. Cortina, Val Gardena and the villages of the Alta Badia sit within an hour of everything, full of terraces made for exactly this kind of celebrating. We are happy to point you to the good ones.","Macht auch einen Tag daraus. Die Dolomiten belohnen einen langsamen Morgen danach: ein Hüttenfrühstück, ein Bad in einem kalten See, eine ruhige Fahrt über die Pässe, während alles ankommt. Cortina, Gröden und die Dörfer der Alta Badia liegen keine Stunde von allem entfernt, voller Terrassen wie gemacht für genau diese Art zu feiern. Wir zeigen euch gern die guten."))
    C.append(fig('13-antrag-laufen-im-abendlicht.webp',"The couple playing in the last evening light after the yes","Das Paar tollt im letzten Abendlicht nach dem Ja"))

    C.append(h2('elope','From proposal to wedding','Vom Antrag zur Hochzeit'))
    C.append(p("A surprising number of our couples propose here and then come back to marry here &mdash; the mountains that held the question turn out to be exactly where they want to say the vows. If that thought is already flickering, we can plant the seed on the same trip: show you the spot that would make a perfect elopement, talk through how the legal side works in Italy and Austria, and hand you a plan for later with zero pressure now. The proposal is the beginning of the story; sometimes we get to photograph the whole thing.","Erstaunlich viele unserer Paare machen hier den Antrag und kommen dann zum Heiraten zurück &mdash; die Berge, die die Frage hielten, sind genau dort, wo sie das Ja geben wollen. Flackert dieser Gedanke schon, können wir auf derselben Reise den Samen legen: euch den Ort zeigen, der ein perfektes Elopement abgäbe, durchsprechen, wie das Rechtliche in Italien und Österreich läuft, und euch einen Plan für später mitgeben &mdash; ganz ohne Druck jetzt. Der Antrag ist der Anfang der Geschichte; manchmal dürfen wir das Ganze fotografieren."))
    C.append(fig('p-kiss-ring.webp',"A first kiss as she shows the new ring to the camera","Ein erster Kuss, während sie den neuen Ring zur Kamera zeigt"))

    faq_html='<h2 id="faq" style="'+H2S+'">'+L('Mountain proposal FAQ','FAQ zum Bergantrag')+'</h2>'
    FAQL=[FQ(*x) for x in PROP_FAQ]
    faq_html+=''.join('<div style="margin:1.3em 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:1.1em">'
      f'<h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:20px;margin:0 0 .3em">{q}</h3>'
      f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2);margin:0">{a}</p></div>' for q,a in FAQL)
    faq_ld={"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
      {"@type":"Question","name":_plain(q),"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":_plain(a)}} for q,a in FAQL]}
    related=''.join(story_card(lang,P,STORYBY[sl]) for sl in ex['stories'])
    more=''.join(guide_card(lang,P,x) for x in GUIDES if x['slug']!=slug)
    body=(nav(lang,rel,'howto')+
      f'<section class="page-hero" style="padding:0">{herobg(P,HERO_IMG,g["title"][lang])}'
      f'<div class="content"><div class="wrap"><div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"guide_kick")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h1>{g["title"][lang]}</h1></div></div></section>'
      '<section><div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">'+''.join(C)+faq_html+
      f'<p style="margin-top:2.4em"><a href="{u(P,lang,"how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/")}" class="arrow-link">&larr; {T["nav"]["howto"][lang]}</a></p></div></section>'
      '<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"related_stories")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"related_stories")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{related}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="stories" style="padding-top:clamp(40px,6vw,80px)"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"more_guides")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"more_guides")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{more}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="cta"><div class="wrap row reveal"><div>'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"cta_k")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2 style="margin-top:20px">{t(lang,"cta_h")}</h2></div>'
      f'<a href="{u(P,lang,"get-in-touch/")}" class="btn light">{t(lang,"start_planning")}</a></div></section>'
      +footer(lang,rel))
    write(lang,rel,head(lang,rel,g['title'][lang]+' — Mountain Elopement',g['excerpt'][lang],ld_extra=faq_ld,pre=herolink(P,HERO_IMG))+body+scripts(P))

SUN_FAQ=[
 ("Sunrise or sunset — which is better for an elopement?",
  "Honestly, sunrise wins on light and solitude: empty peaks, pink alpenglow and a private ceremony no one else can crowd. Sunset wins on ease: no alarm, a relaxed walk up and warm light that lingers. If you can face the early start, take sunrise; if mornings are not your thing or you have guests, sunset is the reliable, beautiful choice.",
  "Sonnenaufgang oder Sonnenuntergang &mdash; was ist besser fürs Elopement?",
  "Ehrlich: Der Sonnenaufgang gewinnt bei Licht und Ruhe &mdash; leere Gipfel, rosa Alpenglühen und eine private Zeremonie, die niemand stören kann. Der Sonnenuntergang gewinnt bei der Bequemlichkeit: kein Wecker, ein entspannter Aufstieg und warmes Licht, das bleibt. Wenn ihr den frühen Start schafft, nehmt den Sonnenaufgang; sind Morgen nicht euer Ding oder habt ihr Gäste, ist der Sonnenuntergang die verlässliche, schöne Wahl."),
 ("How early do we have to get up for a sunrise elopement?",
  "It depends on the month and the walk &mdash; the alarm usually falls between 03:00 and 05:00, earlier in June, later in October. We scout the trail the day before and time the climb so you reach your spot with light to spare, and we carry the plan so all you have to do is get up.",
  "Wie früh müssen wir für ein Sonnenaufgangs-Elopement aufstehen?",
  "Das hängt vom Monat und vom Weg ab &mdash; der Wecker liegt meist zwischen 03:00 und 05:00 Uhr, früher im Juni, später im Oktober. Wir erkunden den Weg am Vortag und timen den Aufstieg so, dass ihr euren Ort mit Licht im Vorrat erreicht &mdash; und wir tragen den Plan, ihr müsst nur aufstehen."),
 ("Can we reach a ridge like the Seceda for sunrise by cable car?",
  "No. The first cabins run too late for dawn &mdash; the Seceda from around 08:30 and the Nordkette above Innsbruck from around 08:00 &mdash; so a true ridge sunrise means either a head-torch hike in the dark or a night in a mountain hut. Roadside spots and toll-road summits are the easier way to first light.",
  "Erreichen wir einen Grat wie die Seceda zum Sonnenaufgang mit der Bahn?",
  "Nein. Die ersten Gondeln fahren zu spät für den Morgen &mdash; die Seceda ab etwa 08:30 Uhr, die Nordkette über Innsbruck ab etwa 08:00 Uhr &mdash;, ein echter Grat-Sonnenaufgang heißt also entweder ein Stirnlampen-Aufstieg im Dunkeln oder eine Nacht in einer Berghütte. Orte am Straßenrand und Maut­straßen-Gipfel sind der leichtere Weg zum ersten Licht."),
 ("Is being up there in the dark difficult or unsafe?",
  "It is easier than it sounds when it is planned. We scout the trail in daylight first, bring spare head-torches and warm drinks, keep the group together and time everything with a buffer. For most couples the dark walk becomes one of the best parts of the day &mdash; quiet, close and full of anticipation.",
  "Ist es schwierig oder unsicher, im Dunkeln dort oben zu sein?",
  "Es ist leichter, als es klingt, wenn es geplant ist. Wir erkunden den Weg zuerst bei Tag, bringen Ersatz-Stirnlampen und warme Getränke mit, halten die Gruppe zusammen und timen alles mit Puffer. Für die meisten Paare wird der Weg im Dunkeln zu einem der schönsten Teile des Tages &mdash; still, nah und voller Vorfreude."),
 ("For a sunset elopement, how do we get down afterwards?",
  "That is the one thing to plan carefully. Where you have come up by cable car, we check the last descent to the minute and keep you ahead of it; where there is no late option, we simply book a rifugio so you can stay the night and skip the descent entirely. Either way we plan the way down as carefully as the way up.",
  "Wie kommen wir nach einem Sonnenuntergangs-Elopement wieder hinunter?",
  "Das ist die eine Sache, die man sorgfältig plant. Wo ihr per Seilbahn hochgekommen seid, prüfen wir die letzte Talfahrt auf die Minute und halten euch ihr voraus; wo es keine späte Option gibt, buchen wir einfach eine Hütte, damit ihr oben übernachtet und den Abstieg ganz auslasst. So oder so planen wir den Weg hinunter so sorgfältig wie den Weg hinauf."),
 ("When is the best month for the light?",
  "Every month has its trade-off. June has the warmest, longest days but the earliest alarm; September and October bring civilised sunrise times, cool clear air and far thinner crowds, with the bonus of golden larches. The table above has the numbers for each month, and we build your morning or evening around them.",
  "Welcher Monat hat das beste Licht?",
  "Jeder Monat hat seinen Kompromiss. Der Juni hat die wärmsten, längsten Tage, aber den frühesten Wecker; September und Oktober bringen zivilisierte Sonnenaufgangszeiten, kühle klare Luft und viel dünnere Menschenmengen &mdash; mit goldenen Lärchen als Zugabe. Die Tabelle oben hat die Zahlen für jeden Monat, und wir bauen euren Morgen oder Abend darum."),
]

# --- Sunrise/Sunset guide ES/IT translations (auto-generated, keyed by exact EN string) ---
SUN_ES = {
  'The two-day question': 'La cuestión de los dos días',
  'Think of it as choosing a character for the day. A sunrise elopement is quiet and a little heroic: you rise in the dark, climb by head-torch, and arrive as the first light sets the peaks on fire, often entirely alone. A sunset elopement is generous and relaxed: a slow afternoon walk, warm light that lingers for an hour, and a celebratory dinner waiting below. Everything downstream &mdash; how you dress, where you go, how many people you can bring &mdash; follows from that one decision, which is why we make it first.': 'Vedlo como elegir un carácter para el día. Un elopement al amanecer es silencioso y un poco heroico: os levantáis a oscuras, subís con frontal y llegáis cuando la primera luz prende las cumbres, a menudo completamente solos. Un elopement al atardecer es generoso y relajado: un paseo lento por la tarde, luz cálida que perdura una hora y una cena de celebración esperando abajo. Todo lo demás &mdash; cómo os vestís, adónde vais, cuánta gente podéis llevar &mdash; se deriva de esa única decisión, y por eso la tomamos primero.',
  'A couple kissing on a misty Dolomite ridge as a peak breaks the cloud': 'Una pareja besándose en una arista dolomítica entre la niebla mientras una cumbre rompe las nubes',
  'Sunrise: solitude &amp; soft light': 'Amanecer: soledad y luz suave',
  'A pre-dawn start is the closest thing we know to having the mountains to yourselves. The trailhead is empty, the air is sharp and still, and as the sun lifts, the rock turns from grey to rose to gold in a matter of minutes &mdash; the alpenglow that no filter can fake. There is a stillness at that hour that changes how people stand and speak; vows at sunrise come out softer and truer, because there is nobody within miles to perform for.': 'Salir antes del alba es lo más parecido que conocemos a tener las montañas para vosotros. El inicio del sendero está vacío, el aire es cortante y quieto, y cuando el sol asciende la roca pasa de gris a rosa a oro en cuestión de minutos &mdash; el alpenglow que ningún filtro puede fingir. Hay una quietud a esa hora que cambia cómo la gente se yergue y habla; los votos al amanecer salen más suaves y verdaderos, porque no hay nadie en kilómetros ante quien actuar.',
  'A backlit portrait as the rising sun flares between the couple': 'Un retrato a contraluz mientras el sol naciente destella entre la pareja',
  'It asks something of you: an alarm somewhere between 03:00 and 05:00 depending on the month, a walk in the dark, and warm layers for a summit that can sit near freezing even in July. We scout the trail the day before, walk it with you by head-torch, and time the climb so you are in position with light to spare. The reward is a version of the mountains almost no one sees &mdash; and photographs with a quality of light the middle of the day simply cannot give.': 'Os pide algo: una alarma en algún punto entre las 03:00 y las 05:00 según el mes, una caminata a oscuras y capas de abrigo para una cumbre que puede rozar el punto de congelación incluso en julio. Exploramos el sendero la víspera, lo recorremos con vosotros con frontal y calculamos la subida para que estéis en posición con luz de sobra. La recompensa es una versión de las montañas que casi nadie ve &mdash; y fotos con una calidad de luz que el mediodía sencillamente no puede dar.',
  'The bride ready with a head-torch before the dark climb': 'La novia lista con un frontal antes de la subida a oscuras',
  'Sunset: warm &amp; unhurried': 'Atardecer: cálido y sin prisa',
  'Sunset is the forgiving choice, and there is no shame in it &mdash; some of our most beautiful days end rather than begin in the light. There is no alarm; you get ready at a civilised hour, walk up in the afternoon, and let the light come to you. Golden hour in the mountains is long and generous, the warm side-light wrapping around faces and rock, and it slides into the fireshow of enrosadira, when the Dolomite walls glow ember-red for a few unrepeatable minutes.': 'El atardecer es la opción indulgente, y no hay vergüenza en ello &mdash; algunos de nuestros días más bellos terminan en la luz en vez de empezar en ella. No hay alarma; os preparáis a una hora civilizada, subís por la tarde y dejáis que la luz venga a vosotros. La hora dorada en la montaña es larga y generosa, la cálida luz lateral envolviendo rostros y roca, y se desliza hacia el espectáculo de fuego de la enrosadira, cuando las paredes dolomíticas brillan de un rojo brasa durante unos minutos irrepetibles.',
  'A sunset ceremony under a circular floral arch, the sun flaring through': 'Una ceremonia al atardecer bajo un arco floral circular, el sol destellando a través',
  'The trade-off is company. The good viewpoints that are empty at dawn can be busy at dusk, so we steer you to lesser-known ledges and meadows, or to spots where the crowd thins the moment the last cable car goes down. Sunset also runs on a hard clock in the other direction: the light fails fast, and you do not want to be finding the trail in the dark by accident. We plan the descent as carefully as the climb &mdash; or, on our favourite evenings, book a mountain hut so you never have to come down at all.': 'A cambio hay compañía. Los buenos miradores que están vacíos al alba pueden estar concurridos al ocaso, así que os llevamos a salientes y prados menos conocidos, o a lugares donde la gente se despeja en cuanto baja el último teleférico. El atardecer también corre contra el reloj en la otra dirección: la luz se apaga rápido, y no queréis andar buscando el sendero a oscuras por accidente. Planificamos la bajada con tanto cuidado como la subida &mdash; o, en nuestras tardes favoritas, reservamos un refugio de montaña para no tener que bajar en absoluto.',
  'The couple on a rock outcrop against the sunset mountains': 'La pareja sobre un saliente rocoso frente a las montañas al atardecer',
  'Which one is yours': '¿Cuál es el vuestro?',
  'So which is yours? Choose sunrise if the picture in your head is solitude &mdash; empty peaks, soft pink light, a private ceremony with nobody in the frame but you. Choose it, too, if you want the most dramatic locations at their quietest, or if summer heat and crowds put you off. Choose sunset if mornings are genuinely not your thing, if you are bringing a few guests who would struggle with a 4 a.m. start, or if you want the day to end in warmth and a dinner rather than begin in the cold. When couples truly cannot decide, we sometimes do both across two days &mdash; a sunset to settle in, a sunrise for the main event.': 'Entonces, ¿cuál es el vuestro? Elegid el amanecer si la imagen en vuestra cabeza es soledad &mdash; cumbres vacías, luz rosa suave, una ceremonia privada con nadie en el encuadre salvo vosotros. Elegidlo también si queréis los lugares más dramáticos en su versión más tranquila, o si el calor y las multitudes del verano os echan atrás. Elegid el atardecer si las mañanas no son lo vuestro, si lleváis a unos invitados a quienes costaría un inicio a las 4 de la mañana, o si queréis que el día termine en calidez y una cena en vez de empezar en el frío. Cuando una pareja de verdad no consigue decidir, a veces hacemos ambos en dos días &mdash; un atardecer para asentaros, un amanecer para el acto principal.',
  'It also comes down to temperament. Sunrise rewards the couple who love a shared mission &mdash; the alarm, the climb, the pay-off feel earned, and the day starts on a high that colours everything after. Sunset suits the couple who want to savour, not strive: a long lunch, an unhurried walk, and the whole thing melting into dinner. Neither is more romantic; they are romantic in different keys. Tell us which one sounds like you, and we will tell you honestly whether your dream location can deliver it.': 'También es cuestión de temperamento. El amanecer premia a la pareja que ama una misión compartida &mdash; la alarma, la subida, la recompensa se sienten ganadas, y el día empieza en un subidón que tiñe todo lo que viene después. El atardecer va con la pareja que quiere saborear, no esforzarse: una comida larga, un paseo sin prisa y todo fundiéndose en una cena. Ninguno es más romántico; son románticos en tonos distintos. Decidnos cuál suena a vosotros y os diremos con honestidad si vuestro lugar soñado puede ofrecerlo.',
  'The sun bursting over snow-dusted Dolomite peaks': 'El sol irrumpiendo sobre cumbres dolomíticas espolvoreadas de nieve',
  'Best spots for sunrise': 'Mejores lugares para el amanecer',
  'Dawn suits places you can reach before the machinery of the day starts. Lago di Braies is the classic: mirror-still and empty at first light, long before the crowds &mdash; note that from 1 July to 15 September the access road needs an advance reservation between 09:00 and 16:00, another reason we are there at sunrise instead. The Tre Cime di Lavaredo are reachable by the Auronzo toll road, which in summer (roughly late May to late October, season- and weather-dependent) is passable in the early hours, so you can drive up in the dark and be on the peaks for the first colour. The car toll is around &euro;40, and an advance online ticket may be required &mdash; we sort that out for you.': 'El alba va con lugares a los que llegáis antes de que arranque la maquinaria del día. El Lago di Braies es el clásico: espejado y vacío con la primera luz, mucho antes de las multitudes &mdash; tened en cuenta que del 1 de julio al 15 de septiembre la carretera de acceso necesita una reserva anticipada entre las 09:00 y las 16:00, otra razón por la que preferimos estar allí al amanecer. Las Tre Cime di Lavaredo se alcanzan por la carretera de peaje de Auronzo, que en verano (aproximadamente de finales de mayo a finales de octubre, según temporada y clima) es transitable a primera hora, así que podéis subir a oscuras y estar en las cumbres para el primer color. El peaje del coche ronda los 40&nbsp;&euro;, y puede requerirse un billete online anticipado &mdash; de eso nos ocupamos nosotros.',
  'Dawn on the Lago di Braies jetty, the water mirror-still': 'El alba en el pantalán del Lago di Braies, el agua como un espejo',
  'Ridgelines like the Seceda are the exception that proves the rule: the first cabin comes up around 08:30, far too late for dawn colour, so a true Seceda sunrise means either a head-torch hike in the dark or a night in a nearby rifugio. That sounds like a lot, and it is &mdash; but standing on that ridge as it turns pink, with the cable car still hours from its first run, is one of the great experiences these mountains offer. We only suggest it to couples who like the idea of earning it.': 'Las crestas como el Seceda son la excepción que confirma la regla: la primera cabina sube hacia las 08:30, demasiado tarde para el color del alba, así que un amanecer real en el Seceda implica o una subida con frontal a oscuras o una noche en un refugio cercano. Suena a mucho, y lo es &mdash; pero estar en esa cresta mientras se vuelve rosa, con el teleférico aún a horas de su primer viaje, es una de las grandes experiencias que ofrecen estas montañas. Solo se lo proponemos a las parejas a las que les gusta la idea de ganárselo.',
  'A group climbing in the dark by the beam of head-torches': 'Un grupo subiendo a oscuras al haz de los frontales',
  'Best spots for sunset': 'Mejores lugares para el atardecer',
  'Evening favours viewpoints you can reach by lift and leave in warmth &mdash; ideally ones where you can catch the last cabin down, or, better still, sleep at the top. The Sass Pordoi terrace, Lagazuoi with its cliff-edge refuge, the rolling Alpe di Siusi and the Nordkette right above Innsbruck all catch golden hour beautifully and empty out the moment the day-trippers head home. The single rule is to know your last descent: check the final cable-car time to the minute, and where there is no late option, we simply book the mountain hut and make a night of it.': 'La tarde favorece los miradores a los que llegáis en teleférico y dejáis en calidez &mdash; idealmente aquellos donde podéis coger la última cabina de bajada o, mejor aún, dormir arriba. La terraza del Sass Pordoi, el Lagazuoi con su refugio al borde del precipicio, el ondulante Alpe di Siusi y la Nordkette justo sobre Innsbruck captan la hora dorada de maravilla y se vacían en cuanto los excursionistas de día se van a casa. La única regla es conocer vuestra última bajada: comprobad la hora del último teleférico al minuto, y donde no hay opción tardía, simplemente reservamos el refugio de montaña y hacemos noche.',
  'The couple walking through snow with the low sun behind': 'La pareja caminando por la nieve con el sol bajo detrás',
  'Meadows deserve a special mention for sunset. Where a ridge can be windy and exposed as the temperature drops, the open pastures of the Alpe di Siusi or a quiet valley shoulder stay gentle underfoot and glow beautifully as the side-light rakes across the grass. They are easy to reach, easy to move around on, and forgiving if you are bringing guests or a longer dress &mdash; a soft landing for the end of the day.': 'Los prados merecen una mención especial para el atardecer. Donde una cresta puede ser ventosa y expuesta al caer la temperatura, los pastos abiertos del Alpe di Siusi o un tranquilo hombro de valle quedan suaves bajo los pies y brillan de maravilla cuando la luz lateral rastrilla la hierba. Son fáciles de alcanzar, fáciles de recorrer e indulgentes si lleváis invitados o un vestido más largo &mdash; un aterrizaje suave para el final del día.',
  'Reading the light': 'Leer la luz',
  'It helps to know the names for what you are chasing. <strong>Alpenglow</strong> is the pink-to-violet wash on the peaks in the minutes before sunrise and after sunset, when the sun is still below the horizon. <strong>Golden hour</strong> is the warm, low, flattering light in the 30&ndash;40 minutes just after the sun clears the ridge or just before it drops. <strong>Enrosadira</strong> is the Dolomites&rsquo; own miracle, the ember-red glow the pale limestone throws back at dusk and dawn. And <strong>blue hour</strong>, the cool, quiet window after the warm light has gone, is the one most people miss by packing up too soon &mdash; we never do.': 'Ayuda conocer los nombres de lo que perseguís. El <strong>alpenglow</strong> es el baño rosa a violeta sobre las cumbres en los minutos antes del amanecer y después del atardecer, cuando el sol sigue bajo el horizonte. La <strong>hora dorada</strong> es la luz cálida, baja y favorecedora en los 30&ndash;40 minutos justo después de que el sol supere la cresta o justo antes de que caiga. La <strong>enrosadira</strong> es el milagro propio de los Dolomitas, el brillo rojo brasa que la pálida caliza devuelve al ocaso y al alba. Y la <strong>hora azul</strong>, la ventana fresca y tranquila tras irse la luz cálida, es la que la mayoría se pierde por recoger demasiado pronto &mdash; nosotros nunca.',
  'Knowing the sequence lets us build the day like a piece of music. At a sunrise we shoot the cold alpenglow first, then the vows as the warm light lands, then loose, joyful portraits once the sun is properly up. At a sunset we run it in reverse: portraits in the generous golden light, the ceremony timed to the enrosadira, and the quiet blue-hour frames to close. Same peaks, opposite rhythm &mdash; and once you know which rhythm you want, the whole plan almost writes itself.': 'Conocer la secuencia nos deja construir el día como una pieza de música. En un amanecer fotografiamos primero el frío alpenglow, luego los votos cuando llega la luz cálida, luego retratos sueltos y alegres una vez que el sol ya está alto. En un atardecer lo hacemos al revés: retratos en la generosa luz dorada, la ceremonia sincronizada con la enrosadira y los tranquilos fotogramas de la hora azul para cerrar. Las mismas cumbres, ritmo opuesto &mdash; y en cuanto sabéis qué ritmo queréis, todo el plan casi se escribe solo.',
  'The logistics of dawn &amp; dusk': 'La logística del alba y el ocaso',
  'The practical difference between the two days is really about darkness and time. A sunrise means moving in the dark: head-torches for everyone, a trail we have already scouted, spare batteries, and gloves you will be glad of at the top. A sunset means racing the failing light home &mdash; or removing the race entirely by staying up high. Roads matter too: the Tre Cime toll road is open in the early hours in summer for dawn access, while most cable cars only serve the middle of the day, which is exactly why the lift-dependent spots are evening spots.': 'La diferencia práctica entre los dos días va, en realidad, de oscuridad y tiempo. Un amanecer significa moverse a oscuras: frontales para todos, un sendero que ya hemos explorado, pilas de repuesto y guantes que agradeceréis arriba. Un atardecer significa correr contra la luz que se apaga de vuelta a casa &mdash; o eliminar la carrera del todo quedándoos arriba. Las carreteras también importan: la carretera de peaje de las Tre Cime está abierta a primera hora en verano para el acceso al alba, mientras que la mayoría de los teleféricos solo sirven el mediodía, que es justo por lo que los lugares dependientes de teleférico son lugares de tarde.',
  'Gearing up at the trailhead car park in the dark before dawn': 'Preparando el equipo en el aparcamiento del sendero, a oscuras antes del alba',
  'None of this is meant to scare you off the early start &mdash; it is meant to make it effortless. We carry the plan so you carry nothing but the nerves: we scout, we time, we bring the spare torch and a flask of something warm, and we get you into position with light to spare. Bring a few guests to a sunrise and we brief them too, so the group moves as one in the dark instead of scattering.': 'Nada de esto pretende asustaros del inicio temprano &mdash; pretende hacerlo sin esfuerzo. Nosotros cargamos el plan para que vosotros no carguéis más que los nervios: exploramos, calculamos, traemos el frontal de repuesto y un termo de algo caliente, y os llevamos a posición con luz de sobra. Llevad a unos invitados a un amanecer y también los instruimos, para que el grupo se mueva como uno a oscuras en vez de dispersarse.',
  'The group lit only by a head-torch beam on the dark trail': 'El grupo iluminado solo por el haz de un frontal en el sendero oscuro',
  'What to wear': 'Qué llevar',
  'Dress for the hour, not the postcard. At dawn a summit can sit near freezing even in high summer, so we layer: the dress or suit you love, with warm, strippable layers over the top that come off for the frames and go straight back on between them. Good footwear for the walk and the pretty shoes in a bag; gloves and a hat that live in a pocket until the camera is down. Sunset is kinder but not warm &mdash; once the sun goes, the temperature drops fast, so the same rule holds an hour later. We tell you exactly what to expect for your date, your spot and your light.': 'Vestíos para la hora, no para la postal. Al alba una cumbre puede rozar el punto de congelación incluso en pleno verano, así que superponemos: el vestido o el traje que amáis, con capas de abrigo por encima que se quitan para las fotos y vuelven a ponerse entre ellas. Buen calzado para la caminata y los zapatos bonitos en una bolsa; guantes y gorro que viven en un bolsillo hasta que baja la cámara. El atardecer es más amable pero no cálido &mdash; en cuanto se va el sol, la temperatura cae rápido, así que la misma regla vale una hora después. Os decimos exactamente qué esperar para vuestra fecha, vuestro lugar y vuestra luz.',
  'Slipping into the dress at the summit as dawn colours the peaks': 'Poniéndose el vestido en la cumbre mientras el alba tiñe los picos',
  'How the light shifts by season': 'Cómo cambia la luz según la estación',
  'The light itself moves through the year, and it changes the maths. In June the sun is up before 05:30 and sets after 21:00 &mdash; short nights and a brutally early alarm, but the warmest, longest days. By October dawn slips to nearly 07:30 and dusk to around 18:00, which makes a sunrise elopement genuinely civilised and an autumn sunset gorgeously early. The shoulder months trade a little warmth for kinder timings and thinner crowds; deep summer gives you the softest weather and the busiest trails. The table above has the numbers &mdash; we build your morning or evening around them.': 'La luz misma se mueve a lo largo del año, y cambia las cuentas. En junio el sol sale antes de las 05:30 y se pone después de las 21:00 &mdash; noches cortas y una alarma brutalmente temprana, pero los días más cálidos y largos. Para octubre el alba se desliza casi a las 07:30 y el ocaso a eso de las 18:00, lo que hace un elopement al amanecer de verdad civilizado y un atardecer de otoño maravillosamente temprano. Los meses intermedios cambian algo de calidez por horarios más amables y menos gente; el pleno verano os da el clima más suave y los senderos más concurridos. La tabla de arriba tiene los números &mdash; construimos vuestra mañana o tarde en torno a ellos.',
  'Blue hour &amp; after': 'Hora azul y después',
  'Whichever light you choose, do not pack up when it fades. After sunrise there is a soft, clear morning to enjoy &mdash; a hut breakfast, an empty trail down, the whole day still ahead. After sunset comes blue hour, the cool quiet window when the sky goes deep and the first lights appear in the valley; it is our favourite ten minutes for a last, tender frame before the torches come on. Then the celebration: a rifugio dinner, a drive through the dark passes, or simply the walk down with a new ring and nowhere to be.': 'Sea cual sea la luz que elijáis, no recojáis cuando se desvanezca. Tras el amanecer hay una mañana suave y clara que disfrutar &mdash; un desayuno en un refugio, un sendero vacío de bajada, todo el día aún por delante. Tras el atardecer llega la hora azul, la ventana fresca y tranquila cuando el cielo se vuelve profundo y aparecen las primeras luces en el valle; son nuestros diez minutos favoritos para un último fotograma tierno antes de encender los frontales. Luego la celebración: una cena en un refugio, un recorrido por los puertos a oscuras, o simplemente la bajada con un anillo nuevo y sin ningún sitio adonde ir.',
  'The couple as a silhouette on the ridge under a wide sunset sky': 'La pareja como una silueta en la cresta bajo un amplio cielo de atardecer',
  'Sunrise': 'Amanecer',
  'Sunset': 'Atardecer',
  'Which is yours': '¿Cuál es el vuestro?',
  'Sunrise & sunset times': 'Horas de amanecer y atardecer',
  'Sunrise spots': 'Lugares para el amanecer',
  'Sunset spots': 'Lugares para el atardecer',
  'Dawn & dusk logistics': 'Logística de alba y ocaso',
  'Light by season': 'Luz según la estación',
  'Blue hour & after': 'Hora azul y después',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'Sunrise or sunset FAQ': 'Preguntas frecuentes sobre amanecer o atardecer',
  'The same summit is two different places at dawn and at dusk. Sunrise buys you solitude, cold air and the pink alpenglow before the valley wakes; sunset gives you warmth, an easy pace and a sky that burns as it goes. Neither is better &mdash; they are different days, and the choice quietly shapes everything: the alarm, the effort, the crowds, the mood of your photographs. Here is how we help couples choose their light, with the honest trade-offs and the spots that suit each.': 'La misma cumbre es dos lugares distintos al alba y al ocaso. El amanecer os compra soledad, aire frío y el alpenglow rosado antes de que despierte el valle; el atardecer os da calidez, un ritmo tranquilo y un cielo que arde al irse. Ninguno es mejor &mdash; son días distintos, y la elección marca en silencio todo: la alarma, el esfuerzo, la gente, el ambiente de vuestras fotos. Así ayudamos a las parejas a elegir su luz, con las concesiones honestas y los lugares que van con cada una.',
  'On this page': 'En esta página',
}
SUN_IT = {
  'The two-day question': 'La questione dei due giorni',
  'Think of it as choosing a character for the day. A sunrise elopement is quiet and a little heroic: you rise in the dark, climb by head-torch, and arrive as the first light sets the peaks on fire, often entirely alone. A sunset elopement is generous and relaxed: a slow afternoon walk, warm light that lingers for an hour, and a celebratory dinner waiting below. Everything downstream &mdash; how you dress, where you go, how many people you can bring &mdash; follows from that one decision, which is why we make it first.': "Vedetela come scegliere un carattere per la giornata. Un elopement all'alba è silenzioso e un po' eroico: vi alzate al buio, salite con la frontale e arrivate mentre la prima luce incendia le cime, spesso completamente soli. Un elopement al tramonto è generoso e rilassato: una lenta passeggiata pomeridiana, luce calda che indugia per un'ora e una cena di festa che aspetta a valle. Tutto il resto &mdash; come vi vestite, dove andate, quante persone potete portare &mdash; discende da quell'unica decisione, ed è per questo che la prendiamo per prima.",
  'A couple kissing on a misty Dolomite ridge as a peak breaks the cloud': 'Una coppia che si bacia su una cresta dolomitica nella nebbia mentre una cima buca le nuvole',
  'Sunrise: solitude &amp; soft light': 'Alba: solitudine e luce morbida',
  'A pre-dawn start is the closest thing we know to having the mountains to yourselves. The trailhead is empty, the air is sharp and still, and as the sun lifts, the rock turns from grey to rose to gold in a matter of minutes &mdash; the alpenglow that no filter can fake. There is a stillness at that hour that changes how people stand and speak; vows at sunrise come out softer and truer, because there is nobody within miles to perform for.': "Partire prima dell'alba è la cosa più vicina che conosciamo ad avere le montagne per voi. L'inizio del sentiero è vuoto, l'aria è tagliente e ferma, e quando il sole sale la roccia passa dal grigio al rosa all'oro in pochi minuti &mdash; l'alpenglow che nessun filtro può fingere. C'è una quiete a quell'ora che cambia il modo in cui le persone stanno e parlano; le promesse all'alba escono più morbide e vere, perché non c'è nessuno per chilometri davanti a cui recitare.",
  'A backlit portrait as the rising sun flares between the couple': 'Un ritratto in controluce mentre il sole nascente sfavilla tra la coppia',
  'It asks something of you: an alarm somewhere between 03:00 and 05:00 depending on the month, a walk in the dark, and warm layers for a summit that can sit near freezing even in July. We scout the trail the day before, walk it with you by head-torch, and time the climb so you are in position with light to spare. The reward is a version of the mountains almost no one sees &mdash; and photographs with a quality of light the middle of the day simply cannot give.': 'Vi chiede qualcosa: una sveglia da qualche parte tra le 03:00 e le 05:00 a seconda del mese, una camminata al buio e strati caldi per una vetta che può essere vicina allo zero anche a luglio. Perlustriamo il sentiero il giorno prima, lo percorriamo con voi con la frontale e calcoliamo la salita così da essere in posizione con luce in anticipo. La ricompensa è una versione delle montagne che quasi nessuno vede &mdash; e foto con una qualità di luce che il pieno giorno semplicemente non può dare.',
  'The bride ready with a head-torch before the dark climb': 'La sposa pronta con una frontale prima della salita al buio',
  'Sunset: warm &amp; unhurried': 'Tramonto: caldo e senza fretta',
  'Sunset is the forgiving choice, and there is no shame in it &mdash; some of our most beautiful days end rather than begin in the light. There is no alarm; you get ready at a civilised hour, walk up in the afternoon, and let the light come to you. Golden hour in the mountains is long and generous, the warm side-light wrapping around faces and rock, and it slides into the fireshow of enrosadira, when the Dolomite walls glow ember-red for a few unrepeatable minutes.': "Il tramonto è la scelta indulgente, e non c'è vergogna in ciò &mdash; alcune delle nostre giornate più belle finiscono nella luce invece di iniziarvi. Niente sveglia; vi preparate a un'ora civile, salite nel pomeriggio e lasciate che la luce venga a voi. L'ora dorata in montagna è lunga e generosa, la calda luce laterale che avvolge volti e roccia, e scivola nello spettacolo di fuoco dell'enrosadira, quando le pareti dolomitiche brillano di un rosso brace per pochi minuti irripetibili.",
  'A sunset ceremony under a circular floral arch, the sun flaring through': 'Una cerimonia al tramonto sotto un arco floreale circolare, il sole che sfavilla attraverso',
  'The trade-off is company. The good viewpoints that are empty at dawn can be busy at dusk, so we steer you to lesser-known ledges and meadows, or to spots where the crowd thins the moment the last cable car goes down. Sunset also runs on a hard clock in the other direction: the light fails fast, and you do not want to be finding the trail in the dark by accident. We plan the descent as carefully as the climb &mdash; or, on our favourite evenings, book a mountain hut so you never have to come down at all.': "Il prezzo è la compagnia. I buoni punti panoramici vuoti all'alba possono essere affollati al tramonto, quindi vi indirizziamo verso lembi e prati meno noti, o verso luoghi dove la folla si dirada nel momento in cui scende l'ultima funivia. Il tramonto corre anche contro l'orologio nell'altra direzione: la luce cala in fretta, e non volete ritrovarvi a cercare il sentiero al buio per sbaglio. Pianifichiamo la discesa con la stessa cura della salita &mdash; o, nelle nostre serate preferite, prenotiamo un rifugio così non dovete scendere affatto.",
  'The couple on a rock outcrop against the sunset mountains': 'La coppia su uno sperone di roccia contro le montagne al tramonto',
  'Which one is yours': 'Qual è il vostro?',
  'So which is yours? Choose sunrise if the picture in your head is solitude &mdash; empty peaks, soft pink light, a private ceremony with nobody in the frame but you. Choose it, too, if you want the most dramatic locations at their quietest, or if summer heat and crowds put you off. Choose sunset if mornings are genuinely not your thing, if you are bringing a few guests who would struggle with a 4 a.m. start, or if you want the day to end in warmth and a dinner rather than begin in the cold. When couples truly cannot decide, we sometimes do both across two days &mdash; a sunset to settle in, a sunrise for the main event.': "Allora, qual è il vostro? Scegliete l'alba se l'immagine nella vostra testa è solitudine &mdash; cime vuote, luce rosa morbida, una cerimonia privata con nessuno nell'inquadratura tranne voi. Sceglietela anche se volete i luoghi più drammatici nella loro versione più tranquilla, o se il caldo e la folla dell'estate vi scoraggiano. Scegliete il tramonto se le mattine proprio non fanno per voi, se portate qualche invitato a cui una partenza alle 4 del mattino peserebbe, o se volete che la giornata finisca nel calore e in una cena invece di iniziare al freddo. Quando una coppia davvero non riesce a decidere, a volte facciamo entrambi in due giorni &mdash; un tramonto per ambientarsi, un'alba per l'evento principale.",
  'It also comes down to temperament. Sunrise rewards the couple who love a shared mission &mdash; the alarm, the climb, the pay-off feel earned, and the day starts on a high that colours everything after. Sunset suits the couple who want to savour, not strive: a long lunch, an unhurried walk, and the whole thing melting into dinner. Neither is more romantic; they are romantic in different keys. Tell us which one sounds like you, and we will tell you honestly whether your dream location can deliver it.': "È anche questione di temperamento. L'alba premia la coppia che ama una missione condivisa &mdash; la sveglia, la salita, la ricompensa si sentono guadagnate, e la giornata inizia su un'euforia che colora tutto ciò che viene dopo. Il tramonto si addice alla coppia che vuole assaporare, non faticare: un lungo pranzo, una passeggiata senza fretta e il tutto che si scioglie in una cena. Nessuno dei due è più romantico; sono romantici in tonalità diverse. Diteci quale suona come voi e vi diremo con onestà se il vostro luogo dei sogni può offrirlo.",
  'The sun bursting over snow-dusted Dolomite peaks': 'Il sole che erompe sopra cime dolomitiche spolverate di neve',
  'Best spots for sunrise': "I migliori luoghi per l'alba",
  'Dawn suits places you can reach before the machinery of the day starts. Lago di Braies is the classic: mirror-still and empty at first light, long before the crowds &mdash; note that from 1 July to 15 September the access road needs an advance reservation between 09:00 and 16:00, another reason we are there at sunrise instead. The Tre Cime di Lavaredo are reachable by the Auronzo toll road, which in summer (roughly late May to late October, season- and weather-dependent) is passable in the early hours, so you can drive up in the dark and be on the peaks for the first colour. The car toll is around &euro;40, and an advance online ticket may be required &mdash; we sort that out for you.': "L'alba si addice ai luoghi che raggiungete prima che parta la macchina della giornata. Il Lago di Braies è il classico: liscio come uno specchio e vuoto alla prima luce, molto prima della folla &mdash; tenete presente che dal 1° luglio al 15 settembre la strada di accesso richiede una prenotazione anticipata tra le 09:00 e le 16:00, un altro motivo per cui preferiamo esserci all'alba. Le Tre Cime di Lavaredo si raggiungono con la strada a pedaggio di Auronzo, che in estate (all'incirca da fine maggio a fine ottobre, secondo stagione e meteo) è percorribile nelle prime ore, così potete salire al buio ed essere sulle cime per il primo colore. Il pedaggio dell'auto è di circa 40&nbsp;&euro;, e può essere richiesto un biglietto online in anticipo &mdash; a questo pensiamo noi.",
  'Dawn on the Lago di Braies jetty, the water mirror-still': "L'alba sul pontile del Lago di Braies, l'acqua liscia come uno specchio",
  'Ridgelines like the Seceda are the exception that proves the rule: the first cabin comes up around 08:30, far too late for dawn colour, so a true Seceda sunrise means either a head-torch hike in the dark or a night in a nearby rifugio. That sounds like a lot, and it is &mdash; but standing on that ridge as it turns pink, with the cable car still hours from its first run, is one of the great experiences these mountains offer. We only suggest it to couples who like the idea of earning it.': "Le creste come la Seceda sono l'eccezione che conferma la regola: la prima cabina sale verso le 08:30, troppo tardi per il colore dell'alba, quindi una vera alba sulla Seceda significa o una salita con la frontale al buio o una notte in un rifugio vicino. Sembra tanto, e lo è &mdash; ma stare su quella cresta mentre si tinge di rosa, con la funivia ancora a ore dalla prima corsa, è una delle grandi esperienze che queste montagne offrono. Lo proponiamo solo alle coppie a cui piace l'idea di guadagnarselo.",
  'A group climbing in the dark by the beam of head-torches': 'Un gruppo che sale al buio nel fascio delle frontali',
  'Best spots for sunset': 'I migliori luoghi per il tramonto',
  'Evening favours viewpoints you can reach by lift and leave in warmth &mdash; ideally ones where you can catch the last cabin down, or, better still, sleep at the top. The Sass Pordoi terrace, Lagazuoi with its cliff-edge refuge, the rolling Alpe di Siusi and the Nordkette right above Innsbruck all catch golden hour beautifully and empty out the moment the day-trippers head home. The single rule is to know your last descent: check the final cable-car time to the minute, and where there is no late option, we simply book the mountain hut and make a night of it.': "La sera predilige i punti panoramici che raggiungete in funivia e lasciate nel calore &mdash; idealmente quelli dove potete prendere l'ultima cabina di discesa o, meglio ancora, dormire in cima. La terrazza del Sass Pordoi, il Lagazuoi con il suo rifugio a strapiombo, la distesa dell'Alpe di Siusi e la Nordkette proprio sopra Innsbruck catturano l'ora dorata magnificamente e si svuotano nel momento in cui i gitanti tornano a casa. L'unica regola è conoscere la vostra ultima discesa: controllate l'orario dell'ultima funivia al minuto, e dove non c'è un'opzione tardiva prenotiamo semplicemente il rifugio e ne facciamo una notte.",
  'The couple walking through snow with the low sun behind': 'La coppia che cammina nella neve con il sole basso alle spalle',
  'Meadows deserve a special mention for sunset. Where a ridge can be windy and exposed as the temperature drops, the open pastures of the Alpe di Siusi or a quiet valley shoulder stay gentle underfoot and glow beautifully as the side-light rakes across the grass. They are easy to reach, easy to move around on, and forgiving if you are bringing guests or a longer dress &mdash; a soft landing for the end of the day.': "I prati meritano una menzione speciale per il tramonto. Dove una cresta può essere ventosa ed esposta al calare della temperatura, i pascoli aperti dell'Alpe di Siusi o una tranquilla spalla di valle restano dolci sotto i piedi e brillano magnificamente quando la luce laterale rastrella l'erba. Sono facili da raggiungere, facili da percorrere e indulgenti se portate invitati o un abito più lungo &mdash; un atterraggio morbido per la fine della giornata.",
  'Reading the light': 'Leggere la luce',
  'It helps to know the names for what you are chasing. <strong>Alpenglow</strong> is the pink-to-violet wash on the peaks in the minutes before sunrise and after sunset, when the sun is still below the horizon. <strong>Golden hour</strong> is the warm, low, flattering light in the 30&ndash;40 minutes just after the sun clears the ridge or just before it drops. <strong>Enrosadira</strong> is the Dolomites&rsquo; own miracle, the ember-red glow the pale limestone throws back at dusk and dawn. And <strong>blue hour</strong>, the cool, quiet window after the warm light has gone, is the one most people miss by packing up too soon &mdash; we never do.': "Aiuta conoscere i nomi di ciò che inseguite. L'<strong>alpenglow</strong> è la sfumatura dal rosa al violetto sulle cime nei minuti prima dell'alba e dopo il tramonto, quando il sole è ancora sotto l'orizzonte. L'<strong>ora dorata</strong> è la luce calda, bassa e lusinghiera nei 30&ndash;40 minuti subito dopo che il sole supera la cresta o poco prima che cali. L'<strong>enrosadira</strong> è il miracolo proprio delle Dolomiti, il bagliore rosso brace che il pallido calcare restituisce al tramonto e all'alba. E l'<strong>ora blu</strong>, la finestra fresca e quieta dopo che la luce calda se n'è andata, è quella che la maggior parte perde smontando troppo presto &mdash; noi mai.",
  'Knowing the sequence lets us build the day like a piece of music. At a sunrise we shoot the cold alpenglow first, then the vows as the warm light lands, then loose, joyful portraits once the sun is properly up. At a sunset we run it in reverse: portraits in the generous golden light, the ceremony timed to the enrosadira, and the quiet blue-hour frames to close. Same peaks, opposite rhythm &mdash; and once you know which rhythm you want, the whole plan almost writes itself.': "Conoscere la sequenza ci fa costruire la giornata come un pezzo di musica. A un'alba fotografiamo prima il freddo alpenglow, poi le promesse quando arriva la luce calda, poi ritratti sciolti e gioiosi una volta che il sole è ben alto. A un tramonto lo facciamo al contrario: ritratti nella generosa luce dorata, la cerimonia sincronizzata con l'enrosadira e i quieti fotogrammi dell'ora blu per chiudere. Le stesse cime, ritmo opposto &mdash; e una volta che sapete quale ritmo volete, l'intero piano si scrive quasi da sé.",
  'The logistics of dawn &amp; dusk': "La logistica dell'alba e del tramonto",
  'The practical difference between the two days is really about darkness and time. A sunrise means moving in the dark: head-torches for everyone, a trail we have already scouted, spare batteries, and gloves you will be glad of at the top. A sunset means racing the failing light home &mdash; or removing the race entirely by staying up high. Roads matter too: the Tre Cime toll road is open in the early hours in summer for dawn access, while most cable cars only serve the middle of the day, which is exactly why the lift-dependent spots are evening spots.': "La differenza pratica tra le due giornate riguarda davvero il buio e il tempo. Un'alba significa muoversi al buio: frontali per tutti, un sentiero che abbiamo già perlustrato, pile di scorta e guanti di cui sarete grati in cima. Un tramonto significa correre contro la luce che cala verso casa &mdash; o eliminare del tutto la corsa restando in quota. Contano anche le strade: la strada a pedaggio delle Tre Cime è aperta nelle prime ore in estate per l'accesso all'alba, mentre la maggior parte delle funivie serve solo il pieno giorno, ed è esattamente per questo che i luoghi dipendenti dagli impianti sono luoghi da sera.",
  'Gearing up at the trailhead car park in the dark before dawn': "Preparare l'attrezzatura al parcheggio del sentiero, al buio prima dell'alba",
  'None of this is meant to scare you off the early start &mdash; it is meant to make it effortless. We carry the plan so you carry nothing but the nerves: we scout, we time, we bring the spare torch and a flask of something warm, and we get you into position with light to spare. Bring a few guests to a sunrise and we brief them too, so the group moves as one in the dark instead of scattering.': "Niente di tutto ciò vuole scoraggiarvi dalla partenza presto &mdash; vuole renderla senza sforzo. Portiamo noi il piano così voi portate solo l'emozione: perlustriamo, calcoliamo i tempi, portiamo la frontale di scorta e un thermos di qualcosa di caldo, e vi mettiamo in posizione con luce in anticipo. Portate qualche invitato a un'alba e istruiamo anche loro, così il gruppo si muove come uno al buio invece di disperdersi.",
  'The group lit only by a head-torch beam on the dark trail': 'Il gruppo illuminato solo dal fascio di una frontale sul sentiero buio',
  'What to wear': 'Cosa indossare',
  'Dress for the hour, not the postcard. At dawn a summit can sit near freezing even in high summer, so we layer: the dress or suit you love, with warm, strippable layers over the top that come off for the frames and go straight back on between them. Good footwear for the walk and the pretty shoes in a bag; gloves and a hat that live in a pocket until the camera is down. Sunset is kinder but not warm &mdash; once the sun goes, the temperature drops fast, so the same rule holds an hour later. We tell you exactly what to expect for your date, your spot and your light.': "Vestitevi per l'ora, non per la cartolina. All'alba una vetta può essere vicina allo zero anche in piena estate, quindi facciamo a strati: l'abito o il completo che amate, con strati caldi e sfilabili sopra che si tolgono per le foto e si rimettono subito tra una e l'altra. Buone calzature per la camminata e le scarpe belle in una borsa; guanti e cappello che vivono in tasca finché la fotocamera non è giù. Il tramonto è più gentile ma non caldo &mdash; una volta che il sole se ne va, la temperatura cala in fretta, quindi la stessa regola vale un'ora dopo. Vi diciamo esattamente cosa aspettarvi per la vostra data, il vostro luogo e la vostra luce.",
  'Slipping into the dress at the summit as dawn colours the peaks': "Indossare l'abito in vetta mentre l'alba tinge le cime",
  'How the light shifts by season': 'Come cambia la luce con la stagione',
  'The light itself moves through the year, and it changes the maths. In June the sun is up before 05:30 and sets after 21:00 &mdash; short nights and a brutally early alarm, but the warmest, longest days. By October dawn slips to nearly 07:30 and dusk to around 18:00, which makes a sunrise elopement genuinely civilised and an autumn sunset gorgeously early. The shoulder months trade a little warmth for kinder timings and thinner crowds; deep summer gives you the softest weather and the busiest trails. The table above has the numbers &mdash; we build your morning or evening around them.': "La luce stessa si muove nell'arco dell'anno, e cambia i conti. A giugno il sole è su prima delle 05:30 e tramonta dopo le 21:00 &mdash; notti corte e una sveglia brutalmente presto, ma le giornate più calde e lunghe. Entro ottobre l'alba scivola quasi alle 07:30 e il tramonto verso le 18:00, il che rende un elopement all'alba davvero civile e un tramonto autunnale splendidamente presto. I mesi di mezzo scambiano un po' di calore con orari più gentili e meno folla; la piena estate vi dà il tempo più mite e i sentieri più affollati. La tabella qui sopra ha i numeri &mdash; costruiamo la vostra mattina o sera attorno a essi.",
  'Blue hour &amp; after': 'Ora blu e dopo',
  'Whichever light you choose, do not pack up when it fades. After sunrise there is a soft, clear morning to enjoy &mdash; a hut breakfast, an empty trail down, the whole day still ahead. After sunset comes blue hour, the cool quiet window when the sky goes deep and the first lights appear in the valley; it is our favourite ten minutes for a last, tender frame before the torches come on. Then the celebration: a rifugio dinner, a drive through the dark passes, or simply the walk down with a new ring and nowhere to be.': "Qualunque luce scegliate, non smontate quando svanisce. Dopo l'alba c'è una mattina morbida e limpida da godersi &mdash; una colazione in rifugio, un sentiero vuoto in discesa, l'intera giornata ancora davanti. Dopo il tramonto arriva l'ora blu, la finestra fresca e quieta quando il cielo si fa profondo e appaiono le prime luci in valle; sono i nostri dieci minuti preferiti per un ultimo, tenero fotogramma prima che si accendano le frontali. Poi la festa: una cena in rifugio, un giro tra i passi al buio, o semplicemente la discesa con un anello nuovo e nessun posto dove andare.",
  'The couple as a silhouette on the ridge under a wide sunset sky': 'La coppia come una silhouette sulla cresta sotto un ampio cielo al tramonto',
  'Sunrise': 'Alba',
  'Sunset': 'Tramonto',
  'Which is yours': 'Qual è il vostro?',
  'Sunrise & sunset times': 'Orari di alba e tramonto',
  'Sunrise spots': "Luoghi per l'alba",
  'Sunset spots': 'Luoghi per il tramonto',
  'Dawn & dusk logistics': 'Logistica alba e tramonto',
  'Light by season': 'Luce per stagione',
  'Blue hour & after': 'Ora blu e dopo',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'Sunrise or sunset FAQ': 'Domande frequenti su alba o tramonto',
  'The same summit is two different places at dawn and at dusk. Sunrise buys you solitude, cold air and the pink alpenglow before the valley wakes; sunset gives you warmth, an easy pace and a sky that burns as it goes. Neither is better &mdash; they are different days, and the choice quietly shapes everything: the alarm, the effort, the crowds, the mood of your photographs. Here is how we help couples choose their light, with the honest trade-offs and the spots that suit each.': "La stessa vetta è due luoghi diversi all'alba e al tramonto. L'alba vi compra solitudine, aria fredda e l'alpenglow rosato prima che la valle si svegli; il tramonto vi dà calore, un ritmo tranquillo e un cielo che brucia mentre se ne va. Nessuno è migliore &mdash; sono giornate diverse, e la scelta plasma in silenzio tutto: la sveglia, la fatica, la folla, l'atmosfera delle vostre foto. Ecco come aiutiamo le coppie a scegliere la loro luce, con i compromessi onesti e i luoghi che si addicono a ciascuna.",
  'On this page': 'In questa pagina',
}
SUN_FAQ_ES = {
  'Sunrise or sunset — which is better for an elopement?': ('Amanecer o atardecer, ¿qué es mejor para un elopement?', 'Con honestidad, el amanecer gana en luz y soledad: cumbres vacías, alpenglow rosado y una ceremonia privada que nadie puede abarrotar. El atardecer gana en comodidad: sin alarma, una subida relajada y luz cálida que perdura. Si podéis con el inicio temprano, tomad el amanecer; si las mañanas no son lo vuestro o lleváis invitados, el atardecer es la opción fiable y bella.'),
  'How early do we have to get up for a sunrise elopement?': ('¿Con cuánta antelación hay que levantarse para un elopement al amanecer?', 'Depende del mes y de la caminata &mdash; la alarma suele caer entre las 03:00 y las 05:00, más temprano en junio, más tarde en octubre. Exploramos el sendero la víspera y calculamos la subida para que lleguéis a vuestro lugar con luz de sobra, y cargamos el plan para que lo único que tengáis que hacer sea levantaros.'),
  'Can we reach a ridge like the Seceda for sunrise by cable car?': ('¿Podemos llegar a una cresta como el Seceda para el amanecer en teleférico?', 'No. Las primeras cabinas suben demasiado tarde para el alba &mdash; el Seceda desde las 08:30 aprox. y la Nordkette sobre Innsbruck desde las 08:00 aprox. &mdash;, así que un amanecer real en una cresta implica o una subida con frontal a oscuras o una noche en un refugio. Los lugares junto a la carretera y las cumbres con carretera de peaje son la vía más fácil a la primera luz.'),
  'Is being up there in the dark difficult or unsafe?': ('¿Es difícil o peligroso estar allí arriba a oscuras?', 'Es más fácil de lo que suena cuando está planificado. Exploramos el sendero primero de día, traemos frontales de repuesto y bebidas calientes, mantenemos al grupo unido y calculamos todo con margen. Para la mayoría de las parejas, la caminata a oscuras se convierte en una de las mejores partes del día &mdash; tranquila, íntima y llena de expectación.'),
  'For a sunset elopement, how do we get down afterwards?': ('Para un elopement al atardecer, ¿cómo bajamos después?', 'Eso es lo único que hay que planificar con cuidado. Donde habéis subido en teleférico, comprobamos la última bajada al minuto y os mantenemos por delante de ella; donde no hay opción tardía, simplemente reservamos un refugio para que paséis la noche y os saltéis la bajada por completo. En cualquier caso planificamos el camino de vuelta con tanto cuidado como el de subida.'),
  'When is the best month for the light?': ('¿Cuál es el mejor mes para la luz?', 'Cada mes tiene su compensación. Junio tiene los días más cálidos y largos, pero la alarma más temprana; septiembre y octubre traen horas de amanecer civilizadas, aire fresco y claro y multitudes mucho más finas, con el añadido de los alerces dorados. La tabla de arriba tiene los números de cada mes, y construimos vuestra mañana o tarde en torno a ellos.'),
}
SUN_FAQ_IT = {
  'Sunrise or sunset — which is better for an elopement?': ('Alba o tramonto, cosa è meglio per un elopement?', "Onestamente, l'alba vince su luce e solitudine: cime vuote, alpenglow rosato e una cerimonia privata che nessuno può affollare. Il tramonto vince sulla comodità: niente sveglia, una salita rilassata e luce calda che indugia. Se ce la fate con la partenza presto, prendete l'alba; se le mattine non fanno per voi o avete invitati, il tramonto è la scelta affidabile e bella."),
  'How early do we have to get up for a sunrise elopement?': ("Quanto presto dobbiamo alzarci per un elopement all'alba?", "Dipende dal mese e dalla camminata &mdash; la sveglia di solito cade tra le 03:00 e le 05:00, prima a giugno, più tardi a ottobre. Perlustriamo il sentiero il giorno prima e calcoliamo la salita così da farvi arrivare al vostro luogo con luce in anticipo, e portiamo noi il piano così l'unica cosa che dovete fare è alzarvi."),
  'Can we reach a ridge like the Seceda for sunrise by cable car?': ("Possiamo raggiungere una cresta come la Seceda per l'alba in funivia?", "No. Le prime cabine salgono troppo tardi per l'alba &mdash; la Seceda dalle 08:30 circa e la Nordkette sopra Innsbruck dalle 08:00 circa &mdash;, quindi una vera alba su una cresta significa o una salita con la frontale al buio o una notte in un rifugio. I luoghi sul ciglio della strada e le vette con strada a pedaggio sono la via più facile alla prima luce."),
  'Is being up there in the dark difficult or unsafe?': ('È difficile o pericoloso stare lassù al buio?', 'È più facile di quanto sembri quando è pianificato. Perlustriamo prima il sentiero di giorno, portiamo frontali di scorta e bevande calde, teniamo il gruppo unito e calcoliamo tutto con un margine. Per la maggior parte delle coppie la camminata al buio diventa una delle parti più belle della giornata &mdash; quieta, intima e piena di attesa.'),
  'For a sunset elopement, how do we get down afterwards?': ('Per un elopement al tramonto, come scendiamo dopo?', "È l'unica cosa da pianificare con cura. Dove siete saliti in funivia, controlliamo l'ultima discesa al minuto e vi teniamo in anticipo su di essa; dove non c'è un'opzione tardiva, prenotiamo semplicemente un rifugio così passate la notte e saltate del tutto la discesa. In ogni caso pianifichiamo la via del ritorno con la stessa cura di quella di salita."),
  'When is the best month for the light?': ('Qual è il mese migliore per la luce?', "Ogni mese ha il suo compromesso. Giugno ha le giornate più calde e lunghe, ma la sveglia più presto; settembre e ottobre portano orari d'alba civili, aria fresca e limpida e folla molto più rada, con il bonus dei larici dorati. La tabella qui sopra ha i numeri per ogni mese, e costruiamo la vostra mattina o sera attorno a essi."),
}

def build_sunset_guide(lang):
    slug='sunrise-or-sunset-elopement'
    g=next(x for x in GUIDES if x['slug']==slug); ex=GUIDE_EXTRA[slug]
    rel='how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/'+slug+'/'; P=prefix(lang,rel)
    DE=(lang=='de')
    def L(en,de):
        if lang=='de': return de
        if lang=='es': return SUN_ES.get(en,en)
        if lang=='it': return SUN_IT.get(en,en)
        return en
    def FQ(qen,aen,qde,ade):
        if lang=='de': return (qde,ade)
        if lang=='es': return SUN_FAQ_ES.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        if lang=='it': return SUN_FAQ_IT.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        return (qen,aen)
    GI=f'{P}img/guide-sunrise-sunset/'; GIREL='img/guide-sunrise-sunset/'; HERO_IMG='img/guide-sunrise-sunset/07-sonne-geluebde-bei-sonnenaufgang.webp'
    H2S='font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,3vw,36px);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:1.7em 0 .4em;scroll-margin-top:96px'
    def h2(i,en,de): return f'<h2 id="{i}" style="{H2S}">{L(en,de)}</h2>'
    def p(en,de): return f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2)">{L(en,de)}</p>'
    def fig(name,en,de): return '<figure class="guide-fig">'+bild(P,GIREL+name,L(en,de),sizes='(max-width:820px) 100vw, 820px')+'</figure>'
    toc=[('what',L('The two-day question','Die Zwei-Tage-Frage')),('sunrise',L('Sunrise','Sonnenaufgang')),
         ('sunset',L('Sunset','Sonnenuntergang')),('decide',L('Which is yours','Was zu euch passt')),
         ('times',L('Sunrise & sunset times','Auf- & Untergangszeiten')),
         ('spots-sunrise',L('Sunrise spots','Sonnenaufgangs-Orte')),('spots-sunset',L('Sunset spots','Sonnenuntergangs-Orte')),
         ('light',L('Reading the light','Das Licht lesen')),('logistics',L('Dawn & dusk logistics','Logistik Morgen & Abend')),
         ('wear',L('What to wear','Was anziehen')),('season',L('Light by season','Licht nach Saison')),
         ('after',L('Blue hour & after','Blaue Stunde & danach')),('faq',L('FAQ','FAQ'))]
    toc_html=('<nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'"><div class="cap">'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'</div><ol>'
      +''.join(f'<li><a href="#{i}">{lbl}</a></li>' for i,lbl in toc)+'</ol></nav>')
    facts='<div class="facts">'+''.join(f'<div class="fct"><div class="fl">{LBL[k][lang]}</div><div class="fv">{val[lang]}</div></div>' for k,val in ex['facts'])+'</div>'
    C=[]
    C.append(f'<p class="lead">{L("The same summit is two different places at dawn and at dusk. Sunrise buys you solitude, cold air and the pink alpenglow before the valley wakes; sunset gives you warmth, an easy pace and a sky that burns as it goes. Neither is better &mdash; they are different days, and the choice quietly shapes everything: the alarm, the effort, the crowds, the mood of your photographs. Here is how we help couples choose their light, with the honest trade-offs and the spots that suit each.","Derselbe Gipfel ist bei Morgen- und Abendlicht zwei verschiedene Orte. Der Sonnenaufgang schenkt euch Einsamkeit, kalte Luft und das rosa Alpenglühen, ehe das Tal erwacht; der Sonnenuntergang gibt Wärme, ein gemächliches Tempo und einen Himmel, der beim Gehen brennt. Keines ist besser &mdash; es sind verschiedene Tage, und die Wahl prägt leise alles: den Wecker, den Aufwand, den Trubel, die Stimmung eurer Bilder. So helfen wir Paaren, ihr Licht zu wählen &mdash; mit den ehrlichen Kompromissen und den Orten, die zu jedem passen.")}</p>')
    C.append(f'<div class="cap" style="margin:0 0 -14px">{t(lang,"quick_facts")}</div>{facts}')
    C.append(toc_html)

    C.append(h2('what','The two-day question','Die Zwei-Tage-Frage'))
    C.append(p("Think of it as choosing a character for the day. A sunrise elopement is quiet and a little heroic: you rise in the dark, climb by head-torch, and arrive as the first light sets the peaks on fire, often entirely alone. A sunset elopement is generous and relaxed: a slow afternoon walk, warm light that lingers for an hour, and a celebratory dinner waiting below. Everything downstream &mdash; how you dress, where you go, how many people you can bring &mdash; follows from that one decision, which is why we make it first.","Seht es als Wahl eines Charakters für den Tag. Ein Sonnenaufgangs-Elopement ist still und ein wenig heldenhaft: Ihr steht im Dunkeln auf, steigt mit Stirnlampe auf und kommt an, wenn das erste Licht die Gipfel in Brand setzt &mdash; oft ganz allein. Ein Sonnenuntergangs-Elopement ist großzügig und entspannt: ein gemächlicher Nachmittagsweg, warmes Licht, das eine Stunde bleibt, und ein festliches Abendessen, das unten wartet. Alles Weitere &mdash; wie ihr euch kleidet, wohin ihr geht, wie viele Menschen ihr mitnehmen könnt &mdash; folgt aus dieser einen Entscheidung, deshalb treffen wir sie zuerst."))
    C.append(fig('s-mist-ridge-kiss.webp',"A couple kissing on a misty Dolomite ridge as a peak breaks the cloud","Ein Paar küsst sich auf einem neblig­en Dolomitengrat, während ein Gipfel die Wolken durchbricht"))

    C.append(h2('sunrise','Sunrise: solitude &amp; soft light','Sonnenaufgang: Ruhe &amp; weiches Licht'))
    C.append(p("A pre-dawn start is the closest thing we know to having the mountains to yourselves. The trailhead is empty, the air is sharp and still, and as the sun lifts, the rock turns from grey to rose to gold in a matter of minutes &mdash; the alpenglow that no filter can fake. There is a stillness at that hour that changes how people stand and speak; vows at sunrise come out softer and truer, because there is nobody within miles to perform for.","Ein Start vor Morgengrauen ist das Nächste, was wir kennen, um die Berge für euch allein zu haben. Der Ausgangspunkt ist leer, die Luft scharf und still, und wenn die Sonne steigt, wechselt der Fels in Minuten von Grau zu Rosa zu Gold &mdash; das Alpenglühen, das kein Filter vortäuschen kann. In dieser Stunde liegt eine Ruhe, die verändert, wie Menschen stehen und sprechen; Gelübde bei Sonnenaufgang klingen weicher und wahrer, weil meilenweit niemand da ist, für den man sich in Szene setzt."))
    C.append(fig('08-sonne-gegenlicht-portrait-morgens.webp',"A backlit portrait as the rising sun flares between the couple","Ein Gegenlicht-Porträt, während die aufgehende Sonne zwischen dem Paar aufblitzt"))
    C.append(p("It asks something of you: an alarm somewhere between 03:00 and 05:00 depending on the month, a walk in the dark, and warm layers for a summit that can sit near freezing even in July. We scout the trail the day before, walk it with you by head-torch, and time the climb so you are in position with light to spare. The reward is a version of the mountains almost no one sees &mdash; and photographs with a quality of light the middle of the day simply cannot give.","Es verlangt etwas von euch: einen Wecker irgendwo zwischen 03:00 und 05:00 Uhr je nach Monat, einen Weg im Dunkeln und warme Schichten für einen Gipfel, der selbst im Juli nahe null Grad liegen kann. Wir erkunden den Weg am Vortag, gehen ihn mit euch per Stirnlampe und timen den Aufstieg so, dass ihr mit Licht im Vorrat in Position seid. Der Lohn ist eine Version der Berge, die fast niemand sieht &mdash; und Bilder mit einer Lichtqualität, die die Tagesmitte schlicht nicht geben kann."))
    C.append(fig('02-sonne-stirnlampen-vorbereitung.webp',"The bride ready with a head-torch before the dark climb","Die Braut mit Stirnlampe bereit vor dem Aufstieg im Dunkeln"))

    C.append(h2('sunset','Sunset: warm &amp; unhurried','Sonnenuntergang: warm &amp; gemächlich'))
    C.append(p("Sunset is the forgiving choice, and there is no shame in it &mdash; some of our most beautiful days end rather than begin in the light. There is no alarm; you get ready at a civilised hour, walk up in the afternoon, and let the light come to you. Golden hour in the mountains is long and generous, the warm side-light wrapping around faces and rock, and it slides into the fireshow of enrosadira, when the Dolomite walls glow ember-red for a few unrepeatable minutes.","Der Sonnenuntergang ist die nachsichtige Wahl, und das ist keine Schande &mdash; manche unserer schönsten Tage enden im Licht, statt darin zu beginnen. Kein Wecker; ihr macht euch zu zivilisierter Stunde fertig, steigt am Nachmittag auf und lasst das Licht zu euch kommen. Die goldene Stunde in den Bergen ist lang und großzügig, das warme Seitenlicht legt sich um Gesichter und Fels und geht über in das Feuerwerk der Enrosadira, wenn die Dolomitenwände für ein paar unwiederholbare Minuten glutrot glühen."))
    C.append(fig('13-sonne-untergang-zeremonie.webp',"A sunset ceremony under a circular floral arch, the sun flaring through","Eine Zeremonie im Sonnenuntergang unter einem runden Blumenbogen, die Sonne blitzt hindurch"))
    C.append(p("The trade-off is company. The good viewpoints that are empty at dawn can be busy at dusk, so we steer you to lesser-known ledges and meadows, or to spots where the crowd thins the moment the last cable car goes down. Sunset also runs on a hard clock in the other direction: the light fails fast, and you do not want to be finding the trail in the dark by accident. We plan the descent as carefully as the climb &mdash; or, on our favourite evenings, book a mountain hut so you never have to come down at all.","Der Preis ist Gesellschaft. Die guten Aussichtspunkte, die im Morgengrauen leer sind, können am Abend voll sein, deshalb lenken wir euch zu weniger bekannten Bändern und Wiesen oder zu Orten, wo sich der Andrang lichtet, sobald die letzte Gondel talwärts fährt. Der Sonnenuntergang läuft auch in die andere Richtung gegen die Uhr: Das Licht schwindet schnell, und ihr wollt den Weg nicht aus Versehen im Dunkeln suchen. Wir planen den Abstieg so sorgfältig wie den Aufstieg &mdash; oder buchen an unseren liebsten Abenden eine Berghütte, damit ihr gar nicht mehr hinunter müsst."))
    C.append(fig('15-sonne-untergang-fels-silhouette.webp',"The couple on a rock outcrop against the sunset mountains","Das Paar auf einer Felskanzel vor den Bergen im Sonnenuntergang"))

    C.append(h2('decide','Which one is yours','Was zu euch passt'))
    C.append(p("So which is yours? Choose sunrise if the picture in your head is solitude &mdash; empty peaks, soft pink light, a private ceremony with nobody in the frame but you. Choose it, too, if you want the most dramatic locations at their quietest, or if summer heat and crowds put you off. Choose sunset if mornings are genuinely not your thing, if you are bringing a few guests who would struggle with a 4 a.m. start, or if you want the day to end in warmth and a dinner rather than begin in the cold. When couples truly cannot decide, we sometimes do both across two days &mdash; a sunset to settle in, a sunrise for the main event.","Was ist also eures? Wählt den Sonnenaufgang, wenn das Bild in eurem Kopf Einsamkeit ist &mdash; leere Gipfel, weiches rosa Licht, eine private Zeremonie ohne jemanden im Bild außer euch. Wählt ihn auch, wenn ihr die dramatischsten Orte in ihrer stillsten Form wollt oder wenn euch Sommerhitze und Trubel abschrecken. Wählt den Sonnenuntergang, wenn Morgen wirklich nicht euer Ding sind, wenn ihr ein paar Gäste dabeihabt, die ein Start um 4 Uhr überfordern würde, oder wenn der Tag in Wärme und einem Abendessen enden soll, statt in der Kälte zu beginnen. Wenn Paare sich wirklich nicht entscheiden können, machen wir manchmal beides an zwei Tagen &mdash; ein Sonnenuntergang zum Ankommen, ein Sonnenaufgang fürs Hauptereignis."))

    C.append(p("It also comes down to temperament. Sunrise rewards the couple who love a shared mission &mdash; the alarm, the climb, the pay-off feel earned, and the day starts on a high that colours everything after. Sunset suits the couple who want to savour, not strive: a long lunch, an unhurried walk, and the whole thing melting into dinner. Neither is more romantic; they are romantic in different keys. Tell us which one sounds like you, and we will tell you honestly whether your dream location can deliver it.","Es h\u00e4ngt auch vom Temperament ab. Der Sonnenaufgang belohnt das Paar, das eine gemeinsame Mission liebt &mdash; der Wecker, der Aufstieg, der Lohn f\u00fchlen sich verdient an, und der Tag beginnt auf einem Hoch, das alles danach f\u00e4rbt. Der Sonnenuntergang passt zum Paar, das genie\u00dfen statt streben will: ein langes Mittagessen, ein gem\u00e4chlicher Weg und das Ganze, das in ein Abendessen zerflie\u00dft. Keines ist romantischer; sie sind romantisch in verschiedenen Tonarten. Sagt uns, welches nach euch klingt, und wir sagen euch ehrlich, ob euer Wunschort es liefern kann."))
    C.append(sun_times_block(lang).replace('<h2 style=','<h2 id="times" style=',1))
    C.append(fig('s-sunburst-peaks.webp',"The sun bursting over snow-dusted Dolomite peaks","Die Sonne bricht über schneebestäubten Dolomitengipfeln hervor"))

    C.append(h2('spots-sunrise','Best spots for sunrise','Beste Orte für den Sonnenaufgang'))
    C.append(p("Dawn suits places you can reach before the machinery of the day starts. Lago di Braies is the classic: mirror-still and empty at first light, long before the crowds &mdash; note that from 1 July to 15 September the access road needs an advance reservation between 09:00 and 16:00, another reason we are there at sunrise instead. The Tre Cime di Lavaredo are reachable by the Auronzo toll road, which in summer (roughly late May to late October, season- and weather-dependent) is passable in the early hours, so you can drive up in the dark and be on the peaks for the first colour. The car toll is around &euro;40, and an advance online ticket may be required &mdash; we sort that out for you.","Der Morgen passt zu Orten, die ihr erreicht, bevor die Maschinerie des Tages beginnt. Der Pragser Wildsee ist der Klassiker: spiegelglatt und leer bei erstem Licht, lange vor dem Andrang &mdash; beachtet, dass die Zufahrtsstraße vom 1. Juli bis 15. September zwischen 09:00 und 16:00 Uhr eine Voranmeldung braucht, ein weiterer Grund, warum wir stattdessen zum Sonnenaufgang dort sind. Die Drei Zinnen erreicht ihr über die Auronzo-Mautstraße, die im Sommer (etwa Ende Mai bis Ende Oktober, saison- und wetterabhängig) auch in den frühen Stunden befahrbar ist &mdash; ihr könnt also im Dunkeln hinauffahren und zum ersten Licht auf den Gipfeln sein. Die Pkw-Maut liegt bei etwa 40&nbsp;&euro;, und ein Online-Ticket im Voraus kann nötig sein &mdash; das regeln wir für euch."))
    C.append(fig('s-braies-jetty-dawn.webp',"Dawn on the Lago di Braies jetty, the water mirror-still","Morgengrauen am Steg des Pragser Wildsees, das Wasser spiegelglatt"))
    C.append(p("Ridgelines like the Seceda are the exception that proves the rule: the first cabin comes up around 08:30, far too late for dawn colour, so a true Seceda sunrise means either a head-torch hike in the dark or a night in a nearby rifugio. That sounds like a lot, and it is &mdash; but standing on that ridge as it turns pink, with the cable car still hours from its first run, is one of the great experiences these mountains offer. We only suggest it to couples who like the idea of earning it.","Grate wie die Seceda sind die Ausnahme, die die Regel bestätigt: Die erste Gondel kommt gegen 08:30 Uhr, viel zu spät für die Morgenfarbe &mdash; ein echter Seceda-Sonnenaufgang heißt also entweder ein Stirnlampen-Aufstieg im Dunkeln oder eine Nacht in einer nahen Hütte. Das klingt nach viel, und das ist es &mdash; aber auf diesem Grat zu stehen, während er rosa wird, die Seilbahn noch Stunden von ihrer ersten Fahrt entfernt, ist eines der großen Erlebnisse, die diese Berge bieten. Wir schlagen es nur Paaren vor, denen die Idee gefällt, es sich zu verdienen."))
    C.append(fig('03-sonne-nachtaufstieg-stirnlampen.webp',"A group climbing in the dark by the beam of head-torches","Eine Gruppe steigt im Dunkeln im Schein der Stirnlampen auf"))

    C.append(h2('spots-sunset','Best spots for sunset','Beste Orte für den Sonnenuntergang'))
    C.append(p("Evening favours viewpoints you can reach by lift and leave in warmth &mdash; ideally ones where you can catch the last cabin down, or, better still, sleep at the top. The Sass Pordoi terrace, Lagazuoi with its cliff-edge refuge, the rolling Alpe di Siusi and the Nordkette right above Innsbruck all catch golden hour beautifully and empty out the moment the day-trippers head home. The single rule is to know your last descent: check the final cable-car time to the minute, and where there is no late option, we simply book the mountain hut and make a night of it.","Der Abend begünstigt Aussichten, die ihr per Bahn erreicht und in Wärme verlasst &mdash; idealerweise solche, wo ihr die letzte Gondel nach unten erwischt oder, noch besser, oben schlaft. Die Sass-Pordoi-Terrasse, der Lagazuoi mit seiner Hütte am Felsrand, die weite Seiser Alm und die Nordkette direkt über Innsbruck fangen die goldene Stunde wunderbar und leeren sich, sobald die Tagesgäste heimgehen. Die einzige Regel: Kennt eure letzte Talfahrt &mdash; prüft die letzte Gondelzeit auf die Minute, und wo es keine späte Option gibt, buchen wir einfach die Berghütte und machen eine Nacht daraus."))
    C.append(fig('s-winter-walk-sun.webp',"The couple walking through snow with the low sun behind","Das Paar geht durch den Schnee, die tiefe Sonne im Rücken"))

    C.append(p("Meadows deserve a special mention for sunset. Where a ridge can be windy and exposed as the temperature drops, the open pastures of the Alpe di Siusi or a quiet valley shoulder stay gentle underfoot and glow beautifully as the side-light rakes across the grass. They are easy to reach, easy to move around on, and forgiving if you are bringing guests or a longer dress &mdash; a soft landing for the end of the day.","Wiesen verdienen f\u00fcr den Sonnenuntergang eine besondere Erw\u00e4hnung. Wo ein Grat windig und ausgesetzt sein kann, w\u00e4hrend die Temperatur f\u00e4llt, bleiben die offenen Weiden der Seiser Alm oder eine ruhige Talschulter sanft unter den F\u00fc\u00dfen und gl\u00fchen wunderbar, wenn das Seitenlicht \u00fcber das Gras streift. Sie sind leicht zu erreichen, leicht zu begehen und nachsichtig, wenn ihr G\u00e4ste oder ein l\u00e4ngeres Kleid dabeihabt &mdash; eine weiche Landung f\u00fcr das Ende des Tages."))
    C.append(h2('light','Reading the light','Das Licht lesen'))
    C.append(p("It helps to know the names for what you are chasing. <strong>Alpenglow</strong> is the pink-to-violet wash on the peaks in the minutes before sunrise and after sunset, when the sun is still below the horizon. <strong>Golden hour</strong> is the warm, low, flattering light in the 30&ndash;40 minutes just after the sun clears the ridge or just before it drops. <strong>Enrosadira</strong> is the Dolomites&rsquo; own miracle, the ember-red glow the pale limestone throws back at dusk and dawn. And <strong>blue hour</strong>, the cool, quiet window after the warm light has gone, is the one most people miss by packing up too soon &mdash; we never do.","Es hilft, die Namen für das zu kennen, was ihr jagt. <strong>Alpenglühen</strong> ist der rosa-violette Hauch auf den Gipfeln in den Minuten vor Sonnenaufgang und nach Sonnenuntergang, wenn die Sonne noch unter dem Horizont steht. <strong>Goldene Stunde</strong> ist das warme, tiefe, schmeichelnde Licht in den 30&ndash;40 Minuten direkt nachdem die Sonne über den Grat steigt oder kurz bevor sie fällt. <strong>Enrosadira</strong> ist das eigene Wunder der Dolomiten, das glutrote Glühen, das der bleiche Kalk in Dämmerung und Morgengrauen zurückwirft. Und die <strong>blaue Stunde</strong>, das kühle, stille Fenster, nachdem das warme Licht gegangen ist, verpassen die meisten, weil sie zu früh einpacken &mdash; wir nie."))

    C.append(p("Knowing the sequence lets us build the day like a piece of music. At a sunrise we shoot the cold alpenglow first, then the vows as the warm light lands, then loose, joyful portraits once the sun is properly up. At a sunset we run it in reverse: portraits in the generous golden light, the ceremony timed to the enrosadira, and the quiet blue-hour frames to close. Same peaks, opposite rhythm &mdash; and once you know which rhythm you want, the whole plan almost writes itself.","Die Abfolge zu kennen, l\u00e4sst uns den Tag wie ein Musikst\u00fcck bauen. Beim Sonnenaufgang fotografieren wir zuerst das kalte Alpengl\u00fchen, dann die Gel\u00fcbde, wenn das warme Licht auftrifft, dann lockere, freudige Portr\u00e4ts, sobald die Sonne richtig oben ist. Beim Sonnenuntergang l\u00e4uft es r\u00fcckw\u00e4rts: Portr\u00e4ts im gro\u00dfz\u00fcgigen Goldlicht, die Zeremonie auf die Enrosadira getimt und die stillen Bilder der blauen Stunde zum Abschluss. Dieselben Gipfel, umgekehrter Rhythmus &mdash; und sobald ihr wisst, welchen Rhythmus ihr wollt, schreibt sich der ganze Plan fast von selbst."))
    C.append(h2('logistics','The logistics of dawn &amp; dusk','Die Logistik von Morgen &amp; Abend'))
    C.append(p("The practical difference between the two days is really about darkness and time. A sunrise means moving in the dark: head-torches for everyone, a trail we have already scouted, spare batteries, and gloves you will be glad of at the top. A sunset means racing the failing light home &mdash; or removing the race entirely by staying up high. Roads matter too: the Tre Cime toll road is open in the early hours in summer for dawn access, while most cable cars only serve the middle of the day, which is exactly why the lift-dependent spots are evening spots.","Der praktische Unterschied zwischen den beiden Tagen dreht sich eigentlich um Dunkelheit und Zeit. Ein Sonnenaufgang heißt, sich im Dunkeln zu bewegen: Stirnlampen für alle, ein Weg, den wir schon erkundet haben, Ersatzbatterien und Handschuhe, über die ihr oben froh sein werdet. Ein Sonnenuntergang heißt, mit dem schwindenden Licht nach Hause zu wetteifern &mdash; oder das Wettrennen ganz zu streichen, indem ihr oben bleibt. Auch Straßen zählen: Die Mautstraße zu den Drei Zinnen ist im Sommer in den frühen Stunden für den Morgenzugang befahrbar, während die meisten Seilbahnen nur die Tagesmitte bedienen &mdash; genau deshalb sind die bahnabhängigen Orte Abendorte."))
    C.append(fig('01-sonne-aufbruch-nachts-parkplatz.webp',"Gearing up at the trailhead car park in the dark before dawn","Ausrüsten am Ausgangsparkplatz im Dunkeln vor dem Morgengrauen"))
    C.append(p("None of this is meant to scare you off the early start &mdash; it is meant to make it effortless. We carry the plan so you carry nothing but the nerves: we scout, we time, we bring the spare torch and a flask of something warm, and we get you into position with light to spare. Bring a few guests to a sunrise and we brief them too, so the group moves as one in the dark instead of scattering.","Nichts davon soll euch vom frühen Start abschrecken &mdash; es soll ihn mühelos machen. Wir tragen den Plan, damit ihr nichts tragt außer der Aufregung: Wir erkunden, wir timen, wir bringen die Ersatzlampe und eine Thermoskanne mit etwas Warmem und bringen euch mit Licht im Vorrat in Position. Bringt ein paar Gäste zum Sonnenaufgang, briefen wir auch sie, damit die Gruppe im Dunkeln als eine Einheit geht, statt sich zu zerstreuen."))
    C.append(fig('09-sonne-gruppe-im-dunkeln.webp',"The group lit only by a head-torch beam on the dark trail","Die Gruppe nur vom Strahl einer Stirnlampe erhellt auf dem dunklen Weg"))

    C.append(h2('wear','What to wear','Was ihr anzieht'))
    C.append(p("Dress for the hour, not the postcard. At dawn a summit can sit near freezing even in high summer, so we layer: the dress or suit you love, with warm, strippable layers over the top that come off for the frames and go straight back on between them. Good footwear for the walk and the pretty shoes in a bag; gloves and a hat that live in a pocket until the camera is down. Sunset is kinder but not warm &mdash; once the sun goes, the temperature drops fast, so the same rule holds an hour later. We tell you exactly what to expect for your date, your spot and your light.","Kleidet euch für die Stunde, nicht für die Postkarte. Im Morgengrauen kann ein Gipfel selbst im Hochsommer nahe null Grad liegen, deshalb schichten wir: das Kleid oder der Anzug, den ihr liebt, darüber warme, ablegbare Schichten, die für die Bilder herunterkommen und dazwischen sofort wieder an. Gute Schuhe für den Weg und die schönen im Beutel; Handschuhe und Mütze, die in der Tasche wohnen, bis die Kamera unten ist. Der Sonnenuntergang ist milder, aber nicht warm &mdash; sobald die Sonne weg ist, fällt die Temperatur schnell, dieselbe Regel gilt also eine Stunde später. Wir sagen euch für Termin, Ort und Licht genau, was euch erwartet."))
    C.append(fig('05-sonne-umziehen-am-gipfel.webp',"Slipping into the dress at the summit as dawn colours the peaks","Das Kleid am Gipfel angezogen, während der Morgen die Gipfel färbt"))

    C.append(h2('season','How the light shifts by season','Wie sich das Licht mit der Saison ändert'))
    C.append(p("The light itself moves through the year, and it changes the maths. In June the sun is up before 05:30 and sets after 21:00 &mdash; short nights and a brutally early alarm, but the warmest, longest days. By October dawn slips to nearly 07:30 and dusk to around 18:00, which makes a sunrise elopement genuinely civilised and an autumn sunset gorgeously early. The shoulder months trade a little warmth for kinder timings and thinner crowds; deep summer gives you the softest weather and the busiest trails. The table above has the numbers &mdash; we build your morning or evening around them.","Das Licht selbst wandert durchs Jahr und ändert die Rechnung. Im Juni ist die Sonne vor 05:30 Uhr oben und geht nach 21:00 Uhr unter &mdash; kurze Nächte und ein brutal früher Wecker, aber die wärmsten, längsten Tage. Bis Oktober rutscht der Sonnenaufgang auf fast 07:30 Uhr und die Dämmerung auf etwa 18:00 Uhr, was ein Sonnenaufgangs-Elopement wirklich zivilisiert und einen Herbst-Sonnenuntergang herrlich früh macht. Die Übergangsmonate tauschen etwas Wärme gegen freundlichere Zeiten und dünnere Menschenmengen; der Hochsommer gibt euch das mildeste Wetter und die vollsten Wege. Die Tabelle oben hat die Zahlen &mdash; wir bauen euren Morgen oder Abend darum."))

    C.append(h2('after','Blue hour &amp; after','Blaue Stunde &amp; danach'))
    C.append(p("Whichever light you choose, do not pack up when it fades. After sunrise there is a soft, clear morning to enjoy &mdash; a hut breakfast, an empty trail down, the whole day still ahead. After sunset comes blue hour, the cool quiet window when the sky goes deep and the first lights appear in the valley; it is our favourite ten minutes for a last, tender frame before the torches come on. Then the celebration: a rifugio dinner, a drive through the dark passes, or simply the walk down with a new ring and nowhere to be.","Welches Licht ihr auch wählt &mdash; packt nicht ein, wenn es verblasst. Nach dem Sonnenaufgang gibt es einen weichen, klaren Morgen zu genießen &mdash; ein Hüttenfrühstück, einen leeren Weg hinunter, den ganzen Tag noch vor euch. Nach dem Sonnenuntergang kommt die blaue Stunde, das kühle, stille Fenster, wenn der Himmel tief wird und die ersten Lichter im Tal erscheinen; es sind unsere liebsten zehn Minuten für ein letztes, zärtliches Bild, ehe die Lampen angehen. Dann die Feier: ein Hüttenessen, eine Fahrt durch die dunklen Pässe oder einfach der Weg hinunter mit einem neuen Ring und nirgends, wo man sein muss."))
    C.append(fig('17-sonne-untergang-paar-am-horizont.webp',"The couple as a silhouette on the ridge under a wide sunset sky","Das Paar als Silhouette auf dem Grat unter weitem Abendhimmel"))

    faq_html='<h2 id="faq" style="'+H2S+'">'+L('Sunrise or sunset FAQ','FAQ zu Sonnenaufgang oder -untergang')+'</h2>'
    FAQL=[FQ(*x) for x in SUN_FAQ]
    faq_html+=''.join('<div style="margin:1.3em 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:1.1em">'
      f'<h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:20px;margin:0 0 .3em">{q}</h3>'
      f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2);margin:0">{a}</p></div>' for q,a in FAQL)
    faq_ld={"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
      {"@type":"Question","name":_plain(q),"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":_plain(a)}} for q,a in FAQL]}
    related=''.join(story_card(lang,P,STORYBY[sl]) for sl in ex['stories'])
    more=''.join(guide_card(lang,P,x) for x in GUIDES if x['slug']!=slug)
    body=(nav(lang,rel,'howto')+
      f'<section class="page-hero" style="padding:0">{herobg(P,HERO_IMG,g["title"][lang])}'
      f'<div class="content"><div class="wrap"><div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"guide_kick")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h1>{g["title"][lang]}</h1></div></div></section>'
      '<section><div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">'+''.join(C)+faq_html+
      f'<p style="margin-top:2.4em"><a href="{u(P,lang,"how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/")}" class="arrow-link">&larr; {T["nav"]["howto"][lang]}</a></p></div></section>'
      '<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"related_stories")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"related_stories")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{related}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="stories" style="padding-top:clamp(40px,6vw,80px)"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"more_guides")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"more_guides")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{more}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="cta"><div class="wrap row reveal"><div>'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"cta_k")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2 style="margin-top:20px">{t(lang,"cta_h")}</h2></div>'
      f'<a href="{u(P,lang,"get-in-touch/")}" class="btn light">{t(lang,"start_planning")}</a></div></section>'
      +footer(lang,rel))
    write(lang,rel,head(lang,rel,g['title'][lang]+' — Mountain Elopement',g['excerpt'][lang],ld_extra=faq_ld,pre=herolink(P,HERO_IMG))+body+scripts(P))

SPOTS_FAQ=[
 ("What is the most beautiful place in the Dolomites?",
  "There is no single winner, and that is the honest answer. Lago di Braies is the icon &mdash; the turquoise water and wooden boats everyone pictures &mdash; but the Tre Cime di Lavaredo, the Seceda ridge and the little chapel at Passo Giau each win for a different reason. We help you match the place to the mood and effort you want, and to the light on your date.",
  "Was ist der schönste Ort in den Dolomiten?",
  "Es gibt keinen einzelnen Sieger, und das ist die ehrliche Antwort. Der Pragser Wildsee ist die Ikone &mdash; das türkise Wasser und die Holzboote, die sich jeder vorstellt &mdash;, aber die Drei Zinnen, der Seceda-Grat und die kleine Kapelle am Passo Giau gewinnen jeweils aus einem anderen Grund. Wir helfen euch, den Ort auf die Stimmung und den Aufwand abzustimmen, den ihr wollt, und auf das Licht an eurem Datum."),
 ("Do we need a permit or reservation for these spots?",
  "For a small ceremony in open terrain you generally do not need a special permit, but access rules matter. The road to Lago di Braies needs an advance reservation between 09:00 and 16:00 from 1 July to 15 September; several areas are protected nature zones with rules on set-ups; and private drones are banned across much of the range. We check the specific spot before we book it.",
  "Brauchen wir eine Genehmigung oder Reservierung für diese Orte?",
  "Für eine kleine Zeremonie im offenen Gelände braucht ihr in der Regel keine besondere Genehmigung, aber die Zufahrtsregeln zählen. Die Straße zum Pragser Wildsee braucht vom 1. Juli bis 15. September zwischen 09:00 und 16:00 Uhr eine Voranmeldung; mehrere Gebiete sind geschützte Naturzonen mit Regeln für Aufbauten; und private Drohnen sind in weiten Teilen des Massivs verboten. Wir prüfen den konkreten Ort, bevor wir ihn buchen."),
 ("Can we reach these places without a big hike?",
  "Most of them, yes. Lago di Braies, Passo Giau and the Gardena and Sella passes are roadside; the Seceda and other ridges are reached by cable car; only a handful of the hidden lakes, like Sorapis or Lago di Federa, need a real walk. We can build a whole trip that never asks more than a short stroll, or add a hike if you want to earn the view.",
  "Erreichen wir diese Orte ohne große Wanderung?",
  "Die meisten, ja. Der Pragser Wildsee, der Passo Giau sowie das Grödner- und das Sellajoch liegen an der Straße; die Seceda und andere Grate erreicht ihr per Seilbahn; nur eine Handvoll der versteckten Seen wie der Sorapis oder der Lago di Federa brauchen einen echten Weg. Wir bauen euch eine ganze Reise, die nie mehr als einen kurzen Spaziergang verlangt &mdash; oder fügen eine Wanderung hinzu, wenn ihr euch die Aussicht verdienen wollt."),
 ("When is the best time to photograph these spots?",
  "Sunrise, almost always. The icons like Braies and the Tre Cime are magical and empty at first light and busy by mid-morning, so we plan the day around dawn. Autumn adds golden larches and far thinner crowds; deep summer gives the softest weather but the most visitors. We pick the hour and the season together with you.",
  "Wann ist die beste Zeit, diese Orte zu fotografieren?",
  "Der Sonnenaufgang, fast immer. Ikonen wie Braies und die Drei Zinnen sind bei erstem Licht magisch und leer und ab dem späten Vormittag voll, deshalb planen wir den Tag um die Dämmerung. Der Herbst bringt goldene Lärchen und viel dünnere Menschenmengen; der Hochsommer gibt das mildeste Wetter, aber die meisten Besucher. Wir wählen Stunde und Saison gemeinsam mit euch."),
 ("Which spots are best in winter?",
  "The high, jagged places are unforgettable under snow &mdash; the Tre Cime and the snow ridges turn black-and-white and dramatic. The trade-off is access: some toll roads and lifts close or run reduced in winter, and lakes like Braies freeze over. We plan around what is actually open and safe, and winter rewards you with almost total solitude.",
  "Welche Orte sind im Winter am schönsten?",
  "Die hohen, schroffen Orte sind unter Schnee unvergesslich &mdash; die Drei Zinnen und die Schneegrate werden schwarz-weiß und dramatisch. Der Preis ist die Erreichbarkeit: Manche Mautstraßen und Bahnen schließen im Winter oder fahren reduziert, und Seen wie Braies frieren zu. Wir planen um das, was wirklich offen und sicher ist &mdash; und der Winter belohnt euch mit fast völliger Einsamkeit."),
 ("How many spots can we combine in one day?",
  "Fewer than you would think, and that is on purpose. Chasing five locations means seeing none of them properly; we usually plan one hero spot for the best light and perhaps a second, easier one nearby. Over a few days we can string together a proper tour &mdash; a lake at dawn, a pass in the evening, a ridge the next morning.",
  "Wie viele Orte können wir an einem Tag verbinden?",
  "Weniger, als ihr denkt &mdash; und das mit Absicht. Fünf Orte zu jagen heißt, keinen davon richtig zu sehen; wir planen meist einen Haupt-Ort für das beste Licht und vielleicht einen zweiten, leichteren in der Nähe. Über ein paar Tage reihen wir eine richtige Tour aneinander &mdash; ein See im Morgengrauen, ein Pass am Abend, ein Grat am nächsten Morgen."),
]

# --- Dolomites spots guide ES/IT translations (auto-generated, keyed by exact EN string) ---
SPOTS_ES = {
  'Choosing your spot': 'Elegir vuestro lugar',
  'The right spot is not simply the prettiest one; it is the one that fits your day. Some couples want the postcard &mdash; the boats at Braies, the towers of the Tre Cime &mdash; and are happy to rise before dawn to have it empty. Others want a quiet green pass with a chapel and nobody at all. Effort, access, season and light all pull on the choice, so we start from the feeling you are after and work back to the place. Below are the ones we return to again and again, and what each does best.': 'El lugar adecuado no es simplemente el más bonito; es el que encaja con vuestro día. Algunas parejas quieren la postal &mdash; las barcas del Lago di Braies, las torres de las Tre Cime &mdash; y están felices de madrugar para tenerla vacía. Otras quieren un tranquilo puerto verde con una capilla y nadie más. El esfuerzo, el acceso, la estación y la luz tiran todos de la elección, así que partimos de la sensación que buscáis y trabajamos hacia atrás hasta el lugar. Abajo están aquellos a los que volvemos una y otra vez, y lo que cada uno hace mejor.',
  'Lago di Braies &mdash; the icon': 'Lago di Braies &mdash; el icono',
  'If you have seen one photograph of the Dolomites, it was probably here: emerald water, a wall of peaks, and a wooden boathouse lined with rowing boats. Lago di Braies earns the fame &mdash; on a still morning the reflection is perfect and the colour almost unreal &mdash; but that fame is also its catch, because by mid-morning the shoreline is shoulder to shoulder. The whole trick is to be there first, before the day arrives.': 'Si habéis visto una foto de los Dolomitas, probablemente fue aquí: agua esmeralda, una muralla de cumbres y una caseta de madera flanqueada de botes de remos. El Lago di Braies se gana la fama &mdash; en una mañana quieta el reflejo es perfecto y el color casi irreal &mdash;, pero esa fama es también su trampa, porque a media mañana la orilla está hombro con hombro. Todo el truco es estar allí primero, antes de que llegue el día.',
  'The emerald water and peaks of Lago di Braies at first light': 'El agua esmeralda y las cumbres del Lago di Braies con la primera luz',
  'The couple on the Braies boathouse jetty beside the row of wooden boats': 'La pareja en el pantalán de la caseta de Braies junto a la hilera de botes de madera',
  'The boats are the signature. Renting one for a few minutes on the water gives you the frame everyone dreams of &mdash; the two of you adrift on glass, the great cirque rising behind &mdash; and out on the lake you are suddenly alone even when the shore is filling. It is calm, it is easy, and it is worth timing for the moment the peaks catch the first warm light.': 'Las barcas son la firma. Alquilar una unos minutos en el agua os da el encuadre con el que todos sueñan &mdash; los dos a la deriva sobre un cristal, el gran circo alzándose detrás &mdash;, y en el lago estáis de pronto solos aunque la orilla se llene. Es tranquilo, es fácil, y merece la pena calcularlo para el momento en que las cumbres captan la primera luz cálida.',
  'The couple in a wooden boat on the turquoise water of Lago di Braies': 'La pareja en un bote de madera sobre el agua turquesa del Lago di Braies',
  'Visiting Braies right': 'Visitar Braies bien',
  'Come for sunrise. From 1 July to 15 September the access road needs an advance reservation between 09:00 and 16:00, which is another reason we love the dawn window: arrive before it and the lake is yours, the car park is empty and the light is doing its best work. Off-season, and outside those hours, the reservation does not apply &mdash; but the crowds still favour the early riser, so the plan is the same in any month.': 'Venid al amanecer. Del 1 de julio al 15 de septiembre la carretera de acceso necesita una reserva anticipada entre las 09:00 y las 16:00, otra razón por la que amamos la ventana del alba: llegad antes y el lago es vuestro, el aparcamiento está vacío y la luz hace su mejor trabajo. Fuera de temporada, y fuera de esas horas, la reserva no aplica &mdash; pero la gente sigue favoreciendo al madrugador, así que el plan es el mismo en cualquier mes.',
  'The bride on the jetty at dawn, veil and reflection on the mirror-still water': 'La novia en el pantalán al alba, el velo y el reflejo sobre el agua como un espejo',
  'The moored wooden boats and their perfect reflection at Braies': 'Los botes de madera amarrados y su reflejo perfecto en Braies',
  'Practicalities are easy here, which is part of the appeal. There is a historic hotel and a car park right at the shore, the walk to the boathouse is flat and short, and the whole place suits a dress and nice shoes. That accessibility is exactly why Braies is often where we start a couple&rsquo;s first mountain morning &mdash; maximum beauty, minimum effort, before moving somewhere wilder.': 'Lo práctico es fácil aquí, y eso forma parte del encanto. Hay un hotel histórico y un aparcamiento justo en la orilla, el paseo a la caseta es llano y corto, y todo el lugar va bien con un vestido y zapatos bonitos. Esa accesibilidad es justo por lo que Braies suele ser donde empezamos la primera mañana de montaña de una pareja &mdash; máxima belleza, mínimo esfuerzo, antes de ir a algo más salvaje.',
  'The historic hotel at Lago di Braies as the peak behind catches dawn light': 'El hotel histórico del Lago di Braies mientras la cumbre detrás capta la luz del alba',
  'Tre Cime di Lavaredo': 'Tre Cime di Lavaredo',
  'If Braies is beauty, the Tre Cime di Lavaredo are drama: three colossal stone towers standing alone above everything, arguably the most famous silhouette in the Alps. You reach the foot of them by the Auronzo toll road, which in summer is passable in the early hours, so you can drive up in the dark and be there as the first sun turns the rock to fire. Around them a network of easy paths opens ledge after ledge of jaw-dropping foreground &mdash; there is a reason this is the elopement backdrop couples travel continents for.': 'Si Braies es belleza, las Tre Cime di Lavaredo son drama: tres colosales torres de piedra alzándose solas sobre todo, posiblemente la silueta más famosa de los Alpes. Llegáis a su base por la carretera de peaje de Auronzo, que en verano es transitable a primera hora, así que podéis subir a oscuras y estar allí cuando el primer sol vuelve fuego la roca. A su alrededor una red de senderos fáciles abre saliente tras saliente de un primer plano que quita el aliento &mdash; hay una razón por la que este es el telón de fondo de elopement por el que las parejas cruzan continentes.',
  'The couple in the snow as the Tre Cime area spires glow at sunrise': 'La pareja en la nieve mientras las torres de la zona de las Tre Cime brillan al amanecer',
  'In winter the whole scene turns monochrome and almost unearthly &mdash; snow to the horizon, the towers stripped to black and white &mdash; and you may have it entirely to yourselves. It asks for more: warm layers, sure footing, and a close eye on what is open, because the toll road and mountain huts run on reduced winter schedules or close altogether. When it lines up, it is one of the most spectacular things we photograph all year.': 'En invierno toda la escena se vuelve monocroma y casi de otro mundo &mdash; nieve hasta el horizonte, las torres reducidas a blanco y negro &mdash;, y podéis tenerla enteramente para vosotros. Pide más: capas de abrigo, pisada firme y un ojo atento a lo que está abierto, porque la carretera de peaje y los refugios funcionan con horarios reducidos en invierno o cierran del todo. Cuando cuadra, es una de las cosas más espectaculares que fotografiamos en todo el año.',
  'The couple tiny on a snowy ridge beneath the jagged winter peaks': 'La pareja diminuta en una cresta nevada bajo las escarpadas cumbres invernales',
  'Seceda &amp; Val Gardena': 'Seceda y Val Gardena',
  'Above the green valley of Val Gardena rises the Seceda, whose tilted grass ridge and sawtooth skyline are unlike anywhere else in the range &mdash; a giant knife-edge of meadow falling away to the pale Odle peaks. A cable car from Ortisei carries you up, though it opens only around 08:30, so a true Seceda sunrise means a head-torch hike or a night in a rifugio; for golden hour you simply catch it on the way up. The valley itself is a soft, storybook base of villages, spires and pasture.': 'Sobre el verde valle de Val Gardena se alza el Seceda, cuya inclinada cresta de hierba y horizonte dentado no se parecen a nada más en el macizo &mdash; un gigantesco filo de pradera que cae hacia las pálidas cumbres de las Odle. Un teleférico desde Ortisei os sube, aunque abre solo hacia las 08:30, así que un amanecer real en el Seceda implica una subida con frontal o una noche en un refugio; para la hora dorada simplemente lo cogéis de subida. El valle en sí es una base suave y de cuento, de pueblos, campanarios y pastos.',
  'The green sweep of Val Gardena with its villages far below the peaks': 'La verde extensión de Val Gardena con sus pueblos muy por debajo de las cumbres',
  'The Seceda pairs beautifully with the rest of Val Gardena. Ortisei, Santa Cristina and Selva make a comfortable, storybook base &mdash; timber villages with spires and spas, an easy drive from the passes and the cable cars. Many couples stay here for a few days and let us string the sights together: the ridge one morning, a pass at golden hour, a lake at dawn. It is the gentlest way to see a lot of the range without ever feeling rushed.': 'El Seceda combina de maravilla con el resto de Val Gardena. Ortisei, Santa Cristina y Selva forman una base cómoda y de cuento &mdash; pueblos de madera con campanarios y spas, a un cómodo trayecto de los puertos y los teleféricos. Muchas parejas se quedan aquí unos días y nos dejan enlazar los lugares: la cresta una mañana, un puerto en la hora dorada, un lago al alba. Es la forma más suave de ver mucho del macizo sin sentiros nunca apurados.',
  'The Sella group': 'El grupo del Sella',
  'The Sella is a vast fortress of rock ringed by four mountain passes, and its walls make one of the grandest, most accessible backdrops in the Dolomites &mdash; you can stand on soft meadow with a thousand metres of vertical stone behind you, minutes from the car. It is a favourite of ours for a ceremony: enough drama to take the breath away, gentle enough underfoot for a dress, a celebrant and a guest or two. Morning light rakes across the grass and warms the rock beautifully.': 'El Sella es una vasta fortaleza de roca rodeada de cuatro puertos de montaña, y sus paredes forman uno de los telones de fondo más grandiosos y accesibles de los Dolomitas &mdash; podéis estar en pradera blanda con mil metros de piedra vertical detrás, a minutos del coche. Es uno de nuestros favoritos para una ceremonia: bastante drama para dejar sin aliento, bastante suave bajo los pies para un vestido, un oficiante y un invitado o dos. La luz de la mañana rastrilla la hierba y calienta la roca de maravilla.',
  'A small ceremony on the meadow beneath the walls of the Sella group': 'Una pequeña ceremonia en la pradera bajo las paredes del grupo del Sella',
  'Bride and groom on a ridge at first light near the Sella': 'Novia y novio en una cresta con la primera luz cerca del Sella',
  'What we love most about the Sella is how little it asks for how much it gives. From the passes that ring it you are already at over 2,000 metres, so a few steps put you on open meadow with the walls towering overhead &mdash; no scramble, no exposure, just scale. It works in almost any weather, too: even when cloud is draped over the summits, the base of the Sella stays photogenic and grand. For a bad-forecast morning it is one of our most reliable saves.': 'Lo que más amamos del Sella es lo poco que pide para lo mucho que da. Desde los puertos que lo rodean ya estáis a más de 2.000 metros, así que unos pasos os ponen en pradera abierta con las paredes alzándose por encima &mdash; sin trepar, sin exposición, solo escala. Además funciona con casi cualquier tiempo: incluso cuando la nube cubre las cumbres, la base del Sella sigue siendo fotogénica y grandiosa. Para una mañana de mal pronóstico es uno de nuestros rescates más fiables.',
  'The great passes': 'Los grandes puertos',
  'The high passes that link the valleys &mdash; Passo Gardena, Passo Sella, Passo Pordoi &mdash; are the easy secret of the Dolomites: you drive to over 2,000 metres and step straight onto alpine meadow with the giants all around, no climb required. They are perfect for couples who want the high-mountain feeling without the effort, or who are bringing family. In summer they are open and glorious; in the shoulder season they empty out and glow. We often pair a pass at golden hour with a lake at dawn.': 'Los altos puertos que enlazan los valles &mdash; Passo Gardena, Passo Sella, Passo Pordoi &mdash; son el secreto fácil de los Dolomitas: conducís a más de 2.000 metros y salís directamente a pradera alpina con los gigantes alrededor, sin subida. Son perfectos para parejas que quieren la sensación de alta montaña sin el esfuerzo, o que llevan familia. En verano están abiertos y gloriosos; en temporada media se vacían y brillan. A menudo combinamos un puerto en la hora dorada con un lago al alba.',
  'A couple in Tyrolean dress on the meadow at Passo Gardena, peaks and light behind': 'Una pareja en traje tirolés en la pradera del Passo Gardena, cumbres y luz detrás',
  'Passo Giau &amp; Ra Gusela': 'Passo Giau y Ra Gusela',
  'Of all the passes, Passo Giau is the one we lose our hearts to. A little pointed chapel stands on the green saddle, the shark-fin peak of Ra Gusela rises straight behind it, and at dusk the whole amphitheatre of ridges turns molten. It is roadside and easy, yet it feels remote and wild, and the evening light here is some of the best in the Dolomites. For a couple who want drama and a touch of storybook without a hike, it is very hard to beat.': 'De todos los puertos, el Passo Giau es al que le entregamos el corazón. Una pequeña capilla puntiaguda se yergue en el collado verde, la cumbre en aleta de tiburón de la Ra Gusela se alza justo detrás, y al ocaso todo el anfiteatro de crestas se vuelve incandescente. Está junto a la carretera y es fácil, pero se siente remoto y salvaje, y la luz de la tarde aquí es de las mejores de los Dolomitas. Para una pareja que quiere drama y un toque de cuento sin caminata, es muy difícil de superar.',
  'The little pointed chapel at Passo Giau with Ra Gusela rising behind': 'La pequeña capilla puntiaguda del Passo Giau con la Ra Gusela alzándose detrás',
  'The couple on the meadow at Passo Giau under a dramatic evening sky': 'La pareja en la pradera del Passo Giau bajo un dramático cielo de tarde',
  'Because Giau faces the evening light so well, we usually plan it for sunset rather than dawn &mdash; and because it is a mountain pass, it is one of the few icons you can reach easily late in the day. Park, walk a minute onto the meadow, and let the sky do the rest. When the ridges catch the last colour and the chapel goes to silhouette, it is as cinematic as anywhere we work, and you can be back down to a valley dinner within the hour.': 'Como el Giau da tan bien a la luz de la tarde, solemos planificarlo para el atardecer en vez del alba &mdash; y como es un puerto de montaña, es uno de los pocos iconos que podéis alcanzar fácilmente al final del día. Aparcáis, camináis un minuto a la pradera y dejáis que el cielo haga el resto. Cuando las crestas captan el último color y la capilla se vuelve silueta, es tan cinematográfico como cualquier sitio donde trabajamos, y podéis estar de vuelta para una cena en el valle en una hora.',
  'Summits &amp; the small details': 'Cumbres y los pequeños detalles',
  'Beyond the famous names, some of our favourite frames are the quiet ones: a summit cross catching the first light, a bouquet set down on cold rock, a ridge nobody else has a name for. When a spot is too popular to promise privacy, we will often walk five more minutes to a lesser ledge with the same peaks behind it and none of the crowd in front. The Dolomites are generous like that &mdash; the icon is never the only good picture.': 'Más allá de los nombres famosos, algunos de nuestros encuadres favoritos son los tranquilos: una cruz de cumbre captando la primera luz, un ramo posado en roca fría, una cresta que nadie más sabe nombrar. Cuando un lugar es demasiado popular para prometer intimidad, a menudo caminamos cinco minutos más hasta un saliente menor con las mismas cumbres detrás y sin la multitud delante. Los Dolomitas son generosos así &mdash; el icono nunca es la única buena foto.',
  'A bouquet resting on summit rock with misty peaks beyond': 'Un ramo posado sobre roca de cumbre con cumbres brumosas al fondo',
  'Hidden lakes for the adventurous': 'Lagos escondidos para los aventureros',
  'If you are happy to walk, the range hides quieter water that rewards the effort. Lago di Sorapis glows an improbable milky blue at the end of a rocky trail; Lago di Federa sits under the Croda da Lago and turns golden when the surrounding larches do; little Lago d&rsquo;Antorno and Lago di Limides give big reflections for short walks. None of these carry the crowds of Braies, and a ceremony at one of them feels genuinely discovered. Tell us how far you are willing to walk and we will name the one that fits.': 'Si estáis dispuestos a caminar, el macizo esconde aguas más tranquilas que premian el esfuerzo. El Lago di Sorapis brilla de un improbable azul lechoso al final de un sendero rocoso; el Lago di Federa yace bajo la Croda da Lago y se vuelve dorado cuando lo hacen los alerces de alrededor; el pequeño Lago d&rsquo;Antorno y el Lago di Limides dan grandes reflejos para caminatas cortas. Ninguno de ellos carga con las multitudes de Braies, y una ceremonia en uno de ellos se siente genuinamente descubierta. Decidnos hasta dónde estáis dispuestos a caminar y os nombraremos el que encaja.',
  'When to go': 'Cuándo ir',
  'Season changes these places as much as the hour does. <strong>Summer</strong> (June to September) opens every road, lift and hut, and gives green meadows and the warmest light &mdash; but also the fullest car parks. <strong>Autumn</strong> is our quiet favourite: the larches turn gold, the crowds thin, and the low sun flatters the rock, though the first snows can close the highest passes. <strong>Winter</strong> is for the bold &mdash; monochrome, silent, spectacular, with reduced access. Whatever the month, sunrise is the great equaliser: even the busiest icon is calm at first light.': 'La estación cambia estos lugares tanto como la hora. El <strong>verano</strong> (de junio a septiembre) abre todas las carreteras, remontes y refugios, y da praderas verdes y la luz más cálida &mdash; pero también los aparcamientos más llenos. El <strong>otoño</strong> es nuestro favorito tranquilo: los alerces se vuelven dorados, la gente se adelgaza y el sol bajo favorece la roca, aunque las primeras nieves pueden cerrar los puertos más altos. El <strong>invierno</strong> es para los audaces &mdash; monocromo, silencioso, espectacular, con acceso reducido. Sea cual sea el mes, el amanecer es el gran igualador: incluso el icono más concurrido está tranquilo con la primera luz.',
  'How to reach each one': 'Cómo llegar a cada uno',
  'Getting here is easier than the drama suggests. Most couples fly into Venice, Verona or Innsbruck and drive two to three hours in. From a valley base like Cortina, Val Gardena or the Alta Badia, the icons are within an hour: Braies and the passes are roadside, the Seceda and other ridges are a cable car, the Tre Cime a summer toll road, and the hidden lakes a walk. We build the route around the light &mdash; which spot at dawn, which at dusk &mdash; and handle the reservations, the timings and the driving so your morning stays calm.': 'Llegar aquí es más fácil de lo que sugiere el drama. La mayoría de las parejas vuela a Venecia, Verona o Innsbruck y conduce de dos a tres horas. Desde una base en el valle como Cortina, Val Gardena o la Alta Badia, los iconos están a menos de una hora: Braies y los puertos están junto a la carretera, el Seceda y otras crestas son un teleférico, las Tre Cime una carretera de peaje de verano, y los lagos escondidos una caminata. Construimos la ruta en torno a la luz &mdash; qué lugar al alba, cuál al ocaso &mdash; y gestionamos las reservas, los horarios y la conducción para que vuestra mañana siga tranquila.',
  'Where you base yourself shapes the trip. Cortina d&rsquo;Ampezzo sits closest to Braies, the Tre Cime and Passo Giau; Val Gardena and the Alta Badia are best for the Seceda, the Sella and the western passes. We help you pick the base that keeps your chosen spots within an easy dawn drive, book huts where an overnight makes a sunrise possible, and hand you a simple schedule so the only thing you have to think about on the day is each other.': 'Dónde os alojáis marca el viaje. Cortina d&rsquo;Ampezzo es la más cercana a Braies, las Tre Cime y el Passo Giau; Val Gardena y la Alta Badia son mejores para el Seceda, el Sella y los puertos occidentales. Os ayudamos a elegir la base que mantiene vuestros lugares a un cómodo trayecto al alba, reservamos refugios donde una noche hace posible un amanecer, y os entregamos un horario sencillo para que lo único en lo que tengáis que pensar ese día seáis el uno en el otro.',
  'Rules &amp; respect': 'Reglas y respeto',
  'These places stay beautiful because people look after them, and a few rules keep us welcome. The Braies road needs its summer reservation; several areas are protected nature zones where structures and off-path wandering are limited; and private drones are banned across much of the Dolomites, patrolled and fined. On the ground we stay on durable surfaces, keep groups small, leave no trace and never block the very paths we came to photograph. Respect is part of being allowed back &mdash; and it is why we scout and confirm every spot before we bring you to it.': 'Estos lugares siguen siendo bellos porque la gente los cuida, y unas pocas reglas nos mantienen bienvenidos. La carretera de Braies necesita su reserva de verano; varias zonas son zonas naturales protegidas donde las estructuras y el andar fuera de sendero están limitados; y los drones privados están prohibidos en gran parte de los Dolomitas, vigilados y multados. Sobre el terreno permanecemos en superficies resistentes, mantenemos grupos pequeños, no dejamos rastro y nunca bloqueamos los mismos senderos que vinimos a fotografiar. El respeto es parte de que os dejen volver &mdash; y es por lo que exploramos y confirmamos cada lugar antes de llevaros a él.',
  'Lago di Braies': 'Lago di Braies',
  'Seceda & Val Gardena': 'Seceda y Val Gardena',
  'Passo Giau & Ra Gusela': 'Passo Giau y Ra Gusela',
  'Summits & details': 'Cumbres y detalles',
  'Hidden lakes': 'Lagos escondidos',
  'How to reach each': 'Cómo llegar a cada uno',
  'Rules & respect': 'Reglas y respeto',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'Dolomites spots FAQ': 'Preguntas frecuentes sobre los lugares de los Dolomitas',
  'The Dolomites are the most photographed range in Europe, and it is easy to see why: pale limestone towers, turquoise lakes, tiny chapels on high green passes. But the icons come with crowds, and the best of these places reveal themselves only at the right hour. This is our honest field guide to the most beautiful spots for an elopement &mdash; what makes each one special, when to be there, how to reach it, and how to have it, for an hour, almost to yourselves.': 'Los Dolomitas son el macizo más fotografiado de Europa, y es fácil ver por qué: pálidas torres de caliza, lagos turquesa, capillas diminutas en altos puertos verdes. Pero los iconos vienen con multitudes, y lo mejor de estos lugares se revela solo a la hora adecuada. Esta es nuestra guía de campo sincera de los lugares más bellos para un elopement &mdash; qué hace especial a cada uno, cuándo estar allí, cómo llegar y cómo tenerlo, por una hora, casi para vosotros.',
  'On this page': 'En esta página',
}
SPOTS_IT = {
  'Choosing your spot': 'Scegliere il vostro luogo',
  'The right spot is not simply the prettiest one; it is the one that fits your day. Some couples want the postcard &mdash; the boats at Braies, the towers of the Tre Cime &mdash; and are happy to rise before dawn to have it empty. Others want a quiet green pass with a chapel and nobody at all. Effort, access, season and light all pull on the choice, so we start from the feeling you are after and work back to the place. Below are the ones we return to again and again, and what each does best.': "Il luogo giusto non è semplicemente il più bello; è quello che si adatta alla vostra giornata. Alcune coppie vogliono la cartolina &mdash; le barche del Lago di Braies, le torri delle Tre Cime &mdash; e sono felici di alzarsi prima dell'alba per averla vuota. Altre vogliono un tranquillo passo verde con una cappella e nessun altro. Fatica, accesso, stagione e luce tirano tutti sulla scelta, quindi partiamo dalla sensazione che cercate e torniamo indietro fino al luogo. Qui sotto ci sono quelli a cui torniamo di continuo, e ciò che ciascuno fa meglio.",
  'Lago di Braies &mdash; the icon': "Lago di Braies &mdash; l'icona",
  'If you have seen one photograph of the Dolomites, it was probably here: emerald water, a wall of peaks, and a wooden boathouse lined with rowing boats. Lago di Braies earns the fame &mdash; on a still morning the reflection is perfect and the colour almost unreal &mdash; but that fame is also its catch, because by mid-morning the shoreline is shoulder to shoulder. The whole trick is to be there first, before the day arrives.': 'Se avete visto una foto delle Dolomiti, probabilmente era qui: acqua smeraldo, una parete di cime e una casa delle barche in legno fiancheggiata da barche a remi. Il Lago di Braies si merita la fama &mdash; in una mattina ferma il riflesso è perfetto e il colore quasi irreale &mdash;, ma quella fama è anche la sua trappola, perché a metà mattina la riva è spalla a spalla. Tutto il trucco è esserci per primi, prima che arrivi la giornata.',
  'The emerald water and peaks of Lago di Braies at first light': "L'acqua smeraldo e le cime del Lago di Braies alla prima luce",
  'The couple on the Braies boathouse jetty beside the row of wooden boats': 'La coppia sul pontile della casa delle barche di Braies accanto alla fila di barche di legno',
  'The boats are the signature. Renting one for a few minutes on the water gives you the frame everyone dreams of &mdash; the two of you adrift on glass, the great cirque rising behind &mdash; and out on the lake you are suddenly alone even when the shore is filling. It is calm, it is easy, and it is worth timing for the moment the peaks catch the first warm light.': "Le barche sono la firma. Noleggiarne una per pochi minuti sull'acqua vi dà l'inquadratura che tutti sognano &mdash; voi due alla deriva su un vetro, il grande circo che si alza dietro &mdash;, e sul lago siete all'improvviso soli anche quando la riva si riempie. È calmo, è facile, e vale la pena calcolarlo per il momento in cui le cime catturano la prima luce calda.",
  'The couple in a wooden boat on the turquoise water of Lago di Braies': "La coppia in una barca di legno sull'acqua turchese del Lago di Braies",
  'Visiting Braies right': 'Visitare Braies nel modo giusto',
  'Come for sunrise. From 1 July to 15 September the access road needs an advance reservation between 09:00 and 16:00, which is another reason we love the dawn window: arrive before it and the lake is yours, the car park is empty and the light is doing its best work. Off-season, and outside those hours, the reservation does not apply &mdash; but the crowds still favour the early riser, so the plan is the same in any month.': "Venite all'alba. Dal 1° luglio al 15 settembre la strada di accesso richiede una prenotazione anticipata tra le 09:00 e le 16:00, un altro motivo per cui amiamo la finestra dell'alba: arrivate prima e il lago è vostro, il parcheggio è vuoto e la luce fa il suo lavoro migliore. Fuori stagione, e fuori da quegli orari, la prenotazione non si applica &mdash; ma la folla favorisce comunque chi si alza presto, quindi il piano è lo stesso in qualsiasi mese.",
  'The bride on the jetty at dawn, veil and reflection on the mirror-still water': "La sposa sul pontile all'alba, il velo e il riflesso sull'acqua liscia come uno specchio",
  'The moored wooden boats and their perfect reflection at Braies': 'Le barche di legno ormeggiate e il loro riflesso perfetto a Braies',
  'Practicalities are easy here, which is part of the appeal. There is a historic hotel and a car park right at the shore, the walk to the boathouse is flat and short, and the whole place suits a dress and nice shoes. That accessibility is exactly why Braies is often where we start a couple&rsquo;s first mountain morning &mdash; maximum beauty, minimum effort, before moving somewhere wilder.': "Le cose pratiche qui sono facili, e questo fa parte del fascino. C'è un hotel storico e un parcheggio proprio sulla riva, la passeggiata alla casa delle barche è piana e breve, e tutto il luogo si addice a un abito e a scarpe belle. Proprio quell'accessibilità è il motivo per cui Braies è spesso dove iniziamo la prima mattina di montagna di una coppia &mdash; massima bellezza, minima fatica, prima di spostarsi verso qualcosa di più selvaggio.",
  'The historic hotel at Lago di Braies as the peak behind catches dawn light': "L'hotel storico del Lago di Braies mentre la cima dietro cattura la luce dell'alba",
  'Tre Cime di Lavaredo': 'Tre Cime di Lavaredo',
  'If Braies is beauty, the Tre Cime di Lavaredo are drama: three colossal stone towers standing alone above everything, arguably the most famous silhouette in the Alps. You reach the foot of them by the Auronzo toll road, which in summer is passable in the early hours, so you can drive up in the dark and be there as the first sun turns the rock to fire. Around them a network of easy paths opens ledge after ledge of jaw-dropping foreground &mdash; there is a reason this is the elopement backdrop couples travel continents for.': "Se Braies è bellezza, le Tre Cime di Lavaredo sono dramma: tre colossali torri di pietra che si ergono sole sopra tutto, forse la silhouette più famosa delle Alpi. Ne raggiungete il piede con la strada a pedaggio di Auronzo, che in estate è percorribile nelle prime ore, così potete salire al buio ed esserci quando il primo sole incendia la roccia. Attorno a esse una rete di sentieri facili apre lembo dopo lembo di primo piano da togliere il fiato &mdash; c'è un motivo per cui questo è lo sfondo per elopement per cui le coppie attraversano continenti.",
  'The couple in the snow as the Tre Cime area spires glow at sunrise': "La coppia nella neve mentre le torri della zona delle Tre Cime brillano all'alba",
  'In winter the whole scene turns monochrome and almost unearthly &mdash; snow to the horizon, the towers stripped to black and white &mdash; and you may have it entirely to yourselves. It asks for more: warm layers, sure footing, and a close eye on what is open, because the toll road and mountain huts run on reduced winter schedules or close altogether. When it lines up, it is one of the most spectacular things we photograph all year.': "In inverno l'intera scena diventa monocroma e quasi ultraterrena &mdash; neve fino all'orizzonte, le torri ridotte al bianco e nero &mdash;, e potete averla tutta per voi. Chiede di più: strati caldi, passo sicuro e un occhio attento a ciò che è aperto, perché la strada a pedaggio e i rifugi vanno con orari ridotti in inverno o chiudono del tutto. Quando si allinea, è una delle cose più spettacolari che fotografiamo in tutto l'anno.",
  'The couple tiny on a snowy ridge beneath the jagged winter peaks': 'La coppia minuscola su una cresta innevata sotto le frastagliate cime invernali',
  'Seceda &amp; Val Gardena': 'Seceda e Val Gardena',
  'Above the green valley of Val Gardena rises the Seceda, whose tilted grass ridge and sawtooth skyline are unlike anywhere else in the range &mdash; a giant knife-edge of meadow falling away to the pale Odle peaks. A cable car from Ortisei carries you up, though it opens only around 08:30, so a true Seceda sunrise means a head-torch hike or a night in a rifugio; for golden hour you simply catch it on the way up. The valley itself is a soft, storybook base of villages, spires and pasture.': "Sopra la verde Val Gardena si erge la Seceda, la cui cresta erbosa inclinata e lo skyline dentellato non somigliano a nient'altro nel massiccio &mdash; una gigantesca lama di prato che precipita verso le pallide Odle. Una funivia da Ortisei vi porta su, anche se apre solo verso le 08:30, quindi una vera alba sulla Seceda significa una salita con la frontale o una notte in rifugio; per l'ora dorata la prendete semplicemente in salita. La valle stessa è una base morbida e da fiaba, di paesi, campanili e pascoli.",
  'The green sweep of Val Gardena with its villages far below the peaks': "L'ampia distesa verde della Val Gardena con i suoi paesi molto sotto le cime",
  'The Seceda pairs beautifully with the rest of Val Gardena. Ortisei, Santa Cristina and Selva make a comfortable, storybook base &mdash; timber villages with spires and spas, an easy drive from the passes and the cable cars. Many couples stay here for a few days and let us string the sights together: the ridge one morning, a pass at golden hour, a lake at dawn. It is the gentlest way to see a lot of the range without ever feeling rushed.': "La Seceda si sposa magnificamente con il resto della Val Gardena. Ortisei, Santa Cristina e Selva formano una base comoda e da fiaba &mdash; paesi di legno con campanili e spa, a una comoda distanza in auto dai passi e dalle funivie. Molte coppie restano qui qualche giorno e ci lasciano infilare le mete una dopo l'altra: la cresta una mattina, un passo all'ora dorata, un lago all'alba. È il modo più dolce per vedere molto del massiccio senza sentirvi mai di fretta.",
  'The Sella group': 'Il gruppo del Sella',
  'The Sella is a vast fortress of rock ringed by four mountain passes, and its walls make one of the grandest, most accessible backdrops in the Dolomites &mdash; you can stand on soft meadow with a thousand metres of vertical stone behind you, minutes from the car. It is a favourite of ours for a ceremony: enough drama to take the breath away, gentle enough underfoot for a dress, a celebrant and a guest or two. Morning light rakes across the grass and warms the rock beautifully.': "Il Sella è una vasta fortezza di roccia cinta da quattro passi di montagna, e le sue pareti formano uno degli sfondi più grandiosi e accessibili delle Dolomiti &mdash; potete stare su un morbido prato con mille metri di pietra verticale alle spalle, a minuti dall'auto. È uno dei nostri preferiti per una cerimonia: abbastanza dramma da togliere il fiato, abbastanza dolce sotto i piedi per un abito, un celebrante e un invitato o due. La luce del mattino rastrella l'erba e scalda la roccia magnificamente.",
  'A small ceremony on the meadow beneath the walls of the Sella group': 'Una piccola cerimonia sul prato sotto le pareti del gruppo del Sella',
  'Bride and groom on a ridge at first light near the Sella': 'Sposa e sposo su una cresta alla prima luce vicino al Sella',
  'What we love most about the Sella is how little it asks for how much it gives. From the passes that ring it you are already at over 2,000 metres, so a few steps put you on open meadow with the walls towering overhead &mdash; no scramble, no exposure, just scale. It works in almost any weather, too: even when cloud is draped over the summits, the base of the Sella stays photogenic and grand. For a bad-forecast morning it is one of our most reliable saves.': 'Ciò che amiamo di più del Sella è quanto poco chiede per quanto dà. Dai passi che lo cingono siete già a oltre 2.000 metri, quindi pochi passi vi mettono su prato aperto con le pareti che torreggiano sopra &mdash; niente arrampicata, niente esposizione, solo dimensione. Funziona anche con quasi ogni tempo: perfino quando la nube è drappeggiata sulle vette, il piede del Sella resta fotogenico e grandioso. Per una mattina con brutta previsione è una delle nostre salvezze più affidabili.',
  'The great passes': 'I grandi passi',
  'The high passes that link the valleys &mdash; Passo Gardena, Passo Sella, Passo Pordoi &mdash; are the easy secret of the Dolomites: you drive to over 2,000 metres and step straight onto alpine meadow with the giants all around, no climb required. They are perfect for couples who want the high-mountain feeling without the effort, or who are bringing family. In summer they are open and glorious; in the shoulder season they empty out and glow. We often pair a pass at golden hour with a lake at dawn.': "Gli alti passi che collegano le valli &mdash; Passo Gardena, Passo Sella, Passo Pordoi &mdash; sono il facile segreto delle Dolomiti: guidate a oltre 2.000 metri e uscite dritti sul prato alpino con i giganti tutt'intorno, senza salita. Sono perfetti per le coppie che vogliono la sensazione dell'alta montagna senza la fatica, o che portano la famiglia. In estate sono aperti e gloriosi; nella mezza stagione si svuotano e brillano. Spesso abbiniamo un passo all'ora dorata con un lago all'alba.",
  'A couple in Tyrolean dress on the meadow at Passo Gardena, peaks and light behind': 'Una coppia in abito tirolese sul prato del Passo Gardena, cime e luce dietro',
  'Passo Giau &amp; Ra Gusela': 'Passo Giau e Ra Gusela',
  'Of all the passes, Passo Giau is the one we lose our hearts to. A little pointed chapel stands on the green saddle, the shark-fin peak of Ra Gusela rises straight behind it, and at dusk the whole amphitheatre of ridges turns molten. It is roadside and easy, yet it feels remote and wild, and the evening light here is some of the best in the Dolomites. For a couple who want drama and a touch of storybook without a hike, it is very hard to beat.': "Di tutti i passi, il Passo Giau è quello a cui perdiamo il cuore. Una piccola cappella a punta sorge sulla verde sella, la vetta a pinna di squalo della Ra Gusela si alza proprio dietro, e al crepuscolo l'intero anfiteatro di creste diventa incandescente. È sul ciglio della strada e facile, eppure sembra remoto e selvaggio, e la luce della sera qui è tra le migliori delle Dolomiti. Per una coppia che vuole dramma e un tocco di fiaba senza camminata, è davvero difficile da battere.",
  'The little pointed chapel at Passo Giau with Ra Gusela rising behind': 'La piccola cappella a punta del Passo Giau con la Ra Gusela che si alza dietro',
  'The couple on the meadow at Passo Giau under a dramatic evening sky': 'La coppia sul prato del Passo Giau sotto un drammatico cielo serale',
  'Because Giau faces the evening light so well, we usually plan it for sunset rather than dawn &mdash; and because it is a mountain pass, it is one of the few icons you can reach easily late in the day. Park, walk a minute onto the meadow, and let the sky do the rest. When the ridges catch the last colour and the chapel goes to silhouette, it is as cinematic as anywhere we work, and you can be back down to a valley dinner within the hour.': "Poiché il Giau si affaccia così bene alla luce della sera, di solito lo pianifichiamo per il tramonto invece che per l'alba &mdash; e poiché è un passo di montagna, è una delle poche icone che potete raggiungere facilmente a fine giornata. Parcheggiate, camminate un minuto sul prato e lasciate che il cielo faccia il resto. Quando le creste catturano l'ultimo colore e la cappella diventa silhouette, è cinematografico come ovunque lavoriamo, e potete essere di ritorno per una cena in valle entro un'ora.",
  'Summits &amp; the small details': 'Vette e i piccoli dettagli',
  'Beyond the famous names, some of our favourite frames are the quiet ones: a summit cross catching the first light, a bouquet set down on cold rock, a ridge nobody else has a name for. When a spot is too popular to promise privacy, we will often walk five more minutes to a lesser ledge with the same peaks behind it and none of the crowd in front. The Dolomites are generous like that &mdash; the icon is never the only good picture.': "Oltre ai nomi famosi, alcune delle nostre inquadrature preferite sono quelle quiete: una croce di vetta che cattura la prima luce, un bouquet posato su roccia fredda, una cresta che nessun altro sa nominare. Quando un luogo è troppo popolare per promettere privacy, spesso camminiamo cinque minuti in più fino a un lembo minore con le stesse cime dietro e nessuna folla davanti. Le Dolomiti sono generose così &mdash; l'icona non è mai l'unica buona foto.",
  'A bouquet resting on summit rock with misty peaks beyond': 'Un bouquet posato su roccia di vetta con cime nebbiose sullo sfondo',
  'Hidden lakes for the adventurous': 'Laghi nascosti per gli avventurosi',
  'If you are happy to walk, the range hides quieter water that rewards the effort. Lago di Sorapis glows an improbable milky blue at the end of a rocky trail; Lago di Federa sits under the Croda da Lago and turns golden when the surrounding larches do; little Lago d&rsquo;Antorno and Lago di Limides give big reflections for short walks. None of these carry the crowds of Braies, and a ceremony at one of them feels genuinely discovered. Tell us how far you are willing to walk and we will name the one that fits.': 'Se siete disposti a camminare, il massiccio nasconde acque più quiete che ripagano la fatica. Il Lago di Sorapis brilla di un improbabile azzurro lattiginoso al termine di un sentiero roccioso; il Lago di Federa giace sotto la Croda da Lago e diventa dorato quando lo fanno i larici circostanti; il piccolo Lago d&rsquo;Antorno e il Lago di Limides regalano grandi riflessi per brevi camminate. Nessuno di questi porta le folle di Braies, e una cerimonia a uno di essi sembra davvero una scoperta. Diteci fino a dove siete disposti a camminare e vi nomineremo quello giusto.',
  'When to go': 'Quando andare',
  'Season changes these places as much as the hour does. <strong>Summer</strong> (June to September) opens every road, lift and hut, and gives green meadows and the warmest light &mdash; but also the fullest car parks. <strong>Autumn</strong> is our quiet favourite: the larches turn gold, the crowds thin, and the low sun flatters the rock, though the first snows can close the highest passes. <strong>Winter</strong> is for the bold &mdash; monochrome, silent, spectacular, with reduced access. Whatever the month, sunrise is the great equaliser: even the busiest icon is calm at first light.': "La stagione cambia questi luoghi tanto quanto l'ora. L'<strong>estate</strong> (da giugno a settembre) apre ogni strada, impianto e rifugio, e dà prati verdi e la luce più calda &mdash; ma anche i parcheggi più pieni. L'<strong>autunno</strong> è il nostro preferito tranquillo: i larici diventano dorati, la folla si dirada e il sole basso lusinga la roccia, anche se le prime nevi possono chiudere i passi più alti. L'<strong>inverno</strong> è per gli audaci &mdash; monocromo, silenzioso, spettacolare, con accesso ridotto. Qualunque sia il mese, l'alba è il grande livellatore: perfino l'icona più affollata è quieta alla prima luce.",
  'How to reach each one': 'Come raggiungere ciascuno',
  'Getting here is easier than the drama suggests. Most couples fly into Venice, Verona or Innsbruck and drive two to three hours in. From a valley base like Cortina, Val Gardena or the Alta Badia, the icons are within an hour: Braies and the passes are roadside, the Seceda and other ridges are a cable car, the Tre Cime a summer toll road, and the hidden lakes a walk. We build the route around the light &mdash; which spot at dawn, which at dusk &mdash; and handle the reservations, the timings and the driving so your morning stays calm.': "Arrivare qui è più facile di quanto suggerisca il dramma. La maggior parte delle coppie atterra a Venezia, Verona o Innsbruck e guida due o tre ore verso l'interno. Da una base di valle come Cortina, la Val Gardena o l'Alta Badia, le icone sono entro un'ora: Braies e i passi sono sul ciglio della strada, la Seceda e altre creste sono una funivia, le Tre Cime una strada a pedaggio estiva e i laghi nascosti una camminata. Costruiamo il percorso attorno alla luce &mdash; quale luogo all'alba, quale al tramonto &mdash; e gestiamo le prenotazioni, gli orari e la guida così la vostra mattina resta serena.",
  'Where you base yourself shapes the trip. Cortina d&rsquo;Ampezzo sits closest to Braies, the Tre Cime and Passo Giau; Val Gardena and the Alta Badia are best for the Seceda, the Sella and the western passes. We help you pick the base that keeps your chosen spots within an easy dawn drive, book huts where an overnight makes a sunrise possible, and hand you a simple schedule so the only thing you have to think about on the day is each other.': "Dove vi basate plasma il viaggio. Cortina d&rsquo;Ampezzo è la più vicina a Braies, alle Tre Cime e al Passo Giau; la Val Gardena e l'Alta Badia sono le migliori per la Seceda, il Sella e i passi occidentali. Vi aiutiamo a scegliere la base che tiene i vostri luoghi a una comoda distanza all'alba, prenotiamo rifugi dove un pernottamento rende possibile un'alba, e vi consegniamo un programma semplice così l'unica cosa a cui dovete pensare quel giorno siete l'un l'altra.",
  'Rules &amp; respect': 'Regole e rispetto',
  'These places stay beautiful because people look after them, and a few rules keep us welcome. The Braies road needs its summer reservation; several areas are protected nature zones where structures and off-path wandering are limited; and private drones are banned across much of the Dolomites, patrolled and fined. On the ground we stay on durable surfaces, keep groups small, leave no trace and never block the very paths we came to photograph. Respect is part of being allowed back &mdash; and it is why we scout and confirm every spot before we bring you to it.': 'Questi luoghi restano belli perché le persone se ne prendono cura, e poche regole ci tengono benvenuti. La strada di Braies richiede la sua prenotazione estiva; diverse aree sono zone naturali protette dove strutture e camminare fuori sentiero sono limitati; e i droni privati sono vietati in gran parte delle Dolomiti, sorvegliati e multati. A terra restiamo su superfici resistenti, teniamo i gruppi piccoli, non lasciamo tracce e non blocchiamo mai proprio i sentieri che siamo venuti a fotografare. Il rispetto fa parte del poter tornare &mdash; ed è per questo che perlustriamo e confermiamo ogni luogo prima di portarvici.',
  'Lago di Braies': 'Lago di Braies',
  'Seceda & Val Gardena': 'Seceda e Val Gardena',
  'Passo Giau & Ra Gusela': 'Passo Giau e Ra Gusela',
  'Summits & details': 'Vette e dettagli',
  'Hidden lakes': 'Laghi nascosti',
  'How to reach each': 'Come raggiungere ciascuno',
  'Rules & respect': 'Regole e rispetto',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'Dolomites spots FAQ': 'Domande frequenti sui luoghi delle Dolomiti',
  'The Dolomites are the most photographed range in Europe, and it is easy to see why: pale limestone towers, turquoise lakes, tiny chapels on high green passes. But the icons come with crowds, and the best of these places reveal themselves only at the right hour. This is our honest field guide to the most beautiful spots for an elopement &mdash; what makes each one special, when to be there, how to reach it, and how to have it, for an hour, almost to yourselves.': "Le Dolomiti sono il massiccio più fotografato d'Europa, ed è facile capire perché: pallide torri di calcare, laghi turchesi, minuscole cappelle su alti passi verdi. Ma le icone vengono con la folla, e il meglio di questi luoghi si rivela solo all'ora giusta. Questa è la nostra onesta guida sul campo ai luoghi più belli per un elopement &mdash; cosa rende speciale ciascuno, quando esserci, come arrivarci e come averlo, per un'ora, quasi tutto per voi.",
  'On this page': 'In questa pagina',
}
SPOTS_FAQ_ES = {
  'What is the most beautiful place in the Dolomites?': ('¿Cuál es el lugar más bello de los Dolomitas?', 'No hay un único ganador, y esa es la respuesta sincera. El Lago di Braies es el icono &mdash; el agua turquesa y los botes de madera que todos imaginan &mdash;, pero las Tre Cime di Lavaredo, la cresta del Seceda y la pequeña capilla del Passo Giau ganan cada una por una razón distinta. Os ayudamos a ajustar el lugar al ánimo y el esfuerzo que queréis, y a la luz de vuestra fecha.'),
  'Do we need a permit or reservation for these spots?': ('¿Necesitamos permiso o reserva para estos lugares?', 'Para una pequeña ceremonia en terreno abierto en general no necesitáis un permiso especial, pero las reglas de acceso importan. La carretera al Lago di Braies necesita una reserva anticipada entre las 09:00 y las 16:00 del 1 de julio al 15 de septiembre; varias zonas son áreas naturales protegidas con reglas sobre montajes; y los drones privados están prohibidos en gran parte del macizo. Comprobamos el lugar concreto antes de reservarlo.'),
  'Can we reach these places without a big hike?': ('¿Podemos llegar a estos sitios sin una gran caminata?', 'A la mayoría, sí. El Lago di Braies, el Passo Giau y los puertos de Gardena y Sella están junto a la carretera; el Seceda y otras crestas se alcanzan en teleférico; solo un puñado de los lagos escondidos, como el Sorapis o el Lago di Federa, necesitan un paseo de verdad. Podemos armar un viaje entero que nunca pida más que un corto paseo, o añadir una caminata si queréis ganaros la vista.'),
  'When is the best time to photograph these spots?': ('¿Cuándo es el mejor momento para fotografiar estos lugares?', 'El amanecer, casi siempre. Los iconos como Braies y las Tre Cime son mágicos y vacíos con la primera luz y concurridos a media mañana, así que planificamos el día en torno al alba. El otoño añade alerces dorados y multitudes mucho más finas; el pleno verano da el clima más suave pero los más visitantes. Elegimos la hora y la estación junto a vosotros.'),
  'Which spots are best in winter?': ('¿Qué lugares son mejores en invierno?', 'Los sitios altos y escarpados son inolvidables bajo la nieve &mdash; las Tre Cime y las crestas nevadas se vuelven blanco y negro y dramáticas. A cambio está el acceso: algunas carreteras de peaje y teleféricos cierran o funcionan reducidos en invierno, y lagos como Braies se hielan. Planificamos en torno a lo que está de verdad abierto y seguro, y el invierno os premia con una soledad casi total.'),
  'How many spots can we combine in one day?': ('¿Cuántos lugares podemos combinar en un día?', 'Menos de los que pensáis, y es a propósito. Perseguir cinco sitios significa no ver ninguno bien; solemos planificar un lugar principal para la mejor luz y quizá un segundo, más fácil, cerca. A lo largo de unos días podemos enlazar una verdadera ruta &mdash; un lago al alba, un puerto por la tarde, una cresta a la mañana siguiente.'),
}
SPOTS_FAQ_IT = {
  'What is the most beautiful place in the Dolomites?': ('Qual è il luogo più bello delle Dolomiti?', "Non c'è un unico vincitore, ed è la risposta onesta. Il Lago di Braies è l'icona &mdash; l'acqua turchese e le barche di legno che tutti immaginano &mdash;, ma le Tre Cime di Lavaredo, la cresta della Seceda e la piccola cappella del Passo Giau vincono ciascuna per un motivo diverso. Vi aiutiamo ad abbinare il luogo all'atmosfera e alla fatica che volete, e alla luce della vostra data."),
  'Do we need a permit or reservation for these spots?': ('Serve un permesso o una prenotazione per questi luoghi?', 'Per una piccola cerimonia in terreno aperto in genere non serve un permesso speciale, ma le regole di accesso contano. La strada per il Lago di Braies richiede una prenotazione anticipata tra le 09:00 e le 16:00 dal 1° luglio al 15 settembre; diverse aree sono zone naturali protette con regole sugli allestimenti; e i droni privati sono vietati in gran parte del massiccio. Controlliamo il luogo specifico prima di prenotarlo.'),
  'Can we reach these places without a big hike?': ('Possiamo raggiungere questi posti senza una grande camminata?', "La maggior parte, sì. Il Lago di Braies, il Passo Giau e i passi Gardena e Sella sono sul ciglio della strada; la Seceda e altre creste si raggiungono in funivia; solo una manciata dei laghi nascosti, come il Sorapis o il Lago di Federa, richiedono una vera camminata. Possiamo costruire un intero viaggio che non chieda mai più di una breve passeggiata, o aggiungere un'escursione se volete guadagnarvi la vista."),
  'When is the best time to photograph these spots?': ('Qual è il momento migliore per fotografare questi luoghi?', "L'alba, quasi sempre. Le icone come Braies e le Tre Cime sono magiche e vuote alla prima luce e affollate a metà mattina, quindi pianifichiamo la giornata attorno all'alba. L'autunno aggiunge larici dorati e folla molto più rada; la piena estate dà il tempo più mite ma i più visitatori. Scegliamo l'ora e la stagione insieme a voi."),
  'Which spots are best in winter?': ('Quali luoghi sono migliori in inverno?', "I luoghi alti e frastagliati sono indimenticabili sotto la neve &mdash; le Tre Cime e le creste innevate diventano bianco e nero e drammatiche. In cambio c'è l'accesso: alcune strade a pedaggio e funivie chiudono o vanno ridotte in inverno, e laghi come Braies gelano. Pianifichiamo attorno a ciò che è davvero aperto e sicuro, e l'inverno vi premia con una solitudine quasi totale."),
  'How many spots can we combine in one day?': ('Quanti luoghi possiamo combinare in un giorno?', "Meno di quanto pensiate, ed è di proposito. Inseguire cinque posti significa non vederne bene nessuno; di solito pianifichiamo un luogo principale per la luce migliore e forse un secondo, più facile, vicino. Nell'arco di qualche giorno possiamo mettere insieme un vero tour &mdash; un lago all'alba, un passo la sera, una cresta la mattina dopo."),
}

def build_spots_guide(lang):
    slug='most-beautiful-dolomites-spots'
    g=next(x for x in GUIDES if x['slug']==slug); ex=GUIDE_EXTRA[slug]
    rel='how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/'+slug+'/'; P=prefix(lang,rel)
    DE=(lang=='de')
    def L(en,de):
        if lang=='de': return de
        if lang=='es': return SPOTS_ES.get(en,en)
        if lang=='it': return SPOTS_IT.get(en,en)
        return en
    def FQ(qen,aen,qde,ade):
        if lang=='de': return (qde,ade)
        if lang=='es': return SPOTS_FAQ_ES.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        if lang=='it': return SPOTS_FAQ_IT.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        return (qen,aen)
    GI=f'{P}img/guide-dolomites-spots/'; GIREL='img/guide-dolomites-spots/'; HERO_IMG='img/guide-dolomites-spots/03-spots-braies-ruderboot-paar.webp'
    H2S='font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,3vw,36px);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:1.7em 0 .4em;scroll-margin-top:96px'
    def h2(i,en,de): return f'<h2 id="{i}" style="{H2S}">{L(en,de)}</h2>'
    def p(en,de): return f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2)">{L(en,de)}</p>'
    def fig(name,en,de): return '<figure class="guide-fig">'+bild(P,GIREL+name,L(en,de),sizes='(max-width:820px) 100vw, 820px')+'</figure>'
    toc=[('what',L('Choosing your spot','Den Ort wählen')),('braies',L('Lago di Braies','Pragser Wildsee')),
         ('braies-when',L('Visiting Braies right','Braies richtig besuchen')),('tre-cime',L('Tre Cime di Lavaredo','Drei Zinnen')),
         ('gardena',L('Seceda & Val Gardena','Seceda & Gröden')),('sella',L('The Sella group','Die Sellagruppe')),
         ('passes',L('The great passes','Die großen Pässe')),('giau',L('Passo Giau & Ra Gusela','Passo Giau & Ra Gusela')),
         ('summits',L('Summits & details','Gipfel & Details')),('hidden',L('Hidden lakes','Versteckte Seen')),
         ('when',L('When to go','Wann')),('reach',L('How to reach each','So kommt ihr hin')),
         ('rules',L('Rules & respect','Regeln & Respekt')),('faq',L('FAQ','FAQ'))]
    toc_html=('<nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'"><div class="cap">'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'</div><ol>'
      +''.join(f'<li><a href="#{i}">{lbl}</a></li>' for i,lbl in toc)+'</ol></nav>')
    facts='<div class="facts">'+''.join(f'<div class="fct"><div class="fl">{LBL[k][lang]}</div><div class="fv">{val[lang]}</div></div>' for k,val in ex['facts'])+'</div>'
    C=[]
    C.append(f'<p class="lead">{L("The Dolomites are the most photographed range in Europe, and it is easy to see why: pale limestone towers, turquoise lakes, tiny chapels on high green passes. But the icons come with crowds, and the best of these places reveal themselves only at the right hour. This is our honest field guide to the most beautiful spots for an elopement &mdash; what makes each one special, when to be there, how to reach it, and how to have it, for an hour, almost to yourselves.","Die Dolomiten sind das meistfotografierte Massiv Europas, und man sieht leicht, warum: bleiche Kalktürme, türkise Seen, winzige Kapellen auf hohen grünen Pässen. Doch die Ikonen kommen mit Menschenmengen, und das Beste dieser Orte zeigt sich nur zur richtigen Stunde. Das ist unser ehrlicher Feldführer zu den schönsten Orten für ein Elopement &mdash; was jeden besonders macht, wann ihr dort sein solltet, wie ihr hinkommt und wie ihr ihn für eine Stunde fast für euch allein habt.")}</p>')
    C.append(f'<div class="cap" style="margin:0 0 -14px">{t(lang,"quick_facts")}</div>{facts}')
    C.append(toc_html)

    C.append(h2('what','Choosing your spot','Den Ort wählen'))
    C.append(p("The right spot is not simply the prettiest one; it is the one that fits your day. Some couples want the postcard &mdash; the boats at Braies, the towers of the Tre Cime &mdash; and are happy to rise before dawn to have it empty. Others want a quiet green pass with a chapel and nobody at all. Effort, access, season and light all pull on the choice, so we start from the feeling you are after and work back to the place. Below are the ones we return to again and again, and what each does best.","Der richtige Ort ist nicht einfach der hübscheste &mdash; es ist der, der zu eurem Tag passt. Manche Paare wollen die Postkarte &mdash; die Boote am Pragser Wildsee, die Türme der Drei Zinnen &mdash; und stehen gern vor der Dämmerung auf, um sie leer zu haben. Andere wollen einen stillen grünen Pass mit einer Kapelle und niemandem sonst. Aufwand, Erreichbarkeit, Saison und Licht ziehen alle an der Wahl, deshalb starten wir von dem Gefühl, das ihr sucht, und arbeiten uns zum Ort zurück. Unten stehen die, zu denen wir immer wieder zurückkehren, und was jeder am besten kann."))

    C.append(h2('braies','Lago di Braies &mdash; the icon','Pragser Wildsee &mdash; die Ikone'))
    C.append(p("If you have seen one photograph of the Dolomites, it was probably here: emerald water, a wall of peaks, and a wooden boathouse lined with rowing boats. Lago di Braies earns the fame &mdash; on a still morning the reflection is perfect and the colour almost unreal &mdash; but that fame is also its catch, because by mid-morning the shoreline is shoulder to shoulder. The whole trick is to be there first, before the day arrives.","Wenn ihr ein Foto der Dolomiten gesehen habt, war es wahrscheinlich hier: smaragdgrünes Wasser, eine Gipfelwand und ein hölzernes Bootshaus, gesäumt von Ruderbooten. Der Pragser Wildsee verdient den Ruhm &mdash; an einem stillen Morgen ist die Spiegelung perfekt und die Farbe fast unwirklich &mdash;, doch dieser Ruhm ist auch sein Haken, denn ab dem späten Vormittag steht man am Ufer Schulter an Schulter. Der ganze Trick ist, zuerst da zu sein, ehe der Tag ankommt."))
    C.append(fig('01-spots-lago-di-braies-see.webp',"The emerald water and peaks of Lago di Braies at first light","Das smaragdgrüne Wasser und die Gipfel des Pragser Wildsees bei erstem Licht"))
    C.append(fig('02-spots-braies-bootshaus-steg.webp',"The couple on the Braies boathouse jetty beside the row of wooden boats","Das Paar auf dem Bootshaus-Steg von Braies neben der Reihe der Holzboote"))
    C.append(p("The boats are the signature. Renting one for a few minutes on the water gives you the frame everyone dreams of &mdash; the two of you adrift on glass, the great cirque rising behind &mdash; and out on the lake you are suddenly alone even when the shore is filling. It is calm, it is easy, and it is worth timing for the moment the peaks catch the first warm light.","Die Boote sind das Markenzeichen. Eines für ein paar Minuten auf dem Wasser zu mieten, schenkt euch das Bild, von dem alle träumen &mdash; ihr beide treibend auf Glas, der große Talkessel dahinter aufragend &mdash;, und draußen auf dem See seid ihr plötzlich allein, selbst wenn sich das Ufer füllt. Es ist ruhig, es ist leicht, und es lohnt sich, es auf den Moment zu legen, in dem die Gipfel das erste warme Licht fangen."))
    C.append(fig('04-spots-braies-boot-tuerkis.webp',"The couple in a wooden boat on the turquoise water of Lago di Braies","Das Paar in einem Holzboot auf dem türkisen Wasser des Pragser Wildsees"))

    C.append(h2('braies-when','Visiting Braies right','Braies richtig besuchen'))
    C.append(p("Come for sunrise. From 1 July to 15 September the access road needs an advance reservation between 09:00 and 16:00, which is another reason we love the dawn window: arrive before it and the lake is yours, the car park is empty and the light is doing its best work. Off-season, and outside those hours, the reservation does not apply &mdash; but the crowds still favour the early riser, so the plan is the same in any month.","Kommt zum Sonnenaufgang. Vom 1. Juli bis 15. September braucht die Zufahrtsstraße zwischen 09:00 und 16:00 Uhr eine Voranmeldung, ein weiterer Grund, warum wir das Morgenfenster lieben: Kommt davor an, und der See gehört euch, der Parkplatz ist leer und das Licht leistet seine beste Arbeit. Außerhalb der Saison und außerhalb dieser Zeiten gilt die Reservierung nicht &mdash; doch der Andrang begünstigt weiterhin den Frühaufsteher, also ist der Plan in jedem Monat derselbe."))
    C.append(fig('05-spots-braies-steg-braut.webp',"The bride on the jetty at dawn, veil and reflection on the mirror-still water","Die Braut auf dem Steg im Morgengrauen, Schleier und Spiegelung auf dem spiegelglatten Wasser"))
    C.append(fig('06-spots-braies-boote-spiegelung.webp',"The moored wooden boats and their perfect reflection at Braies","Die vertäuten Holzboote und ihre perfekte Spiegelung am Pragser Wildsee"))
    C.append(p("Practicalities are easy here, which is part of the appeal. There is a historic hotel and a car park right at the shore, the walk to the boathouse is flat and short, and the whole place suits a dress and nice shoes. That accessibility is exactly why Braies is often where we start a couple&rsquo;s first mountain morning &mdash; maximum beauty, minimum effort, before moving somewhere wilder.","Das Praktische ist hier einfach, und das ist Teil des Reizes. Es gibt ein historisches Hotel und einen Parkplatz direkt am Ufer, der Weg zum Bootshaus ist flach und kurz, und der ganze Ort passt zu Kleid und schönen Schuhen. Genau diese Erreichbarkeit ist der Grund, warum Braies oft dort ist, wo wir den ersten Bergmorgen eines Paares beginnen &mdash; maximale Schönheit, minimaler Aufwand, ehe es irgendwohin Wilderes geht."))
    C.append(fig('07-spots-braies-hotel-morgens.webp',"The historic hotel at Lago di Braies as the peak behind catches dawn light","Das historische Hotel am Pragser Wildsee, während der Gipfel dahinter das Morgenlicht fängt"))

    C.append(h2('tre-cime','Tre Cime di Lavaredo','Die Drei Zinnen'))
    C.append(p("If Braies is beauty, the Tre Cime di Lavaredo are drama: three colossal stone towers standing alone above everything, arguably the most famous silhouette in the Alps. You reach the foot of them by the Auronzo toll road, which in summer is passable in the early hours, so you can drive up in the dark and be there as the first sun turns the rock to fire. Around them a network of easy paths opens ledge after ledge of jaw-dropping foreground &mdash; there is a reason this is the elopement backdrop couples travel continents for.","Ist Braies Schönheit, sind die Drei Zinnen Dramatik: drei kolossale Steintürme, die allein über allem stehen &mdash; wohl die berühmteste Silhouette der Alpen. Ihren Fuß erreicht ihr über die Auronzo-Mautstraße, die im Sommer in den frühen Stunden befahrbar ist, ihr könnt also im Dunkeln hinauffahren und da sein, wenn die erste Sonne den Fels in Brand setzt. Rund um sie öffnet ein Netz leichter Wege Band um Band atemberaubenden Vordergrunds &mdash; es gibt einen Grund, warum Paare für diese Elopement-Kulisse über Kontinente reisen."))
    C.append(fig('08-spots-drei-zinnen-winter.webp',"The couple in the snow as the Tre Cime area spires glow at sunrise","Das Paar im Schnee, während die Türme rund um die Drei Zinnen im Sonnenaufgang glühen"))
    C.append(p("In winter the whole scene turns monochrome and almost unearthly &mdash; snow to the horizon, the towers stripped to black and white &mdash; and you may have it entirely to yourselves. It asks for more: warm layers, sure footing, and a close eye on what is open, because the toll road and mountain huts run on reduced winter schedules or close altogether. When it lines up, it is one of the most spectacular things we photograph all year.","Im Winter wird die ganze Szene monochrom und fast überirdisch &mdash; Schnee bis zum Horizont, die Türme auf Schwarzweiß reduziert &mdash;, und ihr habt sie vielleicht ganz für euch. Es verlangt mehr: warme Schichten, sicheren Tritt und einen wachen Blick darauf, was offen ist, denn die Mautstraße und die Berghütten fahren im Winter reduziert oder schließen ganz. Wenn es passt, ist es eines der spektakulärsten Dinge, die wir das ganze Jahr fotografieren."))
    C.append(fig('09-spots-drei-zinnen-schneegrat.webp',"The couple tiny on a snowy ridge beneath the jagged winter peaks","Das Paar winzig auf einem verschneiten Grat unter den schroffen Wintergipfeln"))

    C.append(h2('gardena','Seceda &amp; Val Gardena','Seceda &amp; Gröden'))
    C.append(p("Above the green valley of Val Gardena rises the Seceda, whose tilted grass ridge and sawtooth skyline are unlike anywhere else in the range &mdash; a giant knife-edge of meadow falling away to the pale Odle peaks. A cable car from Ortisei carries you up, though it opens only around 08:30, so a true Seceda sunrise means a head-torch hike or a night in a rifugio; for golden hour you simply catch it on the way up. The valley itself is a soft, storybook base of villages, spires and pasture.","Über dem grünen Grödnertal erhebt sich die Seceda, deren geneigter Wiesengrat und Sägezahn-Horizont anders sind als alles sonst im Massiv &mdash; eine riesige Messerschneide aus Wiese, die zu den bleichen Geislerspitzen abfällt. Eine Seilbahn von St. Ulrich bringt euch hinauf, sie öffnet allerdings erst gegen 08:30 Uhr, ein echter Seceda-Sonnenaufgang heißt also ein Stirnlampen-Aufstieg oder eine Hüttennacht; zur goldenen Stunde nehmt ihr sie einfach auf dem Weg nach oben. Das Tal selbst ist eine sanfte, märchenhafte Basis aus Dörfern, Türmen und Weiden."))
    C.append(fig('10-spots-groedental-panorama.webp',"The green sweep of Val Gardena with its villages far below the peaks","Der grüne Schwung des Grödentals mit seinen Dörfern tief unter den Gipfeln"))

    C.append(p("The Seceda pairs beautifully with the rest of Val Gardena. Ortisei, Santa Cristina and Selva make a comfortable, storybook base &mdash; timber villages with spires and spas, an easy drive from the passes and the cable cars. Many couples stay here for a few days and let us string the sights together: the ridge one morning, a pass at golden hour, a lake at dawn. It is the gentlest way to see a lot of the range without ever feeling rushed.","Die Seceda passt wunderbar zum \u00fcbrigen Gr\u00f6den. St.\u00a0Ulrich, St.\u00a0Christina und Wolkenstein bilden eine bequeme, m\u00e4rchenhafte Basis &mdash; Holzd\u00f6rfer mit T\u00fcrmen und Spas, eine leichte Fahrt von den P\u00e4ssen und Seilbahnen entfernt. Viele Paare bleiben hier ein paar Tage und lassen uns die Sehensw\u00fcrdigkeiten aneinanderreihen: den Grat an einem Morgen, einen Pass zur goldenen Stunde, einen See im Morgengrauen. Es ist der sanfteste Weg, viel vom Massiv zu sehen, ohne sich je gehetzt zu f\u00fchlen."))
    C.append(h2('sella','The Sella group','Die Sellagruppe'))
    C.append(p("The Sella is a vast fortress of rock ringed by four mountain passes, and its walls make one of the grandest, most accessible backdrops in the Dolomites &mdash; you can stand on soft meadow with a thousand metres of vertical stone behind you, minutes from the car. It is a favourite of ours for a ceremony: enough drama to take the breath away, gentle enough underfoot for a dress, a celebrant and a guest or two. Morning light rakes across the grass and warms the rock beautifully.","Die Sella ist eine gewaltige Festung aus Fels, umringt von vier Bergpässen, und ihre Wände bilden eine der grandiosesten und zugleich zugänglichsten Kulissen der Dolomiten &mdash; ihr steht auf weicher Wiese mit tausend Metern senkrechten Steins im Rücken, Minuten vom Auto entfernt. Sie ist ein Favorit von uns für eine Zeremonie: dramatisch genug, um den Atem zu rauben, sanft genug unter den Füßen für Kleid, Trauredner und ein, zwei Gäste. Das Morgenlicht streift über das Gras und wärmt den Fels wunderbar."))
    C.append(fig('13-spots-sellagruppe.webp',"A small ceremony on the meadow beneath the walls of the Sella group","Eine kleine Zeremonie auf der Wiese unter den Wänden der Sellagruppe"))
    C.append(fig('15-spots-sella-grat-morgens.webp',"Bride and groom on a ridge at first light near the Sella","Braut und Bräutigam auf einem Grat bei erstem Licht nahe der Sella"))

    C.append(p("What we love most about the Sella is how little it asks for how much it gives. From the passes that ring it you are already at over 2,000 metres, so a few steps put you on open meadow with the walls towering overhead &mdash; no scramble, no exposure, just scale. It works in almost any weather, too: even when cloud is draped over the summits, the base of the Sella stays photogenic and grand. For a bad-forecast morning it is one of our most reliable saves.","Was wir an der Sella am meisten lieben, ist, wie wenig sie f\u00fcr so viel verlangt. Von den P\u00e4ssen, die sie umringen, seid ihr schon auf \u00fcber 2.000 Metern, ein paar Schritte setzen euch also auf offene Wiese, die W\u00e4nde hoch \u00fcber euch aufragend &mdash; kein Gekraxel, keine Ausgesetztheit, nur Dimension. Sie funktioniert auch bei fast jedem Wetter: Selbst wenn Wolken \u00fcber den Gipfeln h\u00e4ngen, bleibt der Fu\u00df der Sella fotogen und grandios. F\u00fcr einen Morgen mit schlechter Vorhersage ist sie eine unserer verl\u00e4sslichsten Rettungen."))
    C.append(h2('passes','The great passes','Die großen Pässe'))
    C.append(p("The high passes that link the valleys &mdash; Passo Gardena, Passo Sella, Passo Pordoi &mdash; are the easy secret of the Dolomites: you drive to over 2,000 metres and step straight onto alpine meadow with the giants all around, no climb required. They are perfect for couples who want the high-mountain feeling without the effort, or who are bringing family. In summer they are open and glorious; in the shoulder season they empty out and glow. We often pair a pass at golden hour with a lake at dawn.","Die hohen Pässe, die die Täler verbinden &mdash; Grödnerjoch, Sellajoch, Pordoijoch &mdash;, sind das leichte Geheimnis der Dolomiten: Ihr fahrt auf über 2.000 Meter und trett direkt auf Almwiese hinaus, die Riesen ringsum, ohne Aufstieg. Sie sind perfekt für Paare, die das Hochgebirgsgefühl ohne Aufwand wollen oder Familie dabeihaben. Im Sommer sind sie offen und herrlich; in der Nebensaison leeren sie sich und glühen. Wir kombinieren oft einen Pass zur goldenen Stunde mit einem See im Morgengrauen."))
    C.append(fig('14-spots-groednerjoch-paar.webp',"A couple in Tyrolean dress on the meadow at Passo Gardena, peaks and light behind","Ein Paar in Tracht auf der Wiese am Grödnerjoch, Gipfel und Licht dahinter"))

    C.append(h2('giau','Passo Giau &amp; Ra Gusela','Passo Giau &amp; Ra Gusela'))
    C.append(p("Of all the passes, Passo Giau is the one we lose our hearts to. A little pointed chapel stands on the green saddle, the shark-fin peak of Ra Gusela rises straight behind it, and at dusk the whole amphitheatre of ridges turns molten. It is roadside and easy, yet it feels remote and wild, and the evening light here is some of the best in the Dolomites. For a couple who want drama and a touch of storybook without a hike, it is very hard to beat.","Von allen Pässen ist der Passo Giau der, an den wir unser Herz verlieren. Eine kleine spitze Kapelle steht auf dem grünen Sattel, die Haifischflossen-Spitze der Ra Gusela steigt direkt dahinter auf, und in der Dämmerung wird das ganze Amphitheater der Grate glühend. Er liegt an der Straße und ist leicht, wirkt aber abgelegen und wild, und das Abendlicht hier gehört zum besten der Dolomiten. Für ein Paar, das Dramatik und einen Hauch Märchen ohne Wanderung will, ist er kaum zu schlagen."))
    C.append(fig('11-spots-passo-giau-kapelle.webp',"The little pointed chapel at Passo Giau with Ra Gusela rising behind","Die kleine spitze Kapelle am Passo Giau, die Ra Gusela dahinter aufragend"))
    C.append(fig('12-spots-ra-gusela-abendlicht.webp',"The couple on the meadow at Passo Giau under a dramatic evening sky","Das Paar auf der Wiese am Passo Giau unter dramatischem Abendhimmel"))

    C.append(p("Because Giau faces the evening light so well, we usually plan it for sunset rather than dawn &mdash; and because it is a mountain pass, it is one of the few icons you can reach easily late in the day. Park, walk a minute onto the meadow, and let the sky do the rest. When the ridges catch the last colour and the chapel goes to silhouette, it is as cinematic as anywhere we work, and you can be back down to a valley dinner within the hour.","Weil der Giau das Abendlicht so gut nimmt, planen wir ihn meist f\u00fcr den Sonnenuntergang statt den Morgen &mdash; und weil er ein Bergpass ist, geh\u00f6rt er zu den wenigen Ikonen, die ihr sp\u00e4t am Tag leicht erreicht. Parken, eine Minute auf die Wiese gehen und den Himmel den Rest machen lassen. Wenn die Grate das letzte Licht fangen und die Kapelle zur Silhouette wird, ist es so filmreif wie irgendwo, wo wir arbeiten &mdash; und ihr seid binnen einer Stunde zur\u00fcck zu einem Abendessen im Tal."))
    C.append(h2('summits','Summits &amp; the small details','Gipfel &amp; die kleinen Details'))
    C.append(p("Beyond the famous names, some of our favourite frames are the quiet ones: a summit cross catching the first light, a bouquet set down on cold rock, a ridge nobody else has a name for. When a spot is too popular to promise privacy, we will often walk five more minutes to a lesser ledge with the same peaks behind it and none of the crowd in front. The Dolomites are generous like that &mdash; the icon is never the only good picture.","Jenseits der berühmten Namen sind einige unserer liebsten Bilder die stillen: ein Gipfelkreuz, das das erste Licht fängt, ein Brautstrauß, abgelegt auf kaltem Fels, ein Grat, für den sonst niemand einen Namen hat. Ist ein Ort zu beliebt, um Privatsphäre zu versprechen, gehen wir oft fünf Minuten weiter zu einem kleineren Band mit denselben Gipfeln dahinter und ohne die Menge davor. Die Dolomiten sind so großzügig &mdash; die Ikone ist nie das einzige gute Bild."))
    C.append(fig('16-spots-gipfelkreuz-morgens.webp',"A bouquet resting on summit rock with misty peaks beyond","Ein Brautstrauß auf Gipfelfels, dahinter neblige Gipfel"))

    C.append(h2('hidden','Hidden lakes for the adventurous','Versteckte Seen für Abenteuerlustige'))
    C.append(p("If you are happy to walk, the range hides quieter water that rewards the effort. Lago di Sorapis glows an improbable milky blue at the end of a rocky trail; Lago di Federa sits under the Croda da Lago and turns golden when the surrounding larches do; little Lago d&rsquo;Antorno and Lago di Limides give big reflections for short walks. None of these carry the crowds of Braies, and a ceremony at one of them feels genuinely discovered. Tell us how far you are willing to walk and we will name the one that fits.","Wenn ihr gern geht, verbirgt das Massiv stilleres Wasser, das den Aufwand belohnt. Der Lago di Sorapis leuchtet am Ende eines felsigen Wegs in einem unwahrscheinlichen milchigen Blau; der Lago di Federa liegt unter der Croda da Lago und wird golden, wenn es die umstehenden Lärchen tun; der kleine Lago d&rsquo;Antorno und der Lago di Limides schenken große Spiegelungen für kurze Wege. Keiner davon trägt die Menschenmengen von Braies, und eine Zeremonie an einem von ihnen fühlt sich wirklich entdeckt an. Sagt uns, wie weit ihr gehen wollt, und wir nennen euch den passenden."))

    C.append(h2('when','When to go','Wann ihr fahren solltet'))
    C.append(p("Season changes these places as much as the hour does. <strong>Summer</strong> (June to September) opens every road, lift and hut, and gives green meadows and the warmest light &mdash; but also the fullest car parks. <strong>Autumn</strong> is our quiet favourite: the larches turn gold, the crowds thin, and the low sun flatters the rock, though the first snows can close the highest passes. <strong>Winter</strong> is for the bold &mdash; monochrome, silent, spectacular, with reduced access. Whatever the month, sunrise is the great equaliser: even the busiest icon is calm at first light.","Die Saison verändert diese Orte so sehr wie die Stunde. <strong>Sommer</strong> (Juni bis September) öffnet jede Straße, Bahn und Hütte und gibt grüne Wiesen und das wärmste Licht &mdash; aber auch die vollsten Parkplätze. <strong>Herbst</strong> ist unser stiller Favorit: Die Lärchen werden golden, der Andrang lichtet sich, und die tiefe Sonne schmeichelt dem Fels &mdash; wobei die ersten Schneefälle die höchsten Pässe schließen können. <strong>Winter</strong> ist für die Mutigen &mdash; monochrom, still, spektakulär, mit eingeschränktem Zugang. Welcher Monat auch immer: Der Sonnenaufgang ist der große Gleichmacher &mdash; selbst die vollste Ikone ist bei erstem Licht ruhig."))

    C.append(h2('reach','How to reach each one','So kommt ihr zu jedem'))
    C.append(p("Getting here is easier than the drama suggests. Most couples fly into Venice, Verona or Innsbruck and drive two to three hours in. From a valley base like Cortina, Val Gardena or the Alta Badia, the icons are within an hour: Braies and the passes are roadside, the Seceda and other ridges are a cable car, the Tre Cime a summer toll road, and the hidden lakes a walk. We build the route around the light &mdash; which spot at dawn, which at dusk &mdash; and handle the reservations, the timings and the driving so your morning stays calm.","Das Hinkommen ist leichter, als die Dramatik vermuten lässt. Die meisten Paare fliegen nach Venedig, Verona oder Innsbruck und fahren zwei bis drei Stunden hinein. Von einer Talbasis wie Cortina, Gröden oder der Alta Badia sind die Ikonen in einer Stunde erreichbar: Braies und die Pässe liegen an der Straße, die Seceda und andere Grate sind eine Seilbahn, die Drei Zinnen eine Sommer-Mautstraße und die versteckten Seen ein Fußweg. Wir bauen die Route um das Licht &mdash; welcher Ort im Morgengrauen, welcher in der Dämmerung &mdash; und übernehmen Reservierungen, Timing und Fahrerei, damit euer Morgen ruhig bleibt."))

    C.append(p("Where you base yourself shapes the trip. Cortina d&rsquo;Ampezzo sits closest to Braies, the Tre Cime and Passo Giau; Val Gardena and the Alta Badia are best for the Seceda, the Sella and the western passes. We help you pick the base that keeps your chosen spots within an easy dawn drive, book huts where an overnight makes a sunrise possible, and hand you a simple schedule so the only thing you have to think about on the day is each other.","Wo ihr euch einquartiert, pr\u00e4gt die Reise. Cortina d&rsquo;Ampezzo liegt am n\u00e4chsten zu Braies, den Drei Zinnen und dem Passo Giau; Gr\u00f6den und die Alta Badia sind am besten f\u00fcr die Seceda, die Sella und die westlichen P\u00e4sse. Wir helfen euch, die Basis zu w\u00e4hlen, die eure Orte in leichter Morgen-Fahrweite h\u00e4lt, buchen H\u00fctten, wo eine \u00dcbernachtung einen Sonnenaufgang m\u00f6glich macht, und geben euch einen einfachen Ablauf, damit ihr am Tag nur an eines denken m\u00fcsst: aneinander."))
    C.append(h2('rules','Rules &amp; respect','Regeln &amp; Respekt'))
    C.append(p("These places stay beautiful because people look after them, and a few rules keep us welcome. The Braies road needs its summer reservation; several areas are protected nature zones where structures and off-path wandering are limited; and private drones are banned across much of the Dolomites, patrolled and fined. On the ground we stay on durable surfaces, keep groups small, leave no trace and never block the very paths we came to photograph. Respect is part of being allowed back &mdash; and it is why we scout and confirm every spot before we bring you to it.","Diese Orte bleiben schön, weil Menschen auf sie achten, und ein paar Regeln halten uns willkommen. Die Braies-Straße braucht ihre Sommer-Reservierung; mehrere Gebiete sind geschützte Naturzonen, in denen Aufbauten und das Gehen abseits der Wege begrenzt sind; und private Drohnen sind in weiten Teilen der Dolomiten verboten, kontrolliert und mit Bußgeld belegt. Am Boden bleiben wir auf festem Untergrund, halten Gruppen klein, hinterlassen keine Spuren und blockieren nie genau die Wege, die wir fotografieren kamen. Respekt ist Teil des Wiederkommen-Dürfens &mdash; und der Grund, warum wir jeden Ort erkunden und bestätigen, ehe wir euch hinbringen."))


    faq_html='<h2 id="faq" style="'+H2S+'">'+L('Dolomites spots FAQ','FAQ zu den Dolomiten-Orten')+'</h2>'
    FAQL=[FQ(*x) for x in SPOTS_FAQ]
    faq_html+=''.join('<div style="margin:1.3em 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:1.1em">'
      f'<h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:20px;margin:0 0 .3em">{q}</h3>'
      f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2);margin:0">{a}</p></div>' for q,a in FAQL)
    faq_ld={"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
      {"@type":"Question","name":_plain(q),"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":_plain(a)}} for q,a in FAQL]}
    related=''.join(story_card(lang,P,STORYBY[sl]) for sl in ex['stories'])
    more=''.join(guide_card(lang,P,x) for x in GUIDES if x['slug']!=slug)
    body=(nav(lang,rel,'howto')+
      f'<section class="page-hero" style="padding:0">{herobg(P,HERO_IMG,g["title"][lang])}'
      f'<div class="content"><div class="wrap"><div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"guide_kick")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h1>{g["title"][lang]}</h1></div></div></section>'
      '<section><div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">'+''.join(C)+faq_html+
      f'<p style="margin-top:2.4em"><a href="{u(P,lang,"how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/")}" class="arrow-link">&larr; {T["nav"]["howto"][lang]}</a></p></div></section>'
      '<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"related_stories")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"related_stories")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{related}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="stories" style="padding-top:clamp(40px,6vw,80px)"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"more_guides")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"more_guides")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{more}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="cta"><div class="wrap row reveal"><div>'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"cta_k")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2 style="margin-top:20px">{t(lang,"cta_h")}</h2></div>'
      f'<a href="{u(P,lang,"get-in-touch/")}" class="btn light">{t(lang,"start_planning")}</a></div></section>'
      +footer(lang,rel))
    write(lang,rel,head(lang,rel,g['title'][lang]+' — Mountain Elopement',g['excerpt'][lang],ld_extra=faq_ld,pre=herolink(P,HERO_IMG))+body+scripts(P))

PLAN_FAQ=[
 ("How far ahead should we plan a mountain elopement?",
  "Three to nine months is the comfortable range. Nine months gives you the pick of dates and time for a legal marriage abroad; three is plenty for a symbolic ceremony with the paperwork done at home. We have also pulled beautiful elopements together faster when a date opened up &mdash; tell us your timeframe and we will tell you honestly what fits.",
  "Wie lange im Voraus sollten wir ein Berg-Elopement planen?",
  "Drei bis neun Monate sind der bequeme Rahmen. Neun Monate geben euch die freie Wahl der Termine und Zeit für eine rechtsgültige Trauung im Ausland; drei reichen gut für eine symbolische Zeremonie mit den Papieren zu Hause. Wir haben auch schneller schöne Elopements zusammengestellt, wenn ein Termin frei wurde &mdash; sagt uns euren Zeitrahmen, und wir sagen euch ehrlich, was passt."),
 ("Do we have to organise everything ourselves?",
  "No &mdash; that is the whole point of us. You make the two big choices, the feeling and the season, and we handle the rest: location scouting, permits and reservations, the celebrant or registrar, hair and make-up, flowers, transport and the timeline. You show up rested and get married; we carry the plan.",
  "Müssen wir alles selbst organisieren?",
  "Nein &mdash; genau dafür sind wir da. Ihr trefft die zwei großen Entscheidungen, das Gefühl und die Saison, und wir übernehmen den Rest: Location-Suche, Genehmigungen und Reservierungen, Trauredner oder Standesbeamten, Haare und Make-up, Blumen, Transport und den Ablauf. Ihr kommt ausgeruht an und heiratet; wir tragen den Plan."),
 ("Is a mountain elopement actually legally binding?",
  "It can be, and there are two honest paths. Most couples hold a symbolic ceremony in the mountains and sign the legal papers at their home registry; that is the simplest route. A legally binding marriage is also possible &mdash; in Austria as a civil ceremony, in some regions even at an approved outdoor spot, while in Italy the legal act can only happen at a registry office. We point you to the right path for your countries.",
  "Ist ein Berg-Elopement wirklich rechtsgültig?",
  "Es kann es sein, und es gibt zwei ehrliche Wege. Die meisten Paare feiern eine symbolische Zeremonie in den Bergen und unterschreiben die Papiere am heimischen Standesamt; das ist der einfachste Weg. Eine rechtsgültige Trauung ist ebenso möglich &mdash; in Österreich standesamtlich, in manchen Regionen sogar an einem genehmigten Ort im Freien, während in Italien der Rechtsakt nur am Standesamt stattfinden kann. Wir weisen euch den richtigen Weg für eure Länder."),
 ("How many guests can we bring?",
  "Anywhere from none to around twenty. Most of our couples come as just the two of them, or with a handful of the people who matter most; above roughly ten the logistics start to change &mdash; transport, huts and permits all get more involved. We are happy to plan either, and we will always be honest about what changes as the group grows.",
  "Wie viele Gäste können wir mitbringen?",
  "Irgendwo zwischen keinem und etwa zwanzig. Die meisten unserer Paare kommen zu zweit oder mit einer Handvoll der wichtigsten Menschen; ab rund zehn ändert sich die Logistik &mdash; Transport, Hütten und Genehmigungen werden aufwendiger. Wir planen gern beides und sind immer ehrlich, was sich ändert, wenn die Gruppe wächst."),
 ("What does a mountain elopement cost?",
  "Our packages start at around &euro;6,000 and include the photography, the planning, a scouting trip and your private online gallery. Larger packages add hair and make-up, flowers, film and full coordination, up to a whole day with accommodation and transfers. An elopement is usually far less than a big wedding &mdash; the budget goes into the experience and the images rather than a venue and a headcount.",
  "Was kostet ein Berg-Elopement?",
  "Unsere Pakete beginnen bei etwa 6.000&nbsp;&euro; und umfassen die Fotografie, die Planung, eine Erkundungsreise und eure private Online-Galerie. Größere Pakete ergänzen Haare und Make-up, Blumen, Film und die volle Koordination, bis hin zum ganzen Tag mit Unterkunft und Transfers. Ein Elopement ist meist weit günstiger als eine große Hochzeit &mdash; das Budget fließt in das Erlebnis und die Bilder statt in einen Saal und eine Gästezahl."),
 ("What if the weather is bad on the day?",
  "Mountain weather is part of the deal, so we build for it: a flexible window, a backup morning where the trip allows, and a beautiful plan B location that works in worse light. Fog and a little rain are not the enemy either &mdash; some of the most atmospheric photographs we take happen in exactly that soft light. The only weather we truly avoid is the unsafe kind.",
  "Was, wenn das Wetter am Tag schlecht ist?",
  "Bergwetter gehört dazu, deshalb planen wir dafür: ein flexibles Fenster, einen Reservemorgen, wo die Reise es erlaubt, und eine schöne Plan-B-Location, die bei schlechterem Licht funktioniert. Nebel und etwas Regen sind auch kein Feind &mdash; einige der stimmungsvollsten Bilder entstehen genau in diesem weichen Licht. Das einzige Wetter, das wir wirklich meiden, ist das unsichere."),
]

# --- Plan-Hub ES/IT (auto-generated, keyed by exact EN string) ---
PLAN_ES = {
  'What a mountain elopement is': 'Qué es un elopement de montaña',
  'An elopement is a very small, intentional wedding &mdash; usually just the two of you, sometimes a handful of the people you love most. Instead of a big party and a long guest list, the day is built entirely around the two of you and a place that means something. It is not about running away; it is a modern, deliberate way to marry, where the budget and the attention go into the experience and the photographs rather than a venue and a seating chart. Everything below exists to make that simple to pull off.': 'Un elopement es una boda muy pequeña e intencionada &mdash; normalmente solo vosotros dos, a veces un puñado de las personas que más queréis. En vez de una gran fiesta y una larga lista de invitados, el día se construye por completo en torno a vosotros dos y a un lugar que significa algo. No va de huir; es una manera moderna y deliberada de casarse, donde el presupuesto y la atención van a la experiencia y a las fotos en lugar de a un salón y un plano de mesas. Todo lo de abajo existe para que eso sea fácil de lograr.',
  'A couple embracing at a misty Dolomite lake on their elopement day': 'Una pareja abrazada en un nebuloso lago dolomítico el día de su elopement',
  'The freedom is the point. With no reception to seat and no schedule to please, the day bends entirely around you: you can marry at 6 a.m. on a summit, spend an hour saying nothing, swim in a cold lake in your dress, or hike to a second spot for sunset. Couples are often surprised by how emotional a tiny wedding turns out to be &mdash; with no audience to perform for, the words come out real, and the whole thing feels less like an event and more like the truest morning of your life.': 'La libertad es la clave. Sin banquete que sentar ni horario que complacer, el día se pliega por entero a vosotros: podéis casaros a las 6 de la mañana en una cumbre, pasar una hora sin decir nada, bañaros en un lago frío con el vestido o caminar a un segundo lugar para el atardecer. A las parejas les sorprende lo emotiva que resulta una boda diminuta &mdash; sin público ante quien actuar, las palabras salen de verdad, y todo se siente menos como un evento y más como la mañana más verdadera de vuestra vida.',
  '1 &middot; Choose the feeling, then the place': '1 &middot; Elegid el sentimiento, luego el lugar',
  'The wedding dress hanging before a window full of mountains': 'El vestido de novia colgado ante una ventana llena de montañas',
  'It helps to talk in pictures rather than logistics. Send us the images that stopped you scrolling, tell us whether you want to be warm or windswept, alone or with your closest people, gentle underfoot or high and exposed. From that we can already sketch two or three very different days &mdash; a lakeshore at dawn, a green pass at dusk, a flown-in summit &mdash; and you choose the one that makes your chest tighten. The place is just the frame; the feeling is the picture.': 'Ayuda hablar en imágenes en vez de en logística. Enviadnos las fotos que os hicieron dejar de deslizar, decidnos si queréis estar calientes o azotados por el viento, solos o con vuestra gente más cercana, suaves bajo los pies o altos y expuestos. Con eso ya podemos esbozar dos o tres días muy distintos &mdash; una orilla al alba, un puerto verde al ocaso, una cumbre alcanzada en vuelo &mdash; y elegís el que os aprieta el pecho. El lugar es solo el marco; el sentimiento es la imagen.',
  '2 &middot; Pick a season and a date range': '2 &middot; Elegid una estación y un rango de fechas',
  'Loading up at the car park in the dark before a pre-dawn start': 'Cargando el equipo en el aparcamiento a oscuras antes de una salida antes del alba',
  '3 &middot; The legal decision': '3 &middot; La decisión legal',
  'An Italian registrar reading during a civil ceremony': 'Un oficial del registro italiano leyendo durante una ceremonia civil',
  'Signing the marriage documents': 'Firmando los documentos matrimoniales',
  'Do not let the word legal scare you: in practice it is a short list of documents and a bit of lead time, and we have walked dozens of couples through it. For a symbolic ceremony there is almost nothing to do beyond marrying at home whenever suits you. For a civil marriage abroad, the paperwork &mdash; a certificate of no impediment, birth certificates, sometimes an apostille and sworn translations &mdash; simply needs to be started a few months ahead. We give you a country-specific checklist so you never wonder whether you have missed a form.': 'No dejéis que la palabra legal os asuste: en la práctica es una lista corta de documentos y algo de antelación, y hemos guiado por ello a decenas de parejas. Para una ceremonia simbólica no hay casi nada que hacer más allá de casaros en casa cuando os convenga. Para un matrimonio civil en el extranjero, el papeleo &mdash; un certificado de capacidad matrimonial, partidas de nacimiento, a veces una apostilla y traducciones juradas &mdash; simplemente hay que empezarlo unos meses antes. Os damos una lista de verificación por país para que nunca dudéis si os falta un formulario.',
  '4 &middot; The details, made easy': '4 &middot; Los detalles, hechos fáciles',
  'With the big two decided, the rest are the good bits: the dress or suit, hair and make-up, the vows you write, the flowers, the rings. None of it needs to be a project. We bring a trusted hair-and-make-up artist to wherever you are getting ready, arrange a florist who understands mountain conditions, and help you shape vows that sound like you. The small, handwritten, personal things are what the day is really made of &mdash; and they are the easiest to get right with a little guidance.': 'Con las dos grandes decisiones tomadas, el resto son las partes buenas: el vestido o el traje, peluquería y maquillaje, los votos que escribís, las flores, los anillos. Nada de esto tiene que ser un proyecto. Llevamos a una peluquera y maquilladora de confianza allí donde os preparéis, buscamos una floristería que entienda las condiciones de montaña y os ayudamos a dar forma a votos que suenen a vosotros. Las cosas pequeñas, manuscritas y personales son de lo que está hecho el día de verdad &mdash; y son las más fáciles de acertar con un poco de guía.',
  'Handwritten vows laid out beside the rings': 'Votos manuscritos dispuestos junto a los anillos',
  'Vow books, rings and personalised details ready for the day': 'Libros de votos, anillos y detalles personalizados listos para el día',
  'The bride having make-up applied during getting ready': 'La novia a la que aplican el maquillaje durante la preparación',
  'A word on the things couples forget. Bring layers for the cold at the top, and shoes you can actually walk in with the pretty pair in a bag. Write your vows earlier than you think you need to. Decide who holds the rings on the walk. Eat something before a sunrise start. None of this is hard, but it is the difference between a morning that flows and one that snags &mdash; so we send a short, human checklist a few weeks out, and we carry spares of the small things that always get left on a kitchen table.': 'Una palabra sobre lo que las parejas olvidan. Llevad capas para el frío de arriba, y zapatos con los que podáis caminar de verdad, con los bonitos en una bolsa. Escribid vuestros votos antes de lo que creéis necesario. Decidid quién lleva los anillos en la caminata. Comed algo antes de una salida al amanecer. Nada de esto es difícil, pero es la diferencia entre una mañana que fluye y una que se atasca &mdash; así que enviamos una lista breve y humana unas semanas antes, y llevamos repuestos de las pequeñas cosas que siempre se quedan en la mesa de la cocina.',
  '5 &middot; Make it unmistakably yours': '5 &middot; Hacedlo inconfundiblemente vuestro',
  'A celebrant reading during a personal symbolic ceremony': 'Un oficiante leyendo durante una ceremonia simbólica personal',
  'The planning timeline': 'El calendario de planificación',
  '<strong>9&ndash;6 months out:</strong> settle the feeling, the season and a date range, and reserve us. If you want a legal marriage abroad, this is when the paperwork starts. <strong>6&ndash;3 months:</strong> lock the location and any add-ons &mdash; celebrant, film, helicopter &mdash; and sort the dress, suit and rings. <strong>3&ndash;1 months:</strong> hair and make-up, flowers, travel and where you will stay; we finalise the shot list and the route. <strong>The final weeks:</strong> we watch the forecast, confirm the exact timeline and hold a backup plan. <strong>The day:</strong> you show up; we run everything. It really is that short a list, because most of it sits with us.': '<strong>9&ndash;6 meses antes:</strong> definid el sentimiento, la estación y un rango de fechas, y reservadnos. Si queréis un matrimonio legal en el extranjero, aquí empieza el papeleo. <strong>6&ndash;3 meses:</strong> fijad la localización y los extras &mdash; oficiante, vídeo, helicóptero &mdash; y resolved el vestido, el traje y los anillos. <strong>3&ndash;1 meses:</strong> peluquería y maquillaje, flores, viaje y dónde os alojáis; ultimamos el plan de fotos y la ruta. <strong>Las últimas semanas:</strong> vigilamos la previsión, confirmamos el horario exacto y mantenemos un plan B. <strong>El día:</strong> vosotros aparecéis; nosotros lo dirigimos todo. La lista es de verdad así de corta, porque casi todo recae en nosotros.',
  'The make-up artist at work during the calm of getting ready': 'La maquilladora trabajando en la calma de los preparativos',
  'If your timeframe is shorter, do not count yourselves out. A symbolic ceremony can come together in a matter of weeks when a date and the weather line up, because there is no legal lead time to wait on. What a longer runway buys you is choice &mdash; the pick of the best dates, first refusal on the golden mornings, and time for a legal marriage if you want one. Tell us where you are on the calendar and we will tell you honestly what is still possible; the answer is more often yes than couples expect.': 'Si vuestro plazo es más corto, no os descartéis. Una ceremonia simbólica puede armarse en cuestión de semanas cuando una fecha y el tiempo coinciden, porque no hay plazo legal que esperar. Lo que un margen más largo os compra es elección &mdash; los mejores días, la primera opción sobre las mañanas doradas y tiempo para un matrimonio legal si lo queréis. Decidnos dónde estáis en el calendario y os diremos con honestidad qué sigue siendo posible; la respuesta es más a menudo sí de lo que las parejas esperan.',
  'Permits, access &amp; the small costs': 'Permisos, acceso y los pequeños costes',
  'A few practical things sit under the beauty, and we handle all of them. Some places have access rules &mdash; the road to Lago di Braies needs a summer reservation, the Tre Cime is reached by a toll road, several areas are protected nature zones with limits on structures, and private drones are banned across much of the Dolomites. There are small costs beyond the packages, too: cable-car tickets, a landing fee at certain spots, a celebrant, flowers. We lay them all out plainly in advance so nothing is a surprise, and we book and confirm every one before your date.': 'Unas cuantas cosas prácticas hay bajo la belleza, y nos ocupamos de todas. Algunos lugares tienen reglas de acceso &mdash; la carretera al Lago di Braies necesita una reserva de verano, las Tre Cime se alcanzan por una carretera de peaje, varias zonas son áreas naturales protegidas con límites a las estructuras, y los drones privados están prohibidos en gran parte de los Dolomitas. También hay pequeños costes más allá de los paquetes: billetes de teleférico, una tasa de aterrizaje en ciertos lugares, un oficiante, flores. Los detallamos todos con claridad de antemano para que nada sorprenda, y reservamos y confirmamos cada uno antes de vuestra fecha.',
  'A last touch of make-up on location before the peaks': 'Un último toque de maquillaje en la localización ante las cumbres',
  'One more reassurance: none of these rules are yours to track. We hold a live picture of what is open, what needs booking and what each season allows, and we build it all into your plan so the admin is simply done. You will hear about it only as a short list of what to bring and where to be &mdash; the paperwork, the permits and the timings stay on our side of the desk.': 'Una tranquilidad más: ninguna de estas reglas es vuestra para controlar. Tenemos una imagen al día de lo que está abierto, lo que hay que reservar y lo que permite cada estación, y lo integramos todo en vuestro plan para que la gestión quede simplemente hecha. Solo sabréis de ello como una lista corta de qué llevar y dónde estar &mdash; el papeleo, los permisos y los horarios se quedan en nuestro lado de la mesa.',
  'What it costs': 'Cuánto cuesta',
  'Our packages start at around <strong>&euro;6,000</strong> and cover the photography, the planning, a scouting trip and your private online gallery. From there you can add what you want: hair and make-up, flowers, a celebrant, film, and up to full coordination of an entire day with accommodation and transfers. An elopement is usually far less than a traditional wedding, and the money is spent differently &mdash; on the experience, the location and the images that last, instead of a hall, a caterer and a headcount. We quote everything in one clear number so you always know where you stand.': 'Nuestros paquetes empiezan en torno a <strong>6.000&nbsp;&euro;</strong> e incluyen la fotografía, la planificación, un viaje de reconocimiento y vuestra galería online privada. A partir de ahí podéis añadir lo que queráis: peluquería y maquillaje, flores, un oficiante, vídeo, y hasta la coordinación completa de un día entero con alojamiento y traslados. Un elopement suele costar mucho menos que una boda tradicional, y el dinero se gasta de otra manera &mdash; en la experiencia, el lugar y las imágenes que perduran, en vez de en un salón, un catering y un número de invitados. Lo presupuestamos todo en una cifra clara para que siempre sepáis a qué ateneros.',
  'A flatlay of shoes, vow book and ring box': 'Un flatlay de zapatos, libro de votos y caja del anillo',
  'Think of the number as buying time and certainty, not just photos. What you are really paying for is a team that already knows which permit to file, which morning the light will land, which hut has room and which road is open &mdash; the knowledge that turns a logistically fiddly foreign wedding into a calm one. Couples tell us afterwards that the value was not only the gallery, but never once feeling lost or rushed on the most important morning of their lives.': 'Pensad en la cifra como la compra de tiempo y certeza, no solo de fotos. Por lo que de verdad pagáis es por un equipo que ya sabe qué permiso presentar, qué mañana llegará la luz, qué refugio tiene sitio y qué carretera está abierta &mdash; el conocimiento que convierte una boda en el extranjero logísticamente enrevesada en una tranquila. Las parejas nos dicen después que el valor no fue solo la galería, sino no sentirse ni una sola vez perdidas o apuradas en la mañana más importante de su vida.',
  'A day that never feels rushed': 'Un día que nunca se siente apurado',
  'Here is how it usually flows. You get ready in calm &mdash; hair, make-up, a coffee, the dress &mdash; while we handle timing and transport. We reach the spot with light to spare, and the ceremony happens when the light is at its best: your words, the rings, a first kiss with the whole range as witness. Then portraits while it is quiet, a moment to simply stand and take it in, and a celebration to match &mdash; a hut breakfast, a picnic, a toast on the mountain. Because we plan generously, there is always time to breathe, and the day feels long in the best way.': 'Así suele transcurrir. Os preparáis con calma &mdash; peluquería, maquillaje, un café, el vestido &mdash; mientras nosotros nos ocupamos del tiempo y el transporte. Llegamos al lugar con luz de sobra, y la ceremonia ocurre cuando la luz está en su mejor momento: vuestras palabras, los anillos, un primer beso con toda la cordillera de testigo. Luego retratos mientras está tranquilo, un momento para simplemente estar y asimilarlo, y una celebración a la altura &mdash; un desayuno en un refugio, un picnic, un brindis en la montaña. Como planificamos con generosidad, siempre hay tiempo para respirar, y el día se siente largo en el mejor sentido.',
  'A floral arrangement on a wooden chair at the ceremony spot': 'Un arreglo floral en una silla de madera en el lugar de la ceremonia',
  'The best moments are almost never the planned ones. It is the laugh after a shaky first line of vows, the way you both go quiet when the sun finally hits the peaks, the walk back down when it has all sunk in. We plan the structure precisely so that these unplanned things have room to happen &mdash; we are not marching you between poses, we are giving you a whole morning together in a beautiful place and quietly photographing the truth of it. That is the entire craft.': 'Los mejores momentos casi nunca son los planeados. Es la risa tras una primera línea temblorosa de los votos, la forma en que ambos os quedáis callados cuando el sol por fin toca las cumbres, la bajada cuando ya lo habéis asimilado todo. Planificamos la estructura con precisión justamente para que esas cosas no planeadas tengan sitio para ocurrir &mdash; no os marchamos de pose en pose, os damos una mañana entera juntos en un lugar hermoso y fotografiamos en silencio su verdad. En eso consiste todo el oficio.',
  'Leave the rest to us': 'Dejadnos el resto a nosotros',
  'If there is one thing to take from all of this, it is how little of it you have to carry. You bring the two of you, the feeling and a rough season; we bring the location knowledge, the permits, the local team, the timeline and the calm. We live in these mountains and plan elopements in them all year, so the things that would take you weeks of research take us a phone call. Tell us what you are dreaming of, and we will send back a simple plan and an honest answer &mdash; and then all that is left for you to do is turn up and get married.': 'Si hay algo que llevaros de todo esto, es lo poco que tenéis que cargar. Vosotros ponéis los dos, el sentimiento y una estación aproximada; nosotros ponemos el conocimiento del lugar, los permisos, el equipo local, el horario y la calma. Vivimos en estas montañas y planificamos elopements en ellas todo el año, así que lo que a vosotros os llevaría semanas de búsqueda a nosotros nos cuesta una llamada. Decidnos con qué soñáis y os devolveremos un plan sencillo y una respuesta honesta &mdash; y entonces lo único que os queda por hacer es presentaros y casaros.',
  'A registrar at the town hall in Selva, Val Gardena': 'Una oficial del registro en el ayuntamiento de Selva, Val Gardena',
  'What it is': 'Qué es',
  '1 · Feeling, then place': '1 &middot; Sentimiento, luego lugar',
  '2 · Season & date': '2 &middot; Estación y fecha',
  '3 · The legal decision': '3 &middot; La decisión legal',
  '4 · The details': '4 &middot; Los detalles',
  '5 · Make it yours': '5 &middot; Hacedlo vuestro',
  'Permits & costs': 'Permisos y costes',
  'A day without rush': 'Un día sin prisa',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'Planning an elopement: FAQ': 'Planear un elopement: preguntas frecuentes',
  'Planning an elopement should feel like the opposite of planning a wedding: less spreadsheet, more anticipation. There are really only two decisions that are yours to make &mdash; how you want the day to feel, and roughly when &mdash; and everything else is ours to carry. This is the whole roadmap, from first idea to the moment you say the words, laid out simply so you always know what happens next and how little you actually have to worry about.': 'Planear un elopement debería sentirse como lo contrario de planear una boda: menos hoja de cálculo, más ilusión. En realidad solo hay dos decisiones que son vuestras &mdash; cómo queréis que se sienta el día, y más o menos cuándo &mdash; y todo lo demás nos toca a nosotros. Esta es toda la hoja de ruta, desde la primera idea hasta el momento en que decís las palabras, expuesta con sencillez para que siempre sepáis qué viene después y lo poco que en realidad tenéis que preocuparos.',
  'On this page': 'En esta página',
}
PLAN_IT = {
  'What a mountain elopement is': "Cos'è un elopement di montagna",
  'An elopement is a very small, intentional wedding &mdash; usually just the two of you, sometimes a handful of the people you love most. Instead of a big party and a long guest list, the day is built entirely around the two of you and a place that means something. It is not about running away; it is a modern, deliberate way to marry, where the budget and the attention go into the experience and the photographs rather than a venue and a seating chart. Everything below exists to make that simple to pull off.': "Un elopement è un matrimonio molto piccolo e intenzionale &mdash; di solito solo voi due, a volte una manciata delle persone a cui tenete di più. Invece di una grande festa e una lunga lista di invitati, la giornata è costruita interamente attorno a voi due e a un luogo che significa qualcosa. Non si tratta di scappare; è un modo moderno e consapevole di sposarsi, dove il budget e l'attenzione vanno all'esperienza e alle foto invece che a una sala e a una disposizione dei tavoli. Tutto ciò che segue esiste per rendere tutto questo semplice da realizzare.",
  'A couple embracing at a misty Dolomite lake on their elopement day': 'Una coppia abbracciata a un nebbioso lago dolomitico nel giorno del loro elopement',
  'The freedom is the point. With no reception to seat and no schedule to please, the day bends entirely around you: you can marry at 6 a.m. on a summit, spend an hour saying nothing, swim in a cold lake in your dress, or hike to a second spot for sunset. Couples are often surprised by how emotional a tiny wedding turns out to be &mdash; with no audience to perform for, the words come out real, and the whole thing feels less like an event and more like the truest morning of your life.': "La libertà è il punto. Senza ricevimento da far sedere né orari da accontentare, la giornata si piega interamente a voi: potete sposarvi alle 6 del mattino in vetta, passare un'ora senza dire nulla, tuffarvi in un lago freddo con l'abito o camminare fino a un secondo luogo per il tramonto. Le coppie restano spesso sorprese da quanto sia emozionante un matrimonio minuscolo &mdash; senza pubblico per cui recitare, le parole escono vere, e il tutto sembra meno un evento e più il mattino più autentico della vostra vita.",
  '1 &middot; Choose the feeling, then the place': '1 &middot; Scegliete la sensazione, poi il luogo',
  'The wedding dress hanging before a window full of mountains': "L'abito da sposa appeso davanti a una finestra piena di montagne",
  'It helps to talk in pictures rather than logistics. Send us the images that stopped you scrolling, tell us whether you want to be warm or windswept, alone or with your closest people, gentle underfoot or high and exposed. From that we can already sketch two or three very different days &mdash; a lakeshore at dawn, a green pass at dusk, a flown-in summit &mdash; and you choose the one that makes your chest tighten. The place is just the frame; the feeling is the picture.': "Aiuta parlare per immagini invece che di logistica. Mandateci le foto che vi hanno fatto smettere di scorrere, diteci se volete stare al caldo o battuti dal vento, soli o con le persone più vicine, dolci sotto i piedi o in alto ed esposti. Da questo possiamo già abbozzare due o tre giornate molto diverse &mdash; una riva di lago all'alba, un passo verde al tramonto, una vetta raggiunta in volo &mdash; e voi scegliete quella che vi stringe il petto. Il luogo è solo la cornice; la sensazione è l'immagine.",
  '2 &middot; Pick a season and a date range': '2 &middot; Scegliete una stagione e un intervallo di date',
  'Loading up at the car park in the dark before a pre-dawn start': "Il carico dell'attrezzatura al parcheggio, al buio prima di una partenza all'alba",
  '3 &middot; The legal decision': '3 &middot; La decisione legale',
  'An Italian registrar reading during a civil ceremony': 'Un ufficiale di stato civile italiano che legge durante una cerimonia civile',
  'Signing the marriage documents': 'La firma dei documenti di matrimonio',
  'Do not let the word legal scare you: in practice it is a short list of documents and a bit of lead time, and we have walked dozens of couples through it. For a symbolic ceremony there is almost nothing to do beyond marrying at home whenever suits you. For a civil marriage abroad, the paperwork &mdash; a certificate of no impediment, birth certificates, sometimes an apostille and sworn translations &mdash; simply needs to be started a few months ahead. We give you a country-specific checklist so you never wonder whether you have missed a form.': "Non lasciate che la parola legale vi spaventi: in pratica è un breve elenco di documenti e un po' di anticipo, e abbiamo accompagnato decine di coppie attraverso di esso. Per una cerimonia simbolica non c'è quasi nulla da fare oltre a sposarvi a casa quando vi conviene. Per un matrimonio civile all'estero, le pratiche &mdash; un nulla osta, certificati di nascita, a volte un'apostille e traduzioni giurate &mdash; vanno semplicemente avviate qualche mese prima. Vi diamo una checklist specifica per Paese così non vi chiedete mai se avete dimenticato un modulo.",
  '4 &middot; The details, made easy': '4 &middot; I dettagli, resi facili',
  'With the big two decided, the rest are the good bits: the dress or suit, hair and make-up, the vows you write, the flowers, the rings. None of it needs to be a project. We bring a trusted hair-and-make-up artist to wherever you are getting ready, arrange a florist who understands mountain conditions, and help you shape vows that sound like you. The small, handwritten, personal things are what the day is really made of &mdash; and they are the easiest to get right with a little guidance.': "Prese le due grandi decisioni, il resto sono le parti belle: l'abito o il completo, capelli e trucco, le promesse che scrivete, i fiori, gli anelli. Niente di tutto ciò deve essere un progetto. Portiamo una truccatrice e acconciatrice di fiducia ovunque vi prepariate, troviamo una fiorista che comprende le condizioni di montagna e vi aiutiamo a dare forma a promesse che suonino come voi. Le cose piccole, scritte a mano, personali sono ciò di cui la giornata è davvero fatta &mdash; e sono le più facili da azzeccare con un po' di guida.",
  'Handwritten vows laid out beside the rings': 'Promesse scritte a mano disposte accanto agli anelli',
  'Vow books, rings and personalised details ready for the day': 'Libri delle promesse, anelli e dettagli personalizzati pronti per la giornata',
  'The bride having make-up applied during getting ready': 'La sposa a cui viene applicato il trucco durante i preparativi',
  'A word on the things couples forget. Bring layers for the cold at the top, and shoes you can actually walk in with the pretty pair in a bag. Write your vows earlier than you think you need to. Decide who holds the rings on the walk. Eat something before a sunrise start. None of this is hard, but it is the difference between a morning that flows and one that snags &mdash; so we send a short, human checklist a few weeks out, and we carry spares of the small things that always get left on a kitchen table.': "Una parola sulle cose che le coppie dimenticano. Portate strati per il freddo in cima, e scarpe con cui camminare davvero, con quelle belle in una borsa. Scrivete le promesse prima di quanto pensiate serva. Decidete chi tiene gli anelli durante la camminata. Mangiate qualcosa prima di una partenza all'alba. Niente di tutto ciò è difficile, ma è la differenza tra un mattino che scorre e uno che si inceppa &mdash; perciò mandiamo una checklist breve e umana qualche settimana prima, e portiamo dei ricambi delle piccole cose che restano sempre sul tavolo della cucina.",
  '5 &middot; Make it unmistakably yours': '5 &middot; Rendetelo inconfondibilmente vostro',
  'A celebrant reading during a personal symbolic ceremony': 'Un celebrante che legge durante una cerimonia simbolica personale',
  'The planning timeline': 'La tabella di marcia della pianificazione',
  '<strong>9&ndash;6 months out:</strong> settle the feeling, the season and a date range, and reserve us. If you want a legal marriage abroad, this is when the paperwork starts. <strong>6&ndash;3 months:</strong> lock the location and any add-ons &mdash; celebrant, film, helicopter &mdash; and sort the dress, suit and rings. <strong>3&ndash;1 months:</strong> hair and make-up, flowers, travel and where you will stay; we finalise the shot list and the route. <strong>The final weeks:</strong> we watch the forecast, confirm the exact timeline and hold a backup plan. <strong>The day:</strong> you show up; we run everything. It really is that short a list, because most of it sits with us.': "<strong>9&ndash;6 mesi prima:</strong> definite la sensazione, la stagione e un intervallo di date, e prenotateci. Se volete un matrimonio legale all'estero, qui iniziano le pratiche. <strong>6&ndash;3 mesi:</strong> fissate la location e gli extra &mdash; celebrante, video, elicottero &mdash; e sistemate abito, completo e anelli. <strong>3&ndash;1 mesi:</strong> capelli e trucco, fiori, viaggio e dove alloggiate; finalizziamo la scaletta degli scatti e il percorso. <strong>Le ultime settimane:</strong> seguiamo le previsioni, confermiamo l'orario esatto e teniamo un piano B. <strong>Il giorno:</strong> voi vi presentate; noi gestiamo tutto. La lista è davvero così corta, perché quasi tutto resta a noi.",
  'The make-up artist at work during the calm of getting ready': 'La truccatrice al lavoro nella calma dei preparativi',
  'If your timeframe is shorter, do not count yourselves out. A symbolic ceremony can come together in a matter of weeks when a date and the weather line up, because there is no legal lead time to wait on. What a longer runway buys you is choice &mdash; the pick of the best dates, first refusal on the golden mornings, and time for a legal marriage if you want one. Tell us where you are on the calendar and we will tell you honestly what is still possible; the answer is more often yes than couples expect.': "Se il vostro tempo è più breve, non tiratevi fuori. Una cerimonia simbolica può nascere nel giro di settimane quando una data e il meteo si allineano, perché non c'è un tempo legale da aspettare. Ciò che un margine più lungo vi compra è la scelta &mdash; i giorni migliori, la prima opzione sulle mattine dorate e il tempo per un matrimonio legale se lo volete. Diteci a che punto siete sul calendario e vi diremo con onestà cosa è ancora possibile; la risposta è più spesso sì di quanto le coppie si aspettino.",
  'Permits, access &amp; the small costs': 'Permessi, accesso e i piccoli costi',
  'A few practical things sit under the beauty, and we handle all of them. Some places have access rules &mdash; the road to Lago di Braies needs a summer reservation, the Tre Cime is reached by a toll road, several areas are protected nature zones with limits on structures, and private drones are banned across much of the Dolomites. There are small costs beyond the packages, too: cable-car tickets, a landing fee at certain spots, a celebrant, flowers. We lay them all out plainly in advance so nothing is a surprise, and we book and confirm every one before your date.': 'Alcune cose pratiche stanno sotto la bellezza, e ce ne occupiamo tutte noi. Alcuni luoghi hanno regole di accesso &mdash; la strada per il Lago di Braies richiede una prenotazione estiva, le Tre Cime si raggiungono con una strada a pedaggio, diverse aree sono zone naturali protette con limiti agli allestimenti, e i droni privati sono vietati in gran parte delle Dolomiti. Ci sono anche piccoli costi oltre ai pacchetti: biglietti della funivia, una tariffa di atterraggio in certi luoghi, un celebrante, i fiori. Li spieghiamo tutti con chiarezza in anticipo così nulla sorprende, e prenotiamo e confermiamo ognuno prima della vostra data.',
  'A last touch of make-up on location before the peaks': 'Un ultimo tocco di trucco sul posto davanti alle cime',
  'One more reassurance: none of these rules are yours to track. We hold a live picture of what is open, what needs booking and what each season allows, and we build it all into your plan so the admin is simply done. You will hear about it only as a short list of what to bring and where to be &mdash; the paperwork, the permits and the timings stay on our side of the desk.': "Un'ulteriore rassicurazione: nessuna di queste regole è vostra da seguire. Abbiamo un quadro aggiornato di ciò che è aperto, di ciò che va prenotato e di ciò che ogni stagione consente, e integriamo tutto nel vostro piano così l'amministrazione è semplicemente fatta. Ne saprete solo come un breve elenco di cosa portare e dove essere &mdash; le pratiche, i permessi e gli orari restano dalla nostra parte della scrivania.",
  'What it costs': 'Quanto costa',
  'Our packages start at around <strong>&euro;6,000</strong> and cover the photography, the planning, a scouting trip and your private online gallery. From there you can add what you want: hair and make-up, flowers, a celebrant, film, and up to full coordination of an entire day with accommodation and transfers. An elopement is usually far less than a traditional wedding, and the money is spent differently &mdash; on the experience, the location and the images that last, instead of a hall, a caterer and a headcount. We quote everything in one clear number so you always know where you stand.': "I nostri pacchetti partono da circa <strong>6.000&nbsp;&euro;</strong> e comprendono la fotografia, la pianificazione, un sopralluogo e la vostra galleria online privata. Da lì potete aggiungere ciò che volete: capelli e trucco, fiori, un celebrante, video, fino alla coordinazione completa di un'intera giornata con alloggio e transfer. Un elopement costa di solito molto meno di un matrimonio tradizionale, e il denaro si spende diversamente &mdash; nell'esperienza, nel luogo e nelle immagini che restano, invece che in una sala, un catering e un numero di invitati. Quotiamo tutto in una cifra chiara così sapete sempre a che punto siete.",
  'A flatlay of shoes, vow book and ring box': "Un flatlay di scarpe, libro delle promesse e scatola dell'anello",
  'Think of the number as buying time and certainty, not just photos. What you are really paying for is a team that already knows which permit to file, which morning the light will land, which hut has room and which road is open &mdash; the knowledge that turns a logistically fiddly foreign wedding into a calm one. Couples tell us afterwards that the value was not only the gallery, but never once feeling lost or rushed on the most important morning of their lives.': "Pensate alla cifra come all'acquisto di tempo e certezza, non solo di foto. Ciò per cui pagate davvero è una squadra che sa già quale permesso presentare, in quale mattino arriverà la luce, quale rifugio ha posto e quale strada è aperta &mdash; la conoscenza che trasforma un matrimonio all'estero logisticamente complicato in uno sereno. Le coppie ci dicono dopo che il valore non è stato solo la galleria, ma non essersi sentite nemmeno una volta perse o di fretta nel mattino più importante della loro vita.",
  'A day that never feels rushed': 'Una giornata che non sembra mai di fretta',
  'Here is how it usually flows. You get ready in calm &mdash; hair, make-up, a coffee, the dress &mdash; while we handle timing and transport. We reach the spot with light to spare, and the ceremony happens when the light is at its best: your words, the rings, a first kiss with the whole range as witness. Then portraits while it is quiet, a moment to simply stand and take it in, and a celebration to match &mdash; a hut breakfast, a picnic, a toast on the mountain. Because we plan generously, there is always time to breathe, and the day feels long in the best way.': "Ecco come di solito si svolge. Vi preparate con calma &mdash; capelli, trucco, un caffè, l'abito &mdash; mentre noi gestiamo tempi e trasporto. Raggiungiamo il luogo con luce in anticipo, e la cerimonia avviene quando la luce è al suo meglio: le vostre parole, gli anelli, un primo bacio con l'intera catena a fare da testimone. Poi ritratti mentre è tranquillo, un momento per stare semplicemente lì e assaporarlo, e una festa all'altezza &mdash; una colazione in rifugio, un picnic, un brindisi in montagna. Poiché pianifichiamo con generosità, c'è sempre tempo per respirare, e la giornata sembra lunga nel senso migliore.",
  'A floral arrangement on a wooden chair at the ceremony spot': 'Una composizione floreale su una sedia di legno nel luogo della cerimonia',
  'The best moments are almost never the planned ones. It is the laugh after a shaky first line of vows, the way you both go quiet when the sun finally hits the peaks, the walk back down when it has all sunk in. We plan the structure precisely so that these unplanned things have room to happen &mdash; we are not marching you between poses, we are giving you a whole morning together in a beautiful place and quietly photographing the truth of it. That is the entire craft.': "I momenti più belli non sono quasi mai quelli pianificati. È la risata dopo una prima riga incerta delle promesse, il modo in cui entrambi tacete quando il sole finalmente colpisce le cime, la discesa quando tutto è ormai sedimentato. Pianifichiamo la struttura con precisione proprio perché queste cose non pianificate abbiano spazio per accadere &mdash; non vi facciamo marciare da posa a posa, vi diamo un'intera mattina insieme in un luogo bellissimo e ne fotografiamo in silenzio la verità. È tutto qui il mestiere.",
  'Leave the rest to us': 'Lasciate il resto a noi',
  'If there is one thing to take from all of this, it is how little of it you have to carry. You bring the two of you, the feeling and a rough season; we bring the location knowledge, the permits, the local team, the timeline and the calm. We live in these mountains and plan elopements in them all year, so the things that would take you weeks of research take us a phone call. Tell us what you are dreaming of, and we will send back a simple plan and an honest answer &mdash; and then all that is left for you to do is turn up and get married.': "Se c'è una cosa da portare via da tutto questo, è quanto poco dovete portare voi. Voi mettete voi due, la sensazione e una stagione di massima; noi mettiamo la conoscenza dei luoghi, i permessi, la squadra locale, i tempi e la calma. Viviamo in queste montagne e vi pianifichiamo elopement tutto l'anno, quindi ciò che a voi richiederebbe settimane di ricerche a noi costa una telefonata. Diteci cosa sognate e vi rimanderemo un piano semplice e una risposta onesta &mdash; e allora l'unica cosa che vi resta da fare è presentarvi e sposarvi.",
  'A registrar at the town hall in Selva, Val Gardena': "Un'ufficiale di stato civile nel municipio di Selva, in Val Gardena",
  'What it is': "Cos'è",
  '1 · Feeling, then place': '1 &middot; Sensazione, poi luogo',
  '2 · Season & date': '2 &middot; Stagione e data',
  '3 · The legal decision': '3 &middot; La decisione legale',
  '4 · The details': '4 &middot; I dettagli',
  '5 · Make it yours': '5 &middot; Rendetelo vostro',
  'Permits & costs': 'Permessi e costi',
  'A day without rush': 'Una giornata senza fretta',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'Planning an elopement: FAQ': 'Pianificare un elopement: FAQ',
  'Planning an elopement should feel like the opposite of planning a wedding: less spreadsheet, more anticipation. There are really only two decisions that are yours to make &mdash; how you want the day to feel, and roughly when &mdash; and everything else is ours to carry. This is the whole roadmap, from first idea to the moment you say the words, laid out simply so you always know what happens next and how little you actually have to worry about.': "Pianificare un elopement dovrebbe sembrare l'opposto di pianificare un matrimonio: meno foglio di calcolo, più attesa. In realtà ci sono solo due decisioni che spettano a voi &mdash; come volete che la giornata si senta, e all'incirca quando &mdash; e tutto il resto tocca a noi. Questa è l'intera tabella di marcia, dalla prima idea al momento in cui pronunciate le parole, esposta con semplicità così sapete sempre cosa viene dopo e quanto poco dobbiate davvero preoccuparvi.",
  'On this page': 'In questa pagina',
}
PLAN_FAQ_ES = {
  'How far ahead should we plan a mountain elopement?': ('¿Con cuánta antelación deberíamos planear un elopement de montaña?', 'De tres a nueve meses es el rango cómodo. Nueve meses os dan a elegir entre las fechas y tiempo para un matrimonio legal en el extranjero; tres bastan de sobra para una ceremonia simbólica con el papeleo hecho en casa. También hemos montado elopements preciosos más rápido cuando se abrió una fecha &mdash; decidnos vuestro plazo y os diremos con honestidad qué encaja.'),
  'Do we have to organise everything ourselves?': ('¿Tenemos que organizarlo todo nosotros?', 'No &mdash; ese es justo el sentido de que estemos nosotros. Vosotros tomáis las dos grandes decisiones, el sentimiento y la estación, y nosotros nos ocupamos del resto: búsqueda de localización, permisos y reservas, el oficiante o el registro, peluquería y maquillaje, flores, transporte y el horario. Aparecéis descansados y os casáis; nosotros cargamos el plan.'),
  'Is a mountain elopement actually legally binding?': ('¿Es un elopement de montaña realmente con validez legal?', 'Puede serlo, y hay dos caminos honestos. La mayoría de las parejas celebra una ceremonia simbólica en la montaña y firma los papeles legales en su registro de casa; es la vía más simple. Un matrimonio con validez legal también es posible &mdash; en Austria como ceremonia civil, en algunas regiones incluso en un lugar autorizado al aire libre, mientras que en Italia el acto legal solo puede ocurrir en un registro civil. Os indicamos el camino correcto para vuestros países.'),
  'How many guests can we bring?': ('¿Cuántos invitados podemos llevar?', 'Desde ninguno hasta unos veinte. La mayoría de nuestras parejas viene solo los dos, o con un puñado de las personas que más importan; por encima de unos diez la logística empieza a cambiar &mdash; transporte, refugios y permisos se complican. Encantados de planear cualquiera de las dos, y siempre seremos honestos sobre qué cambia a medida que crece el grupo.'),
  'What does a mountain elopement cost?': ('¿Cuánto cuesta un elopement de montaña?', 'Nuestros paquetes empiezan en torno a 6.000&nbsp;&euro; e incluyen la fotografía, la planificación, un viaje de reconocimiento y vuestra galería online privada. Los paquetes mayores añaden peluquería y maquillaje, flores, vídeo y coordinación completa, hasta un día entero con alojamiento y traslados. Un elopement suele costar mucho menos que una gran boda &mdash; el presupuesto va a la experiencia y a las imágenes en vez de a un salón y un número de invitados.'),
  'What if the weather is bad on the day?': ('¿Y si hace mal tiempo el día señalado?', 'El tiempo de montaña es parte del trato, así que planificamos para él: una ventana flexible, una mañana de reserva cuando el viaje lo permite y una bonita localización de plan B que funcione con peor luz. La niebla y algo de lluvia tampoco son el enemigo &mdash; algunas de las fotos más atmosféricas que hacemos ocurren justo con esa luz suave. El único tiempo que de verdad evitamos es el inseguro.'),
}
PLAN_FAQ_IT = {
  'How far ahead should we plan a mountain elopement?': ('Con quanto anticipo dovremmo pianificare un elopement di montagna?', "Da tre a nove mesi è l'intervallo comodo. Nove mesi vi danno la scelta delle date e il tempo per un matrimonio legale all'estero; tre bastano ampiamente per una cerimonia simbolica con le pratiche fatte a casa. Abbiamo anche organizzato elopement bellissimi più in fretta quando si è liberata una data &mdash; diteci il vostro tempo e vi diremo con onestà cosa è possibile."),
  'Do we have to organise everything ourselves?': ('Dobbiamo organizzare tutto noi?', "No &mdash; è proprio a questo che serviamo. Voi prendete le due grandi decisioni, la sensazione e la stagione, e noi ci occupiamo del resto: sopralluoghi, permessi e prenotazioni, il celebrante o l'ufficiale di stato civile, capelli e trucco, fiori, trasporto e i tempi. Vi presentate riposati e vi sposate; noi portiamo il piano."),
  'Is a mountain elopement actually legally binding?': ('Un elopement di montagna ha davvero valore legale?', "Può averlo, e ci sono due strade oneste. La maggior parte delle coppie celebra una cerimonia simbolica in montagna e firma i documenti legali al proprio comune di casa; è la via più semplice. Un matrimonio con valore legale è anch'esso possibile &mdash; in Austria come cerimonia civile, in alcune regioni persino in un luogo all'aperto autorizzato, mentre in Italia l'atto legale può avvenire solo in comune. Vi indichiamo la strada giusta per i vostri Paesi."),
  'How many guests can we bring?': ('Quanti invitati possiamo portare?', "Da nessuno a una ventina. La maggior parte delle nostre coppie viene solo in due, o con una manciata delle persone che contano di più; oltre una decina la logistica inizia a cambiare &mdash; trasporto, rifugi e permessi si complicano. Con piacere pianifichiamo l'una o l'altra cosa, e saremo sempre onesti su cosa cambia man mano che il gruppo cresce."),
  'What does a mountain elopement cost?': ('Quanto costa un elopement di montagna?', "I nostri pacchetti partono da circa 6.000&nbsp;&euro; e comprendono la fotografia, la pianificazione, un sopralluogo e la vostra galleria online privata. I pacchetti più grandi aggiungono capelli e trucco, fiori, video e coordinazione completa, fino a un'intera giornata con alloggio e transfer. Un elopement costa di solito molto meno di un grande matrimonio &mdash; il budget va nell'esperienza e nelle immagini invece che in una sala e nel numero di invitati."),
  'What if the weather is bad on the day?': ('E se il tempo è brutto nel giorno stabilito?', "Il meteo di montagna fa parte del gioco, quindi pianifichiamo per questo: una finestra flessibile, una mattina di riserva quando il viaggio lo consente e una bella location di piano B che funziona con luce peggiore. Nebbia e un po' di pioggia non sono nemmeno il nemico &mdash; alcune delle foto più suggestive che facciamo nascono proprio con quella luce morbida. L'unico tempo che evitiamo davvero è quello non sicuro."),
}

def build_plan_guide(lang):
    slug='how-to-plan-your-elopement'
    g=next(x for x in GUIDES if x['slug']==slug); ex=GUIDE_EXTRA[slug]
    rel='how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/'+slug+'/'; P=prefix(lang,rel)
    DE=(lang=='de')
    def L(en,de):
        if lang=='de': return de
        if lang=='es': return PLAN_ES.get(en,en)
        if lang=='it': return PLAN_IT.get(en,en)
        return en
    def LP(en,de,es,it): return {"en":en,"de":de,"es":es,"it":it}[lang]
    def p4(en,de,es,it): return f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2)">{LP(en,de,es,it)}</p>'
    def FQ(qen,aen,qde,ade):
        if lang=='de': return (qde,ade)
        if lang=='es': return PLAN_FAQ_ES.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        if lang=='it': return PLAN_FAQ_IT.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        return (qen,aen)
    GI=f'{P}img/guide-plan-your-elopement/'; GIREL='img/guide-plan-your-elopement/'; HERO_IMG='img/guide-plan-your-elopement/15-planung-anstossen-kleine-gruppe.webp'
    GB='how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/'
    def gu(s): return u(P,lang,GB+s+'/')
    hh=gu('helicopter-elopement-dolomites-guide'); hp=gu('mountain-proposal-guide')
    hs=gu('sunrise-or-sunset-elopement'); hd=gu('most-beautiful-dolomites-spots')
    ha=gu('best-alps-elopement-locations'); haus=gu('elope-in-austria')
    H2S='font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,3vw,36px);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:1.7em 0 .4em;scroll-margin-top:96px'
    def h2(i,en,de): return f'<h2 id="{i}" style="{H2S}">{L(en,de)}</h2>'
    def p(en,de): return f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2)">{L(en,de)}</p>'
    def fig(name,en,de): return '<figure class="guide-fig">'+bild(P,GIREL+name,L(en,de),sizes='(max-width:820px) 100vw, 820px')+'</figure>'
    def A(h,t): return '<a href="'+h+'">'+t+'</a>'
    toc=[('what',L('What it is','Worum es geht')),('feeling',L('1 · Feeling, then place','1 · Gefühl, dann Ort')),
         ('season',L('2 · Season & date','2 · Saison & Termin')),('legal',L('3 · The legal decision','3 · Das Rechtliche')),
         ('details',L('4 · The details','4 · Die Details')),('experience',L('5 · Make it yours','5 · Macht es zu eurem')),
         ('timeline',L('The planning timeline','Der Planungs-Fahrplan')),('permits',L('Permits & costs','Genehmigungen & Kosten')),
         ('budget',L('What it costs','Was es kostet')),('day',L('A day without rush','Ein Tag ohne Hetze')),
         ('us',L('Leave the rest to us','Den Rest uns überlassen')),('faq',L('FAQ','FAQ'))]
    toc_html=('<nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'"><div class="cap">'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'</div><ol>'
      +''.join(f'<li><a href="#{i}">{lbl}</a></li>' for i,lbl in toc)+'</ol></nav>')
    facts='<div class="facts">'+''.join(f'<div class="fct"><div class="fl">{LBL[k][lang]}</div><div class="fv">{val[lang]}</div></div>' for k,val in ex['facts'])+'</div>'
    C=[]
    C.append(f'<p class="lead">{L("Planning an elopement should feel like the opposite of planning a wedding: less spreadsheet, more anticipation. There are really only two decisions that are yours to make &mdash; how you want the day to feel, and roughly when &mdash; and everything else is ours to carry. This is the whole roadmap, from first idea to the moment you say the words, laid out simply so you always know what happens next and how little you actually have to worry about.","Ein Elopement zu planen sollte sich wie das Gegenteil einer Hochzeitsplanung anfühlen: weniger Tabelle, mehr Vorfreude. Es gibt eigentlich nur zwei Entscheidungen, die euch gehören &mdash; wie sich der Tag anfühlen soll und ungefähr wann &mdash;, und alles andere tragen wir. Hier ist der ganze Fahrplan, von der ersten Idee bis zu dem Moment, in dem ihr die Worte sagt &mdash; einfach ausgelegt, damit ihr immer wisst, was als Nächstes kommt und wie wenig ihr euch wirklich kümmern müsst.")}</p>')
    C.append(f'<div class="cap" style="margin:0 0 -14px">{t(lang,"quick_facts")}</div>{facts}')
    C.append(toc_html)

    C.append(h2('what','What a mountain elopement is','Was ein Berg-Elopement ist'))
    C.append(p("An elopement is a very small, intentional wedding &mdash; usually just the two of you, sometimes a handful of the people you love most. Instead of a big party and a long guest list, the day is built entirely around the two of you and a place that means something. It is not about running away; it is a modern, deliberate way to marry, where the budget and the attention go into the experience and the photographs rather than a venue and a seating chart. Everything below exists to make that simple to pull off.","Ein Elopement ist eine sehr kleine, bewusste Hochzeit &mdash; meist nur ihr beide, manchmal eine Handvoll der Menschen, die euch am meisten bedeuten. Statt einer großen Feier und einer langen Gästeliste ist der Tag ganz um euch zwei und einen Ort gebaut, der etwas bedeutet. Es geht nicht ums Weglaufen; es ist ein moderner, bewusster Weg zu heiraten, bei dem Budget und Aufmerksamkeit in das Erlebnis und die Bilder fließen statt in einen Saal und einen Sitzplan. Alles Weitere unten ist dafür da, das einfach zu machen."))
    C.append(fig('07-planung-standesbeamter-italien.webp',"A couple embracing at a misty Dolomite lake on their elopement day","Ein Paar umarmt sich an einem nebligen Dolomitensee an ihrem Elopement-Tag"))

    C.append(p("The freedom is the point. With no reception to seat and no schedule to please, the day bends entirely around you: you can marry at 6 a.m. on a summit, spend an hour saying nothing, swim in a cold lake in your dress, or hike to a second spot for sunset. Couples are often surprised by how emotional a tiny wedding turns out to be &mdash; with no audience to perform for, the words come out real, and the whole thing feels less like an event and more like the truest morning of your life.","Die Freiheit ist der Kern. Ohne Empfang zu bestuhlen und ohne Zeitplan, den es zu gefallen gilt, biegt sich der Tag ganz um euch: Ihr k\u00f6nnt um 6 Uhr fr\u00fch auf einem Gipfel heiraten, eine Stunde lang nichts sagen, im Kleid in einem kalten See baden oder zu einem zweiten Ort f\u00fcr den Sonnenuntergang wandern. Paare sind oft \u00fcberrascht, wie emotional eine winzige Hochzeit wird &mdash; ohne Publikum, f\u00fcr das man sich in Szene setzt, kommen die Worte echt heraus, und das Ganze f\u00fchlt sich weniger wie ein Event an und mehr wie der wahrste Morgen eures Lebens."))
    C.append(h2('feeling','1 &middot; Choose the feeling, then the place','1 &middot; Erst das Gefühl, dann den Ort'))
    C.append(p4(f"Start with the feeling, not the pin on the map. Do you picture total solitude on a high ridge, a mirror-still lake at first light, a green pass with a little chapel, or a summit you fly to? Once we know the mood, the location almost chooses itself. When you are ready to look at actual places, our guide to {A(hd,'the most beautiful spots in the Dolomites')} and the wider {A(ha,'best locations across the Alps')} are the perfect next read &mdash; but you do not have to decide alone, and you do not have to decide first.",f"Beginnt mit dem Gefühl, nicht mit der Stecknadel auf der Karte. Stellt ihr euch völlige Einsamkeit auf einem hohen Grat vor, einen spiegelglatten See bei erstem Licht, einen grünen Pass mit einer kleinen Kapelle oder einen Gipfel, zu dem ihr fliegt? Sobald wir die Stimmung kennen, wählt sich der Ort fast von selbst. Wenn ihr bereit seid, konkrete Orte anzusehen, sind unser Guide zu {A(hd,'den schönsten Orten in den Dolomiten')} und den weiteren {A(ha,'besten Orten in den Alpen')} die perfekte nächste Lektüre &mdash; aber ihr müsst nicht allein entscheiden, und ihr müsst nicht zuerst entscheiden.",f"Empezad por el sentimiento, no por el punto en el mapa. ¿Imagináis soledad total en una arista alta, un lago espejado con la primera luz, un puerto verde con una pequeña capilla o una cumbre a la que llegáis en vuelo? En cuanto conocemos el ambiente, el lugar casi se elige solo. Cuando estéis listos para mirar sitios concretos, nuestra guía de {A(hd,'los lugares más bellos de los Dolomitas')} y las más amplias {A(ha,'mejores ubicaciones de los Alpes')} son la lectura perfecta a continuación &mdash; pero no tenéis que decidir solos, ni tenéis que decidir primero.",f"Partite dalla sensazione, non dallo spillo sulla mappa. Immaginate solitudine totale su una cresta alta, un lago a specchio alla prima luce, un passo verde con una piccola cappella o una vetta che raggiungete in volo? Appena conosciamo l'atmosfera, il luogo si sceglie quasi da sé. Quando siete pronti a guardare luoghi concreti, la nostra guida ai {A(hd,'luoghi più belli delle Dolomiti')} e alle più ampie {A(ha,'migliori location delle Alpi')} è la lettura perfetta successiva &mdash; ma non dovete decidere da soli, né dovete decidere per primi."))
    C.append(fig('02-planung-brautkleid-mit-bergblick.webp',"The wedding dress hanging before a window full of mountains","Das Brautkleid hängt vor einem Fenster voller Berge"))

    C.append(p("It helps to talk in pictures rather than logistics. Send us the images that stopped you scrolling, tell us whether you want to be warm or windswept, alone or with your closest people, gentle underfoot or high and exposed. From that we can already sketch two or three very different days &mdash; a lakeshore at dawn, a green pass at dusk, a flown-in summit &mdash; and you choose the one that makes your chest tighten. The place is just the frame; the feeling is the picture.","Es hilft, in Bildern zu sprechen statt in Logistik. Schickt uns die Fotos, bei denen ihr aufgeh\u00f6rt habt zu scrollen, sagt uns, ob ihr warm oder windzerzaust sein wollt, allein oder mit euren engsten Menschen, sanft unter den F\u00fc\u00dfen oder hoch und ausgesetzt. Daraus skizzieren wir schon zwei, drei ganz verschiedene Tage &mdash; ein Seeufer im Morgengrauen, ein gr\u00fcner Pass in der D\u00e4mmerung, ein eingeflogener Gipfel &mdash;, und ihr w\u00e4hlt den, bei dem euch die Brust eng wird. Der Ort ist nur der Rahmen; das Gef\u00fchl ist das Bild."))
    C.append(h2('season','2 &middot; Pick a season and a date range','2 &middot; Saison und Zeitfenster wählen'))
    C.append(p4(f"The second choice is when. Summer opens every road, lift and hut and gives the warmest, greenest days; autumn brings golden larches and thin crowds; winter is silent, white and dramatic for the bold. Give us a rough range rather than a single fixed day if you can &mdash; it lets us chase the best weather and light. This is also where you decide {A(hs,'sunrise or sunset')}, which quietly shapes the whole day. A range plus a mood is all we need to start holding the good mornings for you.",f"Die zweite Wahl ist das Wann. Der Sommer öffnet jede Straße, Bahn und Hütte und gibt die wärmsten, grünsten Tage; der Herbst bringt goldene Lärchen und dünne Menschenmengen; der Winter ist still, weiß und dramatisch für die Mutigen. Gebt uns wenn möglich ein grobes Fenster statt eines einzelnen fixen Tages &mdash; so können wir dem besten Wetter und Licht nachgehen. Hier entscheidet ihr auch {A(hs,'Sonnenaufgang oder Sonnenuntergang')}, was leise den ganzen Tag prägt. Ein Zeitfenster plus eine Stimmung ist alles, was wir brauchen, um die guten Morgen für euch freizuhalten.",f"La segunda elección es cuándo. El verano abre todas las carreteras, remontes y refugios y da los días más cálidos y verdes; el otoño trae alerces dorados y menos gente; el invierno es silencioso, blanco y dramático para los audaces. Dadnos un rango aproximado en vez de un único día fijo si podéis &mdash; nos deja perseguir el mejor tiempo y la mejor luz. Aquí también decidís {A(hs,'amanecer o atardecer')}, lo que moldea en silencio todo el día. Un rango más un ambiente es todo lo que necesitamos para empezar a reservaros las buenas mañanas.",f"La seconda scelta è il quando. L'estate apre ogni strada, impianto e rifugio e regala le giornate più calde e verdi; l'autunno porta larici dorati e poca folla; l'inverno è silenzioso, bianco e drammatico per gli audaci. Dateci un intervallo di massima invece di un unico giorno fisso se potete &mdash; ci permette di inseguire il tempo e la luce migliori. Qui decidete anche {A(hs,'alba o tramonto')}, che plasma in silenzio l'intera giornata. Un intervallo più un'atmosfera è tutto ciò che ci serve per iniziare a tenervi le mattine buone."))
    C.append(fig('13-planung-aufbruch-vor-sonnenaufgang.webp',"Loading up at the car park in the dark before a pre-dawn start","Ausrüsten am Parkplatz im Dunkeln vor dem Start vor Sonnenaufgang"))

    C.append(h2('legal','3 &middot; The legal decision','3 &middot; Die rechtliche Entscheidung'))
    C.append(p4(f"Here is the one piece of real paperwork, and it is simpler than it sounds. Most couples choose a <strong>symbolic ceremony</strong> in the mountains &mdash; your vows, a celebrant, the two of you &mdash; and sign the legally binding papers at their home registry before or after the trip. The alternative is a <strong>legal civil marriage</strong> abroad: {A(haus,'eloping in Austria')} can be done as a civil ceremony, in some regions even outdoors, while in Italy the legal act happens only at a registry office and the mountain ceremony stays symbolic. We tell you exactly which documents you need for your countries and when to start.",f"Hier ist das eine Stück echtes Papierwerk, und es ist einfacher, als es klingt. Die meisten Paare wählen eine <strong>symbolische Zeremonie</strong> in den Bergen &mdash; eure Gelübde, ein Trauredner, ihr beide &mdash; und unterschreiben die rechtsgültigen Papiere vor oder nach der Reise am heimischen Standesamt. Die Alternative ist eine <strong>standesamtliche Trauung</strong> im Ausland: {A(haus,'in Österreich zu heiraten')} geht standesamtlich, in manchen Regionen sogar im Freien, während in Italien der Rechtsakt nur am Standesamt stattfindet und die Bergzeremonie symbolisch bleibt. Wir sagen euch genau, welche Dokumente ihr für eure Länder braucht und wann ihr beginnen solltet.",f"Aquí está la única pieza de papeleo real, y es más simple de lo que suena. La mayoría de las parejas elige una <strong>ceremonia simbólica</strong> en la montaña &mdash; vuestros votos, un oficiante, los dos &mdash; y firma los papeles con validez legal en su registro de casa antes o después del viaje. La alternativa es un <strong>matrimonio civil legal</strong> en el extranjero: {A(haus,'casarse en Austria')} puede hacerse como ceremonia civil, en algunas regiones incluso al aire libre, mientras que en Italia el acto legal ocurre solo en un registro civil y la ceremonia en la montaña sigue siendo simbólica. Os decimos exactamente qué documentos necesitáis para vuestros países y cuándo empezar.",f"Ecco l'unico vero pezzo di burocrazia, ed è più semplice di quanto sembri. La maggior parte delle coppie sceglie una <strong>cerimonia simbolica</strong> in montagna &mdash; le vostre promesse, un celebrante, voi due &mdash; e firma i documenti con valore legale al proprio comune di casa prima o dopo il viaggio. L'alternativa è un <strong>matrimonio civile con valore legale</strong> all'estero: {A(haus,'sposarsi in Austria')} si può fare come cerimonia civile, in alcune regioni persino all'aperto, mentre in Italia l'atto legale avviene solo in comune e la cerimonia in montagna resta simbolica. Vi diciamo esattamente quali documenti servono per i vostri Paesi e quando iniziare."))
    C.append(fig('08-planung-unterschrift-trauung.webp',"An Italian registrar reading during a civil ceremony","Ein italienischer Standesbeamter liest bei einer standesamtlichen Trauung"))
    C.append(fig('10-planung-eheurkunde-unterschreiben.webp',"Signing the marriage documents","Das Unterschreiben der Trauungsunterlagen"))

    C.append(p("Do not let the word legal scare you: in practice it is a short list of documents and a bit of lead time, and we have walked dozens of couples through it. For a symbolic ceremony there is almost nothing to do beyond marrying at home whenever suits you. For a civil marriage abroad, the paperwork &mdash; a certificate of no impediment, birth certificates, sometimes an apostille and sworn translations &mdash; simply needs to be started a few months ahead. We give you a country-specific checklist so you never wonder whether you have missed a form.","Lasst euch vom Wort rechtlich nicht schrecken: In der Praxis ist es eine kurze Liste an Dokumenten und etwas Vorlauf, und wir haben Dutzende Paare hindurchbegleitet. F\u00fcr eine symbolische Zeremonie ist fast nichts zu tun, au\u00dfer zu Hause zu heiraten, wann es euch passt. F\u00fcr eine standesamtliche Trauung im Ausland m\u00fcssen die Papiere &mdash; ein Ehef\u00e4higkeitszeugnis, Geburtsurkunden, manchmal eine Apostille und beglaubigte \u00dcbersetzungen &mdash; einfach ein paar Monate vorher begonnen werden. Wir geben euch eine l\u00e4nderspezifische Checkliste, damit ihr euch nie fragt, ob ihr ein Formular vergessen habt."))
    C.append(h2('details','4 &middot; The details, made easy','4 &middot; Die Details, leicht gemacht'))
    C.append(p("With the big two decided, the rest are the good bits: the dress or suit, hair and make-up, the vows you write, the flowers, the rings. None of it needs to be a project. We bring a trusted hair-and-make-up artist to wherever you are getting ready, arrange a florist who understands mountain conditions, and help you shape vows that sound like you. The small, handwritten, personal things are what the day is really made of &mdash; and they are the easiest to get right with a little guidance.","Sind die großen zwei entschieden, ist der Rest das Schöne: das Kleid oder der Anzug, Haare und Make-up, die Gelübde, die ihr schreibt, die Blumen, die Ringe. Nichts davon muss ein Projekt sein. Wir bringen eine vertraute Haar- und Make-up-Künstlerin dorthin, wo ihr euch fertig macht, organisieren eine Floristin, die Bergbedingungen versteht, und helfen euch, Gelübde zu formen, die nach euch klingen. Die kleinen, handgeschriebenen, persönlichen Dinge sind das, woraus der Tag wirklich besteht &mdash; und sie gelingen mit etwas Anleitung am leichtesten."))
    C.append(fig('04-planung-handgeschriebene-geluebde.webp',"Handwritten vows laid out beside the rings","Handgeschriebene Gelübde neben den Ringen ausgelegt"))
    C.append(fig('01-planung-eheversprechen-und-ringe.webp',"Vow books, rings and personalised details ready for the day","Gelübdebücher, Ringe und persönliche Details bereit für den Tag"))
    C.append(fig('03-planung-braut-styling.webp',"The bride having make-up applied during getting ready","Der Braut wird beim Fertigmachen das Make-up aufgelegt"))

    C.append(p("A word on the things couples forget. Bring layers for the cold at the top, and shoes you can actually walk in with the pretty pair in a bag. Write your vows earlier than you think you need to. Decide who holds the rings on the walk. Eat something before a sunrise start. None of this is hard, but it is the difference between a morning that flows and one that snags &mdash; so we send a short, human checklist a few weeks out, and we carry spares of the small things that always get left on a kitchen table.","Ein Wort zu dem, was Paare vergessen. Nehmt Schichten f\u00fcr die K\u00e4lte oben mit und Schuhe, in denen ihr wirklich gehen k\u00f6nnt, die sch\u00f6nen im Beutel. Schreibt eure Gel\u00fcbde fr\u00fcher, als ihr denkt. Legt fest, wer auf dem Weg die Ringe tr\u00e4gt. Esst etwas vor einem Sonnenaufgangs-Start. Nichts davon ist schwer, aber es ist der Unterschied zwischen einem Morgen, der flie\u00dft, und einem, der hakt &mdash; deshalb schicken wir ein paar Wochen vorher eine kurze, menschliche Checkliste und tragen Ersatz der kleinen Dinge mit, die immer auf einem K\u00fcchentisch liegen bleiben."))
    C.append(h2('experience','5 &middot; Make it unmistakably yours','5 &middot; Macht es unverkennbar zu eurem'))
    C.append(p4(f"This is where an elopement stops being a template. Want a celebrant to lead a truly personal ceremony? A film as well as photographs? A pizza carried to a summit, a cold-water swim, a first dance on an empty ridge? We build the day around your ideas, not a package. Two of our favourites: {A(hh,'arriving by helicopter')} on a remote peak, and, for couples who want the whole story, {A(hp,'proposing here first')} and coming back to marry. If you can picture it, tell us &mdash; the wilder ideas are usually the ones we love most.",f"Hier hört ein Elopement auf, eine Schablone zu sein. Wollt ihr einen Trauredner für eine wirklich persönliche Zeremonie? Einen Film zusätzlich zu den Fotos? Eine Pizza, auf einen Gipfel getragen, ein Bad im kalten Wasser, einen ersten Tanz auf einem leeren Grat? Wir bauen den Tag um eure Ideen, nicht um ein Paket. Zwei unserer Favoriten: {A(hh,'die Anreise per Helikopter')} auf einen abgelegenen Gipfel und, für Paare, die die ganze Geschichte wollen, {A(hp,'hier zuerst den Antrag')} zu machen und zum Heiraten zurückzukommen. Wenn ihr es euch vorstellen könnt, sagt es uns &mdash; die wilderen Ideen sind meist die, die wir am meisten lieben.",f"Aquí es donde un elopement deja de ser una plantilla. ¿Queréis un oficiante que dirija una ceremonia realmente personal? ¿Un vídeo además de las fotos? ¿Una pizza subida a una cumbre, un baño en agua fría, un primer baile en una arista vacía? Construimos el día en torno a vuestras ideas, no a un paquete. Dos de nuestras favoritas: {A(hh,'llegar en helicóptero')} a una cumbre remota y, para las parejas que quieren la historia entera, {A(hp,'pedir matrimonio aquí primero')} y volver a casaros. Si os lo podéis imaginar, decídnoslo &mdash; las ideas más locas suelen ser las que más nos gustan.",f"È qui che un elopement smette di essere un modello. Volete un celebrante che guidi una cerimonia davvero personale? Un video oltre alle foto? Una pizza portata in vetta, un tuffo nell'acqua fredda, un primo ballo su una cresta deserta? Costruiamo la giornata attorno alle vostre idee, non a un pacchetto. Due delle nostre preferite: {A(hh,'arrivare in elicottero')} su una vetta remota e, per le coppie che vogliono l'intera storia, {A(hp,'fare la proposta qui prima')} e tornare a sposarsi. Se riuscite a immaginarlo, ditecelo &mdash; le idee più audaci sono di solito quelle che amiamo di più."))
    C.append(fig('14-planung-freie-trauung-redner.webp',"A celebrant reading during a personal symbolic ceremony","Ein Trauredner liest bei einer persönlichen, freien Zeremonie"))

    C.append(h2('timeline','The planning timeline','Der Planungs-Fahrplan'))
    C.append(p("<strong>9&ndash;6 months out:</strong> settle the feeling, the season and a date range, and reserve us. If you want a legal marriage abroad, this is when the paperwork starts. <strong>6&ndash;3 months:</strong> lock the location and any add-ons &mdash; celebrant, film, helicopter &mdash; and sort the dress, suit and rings. <strong>3&ndash;1 months:</strong> hair and make-up, flowers, travel and where you will stay; we finalise the shot list and the route. <strong>The final weeks:</strong> we watch the forecast, confirm the exact timeline and hold a backup plan. <strong>The day:</strong> you show up; we run everything. It really is that short a list, because most of it sits with us.","<strong>9&ndash;6 Monate vorher:</strong> Gefühl, Saison und Zeitfenster festlegen und uns reservieren. Wollt ihr eine rechtsgültige Trauung im Ausland, beginnt jetzt das Papierwerk. <strong>6&ndash;3 Monate:</strong> Location und Zusatzoptionen festzurren &mdash; Trauredner, Film, Helikopter &mdash; und Kleid, Anzug und Ringe klären. <strong>3&ndash;1 Monate:</strong> Haare und Make-up, Blumen, Anreise und Unterkunft; wir finalisieren Bildplan und Route. <strong>Die letzten Wochen:</strong> Wir beobachten die Vorhersage, bestätigen den genauen Ablauf und halten einen Plan B bereit. <strong>Der Tag:</strong> Ihr kommt; wir machen alles. Die Liste ist wirklich so kurz, weil das meiste bei uns liegt."))
    C.append(fig('05-planung-haare-und-make-up.webp',"The make-up artist at work during the calm of getting ready","Die Make-up-Künstlerin bei der Arbeit in der Ruhe des Fertigmachens"))

    C.append(p("If your timeframe is shorter, do not count yourselves out. A symbolic ceremony can come together in a matter of weeks when a date and the weather line up, because there is no legal lead time to wait on. What a longer runway buys you is choice &mdash; the pick of the best dates, first refusal on the golden mornings, and time for a legal marriage if you want one. Tell us where you are on the calendar and we will tell you honestly what is still possible; the answer is more often yes than couples expect.","Ist euer Zeitrahmen k\u00fcrzer, z\u00e4hlt euch nicht ab. Eine symbolische Zeremonie kann in wenigen Wochen zustande kommen, wenn Termin und Wetter passen, weil es keine rechtliche Vorlaufzeit gibt, auf die man warten muss. Was ein l\u00e4ngerer Vorlauf euch kauft, ist Auswahl &mdash; die besten Termine, das erste Zugriffsrecht auf die goldenen Morgen und Zeit f\u00fcr eine rechtsg\u00fcltige Trauung, wenn ihr eine wollt. Sagt uns, wo ihr im Kalender steht, und wir sagen euch ehrlich, was noch m\u00f6glich ist; die Antwort ist \u00f6fter ja, als Paare erwarten."))
    C.append(h2('permits','Permits, access &amp; the small costs','Genehmigungen, Zugang &amp; die kleinen Kosten'))
    C.append(p("A few practical things sit under the beauty, and we handle all of them. Some places have access rules &mdash; the road to Lago di Braies needs a summer reservation, the Tre Cime is reached by a toll road, several areas are protected nature zones with limits on structures, and private drones are banned across much of the Dolomites. There are small costs beyond the packages, too: cable-car tickets, a landing fee at certain spots, a celebrant, flowers. We lay them all out plainly in advance so nothing is a surprise, and we book and confirm every one before your date.","Ein paar praktische Dinge liegen unter der Schönheit, und wir übernehmen sie alle. Manche Orte haben Zugangsregeln &mdash; die Straße zum Pragser Wildsee braucht eine Sommer-Reservierung, die Drei Zinnen erreicht man über eine Mautstraße, mehrere Gebiete sind geschützte Naturzonen mit Grenzen für Aufbauten, und private Drohnen sind in weiten Teilen der Dolomiten verboten. Es gibt auch kleine Kosten neben den Paketen: Seilbahntickets, eine Landegebühr an bestimmten Orten, einen Trauredner, Blumen. Wir legen sie alle vorab klar dar, damit nichts überrascht, und buchen und bestätigen jede vor eurem Termin."))
    C.append(fig('12-planung-letzte-korrektur.webp',"A last touch of make-up on location before the peaks","Eine letzte Make-up-Korrektur vor Ort vor den Gipfeln"))

    C.append(p("One more reassurance: none of these rules are yours to track. We hold a live picture of what is open, what needs booking and what each season allows, and we build it all into your plan so the admin is simply done. You will hear about it only as a short list of what to bring and where to be &mdash; the paperwork, the permits and the timings stay on our side of the desk.","Noch eine Beruhigung: Keine dieser Regeln m\u00fcsst ihr im Blick behalten. Wir haben ein aktuelles Bild davon, was offen ist, was gebucht werden muss und was jede Saison erlaubt, und bauen alles in euren Plan ein, sodass das Administrative einfach erledigt ist. Ihr h\u00f6rt davon nur als kurze Liste, was mitzubringen ist und wo ihr sein sollt &mdash; die Papiere, die Genehmigungen und das Timing bleiben auf unserer Seite des Schreibtischs."))
    C.append(h2('budget','What it costs','Was es kostet'))
    C.append(p("Our packages start at around <strong>&euro;6,000</strong> and cover the photography, the planning, a scouting trip and your private online gallery. From there you can add what you want: hair and make-up, flowers, a celebrant, film, and up to full coordination of an entire day with accommodation and transfers. An elopement is usually far less than a traditional wedding, and the money is spent differently &mdash; on the experience, the location and the images that last, instead of a hall, a caterer and a headcount. We quote everything in one clear number so you always know where you stand.","Unsere Pakete beginnen bei etwa <strong>6.000&nbsp;&euro;</strong> und umfassen die Fotografie, die Planung, eine Erkundungsreise und eure private Online-Galerie. Von dort ergänzt ihr, was ihr wollt: Haare und Make-up, Blumen, einen Trauredner, Film und bis zur vollen Koordination eines ganzen Tages mit Unterkunft und Transfers. Ein Elopement ist meist weit günstiger als eine klassische Hochzeit, und das Geld wird anders ausgegeben &mdash; für das Erlebnis, den Ort und die Bilder, die bleiben, statt für Saal, Catering und Gästezahl. Wir kalkulieren alles in einer klaren Zahl, damit ihr immer wisst, woran ihr seid."))
    C.append(fig('06-planung-schuhe-ringe-geluebde.webp',"A flatlay of shoes, vow book and ring box","Ein Flatlay aus Schuhen, Gelübdebuch und Ringschachtel"))

    C.append(p("Think of the number as buying time and certainty, not just photos. What you are really paying for is a team that already knows which permit to file, which morning the light will land, which hut has room and which road is open &mdash; the knowledge that turns a logistically fiddly foreign wedding into a calm one. Couples tell us afterwards that the value was not only the gallery, but never once feeling lost or rushed on the most important morning of their lives.","Seht die Zahl als Kauf von Zeit und Sicherheit, nicht nur von Fotos. Wof\u00fcr ihr wirklich zahlt, ist ein Team, das schon wei\u00df, welche Genehmigung einzureichen ist, an welchem Morgen das Licht trifft, welche H\u00fctte Platz hat und welche Stra\u00dfe offen ist &mdash; das Wissen, das aus einer logistisch kniffligen Auslandshochzeit eine ruhige macht. Paare sagen uns hinterher, der Wert sei nicht nur die Galerie gewesen, sondern sich am wichtigsten Morgen ihres Lebens kein einziges Mal verloren oder gehetzt zu f\u00fchlen."))
    C.append(h2('day','A day that never feels rushed','Ein Tag, der sich nie gehetzt anfühlt'))
    C.append(p("Here is how it usually flows. You get ready in calm &mdash; hair, make-up, a coffee, the dress &mdash; while we handle timing and transport. We reach the spot with light to spare, and the ceremony happens when the light is at its best: your words, the rings, a first kiss with the whole range as witness. Then portraits while it is quiet, a moment to simply stand and take it in, and a celebration to match &mdash; a hut breakfast, a picnic, a toast on the mountain. Because we plan generously, there is always time to breathe, and the day feels long in the best way.","So läuft er meist ab. Ihr macht euch in Ruhe fertig &mdash; Haare, Make-up, ein Kaffee, das Kleid &mdash;, während wir Timing und Transport übernehmen. Wir erreichen den Ort mit Licht im Vorrat, und die Zeremonie passiert, wenn das Licht am schönsten ist: eure Worte, die Ringe, ein erster Kuss mit dem ganzen Massiv als Zeugen. Dann Porträts, solange es still ist, ein Moment, einfach zu stehen und es aufzunehmen, und eine Feier passend dazu &mdash; ein Hüttenfrühstück, ein Picknick, ein Toast am Berg. Weil wir großzügig planen, ist immer Zeit zum Atmen, und der Tag fühlt sich lang an &mdash; im besten Sinne."))
    C.append(fig('11-planung-aufbau-zeremonie.webp',"A floral arrangement on a wooden chair at the ceremony spot","Ein Blumenarrangement auf einem Holzstuhl am Zeremonienort"))

    C.append(p("The best moments are almost never the planned ones. It is the laugh after a shaky first line of vows, the way you both go quiet when the sun finally hits the peaks, the walk back down when it has all sunk in. We plan the structure precisely so that these unplanned things have room to happen &mdash; we are not marching you between poses, we are giving you a whole morning together in a beautiful place and quietly photographing the truth of it. That is the entire craft.","Die sch\u00f6nsten Momente sind fast nie die geplanten. Es ist das Lachen nach einer zittrigen ersten Zeile der Gel\u00fcbde, die Art, wie ihr beide still werdet, wenn die Sonne endlich die Gipfel trifft, der Weg hinunter, wenn alles angekommen ist. Wir planen die Struktur genau, damit diese ungeplanten Dinge Raum haben zu geschehen &mdash; wir marschieren euch nicht von Pose zu Pose, wir schenken euch einen ganzen Morgen gemeinsam an einem sch\u00f6nen Ort und fotografieren leise seine Wahrheit. Das ist das ganze Handwerk."))
    C.append(h2('us','Leave the rest to us','Den Rest uns überlassen'))
    C.append(p("If there is one thing to take from all of this, it is how little of it you have to carry. You bring the two of you, the feeling and a rough season; we bring the location knowledge, the permits, the local team, the timeline and the calm. We live in these mountains and plan elopements in them all year, so the things that would take you weeks of research take us a phone call. Tell us what you are dreaming of, and we will send back a simple plan and an honest answer &mdash; and then all that is left for you to do is turn up and get married.","Wenn ihr aus all dem eines mitnehmt, dann, wie wenig ihr davon tragen müsst. Ihr bringt euch beide, das Gefühl und eine grobe Saison; wir bringen das Ortswissen, die Genehmigungen, das lokale Team, den Ablauf und die Ruhe. Wir leben in diesen Bergen und planen das ganze Jahr Elopements darin, deshalb kostet uns ein Anruf, was euch Wochen Recherche kosten würde. Sagt uns, wovon ihr träumt, und wir schicken einen einfachen Plan und eine ehrliche Antwort zurück &mdash; und dann bleibt euch nur noch, aufzutauchen und zu heiraten."))
    C.append(fig('09-planung-standesamt-selva.webp',"A registrar at the town hall in Selva, Val Gardena","Eine Standesbeamtin im Rathaus von Wolkenstein in Gröden"))

    faq_html='<h2 id="faq" style="'+H2S+'">'+L('Planning an elopement: FAQ','Elopement planen: FAQ')+'</h2>'
    FAQL=[FQ(*x) for x in PLAN_FAQ]
    faq_html+=''.join('<div style="margin:1.3em 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:1.1em">'
      f'<h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:20px;margin:0 0 .3em">{q}</h3>'
      f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2);margin:0">{a}</p></div>' for q,a in FAQL)
    faq_ld={"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
      {"@type":"Question","name":_plain(q),"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":_plain(a)}} for q,a in FAQL]}
    related=''.join(story_card(lang,P,STORYBY[sl]) for sl in ex['stories'])
    more=''.join(guide_card(lang,P,x) for x in GUIDES if x['slug']!=slug)
    body=(nav(lang,rel,'howto')+
      f'<section class="page-hero" style="padding:0">{herobg(P,HERO_IMG,g["title"][lang])}'
      f'<div class="content"><div class="wrap"><div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"guide_kick")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h1>{g["title"][lang]}</h1></div></div></section>'
      '<section><div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">'+''.join(C)+faq_html+
      f'<p style="margin-top:2.4em"><a href="{u(P,lang,"how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/")}" class="arrow-link">&larr; {T["nav"]["howto"][lang]}</a></p></div></section>'
      '<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"related_stories")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"related_stories")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{related}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="stories" style="padding-top:clamp(40px,6vw,80px)"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"more_guides")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"more_guides")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{more}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="cta"><div class="wrap row reveal"><div>'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"cta_k")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2 style="margin-top:20px">{t(lang,"cta_h")}</h2></div>'
      f'<a href="{u(P,lang,"get-in-touch/")}" class="btn light">{t(lang,"start_planning")}</a></div></section>'
      +footer(lang,rel))
    write(lang,rel,head(lang,rel,g['title'][lang]+' — Mountain Elopement',g['excerpt'][lang],ld_extra=faq_ld,pre=herolink(P,HERO_IMG))+body+scripts(P))

ALPS_FAQ=[
 ("Dolomites or Tyrol &mdash; which is better for an elopement?",
  "Both are extraordinary; they just feel different. The Dolomites give you the most dramatic, iconic scenery &mdash; pale towers, turquoise lakes, the photos everyone recognises. Tyrol and the Bavarian border give you quieter lakes and meadows, a gentler feel, and the easiest route to a legally binding ceremony. We help you match the range to the mood and the paperwork you want.",
  "Dolomiten oder Tirol &mdash; was ist besser fürs Elopement?",
  "Beide sind außergewöhnlich; sie fühlen sich nur verschieden an. Die Dolomiten geben euch die dramatischste, ikonischste Kulisse &mdash; bleiche Türme, türkise Seen, die Bilder, die jeder erkennt. Tirol und das bayerische Grenzland geben euch stillere Seen und Wiesen, ein sanfteres Gefühl und den einfachsten Weg zu einer rechtsgültigen Zeremonie. Wir stimmen das Massiv auf die Stimmung und die Papiere ab, die ihr wollt."),
 ("Can we get legally married in the mountains here?",
  "In Austria, yes &mdash; a civil ceremony is possible, and in some Tyrolean regions even at an approved outdoor spot, which is why couples who want the legal act on the mountain often choose Tyrol. In Italy the legal marriage happens only at a registry office, so a Dolomite ceremony stays symbolic with the paperwork signed at home. We point you to the right country and path for you.",
  "Können wir hier in den Bergen rechtsgültig heiraten?",
  "In Österreich ja &mdash; eine standesamtliche Trauung ist möglich, in manchen Tiroler Regionen sogar an einem genehmigten Ort im Freien; deshalb wählen Paare, die den Rechtsakt am Berg wollen, oft Tirol. In Italien findet die rechtsgültige Trauung nur am Standesamt statt, eine Dolomitenzeremonie bleibt also symbolisch mit den Papieren zu Hause. Wir weisen euch das richtige Land und den richtigen Weg."),
 ("Which spots need a hike, and which are roadside or by cable car?",
  "It is a real mix, and that is the point &mdash; there is something for every level. Lago di Braies, the Eibsee, Passo Giau and the high passes are essentially roadside; the Zugspitze and other ridges come by cable car; a handful of the quieter lakes and summits want a walk. Tell us how far you like to move and we build the day to fit.",
  "Welche Orte brauchen eine Wanderung, welche sind an der Straße oder per Bergbahn?",
  "Es ist eine echte Mischung, und das ist der Reiz &mdash; für jedes Niveau etwas. Der Pragser Wildsee, der Eibsee, der Passo Giau und die hohen Pässe liegen quasi an der Straße; die Zugspitze und andere Grate erreicht ihr per Bergbahn; eine Handvoll stillerer Seen und Gipfel wollen einen Fußweg. Sagt uns, wie weit ihr euch gern bewegt, und wir bauen den Tag passend."),
 ("Where is best for a lake elopement in the Alps?",
  "You are spoilt for choice. Lago di Braies is the turquoise icon; the Eibsee below the Zugspitze is emerald green and framed by forest; and the quieter Tyrolean mountain lakes give you the same mirror water with almost no one around. All of them are best at first light, before the day arrives.",
  "Wo eignet sich in den Alpen ein See-Elopement am besten?",
  "Die Auswahl ist üppig. Der Pragser Wildsee ist die türkise Ikone; der Eibsee unter der Zugspitze ist smaragdgrün und von Wald gerahmt; und die stilleren Tiroler Bergseen geben euch dasselbe Spiegelwasser fast ohne Menschen. Alle sind bei erstem Licht am schönsten, ehe der Tag kommt."),
 ("Which locations work best in winter?",
  "The high, jagged places are unforgettable under snow &mdash; the Tre Cime and the snow ridges turn monochrome and dramatic, and you may have them entirely to yourselves. The trade-off is access: some toll roads and lifts run reduced or close, and it asks for warm layers and sure footing. We plan around what is actually open and safe.",
  "Welche Orte funktionieren im Winter am besten?",
  "Die hohen, schroffen Orte sind unter Schnee unvergesslich &mdash; die Drei Zinnen und die Schneegrate werden monochrom und dramatisch, und ihr habt sie vielleicht ganz für euch. Der Preis ist die Erreichbarkeit: Manche Mautstraßen und Bahnen fahren reduziert oder schließen, und es verlangt warme Schichten und sicheren Tritt. Wir planen um das, was wirklich offen und sicher ist."),
 ("How many locations can we combine?",
  "Fewer than you might think, and on purpose. Chasing five spots means seeing none of them properly; we usually plan one hero location for the best light and perhaps an easier second nearby. Over a few days across the range we can string together a proper tour &mdash; a lake at dawn, a pass in the evening, a summit the next morning.",
  "Wie viele Orte können wir verbinden?",
  "Weniger, als ihr denkt &mdash; mit Absicht. Fünf Orte zu jagen heißt, keinen richtig zu sehen; wir planen meist einen Haupt-Ort für das beste Licht und vielleicht einen leichteren zweiten in der Nähe. Über ein paar Tage quer durchs Massiv reihen wir eine richtige Tour aneinander &mdash; ein See im Morgengrauen, ein Pass am Abend, ein Gipfel am nächsten Morgen."),
]

# --- best-alps guide ES/IT (auto-generated, keyed by exact EN string) ---
ALPS_ES = {
  'Choosing your range': 'Elegir vuestro macizo',
  'Start with the feeling, not the pin. Do you want the postcard drama of the Dolomites, the alpine calm of a Tyrolean lake, or a summit you can stand on above everything? Effort, access, season and &mdash; importantly &mdash; where you can legally marry all pull on the choice. Below we walk through the corners of the Alps we love most, what each does best, and who each one suits. You do not have to know the place before you know the mood; that is our job.': 'Empezad por el sentimiento, no por el punto en el mapa. ¿Queréis el drama de postal de los Dolomitas, la calma alpina de un lago tirolés o una cumbre sobre la que estar por encima de todo? El esfuerzo, el acceso, la estación y &mdash; importante &mdash; dónde podéis casaros legalmente tiran todos de la elección. Abajo recorremos los rincones de los Alpes que más amamos, lo que cada uno hace mejor y a quién le va cada uno. No tenéis que conocer el lugar antes de conocer el ambiente; ese es nuestro trabajo.',
  'The turquoise water and peaks of Lago di Braies in the Dolomites': 'El agua turquesa y las cumbres del Lago di Braies en los Dolomitas',
  'A few honest questions shorten the whole search. How far are you happy to walk? Do you need to be legally married on the day, or is a symbolic ceremony with the paperwork at home fine? Warm and green, or cold and white? Just the two of you, or a few guests who need an easy path? Your answers rule half the map out in minutes &mdash; and what is left is almost always a place you did not know to ask for.': 'Unas pocas preguntas honestas acortan toda la búsqueda. ¿Hasta dónde estáis dispuestos a caminar? ¿Necesitáis estar legalmente casados el día señalado, o basta una ceremonia simbólica con el papeleo en casa? ¿Cálido y verde, o frío y blanco? ¿Solo los dos, o unos invitados que necesitan un camino fácil? Vuestras respuestas descartan media mapa en minutos &mdash; y lo que queda es casi siempre un lugar que no sabíais pedir.',
  'The Dolomites &mdash; the icons': 'Los Dolomitas &mdash; los iconos',
  'The Dolomites are where most couples start dreaming, and for good reason: pale limestone towers that blush pink at dusk, turquoise lakes, tiny chapels on green passes. It is the most dramatic, most recognisable scenery in the Alps &mdash; Lago di Braies, the Tre Cime, the Seceda ridge, Passo Giau. The catch is fame: the icons fill up, so we plan around first light and quieter twins. If the Dolomites are calling, we have a whole separate guide to their most beautiful spots &mdash; but here is the short version of why they are worth it.': 'Los Dolomitas son donde la mayoría de las parejas empieza a soñar, y con razón: pálidas torres de caliza que se sonrojan de rosa al atardecer, lagos turquesa, capillas diminutas en puertos verdes. Es la escena más dramática y reconocible de los Alpes &mdash; el Lago di Braies, las Tre Cime, la cresta del Seceda, el Passo Giau. La trampa es la fama: los iconos se llenan, así que planificamos en torno a la primera luz y a gemelos más tranquilos. Si los Dolomitas os llaman, tenemos una guía aparte de sus lugares más bellos &mdash; pero aquí va la versión corta de por qué merecen la pena.',
  'A couple small on a green meadow beneath the Ra Gusela and Croda da Lago peaks': 'Una pareja pequeña en un prado verde bajo las cumbres de la Ra Gusela y la Croda da Lago',
  'The couple embracing at the shore of Lago di Braies': 'La pareja abrazada en la orilla del Lago di Braies',
  'What makes the Dolomites unlike other mountains is the colour. At dusk the pale limestone catches the last light and glows ember-red for a few unrepeatable minutes &mdash; the locals call it enrosadira, and no photograph quite prepares you for it in person. Pair that with water the colour of a swimming pool and meadows full of cotton grass, and you understand why this is where the dreaming starts. We simply make sure you are standing in the right spot when the rock catches fire.': 'Lo que hace a los Dolomitas distintos de otras montañas es el color. Al atardecer la pálida caliza atrapa la última luz y brilla de un rojo brasa durante unos minutos irrepetibles &mdash; los lugareños lo llaman enrosadira, y ninguna foto os prepara del todo para verlo en persona. Sumadle agua del color de una piscina y prados llenos de algodón de pantano, y entendéis por qué aquí empieza el sueño. Nosotros solo nos aseguramos de que estéis en el lugar correcto cuando la roca prende fuego.',
  'The Zugspitze &mdash; Germany&rsquo;s roof': 'La Zugspitze &mdash; el techo de Alemania',
  'On the German&ndash;Austrian border stands the Zugspitze, the highest peak in Germany, and standing on its ridges feels like standing on the roof of the country &mdash; a sea of summits in every direction. A cable car carries you most of the way, so the drama comes without a two-day climb, and the rock up here is raw and cinematic, especially in the bare light of morning. It is a favourite for couples who want the feeling of real altitude with an easy path to it.': 'En la frontera germano-austriaca se alza la Zugspitze, el pico más alto de Alemania, y estar en sus crestas se siente como estar en el techo del país &mdash; un mar de cumbres en todas las direcciones. Un teleférico os sube casi todo el camino, así que el drama llega sin una ascensión de dos días, y la roca aquí arriba es cruda y cinematográfica, sobre todo en la luz desnuda de la mañana. Es un favorito para las parejas que quieren la sensación de altitud real con un camino fácil hasta ella.',
  'The couple on a rocky ridge near the Zugspitze in dramatic black and white': 'La pareja en una cresta rocosa cerca de la Zugspitze en un dramático blanco y negro',
  'There is something quietly moving about marrying at the top of a whole country. The Zugspitze straddles the border, so on a clear morning you look out over both Germany and Austria at once, ridge after ridge fading into haze. It is exposed and wild up here, so we time it for calm light and keep the ceremony nimble &mdash; but the reward is a sense of scale and height that a valley simply cannot give, reached by a cable car rather than a rope.': 'Hay algo silenciosamente emocionante en casarse en la cima de un país entero. La Zugspitze se asienta sobre la frontera, así que en una mañana clara miráis a la vez sobre Alemania y Austria, cresta tras cresta desvaneciéndose en la bruma. Aquí arriba es expuesto y salvaje, así que lo calculamos para luz tranquila y mantenemos la ceremonia ágil &mdash; pero la recompensa es una sensación de escala y altura que un valle sencillamente no puede dar, alcanzada en teleférico en vez de con cuerda.',
  'There is a rare bonus up here, too: you can actually marry on the Zugspitze summit officially and legally, through the registry office in Garmisch-Partenkirchen. The catch is demand &mdash; the summit slots are hugely popular and go quickly, and dates can only be requested about six months ahead, so this one rewards early, decisive planning. We help you time the request.': 'Aquí arriba hay además un raro extra: en la cumbre de la Zugspitze podéis casaros de verdad de forma oficial y legal, a través del registro civil de Garmisch-Partenkirchen. La pega es la demanda &mdash; las plazas de la cumbre son muy solicitadas y se agotan rápido, y las fechas solo pueden pedirse con unos seis meses de antelación, así que esta recompensa la planificación temprana y decidida. Os ayudamos a calcular la solicitud.',
  'The Eibsee &mdash; emerald water': 'El Eibsee &mdash; agua esmeralda',
  'At the foot of the Zugspitze lies the Eibsee, one of the most beautiful lakes in the Bavarian Alps &mdash; a startling emerald green, ringed by dark forest with the great mountain rising straight behind. It is roadside and easy, gentle for a dress and a small ceremony, and a real alternative to the busier Dolomite lakes for couples who want water and a giant peak without the crowds. First light on still water here is pure calm.': 'Al pie de la Zugspitze se encuentra el Eibsee, uno de los lagos más bellos de los Alpes bávaros &mdash; un sorprendente verde esmeralda, rodeado de bosque oscuro con la gran montaña alzándose justo detrás. Está junto a la carretera y es fácil, suave para un vestido y una pequeña ceremonia, y una verdadera alternativa a los lagos dolomíticos más concurridos para parejas que quieren agua y un pico gigante sin las multitudes. La primera luz sobre el agua quieta es aquí pura calma.',
  'A ceremony at the forested shore of the Eibsee below the Zugspitze': 'Una ceremonia en la orilla boscosa del Eibsee, bajo la Zugspitze',
  'The Eibsee also makes a gentle base for the whole trip. It is minutes from Garmisch-Partenkirchen, easy to reach, and it pairs a lake morning with a summit afternoon on the same mountain &mdash; water and altitude in one day, without a long drive between them. For couples who want the calm of a forest lake first and the drama of a high ridge second, it is one of the neatest days the Alps offer.': 'El Eibsee también es una base suave para todo el viaje. Está a minutos de Garmisch-Partenkirchen, es fácil de alcanzar, y combina una mañana de lago con una tarde de cumbre en la misma montaña &mdash; agua y altitud en un día, sin una larga conducción entre ambas. Para parejas que quieren primero la calma de un lago de bosque y luego el drama de una cresta alta, es uno de los días más redondos que ofrecen los Alpes.',
  'One honest note on the legal side: a free, symbolic ceremony at the Eibsee is straightforward and needs no special permit &mdash; but it is not legally binding, so the marriage itself is signed at a registry, either at home or beforehand. If you want the legal act on the mountain in Bavaria, the Zugspitze summit above is the route; otherwise the Eibsee is a beautiful place to say your own words and keep the paperwork simple.': 'Una nota honesta sobre lo legal: una ceremonia libre y simbólica en el Eibsee es sencilla y no necesita permiso especial &mdash; pero no tiene validez legal, así que el matrimonio en sí se firma en un registro civil, en casa o de antemano. Si queréis el acto legal en la montaña en Baviera, la cumbre de la Zugspitze de arriba es la vía; si no, el Eibsee es un lugar precioso para decir vuestras propias palabras y mantener el papeleo simple.',
  'Tyrol &mdash; lakes, meadows &amp; the easy legal route': 'Tirol &mdash; lagos, prados y la vía legal fácil',
  'Tyrol is our quiet secret: hidden mountain lakes, rolling green meadows under snow-streaked peaks, and villages an easy drive from Innsbruck. It rarely has the crowds of the famous Dolomite icons, and it has one big practical advantage &mdash; in Austria you can marry legally, and in some regions even at an approved outdoor spot. For couples who want the legal act on the mountain rather than a symbolic one, Tyrol is often the answer, and it is every bit as beautiful.': 'Tirol es nuestro secreto tranquilo: lagos de montaña escondidos, ondulantes prados verdes bajo cumbres veteadas de nieve, y pueblos a un cómodo trayecto de Innsbruck. Rara vez tiene las multitudes de los famosos iconos dolomíticos, y tiene una gran ventaja práctica &mdash; en Austria podéis casaros legalmente, y en algunas regiones incluso en un lugar autorizado al aire libre. Para parejas que quieren el acto legal en la montaña en vez de uno simbólico, Tirol es a menudo la respuesta, y es igual de bello.',
  'A pampas-grass arch set by a Tyrolean mountain lake with autumn larches': 'Un arco de pampa junto a un lago de montaña tirolés con alerces otoñales',
  'The couple at the arch beside the still Tyrolean lake': 'La pareja en el arco junto al quieto lago tirolés',
  'A ceremony in Tyrol with a backdrop of snow-streaked jagged peaks': 'Una ceremonia en Tirol con un fondo de cumbres escarpadas veteadas de nieve',
  'Tyrol also rewards the couple who want a little Alpine culture around the day. Timber villages with onion-domed churches, mountain huts serving long lunches, cable cars that open the high pastures &mdash; it feels lived-in and warm rather than remote. Innsbruck itself, with its old town under the Nordkette, makes a beautiful and practical base, an hour or less from lakes, meadows and the ridges above the city.': 'Tirol premia también a la pareja que quiere un poco de cultura alpina alrededor del día. Pueblos de madera con iglesias de cúpula de cebolla, refugios de montaña que sirven comidas largas, teleféricos que abren los altos pastos &mdash; se siente habitado y cálido más que remoto. La propia Innsbruck, con su casco antiguo bajo la Nordkette, es una base bella y práctica, a una hora o menos de lagos, prados y las crestas sobre la ciudad.',
  'The great passes': 'Los grandes puertos',
  'The high passes that link the valleys &mdash; Passo Giau, Passo Gardena, Passo Sella &mdash; are the easy secret of the range: you drive to over 2,000 metres and step straight onto alpine meadow with the giants all around, no climb required. Giau in particular, with its little pointed chapel under the shark-fin peak of Ra Gusela, gives you drama and a touch of storybook without a hike, and the evening light there is some of the best anywhere. Perfect for couples who want the high-mountain feeling with family in tow.': 'Los altos puertos que enlazan los valles &mdash; Passo Giau, Passo Gardena, Passo Sella &mdash; son el secreto fácil del macizo: conducís a más de 2.000 metros y salís directamente a pradera alpina con los gigantes alrededor, sin subida. El Giau en particular, con su pequeña capilla puntiaguda bajo la cumbre en aleta de tiburón de la Ra Gusela, os da drama y un toque de cuento sin caminata, y la luz de la tarde allí es de las mejores en cualquier parte. Perfecto para parejas que quieren la sensación de alta montaña con la familia a cuestas.',
  'The little pointed chapel at Passo Giau with Ra Gusela rising behind': 'La pequeña capilla puntiaguda del Passo Giau con la Ra Gusela alzándose detrás',
  'A small ceremony on the meadow beneath the walls of the Sella group': 'Una pequeña ceremonia en la pradera bajo las paredes del grupo del Sella',
  'Green meadow and a hut at Passo Gardena as the sun breaks through': 'Pradera verde y un refugio en el Passo Gardena mientras el sol irrumpe',
  'The other gift of the passes is the light. Because they sit high and open, with nothing between you and the horizon, they catch sunrise and sunset in full &mdash; and Giau in particular faces the evening so well that we often plan it for golden hour and enrosadira rather than dawn. Park, walk a minute onto the meadow, and let the sky do the rest; you can be back down to a valley dinner within the hour.': 'El otro regalo de los puertos es la luz. Como están altos y abiertos, sin nada entre vosotros y el horizonte, atrapan el amanecer y el atardecer por completo &mdash; y el Giau en particular da tan bien a la tarde que a menudo lo planificamos para la hora dorada y la enrosadira en vez del alba. Aparcáis, camináis un minuto a la pradera y dejáis que el cielo haga el resto; podéis estar de vuelta para una cena en el valle en una hora.',
  'For the peak-baggers': 'Para los conquistadores de cumbres',
  'If you want the day to feel earned, the Alps reward the effort like nowhere else. A ridge reached on foot or by a short climb from a lift gives you exposure, a 360-degree horizon and a scale that stops the breath &mdash; you standing tiny against a thousand metres of rock. These are the boldest frames we take, and the most private: five more minutes past where most people turn around, and the mountain is yours. We match the walk to your fitness and never oversell what a spot costs to reach.': 'Si queréis que el día se sienta ganado, los Alpes premian el esfuerzo como ningún otro sitio. Una cresta alcanzada a pie o con una corta subida desde un remonte os da exposición, un horizonte de 360 grados y una escala que corta la respiración &mdash; vosotros diminutos ante mil metros de roca. Son los encuadres más audaces que hacemos, y los más íntimos: cinco minutos más allá de donde la mayoría da la vuelta, y la montaña es vuestra. Ajustamos la caminata a vuestra forma y nunca exageramos lo que cuesta llegar a un lugar.',
  'The couple tiny on a ridge before a vast snow-streaked cirque': 'La pareja diminuta en una cresta ante un vasto circo veteado de nieve',
  'None of this has to mean a mountaineering epic. Many of our most dramatic ridge frames sit only a short, safe walk from a cable-car station &mdash; enough to leave the crowds behind, not enough to need ropes or a guide. We scout every route in advance, carry the plan and the spare layers, and pace it so the walk feels like part of the adventure rather than a chore. If you can manage an hour on a trail, we can put you somewhere that looks impossible.': 'Nada de esto tiene que significar una epopeya de alpinismo. Muchos de nuestros encuadres de cresta más dramáticos están a solo un corto y seguro paseo de una estación de teleférico &mdash; suficiente para dejar atrás a la gente, no tanto para necesitar cuerdas o un guía. Exploramos cada ruta de antemano, cargamos el plan y las capas de repuesto y la dosificamos para que la caminata se sienta parte de la aventura en vez de una tarea. Si podéis con una hora en un sendero, os ponemos en un sitio que parece imposible.',
  'The Alps under snow': 'Los Alpes bajo la nieve',
  'Winter turns the whole range monochrome and almost unearthly &mdash; snow to the horizon, the peaks stripped to black and white, and, best of all, near-total solitude. The Tre Cime and the high snow ridges are unforgettable in this light, and a ceremony up here feels like standing inside a snow globe. It asks for more &mdash; warm layers, sure footing, and a close eye on which toll roads and lifts are open, because winter schedules are reduced. When it lines up, it is the most spectacular version of the Alps we photograph all year.': 'El invierno vuelve todo el macizo monocromo y casi de otro mundo &mdash; nieve hasta el horizonte, las cumbres reducidas a blanco y negro y, lo mejor de todo, una soledad casi total. Las Tre Cime y las altas crestas nevadas son inolvidables con esta luz, y una ceremonia aquí arriba se siente como estar dentro de una bola de nieve. Pide más &mdash; capas de abrigo, pisada firme y un ojo atento a qué carreteras de peaje y teleféricos están abiertos, porque los horarios de invierno son reducidos. Cuando cuadra, es la versión más espectacular de los Alpes que fotografiamos en todo el año.',
  'The couple in the snow with the Tre Cime spires glowing behind': 'La pareja en la nieve con las torres de las Tre Cime brillando detrás',
  'The couple on a snowy plateau below the Tre Cime in full winter': 'La pareja en un plateau nevado bajo las Tre Cime en pleno invierno',
  'Winter also thins the calendar in your favour. The couples who brave the cold have the most famous places almost entirely to themselves, and the low sun sits soft and golden for hours instead of minutes. Dress for it &mdash; warm layers under the coat, real boots to the spot, the pretty shoes in a bag &mdash; and a grey, snowing sky is not a setback but a gift, giving some of the most atmospheric mountain photographs we ever take.': 'El invierno también adelgaza el calendario a vuestro favor. Las parejas que se atreven con el frío tienen los lugares más famosos casi enteramente para ellas, y el sol bajo se posa suave y dorado durante horas en vez de minutos. Vestíos para ello &mdash; capas de abrigo bajo el abrigo, botas de verdad hasta el lugar, los zapatos bonitos en una bolsa &mdash; y un cielo gris y nevando no es un contratiempo sino un regalo, que da algunas de las fotos de montaña más atmosféricas que hacemos.',
  'Which one is yours': '¿Cuál es el vuestro?',
  'So how to choose? Go to the <strong>Dolomites</strong> for maximum drama and the icons at their quietest. Go to <strong>Tyrol or Bavaria</strong> for calmer lakes, gentler effort and the easy legal route. Choose a <strong>lake</strong> if you want stillness and reflection, a <strong>pass</strong> if you want big mountains with no hike, a <strong>summit</strong> if you want to earn the view, and <strong>winter</strong> if you want solitude and drama over warmth. When couples truly cannot decide, we split it across a couple of days &mdash; a lake at dawn, a pass at dusk. Tell us the feeling and we will name the place.': 'Entonces, ¿cómo elegir? Id a los <strong>Dolomitas</strong> para el máximo drama y los iconos en su versión más tranquila. Id a <strong>Tirol o Baviera</strong> para lagos más calmados, menos esfuerzo y la vía legal fácil. Elegid un <strong>lago</strong> si queréis quietud y reflejo, un <strong>puerto</strong> si queréis grandes montañas sin caminata, una <strong>cumbre</strong> si queréis ganaros la vista, y el <strong>invierno</strong> si preferís la soledad y el drama a la calidez. Cuando una pareja de verdad no consigue decidir, lo repartimos en un par de días &mdash; un lago al alba, un puerto al ocaso. Decidnos el sentimiento y os nombraremos el lugar.',
  'And you are not locked into one answer. Some of our favourite trips mix two worlds across a few days &mdash; a quiet Tyrolean lake at sunrise, an easy legal ceremony, then a drive south for a Dolomite sunset the next evening. The ranges sit close enough that a single trip can hold both the calm and the drama. Tell us the two feelings you cannot choose between, and we will often find a way to give you both.': 'Y no estáis atados a una sola respuesta. Algunos de nuestros viajes favoritos mezclan dos mundos en unos pocos días &mdash; un tranquilo lago tirolés al amanecer, una ceremonia legal fácil, y luego una conducción al sur para un atardecer dolomítico a la tarde siguiente. Los macizos están lo bastante cerca como para que un solo viaje pueda contener la calma y el drama. Decidnos los dos sentimientos entre los que no podéis elegir, y a menudo encontraremos la manera de daros ambos.',
  'Getting around the Alps': 'Cómo moverse por los Alpes',
  'The range is easier to reach than the drama suggests. Most couples fly into Venice, Verona, Innsbruck or Munich and drive in &mdash; the Dolomites are two to three hours from Venice, the Zugspitze and Eibsee sit right on the Bavarian border near Garmisch, and Tyrol spreads out around Innsbruck. Crossing between Italy and Austria is a simple drive with no fuss. From a single valley base you can often reach several of these spots, and we build the route around the light &mdash; which place at dawn, which at dusk &mdash; and handle the reservations, timings and driving so your mornings stay calm.': 'El macizo es más fácil de alcanzar de lo que sugiere el drama. La mayoría de las parejas vuela a Venecia, Verona, Innsbruck o Múnich y conduce hacia dentro &mdash; los Dolomitas están a dos o tres horas de Venecia, la Zugspitze y el Eibsee se asientan justo en la frontera bávara cerca de Garmisch, y Tirol se extiende alrededor de Innsbruck. Cruzar entre Italia y Austria es una conducción sencilla, sin complicaciones. Desde una sola base en el valle podéis alcanzar a menudo varios de estos lugares, y construimos la ruta en torno a la luz &mdash; qué sitio al alba, cuál al ocaso &mdash; y gestionamos las reservas, los horarios y la conducción para que vuestras mañanas sigan tranquilas.',
  'Where you base yourself shapes the trip as much as where you shoot. Cortina d&rsquo;Ampezzo and the Alta Badia put you in the heart of the Dolomites; Garmisch sits right under the Zugspitze; Innsbruck opens up Tyrol in every direction. We help you pick the base that keeps your chosen spots within an easy dawn drive, book the huts where an overnight makes a sunrise possible, and hand you a simple plan so the only thing you have to think about on the day is each other.': 'Dónde os alojáis marca el viaje tanto como dónde fotografiáis. Cortina d&rsquo;Ampezzo y la Alta Badia os ponen en el corazón de los Dolomitas; Garmisch está justo bajo la Zugspitze; Innsbruck abre Tirol en todas las direcciones. Os ayudamos a elegir la base que mantiene vuestros lugares a un cómodo trayecto al alba, reservamos los refugios donde una noche hace posible un amanecer, y os entregamos un plan sencillo para que lo único en lo que tengáis que pensar ese día seáis el uno en el otro.',
  'Light &amp; the finish': 'La luz y el cierre',
  'Wherever you land in the Alps, the light is the thing &mdash; and the day is not over when the sun drops. Sunrise gives you empty icons and soft colour; golden hour warms the rock and slides into the fireshow of enrosadira on the Dolomite walls; and blue hour, the cool quiet window after, is the one most people miss by packing up too soon. We never do. Then the celebration to match &mdash; a hut dinner, a swim, a toast on the mountain &mdash; because the best locations deserve more than a single frame.': 'Dondequiera que aterricéis en los Alpes, la luz es lo esencial &mdash; y el día no termina cuando cae el sol. El amanecer os da iconos vacíos y color suave; la hora dorada calienta la roca y se desliza hacia el espectáculo de fuego de la enrosadira en las paredes dolomíticas; y la hora azul, la ventana fresca y tranquila de después, es la que la mayoría se pierde por recoger demasiado pronto. Nosotros nunca. Luego la celebración a la altura &mdash; una cena en un refugio, un baño, un brindis en la montaña &mdash; porque los mejores lugares merecen más que un solo fotograma.',
  'The couple at a floral arch backlit by a blazing Tyrolean sunset': 'La pareja en un arco floral a contraluz de un ardiente atardecer tirolés',
  'The Dolomites': 'Los Dolomitas',
  'Zugspitze': 'Zugspitze',
  'Eibsee & the lakes': 'Eibsee y los lagos',
  'Tyrol': 'Tirol',
  'The Alps in winter': 'Los Alpes en invierno',
  'Which suits you': 'Cuál es el vuestro',
  'Getting around': 'Cómo moverse',
  'Light & the finish': 'La luz y el cierre',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'Best Alpine locations FAQ': 'Preguntas frecuentes sobre los mejores lugares alpinos',
  'The Alps are not one landscape but a dozen, and the right elopement spot is the one that matches the day in your head. We shoot across the range &mdash; the pale towers of the Dolomites, the emerald lakes below Germany&rsquo;s highest peak, the quiet meadows and mirror lakes of Tyrol &mdash; and each corner has its own character, its own light and its own rules. This is our honest field guide to the places we return to again and again, and how to choose the one that is yours.': 'Los Alpes no son un paisaje sino una docena, y el lugar de elopement adecuado es el que encaja con el día que tenéis en la cabeza. Fotografiamos por todo el macizo &mdash; las pálidas torres de los Dolomitas, los lagos esmeralda bajo el pico más alto de Alemania, los prados tranquilos y los lagos espejo de Tirol &mdash; y cada rincón tiene su propio carácter, su propia luz y sus propias reglas. Esta es nuestra guía de campo honesta de los lugares a los que volvemos una y otra vez, y cómo elegir el que es vuestro.',
  'On this page': 'En esta página',
}
ALPS_IT = {
  'Choosing your range': 'Scegliere il vostro massiccio',
  'Start with the feeling, not the pin. Do you want the postcard drama of the Dolomites, the alpine calm of a Tyrolean lake, or a summit you can stand on above everything? Effort, access, season and &mdash; importantly &mdash; where you can legally marry all pull on the choice. Below we walk through the corners of the Alps we love most, what each does best, and who each one suits. You do not have to know the place before you know the mood; that is our job.': "Partite dalla sensazione, non dallo spillo. Volete il dramma da cartolina delle Dolomiti, la calma alpina di un lago tirolese o una vetta su cui stare al di sopra di tutto? La fatica, l'accesso, la stagione e &mdash; importante &mdash; dove potete sposarvi legalmente tirano tutti sulla scelta. Qui sotto percorriamo gli angoli delle Alpi che amiamo di più, ciò che ciascuno fa meglio e a chi si addice ognuno. Non dovete conoscere il luogo prima di conoscere l'atmosfera; questo è il nostro lavoro.",
  'The turquoise water and peaks of Lago di Braies in the Dolomites': "L'acqua turchese e le cime del Lago di Braies nelle Dolomiti",
  'A few honest questions shorten the whole search. How far are you happy to walk? Do you need to be legally married on the day, or is a symbolic ceremony with the paperwork at home fine? Warm and green, or cold and white? Just the two of you, or a few guests who need an easy path? Your answers rule half the map out in minutes &mdash; and what is left is almost always a place you did not know to ask for.': 'Poche domande oneste accorciano tutta la ricerca. Fin dove siete disposti a camminare? Dovete essere legalmente sposati nel giorno, o basta una cerimonia simbolica con le pratiche a casa? Caldo e verde, o freddo e bianco? Solo voi due, o qualche invitato che ha bisogno di un percorso facile? Le vostre risposte escludono metà mappa in pochi minuti &mdash; e ciò che resta è quasi sempre un luogo che non sapevate di chiedere.',
  'The Dolomites &mdash; the icons': 'Le Dolomiti &mdash; le icone',
  'The Dolomites are where most couples start dreaming, and for good reason: pale limestone towers that blush pink at dusk, turquoise lakes, tiny chapels on green passes. It is the most dramatic, most recognisable scenery in the Alps &mdash; Lago di Braies, the Tre Cime, the Seceda ridge, Passo Giau. The catch is fame: the icons fill up, so we plan around first light and quieter twins. If the Dolomites are calling, we have a whole separate guide to their most beautiful spots &mdash; but here is the short version of why they are worth it.': 'Le Dolomiti sono dove la maggior parte delle coppie inizia a sognare, e a ragione: pallide torri di calcare che si tingono di rosa al tramonto, laghi turchesi, minuscole cappelle su passi verdi. È la scena più drammatica e riconoscibile delle Alpi &mdash; il Lago di Braies, le Tre Cime, la cresta della Seceda, il Passo Giau. Il rovescio è la fama: le icone si riempiono, quindi pianifichiamo attorno alla prima luce e a gemelli più tranquilli. Se le Dolomiti vi chiamano, abbiamo una guida a parte ai loro luoghi più belli &mdash; ma ecco la versione breve del perché ne valgono la pena.',
  'A couple small on a green meadow beneath the Ra Gusela and Croda da Lago peaks': 'Una coppia piccola su un prato verde sotto le cime della Ra Gusela e della Croda da Lago',
  'The couple embracing at the shore of Lago di Braies': 'La coppia abbracciata sulla riva del Lago di Braies',
  'What makes the Dolomites unlike other mountains is the colour. At dusk the pale limestone catches the last light and glows ember-red for a few unrepeatable minutes &mdash; the locals call it enrosadira, and no photograph quite prepares you for it in person. Pair that with water the colour of a swimming pool and meadows full of cotton grass, and you understand why this is where the dreaming starts. We simply make sure you are standing in the right spot when the rock catches fire.': "Ciò che rende le Dolomiti diverse dalle altre montagne è il colore. Al tramonto il pallido calcare cattura l'ultima luce e brilla di un rosso brace per pochi minuti irripetibili &mdash; la gente del posto lo chiama enrosadira, e nessuna foto vi prepara del tutto a vederlo di persona. Aggiungete acqua del colore di una piscina e prati pieni di erioforo, e capite perché è qui che inizia il sogno. Noi ci assicuriamo solo che siate nel punto giusto quando la roccia prende fuoco.",
  'The Zugspitze &mdash; Germany&rsquo;s roof': 'La Zugspitze &mdash; il tetto della Germania',
  'On the German&ndash;Austrian border stands the Zugspitze, the highest peak in Germany, and standing on its ridges feels like standing on the roof of the country &mdash; a sea of summits in every direction. A cable car carries you most of the way, so the drama comes without a two-day climb, and the rock up here is raw and cinematic, especially in the bare light of morning. It is a favourite for couples who want the feeling of real altitude with an easy path to it.': 'Sul confine tra Germania e Austria si erge la Zugspitze, la vetta più alta della Germania, e stare sulle sue creste è come stare sul tetto del Paese &mdash; un mare di cime in ogni direzione. Una funivia vi porta quasi fino in cima, quindi il dramma arriva senza una salita di due giorni, e la roccia quassù è cruda e cinematografica, soprattutto nella luce spoglia del mattino. È una preferita per le coppie che vogliono la sensazione della vera quota con un percorso facile per raggiungerla.',
  'The couple on a rocky ridge near the Zugspitze in dramatic black and white': 'La coppia su una cresta rocciosa vicino alla Zugspitze in un drammatico bianco e nero',
  'There is something quietly moving about marrying at the top of a whole country. The Zugspitze straddles the border, so on a clear morning you look out over both Germany and Austria at once, ridge after ridge fading into haze. It is exposed and wild up here, so we time it for calm light and keep the ceremony nimble &mdash; but the reward is a sense of scale and height that a valley simply cannot give, reached by a cable car rather than a rope.': "C'è qualcosa di silenziosamente commovente nello sposarsi sulla cima di un intero Paese. La Zugspitze è a cavallo del confine, quindi in una mattina limpida guardate insieme sulla Germania e sull'Austria, cresta dopo cresta che svanisce nella foschia. Quassù è esposto e selvaggio, quindi lo calcoliamo per luce tranquilla e teniamo la cerimonia agile &mdash; ma la ricompensa è un senso di dimensione e altezza che una valle semplicemente non può dare, raggiunto in funivia invece che con la corda.",
  'There is a rare bonus up here, too: you can actually marry on the Zugspitze summit officially and legally, through the registry office in Garmisch-Partenkirchen. The catch is demand &mdash; the summit slots are hugely popular and go quickly, and dates can only be requested about six months ahead, so this one rewards early, decisive planning. We help you time the request.': "Quassù c'è anche un raro bonus: sulla cima della Zugspitze potete sposarvi davvero in modo ufficiale e con valore legale, tramite l'ufficio di stato civile di Garmisch-Partenkirchen. Il problema è la richiesta &mdash; i posti in vetta sono molto ambiti e vanno via in fretta, e le date si possono richiedere solo con circa sei mesi di anticipo, quindi questa ripaga una pianificazione precoce e decisa. Vi aiutiamo a calcolare la richiesta.",
  'The Eibsee &mdash; emerald water': "L'Eibsee &mdash; acqua smeraldo",
  'At the foot of the Zugspitze lies the Eibsee, one of the most beautiful lakes in the Bavarian Alps &mdash; a startling emerald green, ringed by dark forest with the great mountain rising straight behind. It is roadside and easy, gentle for a dress and a small ceremony, and a real alternative to the busier Dolomite lakes for couples who want water and a giant peak without the crowds. First light on still water here is pure calm.': "Ai piedi della Zugspitze si trova l'Eibsee, uno dei laghi più belli delle Alpi bavaresi &mdash; un sorprendente verde smeraldo, cinto da bosco scuro con la grande montagna che si alza proprio dietro. È sul ciglio della strada e facile, dolce per un abito e una piccola cerimonia, e una vera alternativa ai più affollati laghi dolomitici per le coppie che vogliono acqua e una vetta gigante senza la folla. La prima luce sull'acqua ferma è qui pura calma.",
  'A ceremony at the forested shore of the Eibsee below the Zugspitze': "Una cerimonia sulla riva boscosa dell'Eibsee, sotto la Zugspitze",
  'The Eibsee also makes a gentle base for the whole trip. It is minutes from Garmisch-Partenkirchen, easy to reach, and it pairs a lake morning with a summit afternoon on the same mountain &mdash; water and altitude in one day, without a long drive between them. For couples who want the calm of a forest lake first and the drama of a high ridge second, it is one of the neatest days the Alps offer.': "L'Eibsee è anche una base dolce per tutto il viaggio. È a pochi minuti da Garmisch-Partenkirchen, facile da raggiungere, e abbina una mattina al lago con un pomeriggio in vetta sulla stessa montagna &mdash; acqua e quota in un giorno, senza un lungo tragitto tra le due. Per le coppie che vogliono prima la calma di un lago di bosco e poi il dramma di una cresta alta, è una delle giornate più rotonde che le Alpi offrano.",
  'One honest note on the legal side: a free, symbolic ceremony at the Eibsee is straightforward and needs no special permit &mdash; but it is not legally binding, so the marriage itself is signed at a registry, either at home or beforehand. If you want the legal act on the mountain in Bavaria, the Zugspitze summit above is the route; otherwise the Eibsee is a beautiful place to say your own words and keep the paperwork simple.': "Una nota onesta sul piano legale: una cerimonia libera e simbolica all'Eibsee è semplice e non richiede permessi speciali &mdash; ma non ha valore legale, quindi il matrimonio in sé si firma in comune, a casa o in anticipo. Se volete l'atto legale in montagna in Baviera, la via è la cima della Zugspitze qui sopra; altrimenti l'Eibsee è un luogo bellissimo per dire le vostre parole e tenere le pratiche semplici.",
  'Tyrol &mdash; lakes, meadows &amp; the easy legal route': 'Tirolo &mdash; laghi, prati e la via legale facile',
  'Tyrol is our quiet secret: hidden mountain lakes, rolling green meadows under snow-streaked peaks, and villages an easy drive from Innsbruck. It rarely has the crowds of the famous Dolomite icons, and it has one big practical advantage &mdash; in Austria you can marry legally, and in some regions even at an approved outdoor spot. For couples who want the legal act on the mountain rather than a symbolic one, Tyrol is often the answer, and it is every bit as beautiful.': "Il Tirolo è il nostro segreto tranquillo: laghi di montagna nascosti, ondulati prati verdi sotto cime striate di neve, e paesi a una comoda distanza da Innsbruck. Raramente ha la folla delle famose icone dolomitiche, e ha un grande vantaggio pratico &mdash; in Austria potete sposarvi legalmente, e in alcune regioni persino in un luogo all'aperto autorizzato. Per le coppie che vogliono l'atto legale in montagna invece di uno simbolico, il Tirolo è spesso la risposta, ed è altrettanto bello.",
  'A pampas-grass arch set by a Tyrolean mountain lake with autumn larches': 'Un arco di erba della pampa allestito accanto a un lago di montagna tirolese con larici autunnali',
  'The couple at the arch beside the still Tyrolean lake': "La coppia all'arco accanto al quieto lago tirolese",
  'A ceremony in Tyrol with a backdrop of snow-streaked jagged peaks': 'Una cerimonia in Tirolo con uno sfondo di cime frastagliate striate di neve',
  'Tyrol also rewards the couple who want a little Alpine culture around the day. Timber villages with onion-domed churches, mountain huts serving long lunches, cable cars that open the high pastures &mdash; it feels lived-in and warm rather than remote. Innsbruck itself, with its old town under the Nordkette, makes a beautiful and practical base, an hour or less from lakes, meadows and the ridges above the city.': "Il Tirolo premia anche la coppia che vuole un po' di cultura alpina attorno alla giornata. Paesi di legno con chiese dal campanile a cipolla, rifugi che servono lunghi pranzi, funivie che aprono gli alti pascoli &mdash; sembra vissuto e caldo più che remoto. La stessa Innsbruck, con il suo centro storico sotto la Nordkette, è una base bella e pratica, a un'ora o meno da laghi, prati e le creste sopra la città.",
  'The great passes': 'I grandi passi',
  'The high passes that link the valleys &mdash; Passo Giau, Passo Gardena, Passo Sella &mdash; are the easy secret of the range: you drive to over 2,000 metres and step straight onto alpine meadow with the giants all around, no climb required. Giau in particular, with its little pointed chapel under the shark-fin peak of Ra Gusela, gives you drama and a touch of storybook without a hike, and the evening light there is some of the best anywhere. Perfect for couples who want the high-mountain feeling with family in tow.': "Gli alti passi che collegano le valli &mdash; Passo Giau, Passo Gardena, Passo Sella &mdash; sono il facile segreto del massiccio: guidate a oltre 2.000 metri e uscite dritti sul prato alpino con i giganti tutt'intorno, senza salita. Il Giau in particolare, con la sua piccola cappella a punta sotto la vetta a pinna di squalo della Ra Gusela, vi dà dramma e un tocco di fiaba senza camminata, e la luce della sera lì è tra le migliori ovunque. Perfetto per le coppie che vogliono la sensazione dell'alta montagna con la famiglia al seguito.",
  'The little pointed chapel at Passo Giau with Ra Gusela rising behind': 'La piccola cappella a punta del Passo Giau con la Ra Gusela che si alza dietro',
  'A small ceremony on the meadow beneath the walls of the Sella group': 'Una piccola cerimonia sul prato sotto le pareti del gruppo del Sella',
  'Green meadow and a hut at Passo Gardena as the sun breaks through': 'Prato verde e un rifugio al Passo Gardena mentre il sole irrompe',
  'The other gift of the passes is the light. Because they sit high and open, with nothing between you and the horizon, they catch sunrise and sunset in full &mdash; and Giau in particular faces the evening so well that we often plan it for golden hour and enrosadira rather than dawn. Park, walk a minute onto the meadow, and let the sky do the rest; you can be back down to a valley dinner within the hour.': "L'altro dono dei passi è la luce. Poiché stanno alti e aperti, con nulla tra voi e l'orizzonte, catturano alba e tramonto per intero &mdash; e il Giau in particolare si affaccia così bene alla sera che spesso lo pianifichiamo per l'ora dorata e l'enrosadira invece che per l'alba. Parcheggiate, camminate un minuto sul prato e lasciate che il cielo faccia il resto; potete essere di ritorno per una cena in valle entro un'ora.",
  'For the peak-baggers': 'Per i conquistatori di vette',
  'If you want the day to feel earned, the Alps reward the effort like nowhere else. A ridge reached on foot or by a short climb from a lift gives you exposure, a 360-degree horizon and a scale that stops the breath &mdash; you standing tiny against a thousand metres of rock. These are the boldest frames we take, and the most private: five more minutes past where most people turn around, and the mountain is yours. We match the walk to your fitness and never oversell what a spot costs to reach.': 'Se volete che la giornata si senta guadagnata, le Alpi premiano la fatica come nessun altro luogo. Una cresta raggiunta a piedi o con una breve salita da un impianto vi dà esposizione, un orizzonte a 360 gradi e una dimensione che toglie il respiro &mdash; voi minuscoli contro mille metri di roccia. Sono le inquadrature più audaci che facciamo, e le più intime: cinque minuti oltre dove la maggior parte torna indietro, e la montagna è vostra. Adattiamo la camminata alla vostra forma e non esageriamo mai quanto costa raggiungere un luogo.',
  'The couple tiny on a ridge before a vast snow-streaked cirque': 'La coppia minuscola su una cresta davanti a un vasto circo striato di neve',
  'None of this has to mean a mountaineering epic. Many of our most dramatic ridge frames sit only a short, safe walk from a cable-car station &mdash; enough to leave the crowds behind, not enough to need ropes or a guide. We scout every route in advance, carry the plan and the spare layers, and pace it so the walk feels like part of the adventure rather than a chore. If you can manage an hour on a trail, we can put you somewhere that looks impossible.': "Niente di tutto ciò deve significare un'epopea alpinistica. Molte delle nostre inquadrature di cresta più drammatiche sono a soli pochi passi sicuri da una stazione della funivia &mdash; abbastanza da lasciarsi la folla alle spalle, non abbastanza da servire corde o una guida. Perlustriamo ogni percorso in anticipo, portiamo il piano e gli strati di scorta e lo dosiamo così che la camminata sembri parte dell'avventura invece di un peso. Se ce la fate con un'ora su un sentiero, vi mettiamo in un posto che sembra impossibile.",
  'The Alps under snow': 'Le Alpi sotto la neve',
  'Winter turns the whole range monochrome and almost unearthly &mdash; snow to the horizon, the peaks stripped to black and white, and, best of all, near-total solitude. The Tre Cime and the high snow ridges are unforgettable in this light, and a ceremony up here feels like standing inside a snow globe. It asks for more &mdash; warm layers, sure footing, and a close eye on which toll roads and lifts are open, because winter schedules are reduced. When it lines up, it is the most spectacular version of the Alps we photograph all year.': "L'inverno rende l'intero massiccio monocromo e quasi ultraterreno &mdash; neve fino all'orizzonte, le cime ridotte al bianco e nero e, cosa migliore, una solitudine quasi totale. Le Tre Cime e le alte creste innevate sono indimenticabili in questa luce, e una cerimonia quassù è come stare dentro una palla di neve. Chiede di più &mdash; strati caldi, passo sicuro e un occhio attento a quali strade a pedaggio e impianti sono aperti, perché gli orari invernali sono ridotti. Quando si allinea, è la versione più spettacolare delle Alpi che fotografiamo in tutto l'anno.",
  'The couple in the snow with the Tre Cime spires glowing behind': 'La coppia nella neve con le torri delle Tre Cime che brillano dietro',
  'The couple on a snowy plateau below the Tre Cime in full winter': 'La coppia su un plateau innevato sotto le Tre Cime in pieno inverno',
  'Winter also thins the calendar in your favour. The couples who brave the cold have the most famous places almost entirely to themselves, and the low sun sits soft and golden for hours instead of minutes. Dress for it &mdash; warm layers under the coat, real boots to the spot, the pretty shoes in a bag &mdash; and a grey, snowing sky is not a setback but a gift, giving some of the most atmospheric mountain photographs we ever take.': "L'inverno assottiglia anche il calendario a vostro favore. Le coppie che sfidano il freddo hanno i luoghi più famosi quasi interamente per sé, e il sole basso resta morbido e dorato per ore invece che per minuti. Vestitevi per questo &mdash; strati caldi sotto il cappotto, scarponi veri fino al posto, le scarpe belle in una borsa &mdash; e un cielo grigio con la neve non è un contrattempo ma un dono, che regala alcune delle foto di montagna più suggestive che facciamo.",
  'Which one is yours': 'Qual è il vostro?',
  'So how to choose? Go to the <strong>Dolomites</strong> for maximum drama and the icons at their quietest. Go to <strong>Tyrol or Bavaria</strong> for calmer lakes, gentler effort and the easy legal route. Choose a <strong>lake</strong> if you want stillness and reflection, a <strong>pass</strong> if you want big mountains with no hike, a <strong>summit</strong> if you want to earn the view, and <strong>winter</strong> if you want solitude and drama over warmth. When couples truly cannot decide, we split it across a couple of days &mdash; a lake at dawn, a pass at dusk. Tell us the feeling and we will name the place.': "Allora, come scegliere? Andate nelle <strong>Dolomiti</strong> per il massimo dramma e le icone nella loro versione più tranquilla. Andate in <strong>Tirolo o Baviera</strong> per laghi più calmi, meno fatica e la via legale facile. Scegliete un <strong>lago</strong> se volete quiete e riflesso, un <strong>passo</strong> se volete grandi montagne senza camminata, una <strong>vetta</strong> se volete guadagnarvi la vista, e l'<strong>inverno</strong> se preferite solitudine e dramma al calore. Quando una coppia davvero non riesce a decidere, lo dividiamo in un paio di giorni &mdash; un lago all'alba, un passo al tramonto. Diteci la sensazione e vi nomineremo il luogo.",
  'And you are not locked into one answer. Some of our favourite trips mix two worlds across a few days &mdash; a quiet Tyrolean lake at sunrise, an easy legal ceremony, then a drive south for a Dolomite sunset the next evening. The ranges sit close enough that a single trip can hold both the calm and the drama. Tell us the two feelings you cannot choose between, and we will often find a way to give you both.': "E non siete legati a un'unica risposta. Alcuni dei nostri viaggi preferiti mescolano due mondi in pochi giorni &mdash; un tranquillo lago tirolese all'alba, una facile cerimonia legale, poi una guida a sud per un tramonto dolomitico la sera dopo. I massicci sono abbastanza vicini perché un solo viaggio possa contenere sia la calma sia il dramma. Diteci le due sensazioni tra cui non riuscite a scegliere, e spesso troveremo il modo di darvi entrambe.",
  'Getting around the Alps': 'Muoversi tra le Alpi',
  'The range is easier to reach than the drama suggests. Most couples fly into Venice, Verona, Innsbruck or Munich and drive in &mdash; the Dolomites are two to three hours from Venice, the Zugspitze and Eibsee sit right on the Bavarian border near Garmisch, and Tyrol spreads out around Innsbruck. Crossing between Italy and Austria is a simple drive with no fuss. From a single valley base you can often reach several of these spots, and we build the route around the light &mdash; which place at dawn, which at dusk &mdash; and handle the reservations, timings and driving so your mornings stay calm.': "Il massiccio è più facile da raggiungere di quanto suggerisca il dramma. La maggior parte delle coppie atterra a Venezia, Verona, Innsbruck o Monaco e guida verso l'interno &mdash; le Dolomiti sono a due o tre ore da Venezia, la Zugspitze e l'Eibsee stanno proprio sul confine bavarese vicino a Garmisch, e il Tirolo si estende attorno a Innsbruck. Attraversare tra Italia e Austria è una guida semplice, senza complicazioni. Da una sola base di valle potete spesso raggiungere diversi di questi luoghi, e costruiamo il percorso attorno alla luce &mdash; quale luogo all'alba, quale al tramonto &mdash; e gestiamo le prenotazioni, gli orari e la guida così le vostre mattine restano serene.",
  'Where you base yourself shapes the trip as much as where you shoot. Cortina d&rsquo;Ampezzo and the Alta Badia put you in the heart of the Dolomites; Garmisch sits right under the Zugspitze; Innsbruck opens up Tyrol in every direction. We help you pick the base that keeps your chosen spots within an easy dawn drive, book the huts where an overnight makes a sunrise possible, and hand you a simple plan so the only thing you have to think about on the day is each other.': "Dove vi basate plasma il viaggio tanto quanto dove fotografate. Cortina d&rsquo;Ampezzo e l'Alta Badia vi mettono nel cuore delle Dolomiti; Garmisch sta proprio sotto la Zugspitze; Innsbruck apre il Tirolo in ogni direzione. Vi aiutiamo a scegliere la base che tiene i vostri luoghi a una comoda distanza all'alba, prenotiamo i rifugi dove un pernottamento rende possibile un'alba, e vi consegniamo un piano semplice così l'unica cosa a cui dovete pensare quel giorno siete l'un l'altra.",
  'Light &amp; the finish': 'La luce e la chiusura',
  'Wherever you land in the Alps, the light is the thing &mdash; and the day is not over when the sun drops. Sunrise gives you empty icons and soft colour; golden hour warms the rock and slides into the fireshow of enrosadira on the Dolomite walls; and blue hour, the cool quiet window after, is the one most people miss by packing up too soon. We never do. Then the celebration to match &mdash; a hut dinner, a swim, a toast on the mountain &mdash; because the best locations deserve more than a single frame.': "Ovunque atterriate nelle Alpi, la luce è la cosa &mdash; e la giornata non è finita quando cala il sole. L'alba vi dà icone vuote e colore morbido; l'ora dorata scalda la roccia e scivola nello spettacolo di fuoco dell'enrosadira sulle pareti dolomitiche; e l'ora blu, la finestra fresca e quieta dopo, è quella che la maggior parte perde smontando troppo presto. Noi mai. Poi la festa all'altezza &mdash; una cena in rifugio, un tuffo, un brindisi in montagna &mdash; perché i luoghi migliori meritano più di una sola inquadratura.",
  'The couple at a floral arch backlit by a blazing Tyrolean sunset': 'La coppia a un arco floreale in controluce di un ardente tramonto tirolese',
  'The Dolomites': 'Le Dolomiti',
  'Zugspitze': 'Zugspitze',
  'Eibsee & the lakes': 'Eibsee e i laghi',
  'Tyrol': 'Tirolo',
  'The Alps in winter': 'Le Alpi in inverno',
  'Which suits you': 'Qual è il vostro',
  'Getting around': 'Come muoversi',
  'Light & the finish': 'La luce e la chiusura',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'Best Alpine locations FAQ': 'Domande frequenti sui migliori luoghi alpini',
  'The Alps are not one landscape but a dozen, and the right elopement spot is the one that matches the day in your head. We shoot across the range &mdash; the pale towers of the Dolomites, the emerald lakes below Germany&rsquo;s highest peak, the quiet meadows and mirror lakes of Tyrol &mdash; and each corner has its own character, its own light and its own rules. This is our honest field guide to the places we return to again and again, and how to choose the one that is yours.': "Le Alpi non sono un paesaggio ma una dozzina, e il luogo giusto per l'elopement è quello che si adatta alla giornata che avete in testa. Fotografiamo per tutto il massiccio &mdash; le pallide torri delle Dolomiti, i laghi smeraldo sotto la vetta più alta della Germania, i prati tranquilli e i laghi a specchio del Tirolo &mdash; e ogni angolo ha il suo carattere, la sua luce e le sue regole. Questa è la nostra onesta guida sul campo ai luoghi a cui torniamo di continuo, e come scegliere quello che è vostro.",
  'On this page': 'In questa pagina',
}
ALPS_FAQ_ES = {
  'Dolomites or Tyrol &mdash; which is better for an elopement?': ('Dolomitas o Tirol &mdash; ¿qué es mejor para un elopement?', 'Ambos son extraordinarios; solo se sienten distintos. Los Dolomitas os dan la escena más dramática e icónica &mdash; torres pálidas, lagos turquesa, las fotos que todos reconocen. Tirol y la frontera bávara os dan lagos y prados más tranquilos, un ambiente más suave y la vía más fácil a una ceremonia con validez legal. Os ayudamos a ajustar el macizo al ánimo y al papeleo que queréis.'),
  'Can we get legally married in the mountains here?': ('¿Podemos casarnos legalmente en las montañas de aquí?', 'En Austria, sí &mdash; una ceremonia civil es posible, y en algunas regiones tirolesas incluso en un lugar autorizado al aire libre, por lo que las parejas que quieren el acto legal en la montaña suelen elegir Tirol. En Italia el matrimonio legal ocurre solo en un registro civil, así que una ceremonia dolomítica sigue siendo simbólica con el papeleo firmado en casa. Os indicamos el país y el camino correctos para vosotros.'),
  'Which spots need a hike, and which are roadside or by cable car?': ('¿Qué lugares necesitan caminata y cuáles están junto a la carretera o en teleférico?', 'Es una mezcla real, y ese es el punto &mdash; hay algo para cada nivel. El Lago di Braies, el Eibsee, el Passo Giau y los altos puertos están prácticamente junto a la carretera; la Zugspitze y otras crestas se alcanzan en teleférico; un puñado de los lagos y cumbres más tranquilos piden un paseo. Decidnos cuánto os gusta moveros y construimos el día a medida.'),
  'Where is best for a lake elopement in the Alps?': ('¿Dónde es mejor para un elopement de lago en los Alpes?', 'Tenéis para elegir. El Lago di Braies es el icono turquesa; el Eibsee bajo la Zugspitze es verde esmeralda y enmarcado por bosque; y los más tranquilos lagos de montaña tiroleses os dan la misma agua espejo casi sin nadie alrededor. Todos son mejores con la primera luz, antes de que llegue el día.'),
  'Which locations work best in winter?': ('¿Qué lugares funcionan mejor en invierno?', 'Los sitios altos y escarpados son inolvidables bajo la nieve &mdash; las Tre Cime y las crestas nevadas se vuelven monocromas y dramáticas, y podéis tenerlas enteramente para vosotros. A cambio está el acceso: algunas carreteras de peaje y teleféricos funcionan reducidos o cierran, y pide capas de abrigo y pisada firme. Planificamos en torno a lo que está de verdad abierto y seguro.'),
  'How many locations can we combine?': ('¿Cuántos lugares podemos combinar?', 'Menos de los que pensáis, y a propósito. Perseguir cinco sitios significa no ver ninguno bien; solemos planificar un lugar principal para la mejor luz y quizá un segundo más fácil cerca. A lo largo de unos días por el macizo podemos enlazar una verdadera ruta &mdash; un lago al alba, un puerto por la tarde, una cumbre a la mañana siguiente.'),
}
ALPS_FAQ_IT = {
  'Dolomites or Tyrol &mdash; which is better for an elopement?': ('Dolomiti o Tirolo &mdash; cosa è meglio per un elopement?', "Entrambi sono straordinari; si sentono solo diversi. Le Dolomiti vi danno la scena più drammatica e iconica &mdash; torri pallide, laghi turchesi, le foto che tutti riconoscono. Il Tirolo e il confine bavarese vi danno laghi e prati più tranquilli, un'atmosfera più dolce e la via più facile a una cerimonia con valore legale. Vi aiutiamo ad abbinare il massiccio all'atmosfera e alle pratiche che volete."),
  'Can we get legally married in the mountains here?': ('Possiamo sposarci legalmente sulle montagne qui?', "In Austria sì &mdash; una cerimonia civile è possibile, e in alcune regioni tirolesi persino in un luogo all'aperto autorizzato, motivo per cui le coppie che vogliono l'atto legale in montagna scelgono spesso il Tirolo. In Italia il matrimonio legale avviene solo in comune, quindi una cerimonia dolomitica resta simbolica con le pratiche firmate a casa. Vi indichiamo il Paese e la via giusti per voi."),
  'Which spots need a hike, and which are roadside or by cable car?': ('Quali luoghi richiedono una camminata e quali sono sul ciglio della strada o in funivia?', "È una vera mescolanza, ed è il bello &mdash; c'è qualcosa per ogni livello. Il Lago di Braies, l'Eibsee, il Passo Giau e gli alti passi sono praticamente sul ciglio della strada; la Zugspitze e altre creste si raggiungono in funivia; una manciata dei laghi e delle vette più tranquille vuole una camminata. Diteci quanto vi piace muovervi e costruiamo la giornata su misura."),
  'Where is best for a lake elopement in the Alps?': ('Dove è meglio per un elopement al lago nelle Alpi?', "Avete l'imbarazzo della scelta. Il Lago di Braies è l'icona turchese; l'Eibsee sotto la Zugspitze è verde smeraldo e incorniciato dal bosco; e i più tranquilli laghi di montagna tirolesi vi danno la stessa acqua a specchio quasi senza nessuno intorno. Tutti sono migliori alla prima luce, prima che arrivi la giornata."),
  'Which locations work best in winter?': ('Quali luoghi funzionano meglio in inverno?', "I luoghi alti e frastagliati sono indimenticabili sotto la neve &mdash; le Tre Cime e le creste innevate diventano monocrome e drammatiche, e potete averle tutte per voi. In cambio c'è l'accesso: alcune strade a pedaggio e funivie vanno ridotte o chiudono, e chiede strati caldi e passo sicuro. Pianifichiamo attorno a ciò che è davvero aperto e sicuro."),
  'How many locations can we combine?': ('Quanti luoghi possiamo combinare?', "Meno di quanto pensiate, e di proposito. Inseguire cinque posti significa non vederne bene nessuno; di solito pianifichiamo un luogo principale per la luce migliore e forse un secondo più facile vicino. Nell'arco di qualche giorno per il massiccio possiamo mettere insieme un vero tour &mdash; un lago all'alba, un passo la sera, una vetta la mattina dopo."),
}

def build_alps_guide(lang):
    slug='best-alps-elopement-locations'
    g=next(x for x in GUIDES if x['slug']==slug); ex=GUIDE_EXTRA[slug]
    rel='how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/'+slug+'/'; P=prefix(lang,rel)
    DE=(lang=='de')
    def L(en,de):
        if lang=='de': return de
        if lang=='es': return ALPS_ES.get(en,en)
        if lang=='it': return ALPS_IT.get(en,en)
        return en
    def FQ(qen,aen,qde,ade):
        if lang=='de': return (qde,ade)
        if lang=='es': return ALPS_FAQ_ES.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        if lang=='it': return ALPS_FAQ_IT.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        return (qen,aen)
    GI=f'{P}img/guide-best-alps-locations/'
    H2S='font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,3vw,36px);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:1.7em 0 .4em;scroll-margin-top:96px'
    def h2(i,en,de): return f'<h2 id="{i}" style="{H2S}">{L(en,de)}</h2>'
    def p(en,de): return f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2)">{L(en,de)}</p>'
    def fig(name,en,de): return f'<figure class="guide-fig"><img src="{GI}{name}" alt="{L(en,de)}" loading="lazy"></figure>'
    HERO_IMG='img/guide-best-alps-locations/04-alpenorte-zugspitze-weitblick.webp'
    toc=[('what',L('Choosing your range','Das Massiv wählen')),('dolomites',L('The Dolomites','Die Dolomiten')),
         ('zugspitze',L('Zugspitze','Zugspitze')),('eibsee',L('Eibsee & the lakes','Eibsee & die Seen')),
         ('tyrol',L('Tyrol','Tirol')),('passes',L('The great passes','Die großen Pässe')),
         ('peaks',L('For the peak-baggers','Für Gipfelstürmer')),('winter',L('The Alps in winter','Die Alpen im Winter')),
         ('choose',L('Which suits you','Was zu euch passt')),('reach',L('Getting around','Anreise & Wege')),
         ('sunset',L('Light & the finish','Licht & Abschluss')),('faq',L('FAQ','FAQ'))]
    toc_html=('<nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'"><div class="cap">'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'</div><ol>'
      +''.join(f'<li><a href="#{i}">{lbl}</a></li>' for i,lbl in toc)+'</ol></nav>')
    facts='<div class="facts">'+''.join(f'<div class="fct"><div class="fl">{LBL[k][lang]}</div><div class="fv">{val[lang]}</div></div>' for k,val in ex['facts'])+'</div>'
    C=[]
    C.append(f'<p class="lead">{L("The Alps are not one landscape but a dozen, and the right elopement spot is the one that matches the day in your head. We shoot across the range &mdash; the pale towers of the Dolomites, the emerald lakes below Germany&rsquo;s highest peak, the quiet meadows and mirror lakes of Tyrol &mdash; and each corner has its own character, its own light and its own rules. This is our honest field guide to the places we return to again and again, and how to choose the one that is yours.","Die Alpen sind nicht eine Landschaft, sondern ein Dutzend, und der richtige Elopement-Ort ist der, der zu eurem Bild im Kopf passt. Wir fotografieren quer durchs Massiv &mdash; die bleichen Türme der Dolomiten, die smaragdgrünen Seen unter Deutschlands höchstem Gipfel, die stillen Wiesen und Spiegelseen Tirols &mdash;, und jede Ecke hat ihren eigenen Charakter, ihr eigenes Licht und ihre eigenen Regeln. Das ist unser ehrlicher Feldführer zu den Orten, zu denen wir immer wieder zurückkehren, und wie ihr den passenden für euch wählt.")}</p>')
    C.append(f'<div class="cap" style="margin:0 0 -14px">{t(lang,"quick_facts")}</div>{facts}')
    C.append(toc_html)

    C.append(h2('what','Choosing your range','Das Massiv wählen'))
    C.append(p("Start with the feeling, not the pin. Do you want the postcard drama of the Dolomites, the alpine calm of a Tyrolean lake, or a summit you can stand on above everything? Effort, access, season and &mdash; importantly &mdash; where you can legally marry all pull on the choice. Below we walk through the corners of the Alps we love most, what each does best, and who each one suits. You do not have to know the place before you know the mood; that is our job.","Beginnt mit dem Gefühl, nicht mit der Stecknadel. Wollt ihr die Postkarten-Dramatik der Dolomiten, die alpine Ruhe eines Tiroler Sees oder einen Gipfel, auf dem ihr über allem steht? Aufwand, Erreichbarkeit, Saison und &mdash; wichtig &mdash; wo ihr rechtsgültig heiraten könnt, ziehen alle an der Wahl. Unten gehen wir die Ecken der Alpen durch, die wir am meisten lieben, was jede am besten kann und zu wem sie passt. Ihr müsst den Ort nicht kennen, ehe ihr die Stimmung kennt; das ist unsere Aufgabe."))
    C.append(fig('01-alpenorte-lago-di-braies-panorama.webp',"The turquoise water and peaks of Lago di Braies in the Dolomites","Das türkise Wasser und die Gipfel des Pragser Wildsees in den Dolomiten"))

    C.append(p("A few honest questions shorten the whole search. How far are you happy to walk? Do you need to be legally married on the day, or is a symbolic ceremony with the paperwork at home fine? Warm and green, or cold and white? Just the two of you, or a few guests who need an easy path? Your answers rule half the map out in minutes &mdash; and what is left is almost always a place you did not know to ask for.","Ein paar ehrliche Fragen verkürzen die ganze Suche. Wie weit geht ihr gern zu Fuß? Müsst ihr am Tag rechtsgültig verheiratet sein, oder reicht eine symbolische Zeremonie mit den Papieren zu Hause? Warm und grün oder kalt und weiß? Nur ihr zwei oder ein paar Gäste, die einen leichten Weg brauchen? Eure Antworten streichen die halbe Karte in Minuten &mdash; und was bleibt, ist fast immer ein Ort, nach dem ihr nicht zu fragen wusstet."))
    C.append(h2('dolomites','The Dolomites &mdash; the icons','Die Dolomiten &mdash; die Ikonen'))
    C.append(p("The Dolomites are where most couples start dreaming, and for good reason: pale limestone towers that blush pink at dusk, turquoise lakes, tiny chapels on green passes. It is the most dramatic, most recognisable scenery in the Alps &mdash; Lago di Braies, the Tre Cime, the Seceda ridge, Passo Giau. The catch is fame: the icons fill up, so we plan around first light and quieter twins. If the Dolomites are calling, we have a whole separate guide to their most beautiful spots &mdash; but here is the short version of why they are worth it.","Die Dolomiten sind, wo die meisten Paare zu träumen beginnen, und das zu Recht: bleiche Kalktürme, die in der Dämmerung rosa anlaufen, türkise Seen, winzige Kapellen auf grünen Pässen. Es ist die dramatischste, wiedererkennbarste Kulisse der Alpen &mdash; Pragser Wildsee, Drei Zinnen, Seceda-Grat, Passo Giau. Der Haken ist der Ruhm: Die Ikonen füllen sich, deshalb planen wir um das erste Licht und stillere Zwillinge. Wenn die Dolomiten rufen, haben wir einen eigenen Guide zu ihren schönsten Orten &mdash; hier die Kurzfassung, warum sie es wert sind."))
    C.append(fig('09-alpenorte-ra-gusela-wiese.webp',"A couple small on a green meadow beneath the Ra Gusela and Croda da Lago peaks","Ein Paar klein auf grüner Wiese unter Ra Gusela und Croda da Lago"))
    C.append(fig('02-alpenorte-braies-paar-am-ufer.webp',"The couple embracing at the shore of Lago di Braies","Das Paar umarmt sich am Ufer des Pragser Wildsees"))

    C.append(p("What makes the Dolomites unlike other mountains is the colour. At dusk the pale limestone catches the last light and glows ember-red for a few unrepeatable minutes &mdash; the locals call it enrosadira, and no photograph quite prepares you for it in person. Pair that with water the colour of a swimming pool and meadows full of cotton grass, and you understand why this is where the dreaming starts. We simply make sure you are standing in the right spot when the rock catches fire.","Was die Dolomiten anders macht als andere Berge, ist die Farbe. In der Dämmerung fängt der bleiche Kalk das letzte Licht und glüht für ein paar unwiederholbare Minuten glutrot &mdash; die Einheimischen nennen es Enrosadira, und kein Foto bereitet euch wirklich darauf vor, es selbst zu sehen. Dazu Wasser in Schwimmbadfarbe und Wiesen voller Wollgras &mdash; dann versteht ihr, warum hier das Träumen beginnt. Wir sorgen nur dafür, dass ihr am richtigen Ort steht, wenn der Fels Feuer fängt."))
    C.append(h2('zugspitze','The Zugspitze &mdash; Germany&rsquo;s roof','Die Zugspitze &mdash; Deutschlands Dach'))
    C.append(p("On the German&ndash;Austrian border stands the Zugspitze, the highest peak in Germany, and standing on its ridges feels like standing on the roof of the country &mdash; a sea of summits in every direction. A cable car carries you most of the way, so the drama comes without a two-day climb, and the rock up here is raw and cinematic, especially in the bare light of morning. It is a favourite for couples who want the feeling of real altitude with an easy path to it.","An der deutsch-österreichischen Grenze steht die Zugspitze, der höchste Gipfel Deutschlands, und auf ihren Graten zu stehen fühlt sich an wie auf dem Dach des Landes &mdash; ein Meer aus Gipfeln in jede Richtung. Eine Bergbahn bringt euch den Großteil des Wegs, die Dramatik kommt also ohne Zweitagestour, und der Fels hier oben ist roh und filmreif, besonders im kargen Morgenlicht. Ein Favorit für Paare, die das Gefühl echter Höhe mit einem leichten Weg dorthin wollen."))
    C.append(fig('03-alpenorte-zugspitze-grat-paar.webp',"The couple on a rocky ridge near the Zugspitze in dramatic black and white","Das Paar auf einem Felsgrat nahe der Zugspitze in dramatischem Schwarzweiß"))

    C.append(p("There is something quietly moving about marrying at the top of a whole country. The Zugspitze straddles the border, so on a clear morning you look out over both Germany and Austria at once, ridge after ridge fading into haze. It is exposed and wild up here, so we time it for calm light and keep the ceremony nimble &mdash; but the reward is a sense of scale and height that a valley simply cannot give, reached by a cable car rather than a rope.","Es hat etwas leise Bewegendes, an der Spitze eines ganzen Landes zu heiraten. Die Zugspitze liegt auf der Grenze, an einem klaren Morgen blickt ihr also über Deutschland und Österreich zugleich, Grat um Grat, der im Dunst verblasst. Hier oben ist es ausgesetzt und wild, wir legen es also auf ruhiges Licht und halten die Zeremonie flink &mdash; doch der Lohn ist ein Gefühl von Dimension und Höhe, das ein Tal schlicht nicht geben kann, erreicht per Bergbahn statt am Seil."))
    C.append(p("There is a rare bonus up here, too: you can actually marry on the Zugspitze summit officially and legally, through the registry office in Garmisch-Partenkirchen. The catch is demand &mdash; the summit slots are hugely popular and go quickly, and dates can only be requested about six months ahead, so this one rewards early, decisive planning. We help you time the request.","Hier oben gibt es noch einen seltenen Bonus: Auf dem Zugspitz-Gipfel könnt ihr tatsächlich offiziell und rechtsgültig heiraten &mdash; über das Standesamt Garmisch-Partenkirchen. Der Haken ist die Nachfrage &mdash; die Gipfel-Termine sind extrem beliebt und schnell vergeben, und Termine lassen sich erst etwa ein halbes Jahr im Voraus anfragen; das belohnt also frühe, entschlossene Planung. Wir helfen euch, die Anfrage richtig zu timen."))
    C.append(h2('eibsee','The Eibsee &mdash; emerald water','Der Eibsee &mdash; smaragdgrünes Wasser'))
    C.append(p("At the foot of the Zugspitze lies the Eibsee, one of the most beautiful lakes in the Bavarian Alps &mdash; a startling emerald green, ringed by dark forest with the great mountain rising straight behind. It is roadside and easy, gentle for a dress and a small ceremony, and a real alternative to the busier Dolomite lakes for couples who want water and a giant peak without the crowds. First light on still water here is pure calm.","Am Fuß der Zugspitze liegt der Eibsee, einer der schönsten Seen der Bayerischen Alpen &mdash; ein verblüffendes Smaragdgrün, umringt von dunklem Wald, den großen Berg direkt dahinter. Er liegt an der Straße und ist leicht, sanft für Kleid und kleine Zeremonie, und eine echte Alternative zu den volleren Dolomitenseen für Paare, die Wasser und einen Riesengipfel ohne Andrang wollen. Erstes Licht auf stillem Wasser ist hier pure Ruhe."))
    C.append(fig('05-alpenorte-eibsee-zeremonie.webp',"A ceremony at the forested shore of the Eibsee below the Zugspitze","Eine Zeremonie am bewaldeten Ufer des Eibsees unter der Zugspitze"))

    C.append(p("The Eibsee also makes a gentle base for the whole trip. It is minutes from Garmisch-Partenkirchen, easy to reach, and it pairs a lake morning with a summit afternoon on the same mountain &mdash; water and altitude in one day, without a long drive between them. For couples who want the calm of a forest lake first and the drama of a high ridge second, it is one of the neatest days the Alps offer.","Der Eibsee gibt auch eine sanfte Basis für die ganze Reise ab. Er liegt Minuten von Garmisch-Partenkirchen, ist leicht erreichbar und verbindet einen See-Morgen mit einem Gipfel-Nachmittag am selben Berg &mdash; Wasser und Höhe an einem Tag, ohne lange Fahrt dazwischen. Für Paare, die zuerst die Ruhe eines Waldsees und dann die Dramatik eines hohen Grats wollen, ist es einer der rundesten Tage, die die Alpen bieten."))
    C.append(p("One honest note on the legal side: a free, symbolic ceremony at the Eibsee is straightforward and needs no special permit &mdash; but it is not legally binding, so the marriage itself is signed at a registry, either at home or beforehand. If you want the legal act on the mountain in Bavaria, the Zugspitze summit above is the route; otherwise the Eibsee is a beautiful place to say your own words and keep the paperwork simple.","Eine ehrliche Anmerkung zum Rechtlichen: Eine freie, symbolische Zeremonie am Eibsee ist unkompliziert und braucht keine Genehmigung &mdash; sie ist aber nicht rechtsgültig, die Trauung selbst wird also am Standesamt unterschrieben, zu Hause oder vorab. Wollt ihr den Rechtsakt am Berg in Bayern, führt der Weg über den Zugspitz-Gipfel oben; sonst ist der Eibsee ein wunderschöner Ort, um eure eigenen Worte zu sagen und die Papiere einfach zu halten."))
    C.append(h2('tyrol','Tyrol &mdash; lakes, meadows &amp; the easy legal route','Tirol &mdash; Seen, Wiesen &amp; der leichte Rechtsweg'))
    C.append(p("Tyrol is our quiet secret: hidden mountain lakes, rolling green meadows under snow-streaked peaks, and villages an easy drive from Innsbruck. It rarely has the crowds of the famous Dolomite icons, and it has one big practical advantage &mdash; in Austria you can marry legally, and in some regions even at an approved outdoor spot. For couples who want the legal act on the mountain rather than a symbolic one, Tyrol is often the answer, and it is every bit as beautiful.","Tirol ist unser stilles Geheimnis: versteckte Bergseen, sanfte grüne Wiesen unter schneegestreiften Gipfeln und Dörfer in leichter Fahrweite von Innsbruck. Es hat selten den Andrang der berühmten Dolomiten-Ikonen und einen großen praktischen Vorteil &mdash; in Österreich könnt ihr rechtsgültig heiraten, in manchen Regionen sogar an einem genehmigten Ort im Freien. Für Paare, die den Rechtsakt am Berg statt einer symbolischen Zeremonie wollen, ist Tirol oft die Antwort &mdash; und mindestens ebenso schön."))
    C.append(fig('06-alpenorte-tiroler-bergsee-traubogen.webp',"A pampas-grass arch set by a Tyrolean mountain lake with autumn larches","Ein Pampasgras-Bogen an einem Tiroler Bergsee mit herbstlichen Lärchen"))
    C.append(fig('07-alpenorte-tiroler-bergsee-paar.webp',"The couple at the arch beside the still Tyrolean lake","Das Paar am Bogen neben dem stillen Tiroler See"))
    C.append(fig('13-alpenorte-tirol-zeremonie-bergkulisse.webp',"A ceremony in Tyrol with a backdrop of snow-streaked jagged peaks","Eine Zeremonie in Tirol vor schroffen, schneegestreiften Gipfeln"))

    C.append(p("Tyrol also rewards the couple who want a little Alpine culture around the day. Timber villages with onion-domed churches, mountain huts serving long lunches, cable cars that open the high pastures &mdash; it feels lived-in and warm rather than remote. Innsbruck itself, with its old town under the Nordkette, makes a beautiful and practical base, an hour or less from lakes, meadows and the ridges above the city.","Tirol belohnt auch das Paar, das ein wenig alpine Kultur um den Tag will. Holzdörfer mit Zwiebeltürmen, Hütten mit langen Mittagessen, Bergbahnen, die die hohen Almen öffnen &mdash; es wirkt gelebt und warm statt abgelegen. Innsbruck selbst, mit seiner Altstadt unter der Nordkette, gibt eine schöne und praktische Basis ab, eine Stunde oder weniger von Seen, Wiesen und den Graten über der Stadt."))
    C.append(h2('passes','The great passes','Die großen Pässe'))
    C.append(p("The high passes that link the valleys &mdash; Passo Giau, Passo Gardena, Passo Sella &mdash; are the easy secret of the range: you drive to over 2,000 metres and step straight onto alpine meadow with the giants all around, no climb required. Giau in particular, with its little pointed chapel under the shark-fin peak of Ra Gusela, gives you drama and a touch of storybook without a hike, and the evening light there is some of the best anywhere. Perfect for couples who want the high-mountain feeling with family in tow.","Die hohen Pässe, die die Täler verbinden &mdash; Passo Giau, Grödnerjoch, Sellajoch &mdash;, sind das leichte Geheimnis des Massivs: Ihr fahrt auf über 2.000 Meter und tretet direkt auf Almwiese hinaus, die Riesen ringsum, ohne Aufstieg. Besonders der Giau mit seiner kleinen spitzen Kapelle unter der Haifischflossen-Spitze der Ra Gusela schenkt Dramatik und einen Hauch Märchen ohne Wanderung, und das Abendlicht dort gehört zum besten überhaupt. Perfekt für Paare, die das Hochgebirgsgefühl mit Familie im Schlepptau wollen."))
    C.append(fig('08-alpenorte-passo-giau-kapelle.webp',"The little pointed chapel at Passo Giau with Ra Gusela rising behind","Die kleine spitze Kapelle am Passo Giau, die Ra Gusela dahinter"))
    C.append(fig('15-alpenorte-sella-zeremonie.webp',"A small ceremony on the meadow beneath the walls of the Sella group","Eine kleine Zeremonie auf der Wiese unter den Wänden der Sellagruppe"))
    C.append(fig('16-alpenorte-groedner-joch-wiese.webp',"Green meadow and a hut at Passo Gardena as the sun breaks through","Grüne Wiese und eine Hütte am Grödner Joch, während die Sonne durchbricht"))

    C.append(p("The other gift of the passes is the light. Because they sit high and open, with nothing between you and the horizon, they catch sunrise and sunset in full &mdash; and Giau in particular faces the evening so well that we often plan it for golden hour and enrosadira rather than dawn. Park, walk a minute onto the meadow, and let the sky do the rest; you can be back down to a valley dinner within the hour.","Das andere Geschenk der Pässe ist das Licht. Weil sie hoch und offen liegen, mit nichts zwischen euch und dem Horizont, fangen sie Sonnenauf- und -untergang voll &mdash; und besonders der Giau nimmt den Abend so gut, dass wir ihn oft für die goldene Stunde und die Enrosadira planen statt für den Morgen. Parken, eine Minute auf die Wiese gehen und den Himmel den Rest machen lassen; binnen einer Stunde seid ihr zurück zu einem Abendessen im Tal."))
    C.append(h2('peaks','For the peak-baggers','Für Gipfelstürmer'))
    C.append(p("If you want the day to feel earned, the Alps reward the effort like nowhere else. A ridge reached on foot or by a short climb from a lift gives you exposure, a 360-degree horizon and a scale that stops the breath &mdash; you standing tiny against a thousand metres of rock. These are the boldest frames we take, and the most private: five more minutes past where most people turn around, and the mountain is yours. We match the walk to your fitness and never oversell what a spot costs to reach.","Wollt ihr, dass sich der Tag verdient anfühlt, belohnen die Alpen den Aufwand wie kaum ein anderer Ort. Ein zu Fuß oder mit kurzem Aufstieg von der Bahn erreichter Grat gibt euch Ausgesetztheit, einen 360-Grad-Horizont und eine Dimension, die den Atem stocken lässt &mdash; ihr winzig vor tausend Metern Fels. Das sind die kühnsten Bilder, die wir machen, und die privatesten: fünf Minuten weiter, als die meisten umkehren, und der Berg gehört euch. Wir stimmen den Weg auf eure Fitness ab und beschönigen nie, was ein Ort an Aufstieg kostet."))
    C.append(fig('14-alpenorte-tirol-grat-paar.webp',"The couple tiny on a ridge before a vast snow-streaked cirque","Das Paar winzig auf einem Grat vor einem weiten, schneegestreiften Kar"))

    C.append(p("None of this has to mean a mountaineering epic. Many of our most dramatic ridge frames sit only a short, safe walk from a cable-car station &mdash; enough to leave the crowds behind, not enough to need ropes or a guide. We scout every route in advance, carry the plan and the spare layers, and pace it so the walk feels like part of the adventure rather than a chore. If you can manage an hour on a trail, we can put you somewhere that looks impossible.","Nichts davon muss ein Bergsteiger-Epos sein. Viele unserer dramatischsten Grat-Bilder liegen nur einen kurzen, sicheren Weg von einer Bergstation entfernt &mdash; genug, um den Andrang hinter sich zu lassen, nicht genug für Seil oder Bergführer. Wir erkunden jede Route vorab, tragen den Plan und die Ersatzschichten und dosieren es so, dass der Weg Teil des Abenteuers ist statt Pflicht. Wenn ihr eine Stunde auf einem Pfad schafft, bringen wir euch irgendwohin, das unmöglich aussieht."))
    C.append(h2('winter','The Alps under snow','Die Alpen unter Schnee'))
    C.append(p("Winter turns the whole range monochrome and almost unearthly &mdash; snow to the horizon, the peaks stripped to black and white, and, best of all, near-total solitude. The Tre Cime and the high snow ridges are unforgettable in this light, and a ceremony up here feels like standing inside a snow globe. It asks for more &mdash; warm layers, sure footing, and a close eye on which toll roads and lifts are open, because winter schedules are reduced. When it lines up, it is the most spectacular version of the Alps we photograph all year.","Der Winter macht das ganze Massiv monochrom und fast überirdisch &mdash; Schnee bis zum Horizont, die Gipfel auf Schwarzweiß reduziert und, das Beste, fast völlige Einsamkeit. Die Drei Zinnen und die hohen Schneegrate sind in diesem Licht unvergesslich, und eine Zeremonie hier oben fühlt sich an wie im Inneren einer Schneekugel. Es verlangt mehr &mdash; warme Schichten, sicheren Tritt und einen wachen Blick darauf, welche Mautstraßen und Bahnen offen sind, denn die Winterfahrpläne sind reduziert. Wenn es passt, ist es die spektakulärste Version der Alpen, die wir das ganze Jahr fotografieren."))
    C.append(fig('11-alpenorte-tre-cime-winter.webp',"The couple in the snow with the Tre Cime spires glowing behind","Das Paar im Schnee, die Drei-Zinnen-Türme glühen dahinter"))
    C.append(fig('12-alpenorte-tre-cime-panorama-winter.webp',"The couple on a snowy plateau below the Tre Cime in full winter","Das Paar auf einem verschneiten Plateau unter den Drei Zinnen im tiefen Winter"))

    C.append(p("Winter also thins the calendar in your favour. The couples who brave the cold have the most famous places almost entirely to themselves, and the low sun sits soft and golden for hours instead of minutes. Dress for it &mdash; warm layers under the coat, real boots to the spot, the pretty shoes in a bag &mdash; and a grey, snowing sky is not a setback but a gift, giving some of the most atmospheric mountain photographs we ever take.","Der Winter dünnt auch den Kalender zu euren Gunsten. Die Paare, die der Kälte trotzen, haben die berühmtesten Orte fast ganz für sich, und die tiefe Sonne steht stundenlang weich und golden statt nur Minuten. Kleidet euch dafür &mdash; warme Schichten unter dem Mantel, echte Schuhe zum Ort, die schönen im Beutel &mdash;, und ein grauer, schneiender Himmel ist kein Rückschlag, sondern ein Geschenk und schenkt einige der stimmungsvollsten Bergbilder, die wir je machen."))
    C.append(h2('choose','Which one is yours','Was zu euch passt'))
    C.append(p("So how to choose? Go to the <strong>Dolomites</strong> for maximum drama and the icons at their quietest. Go to <strong>Tyrol or Bavaria</strong> for calmer lakes, gentler effort and the easy legal route. Choose a <strong>lake</strong> if you want stillness and reflection, a <strong>pass</strong> if you want big mountains with no hike, a <strong>summit</strong> if you want to earn the view, and <strong>winter</strong> if you want solitude and drama over warmth. When couples truly cannot decide, we split it across a couple of days &mdash; a lake at dawn, a pass at dusk. Tell us the feeling and we will name the place.","Wie also wählen? Geht in die <strong>Dolomiten</strong> für maximale Dramatik und die Ikonen in ihrer stillsten Form. Geht nach <strong>Tirol oder Bayern</strong> für ruhigere Seen, sanfteren Aufwand und den leichten Rechtsweg. Wählt einen <strong>See</strong> für Stille und Spiegelung, einen <strong>Pass</strong> für große Berge ohne Wanderung, einen <strong>Gipfel</strong>, um euch die Aussicht zu verdienen, und den <strong>Winter</strong>, wenn ihr Einsamkeit und Dramatik über Wärme stellt. Wenn Paare sich wirklich nicht entscheiden können, teilen wir es auf ein paar Tage &mdash; ein See im Morgengrauen, ein Pass in der Dämmerung. Sagt uns das Gefühl, und wir nennen den Ort."))

    C.append(p("And you are not locked into one answer. Some of our favourite trips mix two worlds across a few days &mdash; a quiet Tyrolean lake at sunrise, an easy legal ceremony, then a drive south for a Dolomite sunset the next evening. The ranges sit close enough that a single trip can hold both the calm and the drama. Tell us the two feelings you cannot choose between, and we will often find a way to give you both.","Und ihr seid nicht auf eine Antwort festgelegt. Einige unserer liebsten Reisen mischen zwei Welten über ein paar Tage &mdash; ein stiller Tiroler See zum Sonnenaufgang, eine leichte standesamtliche Zeremonie, dann eine Fahrt nach Süden für einen Dolomiten-Sonnenuntergang am nächsten Abend. Die Massive liegen nah genug, dass eine einzige Reise Ruhe und Dramatik zugleich fassen kann. Sagt uns die zwei Gefühle, zwischen denen ihr euch nicht entscheiden könnt, und wir finden oft einen Weg, euch beide zu geben."))
    C.append(h2('reach','Getting around the Alps','Anreise & Wege durch die Alpen'))
    C.append(p("The range is easier to reach than the drama suggests. Most couples fly into Venice, Verona, Innsbruck or Munich and drive in &mdash; the Dolomites are two to three hours from Venice, the Zugspitze and Eibsee sit right on the Bavarian border near Garmisch, and Tyrol spreads out around Innsbruck. Crossing between Italy and Austria is a simple drive with no fuss. From a single valley base you can often reach several of these spots, and we build the route around the light &mdash; which place at dawn, which at dusk &mdash; and handle the reservations, timings and driving so your mornings stay calm.","Das Massiv ist leichter erreichbar, als die Dramatik vermuten lässt. Die meisten Paare fliegen nach Venedig, Verona, Innsbruck oder München und fahren hinein &mdash; die Dolomiten sind zwei bis drei Stunden von Venedig, Zugspitze und Eibsee liegen direkt an der bayerischen Grenze bei Garmisch, und Tirol breitet sich um Innsbruck aus. Der Grenzübertritt zwischen Italien und Österreich ist eine unkomplizierte Fahrt. Von einer einzigen Talbasis erreicht ihr oft mehrere dieser Orte, und wir bauen die Route um das Licht &mdash; welcher Ort im Morgengrauen, welcher in der Dämmerung &mdash; und übernehmen Reservierungen, Timing und Fahrerei, damit eure Morgen ruhig bleiben."))

    C.append(p("Where you base yourself shapes the trip as much as where you shoot. Cortina d&rsquo;Ampezzo and the Alta Badia put you in the heart of the Dolomites; Garmisch sits right under the Zugspitze; Innsbruck opens up Tyrol in every direction. We help you pick the base that keeps your chosen spots within an easy dawn drive, book the huts where an overnight makes a sunrise possible, and hand you a simple plan so the only thing you have to think about on the day is each other.","Wo ihr euch einquartiert, prägt die Reise so sehr wie der Ort, an dem ihr fotografiert. Cortina d&rsquo;Ampezzo und die Alta Badia setzen euch ins Herz der Dolomiten; Garmisch liegt direkt unter der Zugspitze; Innsbruck öffnet Tirol in jede Richtung. Wir helfen euch, die Basis zu wählen, die eure Orte in leichter Morgen-Fahrweite hält, buchen die Hütten, wo eine Übernachtung einen Sonnenaufgang möglich macht, und geben euch einen einfachen Plan, damit ihr am Tag nur an eines denken müsst: aneinander."))
    C.append(h2('sunset','Light &amp; the finish','Licht & Abschluss'))
    C.append(p("Wherever you land in the Alps, the light is the thing &mdash; and the day is not over when the sun drops. Sunrise gives you empty icons and soft colour; golden hour warms the rock and slides into the fireshow of enrosadira on the Dolomite walls; and blue hour, the cool quiet window after, is the one most people miss by packing up too soon. We never do. Then the celebration to match &mdash; a hut dinner, a swim, a toast on the mountain &mdash; because the best locations deserve more than a single frame.","Wo auch immer ihr in den Alpen landet, das Licht ist die Hauptsache &mdash; und der Tag ist nicht vorbei, wenn die Sonne fällt. Der Sonnenaufgang schenkt leere Ikonen und weiche Farben; die goldene Stunde wärmt den Fels und geht über in das Feuerwerk der Enrosadira an den Dolomitenwänden; und die blaue Stunde, das kühle stille Fenster danach, verpassen die meisten, weil sie zu früh einpacken. Wir nie. Dann die passende Feier &mdash; ein Hüttenessen, ein Bad, ein Toast am Berg &mdash;, denn die schönsten Orte verdienen mehr als ein einziges Bild."))
    C.append(fig('10-alpenorte-tirol-sonnenuntergang-bogen.webp',"The couple at a floral arch backlit by a blazing Tyrolean sunset","Das Paar an einem Blumenbogen im Gegenlicht eines glühenden Tiroler Sonnenuntergangs"))

    faq_html='<h2 id="faq" style="'+H2S+'">'+L('Best Alpine locations FAQ','FAQ zu den schönsten Alpen-Orten')+'</h2>'
    FAQL=[FQ(*x) for x in ALPS_FAQ]
    faq_html+=''.join('<div style="margin:1.3em 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:1.1em">'
      f'<h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:20px;margin:0 0 .3em">{q}</h3>'
      f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2);margin:0">{a}</p></div>' for q,a in FAQL)
    faq_ld={"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
      {"@type":"Question","name":_plain(q),"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":_plain(a)}} for q,a in FAQL]}
    related=''.join(story_card(lang,P,STORYBY[sl]) for sl in ex['stories'])
    more=''.join(guide_card(lang,P,x) for x in GUIDES if x['slug']!=slug)
    body=(nav(lang,rel,'howto')+
      f'<section class="page-hero" style="padding:0">{herobg(P,HERO_IMG,g["title"][lang])}'
      f'<div class="content"><div class="wrap"><div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"guide_kick")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h1>{g["title"][lang]}</h1></div></div></section>'
      '<section><div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">'+''.join(C)+faq_html+
      f'<p style="margin-top:2.4em"><a href="{u(P,lang,"how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/")}" class="arrow-link">&larr; {T["nav"]["howto"][lang]}</a></p></div></section>'
      '<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"related_stories")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"related_stories")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{related}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="stories" style="padding-top:clamp(40px,6vw,80px)"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"more_guides")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"more_guides")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{more}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="cta"><div class="wrap row reveal"><div>'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"cta_k")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2 style="margin-top:20px">{t(lang,"cta_h")}</h2></div>'
      f'<a href="{u(P,lang,"get-in-touch/")}" class="btn light">{t(lang,"start_planning")}</a></div></section>'
      +footer(lang,rel))
    write(lang,rel,head(lang,rel,g['title'][lang]+' — Mountain Elopement',g['excerpt'][lang],ld_extra=faq_ld,pre=herolink(P,HERO_IMG))+body+scripts(P))

# ---- elope-in-austria: rich guide (EN+DE; ES/IT still served by generic build_guides until translated) ----
# --- elope-in-austria guide ES/IT (auto-generated, keyed by exact EN string) ---
AUSTRIA_ES = {
  'Why Tyrol is our home ground': 'Por qué el Tirol es nuestro terreno de casa',
  'Every photographer says they know their region. We were born into this one. Andreas is Tyrolean, at home between Innsbruck and the Dolomites, and that means we are not arriving with a map and a rented plan &mdash; we are taking you to the meadow we hiked as teenagers and the ridge we watched the sun set from a hundred times. When the weather turns, we already know the sheltered alternative twenty minutes away. When a lake is mobbed, we know the quiet twin over the pass. That is what local really buys you: not just pretty spots, but the right one, at the right hour, whatever the day throws at you.': 'Todo fotógrafo dice que conoce su región. Nosotros nacimos en esta. Andreas es tirolés, en casa entre Innsbruck y los Dolomitas, y eso significa que no llegamos con un mapa y un plan alquilado &mdash; os llevamos al prado que caminábamos de adolescentes y a la cresta desde la que vimos ponerse el sol cien veces. Cuando el tiempo cambia, ya conocemos la alternativa resguardada a veinte minutos. Cuando un lago está abarrotado, conocemos el gemelo tranquilo al otro lado del puerto. Eso es lo que de verdad compra lo local: no solo lugares bonitos, sino el correcto, a la hora correcta, pase lo que pase.',
  'A couple kissing before a wide Tyrolean mountain backdrop': 'Una pareja besándose ante un amplio fondo de montañas tirolesas',
  'The easy legal marriage': 'La boda legal sin complicaciones',
  'Here is the single biggest reason to elope in Austria rather than over the border in Italy: you can be legally married in the mountains. In Italy a binding wedding can only take place inside a town hall, so every Dolomite ceremony is symbolic. Austria is different. A civil marriage is straightforward for foreign couples, and a number of Tyrolean registry offices will conduct the legal ceremony at an approved outdoor location &mdash; a lakeshore, a viewpoint, a mountain terrace &mdash; not only inside four walls. The act that actually changes your legal status can happen with the peaks right there.': 'Esta es la mayor razón para fugarse en Austria en vez de cruzar la frontera a Italia: podéis casaros legalmente en las montañas. En Italia una boda vinculante solo puede celebrarse dentro de un ayuntamiento, así que toda ceremonia dolomítica es simbólica. Austria es distinta. Un matrimonio civil es sencillo para parejas extranjeras, y varios registros civiles tiroleses celebran la ceremonia legal en un lugar autorizado al aire libre &mdash; una orilla, un mirador, una terraza de montaña &mdash;, no solo entre cuatro paredes. El acto que de verdad cambia vuestro estado legal puede ocurrir con las cumbres justo ahí.',
  'A ceremony in the Tyrolean mountains': 'Una ceremonia en las montañas tirolesas',
  'It is not automatic everywhere &mdash; each office sets its own rules, dates and lead times, and the popular summer slots go early. But the point stands: in Tyrol you do not have to choose between a real wedding and a mountain wedding. We know which offices say yes to the outdoors, we handle the appointment and the documents, and we build the day so the legal minutes and the meaningful ones sit side by side rather than in two different countries.': 'No es automático en todas partes &mdash; cada oficina fija sus propias reglas, fechas y plazos, y las codiciadas citas de verano se agotan pronto. Pero el punto se mantiene: en el Tirol no tenéis que elegir entre una boda de verdad y una boda de montaña. Sabemos qué oficinas dicen sí al aire libre, gestionamos la cita y los documentos, y armamos el día para que los minutos legales y los que importan estén uno al lado del otro, no en dos países distintos.',
  'Symbolic or legal &mdash; both work beautifully': 'Simbólica o legal &mdash; ambas funcionan de maravilla',
  'There are two honest paths, and neither is more romantic than the other. The first: complete the legal marriage in Austria, at the registry or an approved outdoor spot, so the day on the mountain is also the day it counts. The second, which many couples still choose for simplicity: sign the short legal act at your registry office at home, and give the mountain the ceremony that actually matters &mdash; your words, your vows, no clerk, no queue. Both carry all of the feeling. We will tell you plainly which one fits your timeline and your paperwork.': 'Hay dos caminos honestos, y ninguno es más romántico que el otro. El primero: completar el matrimonio legal en Austria, en el registro o en un lugar autorizado al aire libre, para que el día en la montaña sea también el día que cuenta. El segundo, que muchas parejas siguen eligiendo por simplicidad: firmar el breve acto legal en vuestro registro civil en casa, y dar a la montaña la ceremonia que de verdad importa &mdash; vuestras palabras, vuestros votos, sin funcionario, sin cola. Ambos llevan todo el sentimiento. Os diremos con claridad cuál encaja con vuestro calendario y vuestro papeleo.',
  'One partner reading their vows aloud on the mountain': 'Uno de los novios leyendo sus votos en voz alta en la montaña',
  'The exchange of rings with the valley falling away behind': 'El intercambio de anillos con el valle cayendo por detrás',
  'Innsbruck & the Nordkette': 'Innsbruck y la Nordkette',
  'Innsbruck is the only city in the Alps with a high mountain on its doorstep, and it is the reason so many of our Tyrolean days begin here. From the old town, the Hungerburg funicular and the Nordkette cable cars lift you to Hafelekar at 2,256&thinsp;m in about twenty minutes &mdash; coffee under the arcades, and not long after, a ridge with the whole Inn valley laid out below and the Stubai glaciers on the far horizon. It is genuine high-alpine exposure reached in the time it takes to drive across a city, which makes it perfect for couples who want scale without a climb, or a dramatic finish to a day that started at a lake.': 'Innsbruck es la única ciudad de los Alpes con una alta montaña a la puerta, y la razón por la que tantos de nuestros días tiroleses empiezan aquí. Desde el casco antiguo, el funicular de la Hungerburg y los teleféricos de la Nordkette os suben al Hafelekar, a 2.256&thinsp;m, en unos veinte minutos &mdash; café bajo los soportales y, poco después, una cresta con todo el valle del Inn tendido abajo y los glaciares del Stubai en el horizonte lejano. Es exposición alpina de verdad alcanzada en el tiempo que se tarda en cruzar una ciudad, lo que la hace perfecta para parejas que quieren escala sin subida, o un final dramático a un día que empezó en un lago.',
  'The couple on the Hafelekar ridge high above Innsbruck': 'La pareja en la cresta del Hafelekar, muy por encima de Innsbruck',
  'A word of honesty about the light: the first cable car up the Nordkette runs well after sunrise, so a true dawn ceremony on the ridge is not on the menu unless you hike up in the dark. That is fine &mdash; the Nordkette is at its best in the clear morning after the first cabin and again in the long golden evening, and we plan around those windows so the ridge is quiet and the light is soft. For actual sunrise we take you to a lake or a valley spot instead, and save the high ridge for the hours it wears best.': 'Una nota honesta sobre la luz: el primer teleférico de la Nordkette sube bastante después del amanecer, así que una verdadera ceremonia del alba en la cresta no está en el menú, salvo que subáis a pie en la oscuridad. No pasa nada &mdash; la Nordkette da lo mejor en la mañana clara tras la primera cabina y de nuevo en la larga tarde dorada, y planificamos en torno a esas ventanas para que la cresta esté tranquila y la luz sea suave. Para el amanecer de verdad os llevamos a un lago o a un lugar del valle, y reservamos la cresta alta para las horas en que mejor luce.',
  'The Tyrolean lakes': 'Los lagos tiroleses',
  'Tyrol keeps its lakes quieter than the famous Dolomite icons, and that is exactly their gift. Our shortlist starts with the protected Obernberger See near the Brenner, a shallow turquoise bowl ringed by larch and reachable by a gentle walk; the emerald Schlegeisspeicher deep in the Zillertal, milk-blue against grey rock; and the small, still high tarns above K&uuml;htai that most maps do not name. All of them sit close to Innsbruck yet feel a world away, and every one is calmest at first light, before the day arrives &mdash; which is precisely when we plan to be there.': 'El Tirol mantiene sus lagos más tranquilos que los famosos iconos dolomíticos, y ese es justo su regalo. Nuestra lista empieza con el protegido Obernberger See junto al Brennero, una cuenca turquesa poco profunda rodeada de alerces y alcanzable por un paseo suave; el esmeralda Schlegeisspeicher en lo hondo del Zillertal, azul lechoso contra la roca gris; y las pequeñas y quietas lagunas de altura sobre Kühtai que la mayoría de los mapas no nombra. Todos están cerca de Innsbruck y a la vez se sienten en otro mundo, y cada uno está más tranquilo con la primera luz, antes de que llegue el día &mdash; que es exactamente cuando planeamos estar ahí.',
  'A ceremony at the edge of a still Tyrolean mountain lake': 'Una ceremonia a la orilla de un quieto lago de montaña tirolés',
  'A floral arch set beside a Tyrolean lake for the vows': 'Un arco floral montado junto a un lago tirolés para los votos',
  'High roads & toll roads &mdash; big scenery, little walking': 'Carreteras de altura y de peaje &mdash; gran escenario, poca caminata',
  'Some of Tyrol&rsquo;s most cinematic places are reached almost entirely by car, which is a quiet blessing on a wedding day. Two alpine toll roads open turquoise water without a hike: the Schlegeis Alpine Road in the Zillertal, roughly &euro;13 per car, climbs to the milk-blue Schlegeis reservoir; and the high roads over K&uuml;htai and the Timmelsjoch lift you well past the treeline into bare rock and long views. You step out of the car already at altitude, in a dress or a suit, with the big scenery right there &mdash; and we build the timing so you arrive as the light turns rather than when the car parks fill.': 'Algunos de los lugares más cinematográficos del Tirol se alcanzan casi por completo en coche, una silenciosa bendición en un día de boda. Dos carreteras de peaje alpinas abren agua turquesa sin caminata: la Schlegeis Alpenstraße en el Zillertal, unos 13&nbsp;&euro; por coche, sube al azul lechoso embalse del Schlegeis; y las carreteras de altura de Kühtai y del Timmelsjoch os elevan mucho más allá del bosque, a roca desnuda y vistas largas. Salís del coche ya en altura, en vestido o en traje, con el gran escenario justo ahí &mdash; y armamos el tiempo para que lleguéis cuando la luz gira, no cuando se llenan los aparcamientos.',
  'Ridges & summits, for the day that feels earned': 'Crestas y cumbres, para el día que se siente ganado',
  'If you want more than a viewpoint &mdash; if you want the day to feel earned &mdash; Tyrol has ridges that reward a short, honest climb with something you will never forget. A walk up from a lift or a trailhead like the Birgitzk&ouml;pfl puts you on exposed ground with a 360-degree horizon and the two of you tiny against it, the boldest and most private frames we make. None of it needs ropes or a guide; it needs good boots, an early start and someone who has walked the route before. We scout every path in advance, carry the plan and the spare layers, and pace it so the climb is part of the adventure, not a chore.': 'Si queréis más que un mirador &mdash; si queréis que el día se sienta ganado &mdash;, el Tirol tiene crestas que premian una subida corta y honesta con algo que no olvidaréis. Un ascenso desde un remonte o desde un punto de partida como el Birgitzköpfl os pone en terreno expuesto con un horizonte de 360 grados y a vosotros dos diminutos ante él, los encuadres más audaces y más íntimos que hacemos. Nada de esto necesita cuerdas ni guía; necesita buenas botas, un comienzo temprano y alguien que haya caminado la ruta antes. Exploramos cada sendero de antemano, cargamos el plan y las capas de repuesto y lo dosificamos para que la subida sea parte de la aventura, no una tarea.',
  'A trail signpost on the way up to the Birgitzk&ouml;pfl above Innsbruck': 'Un poste indicador de sendero camino del Birgitzköpfl sobre Innsbruck',
  'The couple and their small group on the ascent': 'La pareja y su pequeño grupo en el ascenso',
  'When to come': 'Cuándo venir',
  'May through October is the dependable season: the lifts run, the high roads are open, and the meadows are green. July and August bring the warmest, most settled weather and the most people; late September is our quiet favourite, with the larches turning gold and the crowds thinning out. The shoulder weeks are a gamble worth taking &mdash; you can get fresh snow on the peaks and empty trails in a single morning, and those are often the best pictures of the year. Winter turns Tyrol spectacular and silent, but it needs a close eye on which roads and lifts stay open.': 'De mayo a octubre es la temporada fiable: los remontes funcionan, las carreteras de altura están abiertas y los prados verdes. Julio y agosto traen el tiempo más cálido y estable y la mayor gente; finales de septiembre es nuestro favorito tranquilo, con los alerces dorándose y las multitudes ralas. Las semanas de transición son una apuesta que vale la pena &mdash; podéis tener nieve fresca en las cumbres y senderos vacíos en una misma mañana, y esas son a menudo las mejores fotos del año. El invierno vuelve el Tirol espectacular y silencioso, pero pide un ojo atento a qué carreteras y remontes siguen abiertos.',
  'The couple on the descent in warm evening light': 'La pareja en el descenso bajo la cálida luz de la tarde',
  'Getting here & where to stay': 'Cómo llegar y dónde alojarse',
  'Tyrol is one of the easiest Alpine regions to reach. Innsbruck has its own airport just minutes from the old town, and Munich and Venice are each a simple drive or train ride away, so most couples are under a mountain within an hour or two of landing. Innsbruck itself makes the ideal base &mdash; the Nordkette above you, the Zillertal and its lakes a short drive east, the high roads west, and the Dolomites two to three hours south for couples who want to fold both countries into one trip. We help you choose the base that keeps your chosen spots within an easy dawn drive and hand you a simple plan for the day.': 'El Tirol es una de las regiones alpinas más accesibles. Innsbruck tiene su propio aeropuerto a minutos del casco antiguo, y Múnich y Venecia están cada uno a un sencillo trayecto en coche o tren, así que la mayoría de las parejas está bajo una montaña una o dos horas tras aterrizar. La propia Innsbruck es la base ideal &mdash; la Nordkette sobre vosotros, el Zillertal y sus lagos a un corto trayecto al este, las carreteras de altura al oeste, y los Dolomitas dos o tres horas al sur para parejas que quieren juntar los dos países en un viaje. Os ayudamos a elegir la base que mantiene vuestros lugares a un cómodo trayecto al alba y os entregamos un plan sencillo para el día.',
  'Light & the celebration': 'La luz y la celebración',
  'The day is not over when the vows are said. Tyrol&rsquo;s evenings are long and generous &mdash; the low sun rakes across the ridges and the whole valley goes gold, then rose, then the cool blue hour that most people miss by packing up too early. We never do. And then the celebration to match: a picnic on a warm slab of rock, a toast with the peaks going pink, a slow descent in the last light. A mountain wedding is not one perfect frame at noon; it is a whole day that keeps giving, right down to the walk home.': 'El día no termina cuando se dicen los votos. Las tardes del Tirol son largas y generosas &mdash; el sol bajo rasga las crestas y todo el valle se vuelve dorado, luego rosa, luego la fresca hora azul que la mayoría se pierde por recoger demasiado pronto. Nosotros nunca. Y luego la celebración a juego: un picnic sobre una cálida losa de roca, un brindis con las cumbres tornándose rosas, un lento descenso en la última luz. Una boda de montaña no es un encuadre perfecto al mediodía; es un día entero que sigue dando, hasta el camino de vuelta a casa.',
  'The couple sharing a picnic high on the mountain': 'La pareja compartiendo un picnic en lo alto de la montaña',
  'A toast on the mountain as the peaks turn pink': 'Un brindis en la montaña mientras las cumbres se tornan rosas',
  'A blazing Tyrolean sunset behind the couple': 'Un ardiente atardecer tirolés detrás de la pareja',
  'The couple in the last warm evening light': 'La pareja en la última y cálida luz de la tarde',
  'Why Tyrol': 'Por qué el Tirol',
  'Symbolic or legal': 'Simbólica o legal',
  'High roads & toll roads': 'Carreteras de altura y de peaje',
  'Ridges & summits': 'Crestas y cumbres',
  'Getting here & staying': 'Cómo llegar y alojarse',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'Eloping in Austria &mdash; FAQ': 'Fugarse en Austria &mdash; preguntas frecuentes',
  'Tyrol is our home. We grew up under these ridges, we know which lake is still glass at six in the morning and which registry office will marry you with a mountain behind you &mdash; and that local knowledge is the whole difference between a good day and a flawless one. Austria makes eloping simple in the way that matters most: it is one of the few places in the Alps where the wedding can be both breathtaking and legally binding on the same mountain. This is our honest guide to doing it here.': 'El Tirol es nuestro hogar. Crecimos bajo estas crestas, sabemos qué lago sigue siendo un cristal a las seis de la mañana y qué registro civil os casará con una montaña detrás &mdash; y ese conocimiento local es toda la diferencia entre un buen día y uno impecable. Austria hace que fugarse sea sencillo donde más importa: es uno de los pocos lugares de los Alpes donde la boda puede ser a la vez sobrecogedora y legalmente vinculante en la misma montaña. Esta es nuestra guía honesta para hacerlo aquí.',
  'On this page': 'En esta página',
}
AUSTRIA_IT = {
  'Why Tyrol is our home ground': 'Perché il Tirolo è il nostro campo di casa',
  'Every photographer says they know their region. We were born into this one. Andreas is Tyrolean, at home between Innsbruck and the Dolomites, and that means we are not arriving with a map and a rented plan &mdash; we are taking you to the meadow we hiked as teenagers and the ridge we watched the sun set from a hundred times. When the weather turns, we already know the sheltered alternative twenty minutes away. When a lake is mobbed, we know the quiet twin over the pass. That is what local really buys you: not just pretty spots, but the right one, at the right hour, whatever the day throws at you.': "Ogni fotografo dice di conoscere la propria regione. Noi in questa ci siamo nati. Andreas è tirolese, di casa tra Innsbruck e le Dolomiti, e questo significa che non arriviamo con una mappa e un piano a noleggio &mdash; vi portiamo sul prato che percorrevamo da ragazzi e sulla cresta da cui abbiamo visto il sole tramontare cento volte. Quando il tempo cambia, conosciamo già l'alternativa riparata a venti minuti. Quando un lago è preso d'assalto, conosciamo il gemello tranquillo oltre il passo. È questo che l'essere del posto vi dà davvero: non solo bei posti, ma quello giusto, all'ora giusta, qualunque cosa porti la giornata.",
  'A couple kissing before a wide Tyrolean mountain backdrop': 'Una coppia che si bacia davanti a un ampio sfondo di montagne tirolesi',
  'The easy legal marriage': 'Il matrimonio legale senza complicazioni',
  'Here is the single biggest reason to elope in Austria rather than over the border in Italy: you can be legally married in the mountains. In Italy a binding wedding can only take place inside a town hall, so every Dolomite ceremony is symbolic. Austria is different. A civil marriage is straightforward for foreign couples, and a number of Tyrolean registry offices will conduct the legal ceremony at an approved outdoor location &mdash; a lakeshore, a viewpoint, a mountain terrace &mdash; not only inside four walls. The act that actually changes your legal status can happen with the peaks right there.': "Ecco la ragione più grande per fare l'elopement in Austria invece che oltre confine in Italia: potete sposarvi legalmente in montagna. In Italia un matrimonio vincolante può avvenire solo dentro un municipio, quindi ogni cerimonia dolomitica è simbolica. L'Austria è diversa. Un matrimonio civile è semplice per le coppie straniere, e diversi uffici di stato civile tirolesi celebrano la cerimonia legale in una location autorizzata all'aperto &mdash; una riva, un punto panoramico, una terrazza di montagna &mdash;, non solo tra quattro mura. L'atto che cambia davvero il vostro stato legale può avvenire con le cime proprio lì.",
  'A ceremony in the Tyrolean mountains': 'Una cerimonia sulle montagne tirolesi',
  'It is not automatic everywhere &mdash; each office sets its own rules, dates and lead times, and the popular summer slots go early. But the point stands: in Tyrol you do not have to choose between a real wedding and a mountain wedding. We know which offices say yes to the outdoors, we handle the appointment and the documents, and we build the day so the legal minutes and the meaningful ones sit side by side rather than in two different countries.': "Non è automatico ovunque &mdash; ogni ufficio fissa le proprie regole, date e tempi, e gli ambiti appuntamenti estivi vanno via presto. Ma il punto resta: in Tirolo non dovete scegliere tra un vero matrimonio e un matrimonio in montagna. Sappiamo quali uffici dicono sì all'aperto, gestiamo l'appuntamento e i documenti, e costruiamo la giornata così che i minuti legali e quelli che contano stiano fianco a fianco, non in due Paesi diversi.",
  'Symbolic or legal &mdash; both work beautifully': 'Simbolica o legale &mdash; entrambe funzionano splendidamente',
  'There are two honest paths, and neither is more romantic than the other. The first: complete the legal marriage in Austria, at the registry or an approved outdoor spot, so the day on the mountain is also the day it counts. The second, which many couples still choose for simplicity: sign the short legal act at your registry office at home, and give the mountain the ceremony that actually matters &mdash; your words, your vows, no clerk, no queue. Both carry all of the feeling. We will tell you plainly which one fits your timeline and your paperwork.': "Ci sono due strade oneste, e nessuna è più romantica dell'altra. La prima: completare il matrimonio legale in Austria, in comune o in una location autorizzata all'aperto, così che la giornata in montagna sia anche il giorno che conta. La seconda, che molte coppie scelgono ancora per semplicità: firmare il breve atto legale nel vostro comune a casa, e dare alla montagna la cerimonia che conta davvero &mdash; le vostre parole, le vostre promesse, senza funzionario, senza coda. Entrambe portano tutta l'emozione. Vi diremo chiaramente quale si adatta ai vostri tempi e alle vostre pratiche.",
  'One partner reading their vows aloud on the mountain': 'Uno dei due che legge ad alta voce le promesse in montagna',
  'The exchange of rings with the valley falling away behind': 'Lo scambio degli anelli con la valle che scende dietro',
  'Innsbruck & the Nordkette': 'Innsbruck e la Nordkette',
  'Innsbruck is the only city in the Alps with a high mountain on its doorstep, and it is the reason so many of our Tyrolean days begin here. From the old town, the Hungerburg funicular and the Nordkette cable cars lift you to Hafelekar at 2,256&thinsp;m in about twenty minutes &mdash; coffee under the arcades, and not long after, a ridge with the whole Inn valley laid out below and the Stubai glaciers on the far horizon. It is genuine high-alpine exposure reached in the time it takes to drive across a city, which makes it perfect for couples who want scale without a climb, or a dramatic finish to a day that started at a lake.': "Innsbruck è l'unica città delle Alpi con un'alta montagna alla porta, ed è il motivo per cui tante delle nostre giornate tirolesi iniziano qui. Dal centro storico, la funicolare dell'Hungerburg e le funivie della Nordkette vi portano all'Hafelekar, a 2.256&thinsp;m, in circa venti minuti &mdash; caffè sotto i portici e, poco dopo, una cresta con tutta la valle dell'Inn distesa sotto e i ghiacciai dello Stubai all'orizzonte lontano. È vera esposizione d'alta quota raggiunta nel tempo che serve ad attraversare una città, il che la rende perfetta per le coppie che vogliono la grandezza senza salita, o un finale drammatico a una giornata iniziata a un lago.",
  'The couple on the Hafelekar ridge high above Innsbruck': "La coppia sulla cresta dell'Hafelekar, alta sopra Innsbruck",
  'A word of honesty about the light: the first cable car up the Nordkette runs well after sunrise, so a true dawn ceremony on the ridge is not on the menu unless you hike up in the dark. That is fine &mdash; the Nordkette is at its best in the clear morning after the first cabin and again in the long golden evening, and we plan around those windows so the ridge is quiet and the light is soft. For actual sunrise we take you to a lake or a valley spot instead, and save the high ridge for the hours it wears best.': "Una nota onesta sulla luce: la prima funivia della Nordkette sale ben dopo l'alba, quindi una vera cerimonia all'alba sulla cresta non è nel menu, a meno che non saliate a piedi al buio. Va bene &mdash; la Nordkette dà il meglio nel mattino limpido dopo la prima cabina e di nuovo nella lunga sera dorata, e pianifichiamo attorno a quelle finestre così che la cresta sia tranquilla e la luce morbida. Per l'alba vera vi portiamo invece a un lago o in un punto della valle, e teniamo la cresta alta per le ore in cui rende meglio.",
  'The Tyrolean lakes': 'I laghi tirolesi',
  'Tyrol keeps its lakes quieter than the famous Dolomite icons, and that is exactly their gift. Our shortlist starts with the protected Obernberger See near the Brenner, a shallow turquoise bowl ringed by larch and reachable by a gentle walk; the emerald Schlegeisspeicher deep in the Zillertal, milk-blue against grey rock; and the small, still high tarns above K&uuml;htai that most maps do not name. All of them sit close to Innsbruck yet feel a world away, and every one is calmest at first light, before the day arrives &mdash; which is precisely when we plan to be there.': "Il Tirolo tiene i suoi laghi più tranquilli delle famose icone dolomitiche, ed è proprio questo il loro dono. La nostra rosa inizia con il protetto Obernberger See presso il Brennero, una conca turchese poco profonda cinta di larici e raggiungibile con una camminata dolce; lo smeraldo Schlegeisspeicher in fondo alla Zillertal, azzurro latte contro la roccia grigia; e i piccoli, quieti laghetti d'alta quota sopra Kühtai che le mappe quasi mai nominano. Tutti stanno vicino a Innsbruck eppure sembrano un altro mondo, e ognuno è più calmo alla prima luce, prima che arrivi la giornata &mdash; ed è esattamente quando pianifichiamo di esserci.",
  'A ceremony at the edge of a still Tyrolean mountain lake': 'Una cerimonia sulla riva di un quieto lago di montagna tirolese',
  'A floral arch set beside a Tyrolean lake for the vows': 'Un arco floreale allestito accanto a un lago tirolese per le promesse',
  'High roads & toll roads &mdash; big scenery, little walking': "Strade d'alta quota e a pedaggio &mdash; grande scenario, poca camminata",
  'Some of Tyrol&rsquo;s most cinematic places are reached almost entirely by car, which is a quiet blessing on a wedding day. Two alpine toll roads open turquoise water without a hike: the Schlegeis Alpine Road in the Zillertal, roughly &euro;13 per car, climbs to the milk-blue Schlegeis reservoir; and the high roads over K&uuml;htai and the Timmelsjoch lift you well past the treeline into bare rock and long views. You step out of the car already at altitude, in a dress or a suit, with the big scenery right there &mdash; and we build the timing so you arrive as the light turns rather than when the car parks fill.': "Alcuni dei luoghi più cinematografici del Tirolo si raggiungono quasi interamente in auto, una silenziosa benedizione in un giorno di matrimonio. Due strade a pedaggio alpine aprono acqua turchese senza camminata: la Schlegeis Alpenstraße in Zillertal, circa 13&nbsp;&euro; ad auto, sale al bacino azzurro latte dello Schlegeis; e le strade d'alta quota di Kühtai e del Timmelsjoch vi sollevano ben oltre il limite del bosco, tra roccia nuda e lunghe vedute. Scendete dall'auto già in quota, in abito o in completo, con il grande scenario proprio lì &mdash; e costruiamo i tempi così che arriviate quando la luce gira, non quando i parcheggi si riempiono.",
  'Ridges & summits, for the day that feels earned': 'Creste e vette, per la giornata che si sente guadagnata',
  'If you want more than a viewpoint &mdash; if you want the day to feel earned &mdash; Tyrol has ridges that reward a short, honest climb with something you will never forget. A walk up from a lift or a trailhead like the Birgitzk&ouml;pfl puts you on exposed ground with a 360-degree horizon and the two of you tiny against it, the boldest and most private frames we make. None of it needs ropes or a guide; it needs good boots, an early start and someone who has walked the route before. We scout every path in advance, carry the plan and the spare layers, and pace it so the climb is part of the adventure, not a chore.': "Se volete più di un punto panoramico &mdash; se volete che la giornata si senta guadagnata &mdash;, il Tirolo ha creste che ripagano una salita breve e onesta con qualcosa che non dimenticherete. Una camminata da un impianto o da un punto di partenza come il Birgitzköpfl vi mette su terreno esposto con un orizzonte a 360 gradi e voi due minuscoli davanti, le inquadrature più audaci e più intime che facciamo. Niente di tutto ciò richiede corde o guida; richiede buoni scarponi, una partenza presto e qualcuno che abbia già percorso il tracciato. Perlustriamo ogni sentiero in anticipo, portiamo il piano e gli strati di scorta e lo dosiamo così che la salita sia parte dell'avventura, non un peso.",
  'A trail signpost on the way up to the Birgitzk&ouml;pfl above Innsbruck': 'Un cartello segnavia lungo la salita al Birgitzköpfl sopra Innsbruck',
  'The couple and their small group on the ascent': 'La coppia e il suo piccolo gruppo in salita',
  'When to come': 'Quando venire',
  'May through October is the dependable season: the lifts run, the high roads are open, and the meadows are green. July and August bring the warmest, most settled weather and the most people; late September is our quiet favourite, with the larches turning gold and the crowds thinning out. The shoulder weeks are a gamble worth taking &mdash; you can get fresh snow on the peaks and empty trails in a single morning, and those are often the best pictures of the year. Winter turns Tyrol spectacular and silent, but it needs a close eye on which roads and lifts stay open.': "Da maggio a ottobre è la stagione affidabile: gli impianti funzionano, le strade d'alta quota sono aperte e i prati verdi. Luglio e agosto portano il tempo più caldo e stabile e la maggior gente; fine settembre è il nostro preferito tranquillo, con i larici che si fanno d'oro e la folla che si dirada. Le settimane di transizione sono una scommessa che vale la pena &mdash; potete avere neve fresca sulle cime e sentieri vuoti nello stesso mattino, e sono spesso le foto migliori dell'anno. L'inverno rende il Tirolo spettacolare e silenzioso, ma chiede un occhio attento a quali strade e impianti restano aperti.",
  'The couple on the descent in warm evening light': 'La coppia in discesa nella calda luce della sera',
  'Getting here & where to stay': 'Come arrivare e dove alloggiare',
  'Tyrol is one of the easiest Alpine regions to reach. Innsbruck has its own airport just minutes from the old town, and Munich and Venice are each a simple drive or train ride away, so most couples are under a mountain within an hour or two of landing. Innsbruck itself makes the ideal base &mdash; the Nordkette above you, the Zillertal and its lakes a short drive east, the high roads west, and the Dolomites two to three hours south for couples who want to fold both countries into one trip. We help you choose the base that keeps your chosen spots within an easy dawn drive and hand you a simple plan for the day.': "Il Tirolo è una delle regioni alpine più accessibili. Innsbruck ha un proprio aeroporto a pochi minuti dal centro storico, e Monaco e Venezia sono ciascuna a una semplice guida o a un treno, quindi la maggior parte delle coppie è sotto una montagna un'ora o due dopo l'atterraggio. Innsbruck stessa è la base ideale &mdash; la Nordkette sopra di voi, la Zillertal e i suoi laghi a breve distanza a est, le strade d'alta quota a ovest, e le Dolomiti due o tre ore a sud per le coppie che vogliono unire i due Paesi in un solo viaggio. Vi aiutiamo a scegliere la base che tiene i vostri luoghi a comoda distanza all'alba e vi consegniamo un piano semplice per la giornata.",
  'Light & the celebration': 'La luce e la festa',
  'The day is not over when the vows are said. Tyrol&rsquo;s evenings are long and generous &mdash; the low sun rakes across the ridges and the whole valley goes gold, then rose, then the cool blue hour that most people miss by packing up too early. We never do. And then the celebration to match: a picnic on a warm slab of rock, a toast with the peaks going pink, a slow descent in the last light. A mountain wedding is not one perfect frame at noon; it is a whole day that keeps giving, right down to the walk home.': "La giornata non finisce quando sono dette le promesse. Le sere del Tirolo sono lunghe e generose &mdash; il sole basso rade le creste e tutta la valle si fa d'oro, poi rosa, poi la fresca ora blu che i più perdono smontando troppo presto. Noi mai. E poi la festa all'altezza: un picnic su una calda lastra di roccia, un brindisi con le cime che si tingono di rosa, una lenta discesa nell'ultima luce. Un matrimonio in montagna non è un'inquadratura perfetta a mezzogiorno; è un'intera giornata che continua a dare, fino al cammino verso casa.",
  'The couple sharing a picnic high on the mountain': 'La coppia che condivide un picnic in alto sulla montagna',
  'A toast on the mountain as the peaks turn pink': 'Un brindisi in montagna mentre le cime si tingono di rosa',
  'A blazing Tyrolean sunset behind the couple': 'Un ardente tramonto tirolese dietro la coppia',
  'The couple in the last warm evening light': "La coppia nell'ultima calda luce della sera",
  'Why Tyrol': 'Perché il Tirolo',
  'Symbolic or legal': 'Simbolica o legale',
  'High roads & toll roads': "Strade d'alta quota e a pedaggio",
  'Ridges & summits': 'Creste e vette',
  'Getting here & staying': 'Come arrivare e alloggiare',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'Eloping in Austria &mdash; FAQ': 'Elopement in Austria &mdash; domande frequenti',
  'Tyrol is our home. We grew up under these ridges, we know which lake is still glass at six in the morning and which registry office will marry you with a mountain behind you &mdash; and that local knowledge is the whole difference between a good day and a flawless one. Austria makes eloping simple in the way that matters most: it is one of the few places in the Alps where the wedding can be both breathtaking and legally binding on the same mountain. This is our honest guide to doing it here.': "Il Tirolo è casa nostra. Siamo cresciuti sotto queste creste, sappiamo quale lago è ancora uno specchio alle sei del mattino e quale ufficio di stato civile vi sposerà con una montagna alle spalle &mdash; e questa conoscenza del posto è tutta la differenza tra una bella giornata e una impeccabile. L'Austria rende l'elopement semplice dove più conta: è uno dei pochi luoghi delle Alpi dove il matrimonio può essere insieme mozzafiato e legalmente valido sulla stessa montagna. Questa è la nostra guida onesta per farlo qui.",
  'On this page': 'In questa pagina',
}
AUSTRIA_FAQ_ES = {
  'Can we legally get married in the Austrian mountains?': ('¿Podemos casarnos legalmente en las montañas austriacas?', 'Sí &mdash; y esta es la verdadera razón por la que las parejas eligen el Tirol antes que Italia. Austria permite una ceremonia civil legalmente vinculante, y varios registros civiles tiroleses os casan en un lugar autorizado al aire libre, no solo dentro de la oficina. Eso significa que la ceremonia que cuenta sobre el papel puede ocurrir con una montaña detrás. Donde no es posible una cita al aire libre, las parejas firman el breve acto legal en el registro y guardan la ceremonia emocional para la cumbre. Coordinamos la oficina, la fecha y el papeleo en cualquier caso.'),
  'How is eloping in Austria different from the Dolomites?': ('¿En qué se diferencia fugarse en Austria de los Dolomitas?', 'En dos cosas: la ley y la gente. En Italia una boda vinculante solo puede ocurrir dentro de un ayuntamiento, así que una ceremonia de montaña dolomítica es siempre simbólica; en Austria el propio acto legal puede trasladarse a la montaña. Y el Tirol simplemente ve menos gente que los famosos iconos dolomíticos &mdash; los mismos lagos turquesa y crestas escarpadas, una fracción de la cola. Los Dolomitas quedan dos o tres horas al sur, así que muchas parejas hacen ambos: una mañana legal tirolesa, un atardecer dolomítico un día después.'),
  'Do we have to hike, or can we reach the spots easily?': ('¿Tenemos que caminar, o llegamos fácil a los lugares?', 'Ambas cosas son posibles, y lo ajustamos a vosotros. Innsbruck es la única ciudad de los Alpes con una alta montaña a la puerta &mdash; los teleféricos de la Nordkette os suben del casco antiguo a 2.256&thinsp;m en unos veinte minutos, sin caminar. Varios de nuestros lagos tiroleses favoritos están justo al final de una carretera. Y si queréis que el día se sienta ganado, una corta subida por una cresta os pone en un sitio que parece imposible. Nunca exageramos lo que cuesta llegar a un lugar.'),
  'When is the best time of year for a Tyrolean elopement?': ('¿Cuál es la mejor época del año para un elopement tirolés?', 'De mayo a octubre es la ventana fiable: los remontes funcionan, las carreteras de altura están abiertas y los prados verdes. Julio y agosto dan el tiempo más cálido y estable; finales de septiembre trae alerces dorados y menos gente, y es nuestro favorito tranquilo. Las semanas de transición a cada lado pueden regalaros nieve fresca en las cumbres y senderos vacíos en una misma mañana &mdash; algunas de las mejores fotos del año. El invierno es espectacular pero pide un ojo atento a qué carreteras y remontes están abiertos.'),
  'How do we get to Tyrol?': ('¿Cómo llegamos al Tirol?', 'Fácil &mdash; es una de las regiones alpinas más accesibles. Innsbruck tiene su propio aeropuerto a minutos del casco antiguo, y Múnich y Venecia están cada uno a un sencillo trayecto en coche o tren, así que la mayoría de las parejas está bajo una montaña una o dos horas tras aterrizar. Desde una base en Innsbruck alcanzáis la Nordkette, los lagos del Zillertal y las carreteras de altura sin un largo traslado, y el cruce al sur hacia los Dolomitas es un trayecto sencillo y bello.'),
  'What paperwork do we need for a legal wedding in Austria?': ('¿Qué papeleo necesitamos para una boda legal en Austria?', 'Para un matrimonio civil en Austria, las parejas extranjeras suelen necesitar pasaportes válidos, certificados de nacimiento y un certificado de no impedimento para casarse, normalmente con traducciones juradas y, según vuestro país, una apostilla. Cada registro civil fija sus propios plazos y puede pedir algo más, y las fechas de verano se agotan pronto, así que el consejo honesto es empezar unos meses antes. Decidnos desde qué país os casáis y os entregamos la lista exacta y coordinamos directamente con la oficina.'),
}
AUSTRIA_FAQ_IT = {
  'Can we legally get married in the Austrian mountains?': ('Possiamo sposarci legalmente sulle montagne austriache?', "Sì &mdash; ed è questa la vera ragione per cui le coppie scelgono il Tirolo invece dell'Italia. L'Austria consente una cerimonia civile con valore legale, e diversi uffici di stato civile tirolesi vi sposano in una location autorizzata all'aperto, non solo dentro l'ufficio. Significa che la cerimonia che conta sulla carta può avvenire con una montagna alle spalle. Dove un appuntamento all'aperto non è possibile, le coppie firmano il breve atto legale in comune e tengono la cerimonia emotiva per la vetta. In ogni caso coordiniamo ufficio, data e pratiche."),
  'How is eloping in Austria different from the Dolomites?': ("In cosa è diverso l'elopement in Austria rispetto alle Dolomiti?", "In due cose: la legge e la folla. In Italia un matrimonio vincolante può avvenire solo dentro un municipio, quindi una cerimonia di montagna dolomitica è sempre simbolica; in Austria l'atto legale stesso può spostarsi in montagna. E il Tirolo vede semplicemente meno gente delle famose icone dolomitiche &mdash; gli stessi laghi turchesi e le creste frastagliate, una frazione della coda. Le Dolomiti sono due o tre ore a sud, quindi molte coppie fanno entrambe: un mattino legale tirolese, un tramonto dolomitico un giorno dopo."),
  'Do we have to hike, or can we reach the spots easily?': ('Dobbiamo camminare, o raggiungiamo i luoghi facilmente?', "Entrambe le cose sono possibili, e le adattiamo a voi. Innsbruck è l'unica città delle Alpi con un'alta montagna alla porta &mdash; le funivie della Nordkette vi portano dal centro storico a 2.256&thinsp;m in circa venti minuti, senza camminare. Diversi dei nostri laghi tirolesi preferiti stanno proprio alla fine di una strada. E se volete che la giornata si senta guadagnata, una breve salita in cresta vi mette in un posto che sembra impossibile. Non esageriamo mai quanto costa raggiungere un luogo."),
  'When is the best time of year for a Tyrolean elopement?': ('Qual è il periodo migliore per un elopement tirolese?', "Da maggio a ottobre è la finestra affidabile: gli impianti funzionano, le strade d'alta quota sono aperte e i prati verdi. Luglio e agosto danno il tempo più caldo e stabile; fine settembre porta larici dorati e meno folla, ed è il nostro preferito tranquillo. Le settimane di transizione ai due lati possono regalarvi neve fresca sulle cime e sentieri vuoti nello stesso mattino &mdash; alcune delle foto migliori dell'anno. L'inverno è spettacolare ma chiede un occhio attento a quali strade e impianti sono aperti."),
  'How do we get to Tyrol?': ('Come arriviamo in Tirolo?', "Facilmente &mdash; è una delle regioni alpine più accessibili. Innsbruck ha un proprio aeroporto a pochi minuti dal centro storico, e Monaco e Venezia sono ciascuna a una semplice guida o a un treno, quindi la maggior parte delle coppie è sotto una montagna un'ora o due dopo l'atterraggio. Da una base a Innsbruck raggiungete la Nordkette, i laghi della Zillertal e le strade d'alta quota senza un lungo trasferimento, e il passaggio a sud verso le Dolomiti è una guida semplice e panoramica."),
  'What paperwork do we need for a legal wedding in Austria?': ('Quali documenti servono per un matrimonio legale in Austria?', "Per un matrimonio civile in Austria, le coppie straniere di norma hanno bisogno di passaporti validi, certificati di nascita e un certificato di nulla osta al matrimonio, di solito con traduzioni giurate e, a seconda del vostro Paese, un'apostille. Ogni ufficio di stato civile fissa i propri tempi e può chiedere qualcosa in più, e le date estive vanno via presto, quindi il consiglio onesto è iniziare qualche mese prima. Diteci da quale Paese vi sposate e vi consegniamo la lista esatta e coordiniamo direttamente con l'ufficio."),
}

AUSTRIA_FAQ=[
 ("Can we legally get married in the Austrian mountains?",
  "Yes &mdash; and this is the real reason couples choose Tyrol over Italy. Austria allows a legally binding civil ceremony, and a number of Tyrolean registry offices will marry you at an approved outdoor location, not just inside the office. That means the ceremony that counts on paper can happen with a mountain behind you. Where an outdoor slot is not possible, couples sign the short legal act at the registry and keep the emotional ceremony for the summit. We coordinate the office, the date and the paperwork either way.",
  "Können wir in den österreichischen Bergen rechtsgültig heiraten?",
  "Ja &mdash; und genau das ist der Grund, warum Paare Tirol Italien vorziehen. Österreich erlaubt eine rechtsgültige standesamtliche Trauung, und mehrere Tiroler Standesämter trauen euch auch an einem genehmigten Ort im Freien, nicht nur im Amt. Die Zeremonie, die auf dem Papier zählt, kann also mit einem Berg im Rücken stattfinden. Wo ein Außentermin nicht möglich ist, unterschreibt ihr den kurzen Rechtsakt im Amt und behaltet die eigentliche Zeremonie für den Gipfel. Wir koordinieren so oder so Amt, Termin und Papiere."),
 ("How is eloping in Austria different from the Dolomites?",
  "Two things: the law and the crowds. In Italy a legally binding wedding can only happen inside a town hall, so a Dolomite mountain ceremony is always symbolic; in Austria the legal act itself can move to the mountain. And Tyrol simply sees fewer people than the famous Dolomite icons &mdash; the same turquoise lakes and jagged ridges, a fraction of the queue. The Dolomites are two to three hours south, so many couples do both: a legal Tyrolean morning, a Dolomite sunset a day later.",
  "Worin unterscheidet sich ein Elopement in Österreich von den Dolomiten?",
  "In zwei Dingen: Recht und Andrang. In Italien kann eine rechtsgültige Hochzeit nur im Rathaus stattfinden, eine Dolomiten-Bergzeremonie ist also immer symbolisch; in Österreich kann der Rechtsakt selbst an den Berg wandern. Und Tirol sieht schlicht weniger Menschen als die berühmten Dolomiten-Ikonen &mdash; dieselben türkisen Seen und schroffen Grate, ein Bruchteil der Schlange. Die Dolomiten liegen zwei bis drei Stunden südlich, viele Paare machen also beides: ein rechtsgültiger Tiroler Morgen, ein Dolomiten-Sonnenuntergang einen Tag später."),
 ("Do we have to hike, or can we reach the spots easily?",
  "Both are possible, and we match it to you. Innsbruck is the only city in the Alps with a high mountain on its doorstep &mdash; the Nordkette lifts carry you from the old town to 2,256&thinsp;m in about twenty minutes, no walking required. Several of our favourite Tyrolean lakes sit right at the end of a road. And if you want the day to feel earned, a short ridge walk puts you somewhere that looks impossible. We never oversell what a spot costs to reach.",
  "Müssen wir wandern, oder erreichen wir die Orte leicht?",
  "Beides ist möglich, und wir passen es an euch an. Innsbruck ist die einzige Stadt der Alpen mit einem Hochgebirge direkt vor der Tür &mdash; die Nordkettenbahnen bringen euch in rund zwanzig Minuten von der Altstadt auf 2.256&thinsp;m, ganz ohne Fußweg. Mehrere unserer liebsten Tiroler Seen liegen direkt am Ende einer Straße. Und wenn sich der Tag verdient anfühlen soll, bringt euch ein kurzer Gratweg irgendwohin, das unmöglich aussieht. Wir beschönigen nie, was ein Ort an Aufstieg kostet."),
 ("When is the best time of year for a Tyrolean elopement?",
  "May to October is the reliable window: the lifts run, the high roads are open and the meadows are green. July and August give the warmest, most settled weather; late September brings golden larches and thinner crowds and is our quiet favourite. The shoulder weeks either side can hand you fresh snow on the peaks and empty trails in the same morning &mdash; some of the best pictures of the year. Winter is spectacular but needs a close eye on which roads and lifts are open.",
  "Wann ist die beste Zeit für ein Tiroler Elopement?",
  "Mai bis Oktober ist das verlässliche Fenster: Die Bahnen fahren, die Höhenstraßen sind offen und die Wiesen grün. Juli und August bringen das wärmste, beständigste Wetter; der späte September schenkt goldene Lärchen und weniger Andrang und ist unser stiller Favorit. Die Randwochen davor und danach können euch frischen Schnee auf den Gipfeln und leere Wege am selben Morgen bescheren &mdash; einige der besten Bilder des Jahres. Der Winter ist spektakulär, verlangt aber einen wachen Blick darauf, welche Straßen und Bahnen offen sind."),
 ("How do we get to Tyrol?",
  "Easily &mdash; it is one of the most accessible Alpine regions. Innsbruck has its own airport minutes from the old town, and Munich and Venice are each a straightforward drive or train away, so most couples are standing under a mountain within an hour or two of landing. From an Innsbruck base you can reach the Nordkette, the Zillertal lakes and the high roads without ever facing a long transfer, and the crossing south into the Dolomites is a simple, scenic drive.",
  "Wie kommen wir nach Tirol?",
  "Leicht &mdash; es ist eine der am besten erreichbaren Alpenregionen. Innsbruck hat einen eigenen Flughafen wenige Minuten von der Altstadt, und München und Venedig sind jeweils eine unkomplizierte Fahrt oder Zugverbindung entfernt, die meisten Paare stehen also ein bis zwei Stunden nach der Landung unter einem Berg. Von einer Basis in Innsbruck erreicht ihr die Nordkette, die Zillertaler Seen und die Höhenstraßen ohne langen Transfer, und der Übertritt nach Süden in die Dolomiten ist eine einfache, landschaftlich schöne Fahrt."),
 ("What paperwork do we need for a legal wedding in Austria?",
  "For a civil marriage in Austria, foreign couples generally need valid passports, birth certificates, and a certificate of no impediment to marriage, usually with certified translations and, depending on your home country, an apostille. Each registry office sets its own lead times and can ask for a little more, and summer dates fill up early, so the honest advice is to start a few months ahead. Tell us where you are marrying from and we will hand you the exact list and coordinate directly with the office.",
  "Welche Papiere brauchen wir für eine rechtsgültige Trauung in Österreich?",
  "Für eine standesamtliche Trauung in Österreich brauchen ausländische Paare in der Regel gültige Reisepässe, Geburtsurkunden und ein Ehefähigkeitszeugnis, meist mit beglaubigten Übersetzungen und &mdash; je nach Heimatland &mdash; einer Apostille. Jedes Standesamt legt eigene Vorlaufzeiten fest und kann etwas mehr verlangen, und Sommertermine sind früh vergeben, der ehrliche Rat lautet also: ein paar Monate vorher beginnen. Sagt uns, aus welchem Land ihr heiratet, und wir geben euch die genaue Liste und koordinieren direkt mit dem Amt."),
]

def build_austria_guide(lang):
    slug='elope-in-austria'
    g=next(x for x in GUIDES if x['slug']==slug); ex=GUIDE_EXTRA[slug]
    rel='how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/'+slug+'/'; P=prefix(lang,rel)
    DE=(lang=='de')
    def L(en,de):
        if lang=='de': return de
        if lang=='es': return AUSTRIA_ES.get(en,en)
        if lang=='it': return AUSTRIA_IT.get(en,en)
        return en
    def FQ(qen,aen,qde,ade):
        if lang=='de': return (qde,ade)
        if lang=='es': return AUSTRIA_FAQ_ES.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        if lang=='it': return AUSTRIA_FAQ_IT.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        return (qen,aen)
    GI=f'{P}img/guide-elope-in-austria/'
    H2S='font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,3vw,36px);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:1.7em 0 .4em;scroll-margin-top:96px'
    def h2(i,en,de): return f'<h2 id="{i}" style="{H2S}">{L(en,de)}</h2>'
    def p(en,de): return f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2)">{L(en,de)}</p>'
    def fig(name,en,de): return f'<figure class="guide-fig"><img src="{GI}{name}" alt="{L(en,de)}" loading="lazy"></figure>'
    HERO_IMG='img/guide-elope-in-austria/16-oesterreich-grat-ueber-innsbruck.webp'
    toc=[('why',L('Why Tyrol','Warum Tirol')),('legal',L('The easy legal marriage','Die unkomplizierte Trauung')),
         ('ceremony',L('Symbolic or legal','Symbolisch oder standesamtlich')),('innsbruck',L('Innsbruck & the Nordkette','Innsbruck & die Nordkette')),
         ('lakes',L('The Tyrolean lakes','Die Tiroler Seen')),('roads',L('High roads & toll roads','Höhen- & Mautstraßen')),
         ('ridges',L('Ridges & summits','Grate & Gipfel')),('season',L('When to come','Die beste Zeit')),
         ('reach',L('Getting here & staying','Anreise & Basis')),('finish',L('Light & the celebration','Licht & Feier')),('faq',L('FAQ','FAQ'))]
    toc_html=('<nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'"><div class="cap">'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'</div><ol>'
      +''.join(f'<li><a href="#{i}">{lbl}</a></li>' for i,lbl in toc)+'</ol></nav>')
    facts='<div class="facts">'+''.join(f'<div class="fct"><div class="fl">{LBL[k][lang]}</div><div class="fv">{val[lang]}</div></div>' for k,val in ex['facts'])+'</div>'
    C=[]
    C.append(f'<p class="lead">{L("Tyrol is our home. We grew up under these ridges, we know which lake is still glass at six in the morning and which registry office will marry you with a mountain behind you &mdash; and that local knowledge is the whole difference between a good day and a flawless one. Austria makes eloping simple in the way that matters most: it is one of the few places in the Alps where the wedding can be both breathtaking and legally binding on the same mountain. This is our honest guide to doing it here.","Tirol ist unsere Heimat. Wir sind unter diesen Graten aufgewachsen, wir wissen, welcher See um sechs Uhr früh noch spiegelglatt ist und welches Standesamt euch mit einem Berg im Rücken traut &mdash; und genau dieses lokale Wissen ist der ganze Unterschied zwischen einem guten und einem makellosen Tag. Österreich macht ein Elopement dort einfach, wo es am meisten zählt: Es ist einer der wenigen Orte der Alpen, an dem die Hochzeit am selben Berg zugleich atemberaubend und rechtsgültig sein kann. Das ist unser ehrlicher Guide, wie ihr es hier macht.")}</p>')
    C.append(f'<div class="cap" style="margin:0 0 -14px">{t(lang,"quick_facts")}</div>{facts}')
    C.append(toc_html)

    C.append(h2('why','Why Tyrol is our home ground','Warum Tirol unser Heimspiel ist'))
    C.append(p("Every photographer says they know their region. We were born into this one. Andreas is Tyrolean, at home between Innsbruck and the Dolomites, and that means we are not arriving with a map and a rented plan &mdash; we are taking you to the meadow we hiked as teenagers and the ridge we watched the sun set from a hundred times. When the weather turns, we already know the sheltered alternative twenty minutes away. When a lake is mobbed, we know the quiet twin over the pass. That is what local really buys you: not just pretty spots, but the right one, at the right hour, whatever the day throws at you.","Jeder Fotograf sagt, er kenne seine Region. Wir sind in diese hineingeboren. Andreas ist Tiroler, zu Hause zwischen Innsbruck und den Dolomiten, und das heißt: Wir kommen nicht mit Karte und gemietetem Plan an &mdash; wir bringen euch auf die Wiese, die wir als Jugendliche erwandert haben, und auf den Grat, von dem wir hundertmal die Sonne untergehen sahen. Wenn das Wetter kippt, kennen wir die geschützte Alternative zwanzig Minuten weiter. Wenn ein See überlaufen ist, kennen wir den stillen Zwilling überm Pass. Das ist es, was ortskundig wirklich bringt: nicht bloß schöne Plätze, sondern den richtigen, zur richtigen Stunde, egal was der Tag bringt."))
    C.append(fig('06-oesterreich-kuss-vor-bergkulisse.webp',"A couple kissing before a wide Tyrolean mountain backdrop","Ein Paar küsst sich vor weiter Tiroler Bergkulisse"))

    C.append(h2('legal','The easy legal marriage','Die unkomplizierte Trauung'))
    C.append(p("Here is the single biggest reason to elope in Austria rather than over the border in Italy: you can be legally married in the mountains. In Italy a binding wedding can only take place inside a town hall, so every Dolomite ceremony is symbolic. Austria is different. A civil marriage is straightforward for foreign couples, and a number of Tyrolean registry offices will conduct the legal ceremony at an approved outdoor location &mdash; a lakeshore, a viewpoint, a mountain terrace &mdash; not only inside four walls. The act that actually changes your legal status can happen with the peaks right there.","Hier der größte einzelne Grund, in Österreich statt jenseits der Grenze in Italien zu heiraten: Ihr könnt in den Bergen rechtsgültig verheiratet werden. In Italien kann eine bindende Hochzeit nur im Rathaus stattfinden, jede Dolomiten-Zeremonie ist also symbolisch. Österreich ist anders. Eine standesamtliche Trauung ist für ausländische Paare unkompliziert, und mehrere Tiroler Standesämter vollziehen den Rechtsakt an einem genehmigten Ort im Freien &mdash; einem Seeufer, einem Aussichtspunkt, einer Bergterrasse &mdash;, nicht nur zwischen vier Wänden. Der Akt, der euren rechtlichen Status wirklich ändert, kann mit den Gipfeln direkt daneben geschehen."))
    C.append(fig('03-oesterreich-freie-trauung-tirol.webp',"A ceremony in the Tyrolean mountains","Eine Trauung in den Tiroler Bergen"))
    C.append(p("It is not automatic everywhere &mdash; each office sets its own rules, dates and lead times, and the popular summer slots go early. But the point stands: in Tyrol you do not have to choose between a real wedding and a mountain wedding. We know which offices say yes to the outdoors, we handle the appointment and the documents, and we build the day so the legal minutes and the meaningful ones sit side by side rather than in two different countries.","Es ist nicht überall automatisch &mdash; jedes Amt setzt eigene Regeln, Termine und Vorlaufzeiten, und die beliebten Sommertermine sind früh weg. Aber der Kern bleibt: In Tirol müsst ihr euch nicht zwischen einer echten Hochzeit und einer Berghochzeit entscheiden. Wir wissen, welche Ämter zum Freien Ja sagen, wir übernehmen Termin und Unterlagen und bauen den Tag so, dass die rechtlichen Minuten und die bedeutsamen nebeneinander liegen statt in zwei verschiedenen Ländern."))

    C.append(h2('ceremony','Symbolic or legal &mdash; both work beautifully','Symbolisch oder standesamtlich &mdash; beides trägt'))
    C.append(p("There are two honest paths, and neither is more romantic than the other. The first: complete the legal marriage in Austria, at the registry or an approved outdoor spot, so the day on the mountain is also the day it counts. The second, which many couples still choose for simplicity: sign the short legal act at your registry office at home, and give the mountain the ceremony that actually matters &mdash; your words, your vows, no clerk, no queue. Both carry all of the feeling. We will tell you plainly which one fits your timeline and your paperwork.","Es gibt zwei ehrliche Wege, und keiner ist romantischer als der andere. Der erste: die Trauung in Österreich rechtsgültig vollziehen, im Amt oder an einem genehmigten Ort im Freien, sodass der Tag am Berg auch der Tag ist, der zählt. Der zweite, den viele Paare der Einfachheit halber wählen: den kurzen Rechtsakt zu Hause im Standesamt unterschreiben und dem Berg die Zeremonie geben, die wirklich zählt &mdash; eure Worte, eure Gelübde, kein Beamter, keine Schlange. Beide tragen das ganze Gefühl. Wir sagen euch klar, welcher zu eurem Zeitplan und euren Papieren passt."))
    C.append(fig('05-oesterreich-geluebde-vorlesen.webp',"One partner reading their vows aloud on the mountain","Ein Partner liest die Gelübde am Berg vor"))
    C.append(fig('04-oesterreich-ringtausch.webp',"The exchange of rings with the valley falling away behind","Der Ringtausch, das Tal fällt dahinter ab"))

    C.append(h2('innsbruck','Innsbruck & the Nordkette','Innsbruck & die Nordkette'))
    C.append(p("Innsbruck is the only city in the Alps with a high mountain on its doorstep, and it is the reason so many of our Tyrolean days begin here. From the old town, the Hungerburg funicular and the Nordkette cable cars lift you to Hafelekar at 2,256&thinsp;m in about twenty minutes &mdash; coffee under the arcades, and not long after, a ridge with the whole Inn valley laid out below and the Stubai glaciers on the far horizon. It is genuine high-alpine exposure reached in the time it takes to drive across a city, which makes it perfect for couples who want scale without a climb, or a dramatic finish to a day that started at a lake.","Innsbruck ist die einzige Stadt der Alpen mit einem Hochgebirge direkt vor der Tür, und der Grund, warum so viele unserer Tiroler Tage hier beginnen. Von der Altstadt bringen euch die Hungerburgbahn und die Nordkettenbahnen in rund zwanzig Minuten aufs Hafelekar auf 2.256&thinsp;m &mdash; Kaffee unter den Lauben, und kurz darauf ein Grat mit dem ganzen Inntal darunter und den Stubaier Gletschern am fernen Horizont. Das ist echte hochalpine Ausgesetztheit, erreicht in der Zeit, die man braucht, um eine Stadt zu durchqueren &mdash; perfekt für Paare, die Dimension ohne Aufstieg wollen, oder einen dramatischen Abschluss für einen Tag, der am See begann."))
    C.append(fig('15-oesterreich-hafelekar-innsbruck.webp',"The couple on the Hafelekar ridge high above Innsbruck","Das Paar am Hafelekar-Grat hoch über Innsbruck"))
    C.append(p("A word of honesty about the light: the first cable car up the Nordkette runs well after sunrise, so a true dawn ceremony on the ridge is not on the menu unless you hike up in the dark. That is fine &mdash; the Nordkette is at its best in the clear morning after the first cabin and again in the long golden evening, and we plan around those windows so the ridge is quiet and the light is soft. For actual sunrise we take you to a lake or a valley spot instead, and save the high ridge for the hours it wears best.","Ein ehrliches Wort zum Licht: Die erste Gondel auf die Nordkette fährt deutlich nach Sonnenaufgang, eine echte Morgendämmerungs-Zeremonie am Grat steht also nicht auf der Karte, außer ihr steigt im Dunkeln auf. Das ist in Ordnung &mdash; die Nordkette ist am schönsten im klaren Morgen nach der ersten Kabine und wieder im langen goldenen Abend, und wir planen um diese Fenster, damit der Grat still und das Licht weich ist. Für den echten Sonnenaufgang bringen wir euch stattdessen an einen See oder einen Talort und heben den hohen Grat für die Stunden auf, in denen er am besten wirkt."))

    C.append(h2('lakes','The Tyrolean lakes','Die Tiroler Seen'))
    C.append(p("Tyrol keeps its lakes quieter than the famous Dolomite icons, and that is exactly their gift. Our shortlist starts with the protected Obernberger See near the Brenner, a shallow turquoise bowl ringed by larch and reachable by a gentle walk; the emerald Schlegeisspeicher deep in the Zillertal, milk-blue against grey rock; and the small, still high tarns above K&uuml;htai that most maps do not name. All of them sit close to Innsbruck yet feel a world away, and every one is calmest at first light, before the day arrives &mdash; which is precisely when we plan to be there.","Tirol hält seine Seen stiller als die berühmten Dolomiten-Ikonen, und das ist genau ihr Geschenk. Unsere Auswahl beginnt mit dem geschützten Obernberger See nahe dem Brenner, einer flachen türkisen Schale, von Lärchen umringt und über einen sanften Weg erreichbar; dem smaragdgrünen Schlegeisspeicher tief im Zillertal, milchblau vor grauem Fels; und den kleinen, stillen Hochseen über K&uuml;htai, die die meisten Karten nicht benennen. Alle liegen nah an Innsbruck und fühlen sich doch wie eine andere Welt an, und jeder ist im ersten Licht am ruhigsten, bevor der Tag kommt &mdash; genau dann planen wir, dort zu sein."))
    C.append(fig('13-oesterreich-bergsee-zeremonie.webp',"A ceremony at the edge of a still Tyrolean mountain lake","Eine Zeremonie am Ufer eines stillen Tiroler Bergsees"))
    C.append(fig('09-oesterreich-traubogen-tirol.webp',"A floral arch set beside a Tyrolean lake for the vows","Ein Blumenbogen an einem Tiroler See für das Ja-Wort"))

    C.append(h2('roads','High roads & toll roads &mdash; big scenery, little walking','Höhen- & Mautstraßen &mdash; große Kulisse, wenig Fußweg'))
    C.append(p("Some of Tyrol&rsquo;s most cinematic places are reached almost entirely by car, which is a quiet blessing on a wedding day. Two alpine toll roads open turquoise water without a hike: the Schlegeis Alpine Road in the Zillertal, roughly &euro;13 per car, climbs to the milk-blue Schlegeis reservoir; and the high roads over K&uuml;htai and the Timmelsjoch lift you well past the treeline into bare rock and long views. You step out of the car already at altitude, in a dress or a suit, with the big scenery right there &mdash; and we build the timing so you arrive as the light turns rather than when the car parks fill.","Einige der filmreifsten Orte Tirols erreicht man fast ganz mit dem Auto, ein stiller Segen an einem Hochzeitstag. Zwei alpine Mautstraßen öffnen türkises Wasser ohne Wanderung: Die Schlegeis Alpenstraße im Zillertal, rund 13&nbsp;&euro; pro Auto, steigt zum milchblauen Schlegeisspeicher; und die Höhenstraßen über K&uuml;htai und das Timmelsjoch heben euch weit über die Baumgrenze in kargen Fels und weite Blicke. Ihr steigt bereits in der Höhe aus dem Auto, in Kleid oder Anzug, die große Kulisse direkt da &mdash; und wir legen das Timing so, dass ihr ankommt, wenn das Licht dreht, nicht wenn sich die Parkplätze füllen."))

    C.append(h2('ridges','Ridges & summits, for the day that feels earned','Grate & Gipfel, für den Tag, der sich verdient anfühlt'))
    C.append(p("If you want more than a viewpoint &mdash; if you want the day to feel earned &mdash; Tyrol has ridges that reward a short, honest climb with something you will never forget. A walk up from a lift or a trailhead like the Birgitzk&ouml;pfl puts you on exposed ground with a 360-degree horizon and the two of you tiny against it, the boldest and most private frames we make. None of it needs ropes or a guide; it needs good boots, an early start and someone who has walked the route before. We scout every path in advance, carry the plan and the spare layers, and pace it so the climb is part of the adventure, not a chore.","Wollt ihr mehr als einen Aussichtspunkt &mdash; soll sich der Tag verdient anfühlen &mdash;, hat Tirol Grate, die einen kurzen, ehrlichen Aufstieg mit etwas Unvergesslichem belohnen. Ein Weg hinauf von einer Bahn oder einem Ausgangspunkt wie dem Birgitzk&ouml;pfl stellt euch auf ausgesetzten Boden mit 360-Grad-Horizont, ihr beide winzig davor &mdash; die kühnsten und privatesten Bilder, die wir machen. Nichts davon braucht Seil oder Bergführer; es braucht gute Schuhe, einen frühen Start und jemanden, der die Route vorher gegangen ist. Wir erkunden jeden Pfad vorab, tragen den Plan und die Ersatzschichten und dosieren es so, dass der Aufstieg Teil des Abenteuers ist, keine Pflicht."))
    C.append(fig('01-oesterreich-wegweiser-birgitzkoepfl.webp',"A trail signpost on the way up to the Birgitzk&ouml;pfl above Innsbruck","Ein Wegweiser auf dem Weg zum Birgitzk&ouml;pfl über Innsbruck"))
    C.append(fig('02-oesterreich-aufstieg-gruppe.webp',"The couple and their small group on the ascent","Das Paar und seine kleine Gruppe im Aufstieg"))

    C.append(h2('season','When to come','Die beste Zeit'))
    C.append(p("May through October is the dependable season: the lifts run, the high roads are open, and the meadows are green. July and August bring the warmest, most settled weather and the most people; late September is our quiet favourite, with the larches turning gold and the crowds thinning out. The shoulder weeks are a gamble worth taking &mdash; you can get fresh snow on the peaks and empty trails in a single morning, and those are often the best pictures of the year. Winter turns Tyrol spectacular and silent, but it needs a close eye on which roads and lifts stay open.","Mai bis Oktober ist die verlässliche Saison: Die Bahnen fahren, die Höhenstraßen sind offen und die Wiesen grün. Juli und August bringen das wärmste, beständigste Wetter und die meisten Menschen; der späte September ist unser stiller Favorit, mit golden werdenden Lärchen und dünner werdendem Andrang. Die Randwochen sind ein Wagnis, das sich lohnt &mdash; ihr könnt frischen Schnee auf den Gipfeln und leere Wege an einem einzigen Morgen bekommen, und das sind oft die besten Bilder des Jahres. Der Winter macht Tirol spektakulär und still, verlangt aber einen wachen Blick darauf, welche Straßen und Bahnen offen bleiben."))
    C.append(fig('08-oesterreich-abstieg-abendlicht.webp',"The couple on the descent in warm evening light","Das Paar im Abstieg im warmen Abendlicht"))

    C.append(h2('reach','Getting here & where to stay','Anreise & wo ihr wohnt'))
    C.append(p("Tyrol is one of the easiest Alpine regions to reach. Innsbruck has its own airport just minutes from the old town, and Munich and Venice are each a simple drive or train ride away, so most couples are under a mountain within an hour or two of landing. Innsbruck itself makes the ideal base &mdash; the Nordkette above you, the Zillertal and its lakes a short drive east, the high roads west, and the Dolomites two to three hours south for couples who want to fold both countries into one trip. We help you choose the base that keeps your chosen spots within an easy dawn drive and hand you a simple plan for the day.","Tirol ist eine der am leichtesten erreichbaren Alpenregionen. Innsbruck hat einen eigenen Flughafen nur Minuten von der Altstadt, und München und Venedig sind jeweils eine einfache Fahrt oder Zugverbindung entfernt, die meisten Paare stehen also ein bis zwei Stunden nach der Landung unter einem Berg. Innsbruck selbst ist die ideale Basis &mdash; die Nordkette über euch, das Zillertal und seine Seen eine kurze Fahrt östlich, die Höhenstraßen westlich, und die Dolomiten zwei bis drei Stunden südlich für Paare, die beide Länder in eine Reise fassen wollen. Wir helfen euch, die Basis zu wählen, die eure Orte in leichter Morgen-Fahrweite hält, und geben euch einen einfachen Plan für den Tag."))

    C.append(h2('finish','Light & the celebration','Licht & die Feier'))
    C.append(p("The day is not over when the vows are said. Tyrol&rsquo;s evenings are long and generous &mdash; the low sun rakes across the ridges and the whole valley goes gold, then rose, then the cool blue hour that most people miss by packing up too early. We never do. And then the celebration to match: a picnic on a warm slab of rock, a toast with the peaks going pink, a slow descent in the last light. A mountain wedding is not one perfect frame at noon; it is a whole day that keeps giving, right down to the walk home.","Der Tag ist nicht vorbei, wenn das Ja gesprochen ist. Tirols Abende sind lang und großzügig &mdash; die tiefe Sonne streift über die Grate und das ganze Tal wird golden, dann rosa, dann die kühle blaue Stunde, die die meisten verpassen, weil sie zu früh einpacken. Wir nie. Und dann die passende Feier: ein Picknick auf einer warmen Felsplatte, ein Anstoßen, während die Gipfel rosa anlaufen, ein langsamer Abstieg im letzten Licht. Eine Berghochzeit ist nicht ein perfektes Bild um die Mittagszeit; sie ist ein ganzer Tag, der weitergibt, bis hinunter zum Heimweg."))
    C.append(fig('10-oesterreich-picknick-am-berg.webp',"The couple sharing a picnic high on the mountain","Das Paar teilt ein Picknick hoch am Berg"))
    C.append(fig('07-oesterreich-anstossen-am-berg.webp',"A toast on the mountain as the peaks turn pink","Ein Anstoßen am Berg, während die Gipfel rosa werden"))
    C.append(fig('11-oesterreich-sonnenuntergang-tirol.webp',"A blazing Tyrolean sunset behind the couple","Ein glühender Tiroler Sonnenuntergang hinter dem Paar"))
    C.append(fig('12-oesterreich-paar-abendlicht.webp',"The couple in the last warm evening light","Das Paar im letzten warmen Abendlicht"))

    faq_html='<h2 id="faq" style="'+H2S+'">'+L('Eloping in Austria &mdash; FAQ','Elopement in Österreich &mdash; FAQ')+'</h2>'
    FAQL=[FQ(*x) for x in AUSTRIA_FAQ]
    faq_html+=''.join('<div style="margin:1.3em 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:1.1em">'
      f'<h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:20px;margin:0 0 .3em">{q}</h3>'
      f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2);margin:0">{a}</p></div>' for q,a in FAQL)
    faq_ld={"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
      {"@type":"Question","name":_plain(q),"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":_plain(a)}} for q,a in FAQL]}
    related=''.join(story_card(lang,P,STORYBY[sl]) for sl in ex['stories'])
    more=''.join(guide_card(lang,P,x) for x in GUIDES if x['slug']!=slug)
    body=(nav(lang,rel,'howto')+
      f'<section class="page-hero" style="padding:0">{herobg(P,HERO_IMG,g["title"][lang])}'
      f'<div class="content"><div class="wrap"><div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"guide_kick")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h1>{g["title"][lang]}</h1></div></div></section>'
      '<section><div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">'+''.join(C)+faq_html+
      f'<p style="margin-top:2.4em"><a href="{u(P,lang,"how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/")}" class="arrow-link">&larr; {T["nav"]["howto"][lang]}</a></p></div></section>'
      '<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"related_stories")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"related_stories")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{related}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="stories" style="padding-top:clamp(40px,6vw,80px)"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"more_guides")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"more_guides")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{more}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="cta"><div class="wrap row reveal"><div>'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"cta_k")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2 style="margin-top:20px">{t(lang,"cta_h")}</h2></div>'
      f'<a href="{u(P,lang,"get-in-touch/")}" class="btn light">{t(lang,"start_planning")}</a></div></section>'
      +footer(lang,rel))
    write(lang,rel,head(lang,rel,g['title'][lang]+' — Mountain Elopement',g['excerpt'][lang],ld_extra=faq_ld,pre=herolink(P,HERO_IMG))+body+scripts(P))

# ---- elopement-things-nobody-tells-you: rich guide (EN+DE; ES/IT via generic build_guides until translated) ----
# --- elopement-things-nobody-tells-you ES/IT (auto-generated, keyed by exact EN string) ---
THINGS_ES = {
  'Comfort beats everything &mdash; and it shows': 'El confort gana a todo &mdash; y se nota',
  'If you take one thing from this whole guide, take this: cold, blisters and hunger always show in the photographs. Not in an obvious way &mdash; in the set of a jaw, a hunched shoulder, a smile that does not quite reach the eyes. The couples who look luminous all day are almost always the ones who packed a second pair of real shoes for the walk, warm layers to hide under a coat, water, a snack and hand warmers. The pretty shoes go in a bag and come out for the vows. Nobody ever regretted being warm and fed on their wedding day.': 'Si os quedáis con una sola cosa de toda esta guía, que sea esta: el frío, las ampollas y el hambre siempre se ven en las fotos. No de forma obvia &mdash; en la tensión de una mandíbula, un hombro encogido, una sonrisa que no llega del todo a los ojos. Las parejas que se ven luminosas todo el día son casi siempre las que llevaron un segundo par de zapatos de verdad para caminar, capas de abrigo para esconder bajo el abrigo, agua, un snack y calientamanos. Los zapatos bonitos van en una bolsa y salen para los votos. Nadie lamentó jamás ir abrigado y bien comido el día de su boda.',
  'A partner changing into the ceremony outfit on a flat rock': 'Uno de los novios cambiándose para la ceremonia sobre una roca plana',
  'Backpacks and gear laid out at the summit before the ceremony': 'Mochilas y equipo dispuestos en la cumbre antes de la ceremonia',
  'This is also why we never rush you up a mountain. We scout the route in advance, carry the heavy things, and pace the walk so you arrive with breath to spare rather than red-faced and shaking. A little planning &mdash; the right shoes, a warm layer, a hut with a kitchen at the top &mdash; means the walk becomes part of the adventure instead of the thing you were dreading. And when you are comfortable, you forget the camera, and that is when the real pictures happen.': 'Por eso tampoco os apresuramos nunca montaña arriba. Exploramos la ruta de antemano, cargamos lo pesado y dosificamos la caminata para que lleguéis con aliento de sobra en vez de rojos y temblando. Un poco de planificación &mdash; los zapatos correctos, una capa de abrigo, un refugio con cocina arriba &mdash; convierte la caminata en parte de la aventura en vez de en lo que temíais. Y cuando estáis cómodos, os olvidáis de la cámara, y es entonces cuando ocurren las fotos de verdad.',
  'A simple hut snack &mdash; bread, cheese and a warm drink after the ceremony': 'Un sencillo tentempié de refugio &mdash; pan, queso y una bebida caliente tras la ceremonia',
  'The weather is not the enemy': 'El tiempo no es el enemigo',
  'Everyone plans for sunshine and dreads the grey. We would gently turn that around. Some of the most beautiful, most emotional pictures we have ever taken came out of rain, mist and wind &mdash; cloud pouring over a ridge, a veil caught mid-gust, two people laughing under a shared umbrella because there is nothing else to do. Bad weather strips a day down to what actually matters: the two of you, close, a little defiant, entirely present. We come prepared with clear umbrellas and dry cloths, and we are not afraid of a moody sky. Neither should you be.': 'Todos planean para el sol y temen el gris. Nosotros lo daríamos suavemente la vuelta. Algunas de las fotos más bellas y emotivas que hemos hecho salieron de la lluvia, la niebla y el viento &mdash; nubes vertiéndose sobre una cresta, un velo atrapado en una ráfaga, dos personas riendo bajo un paraguas compartido porque no hay otra cosa que hacer. El mal tiempo reduce el día a lo que de verdad importa: vosotros dos, juntos, un poco desafiantes, del todo presentes. Venimos preparados con paraguas transparentes y paños secos, y no tememos un cielo dramático. Vosotros tampoco deberíais.',
  'The couple under an umbrella on a jetty in the rain': 'La pareja bajo un paraguas en un embarcadero bajo la lluvia',
  'A bride in a dirndl smiling through mountain rain': 'Una novia en dirndl sonriendo bajo la lluvia de montaña',
  'Wind is its own character. It lifts a veil and a dress into something alive, and a meadow in a stiff breeze photographs like a painting &mdash; but it is cold, and it steals words, so we pick sheltered spots for the vows and let the exposed ridges be for the portraits. The honest rule is this: we never cancel for weather, we move around it. A backup day, built into the bigger packages, means we can wait out a storm or chase a clearing. The forecast is a suggestion, not a verdict, and the mountain rarely reads it anyway.': 'El viento es un personaje propio. Levanta un velo y un vestido hasta volverlos algo vivo, y un prado con brisa firme se fotografía como una pintura &mdash; pero es frío y roba las palabras, así que elegimos lugares resguardados para los votos y dejamos las crestas expuestas para los retratos. La regla honesta es esta: nunca cancelamos por el tiempo, lo sorteamos. Un día de reserva, incluido en los paquetes más grandes, significa que podemos esperar a que pase una tormenta o perseguir un claro. El pronóstico es una sugerencia, no un veredicto, y la montaña rara vez lo lee de todos modos.',
  'Dress and veil caught by the wind on an open meadow': 'Vestido y velo atrapados por el viento en un prado abierto',
  'The early-start truth': 'La verdad sobre el comienzo temprano',
  'Nobody warns you quite how early a sunrise elopement begins. Hair and make-up can start at three or four in the morning; the walk up is often in the dark, by headlamp, with the valley asleep below you. It sounds punishing, and for about twenty minutes it is. Then the sky starts to move, you reach the spot, and the whole world is yours alone &mdash; no day-trippers, no queue at the viewpoint, just the first light climbing the rock while you say your words. By the time everyone else arrives, you are already coming down for breakfast, married.': 'Nadie os advierte lo temprano que empieza un elopement al amanecer. El peinado y el maquillaje pueden empezar a las tres o las cuatro de la mañana; la subida es a menudo a oscuras, con frontal, con el valle dormido abajo. Suena penoso, y durante unos veinte minutos lo es. Luego el cielo empieza a moverse, llegáis al lugar y el mundo entero es solo vuestro &mdash; sin excursionistas, sin cola en el mirador, solo la primera luz trepando por la roca mientras decís vuestras palabras. Para cuando llegan los demás, ya bajáis a desayunar, casados.',
  'Getting ready by lamplight at three in the morning': 'Preparándose a la luz de una lámpara a las tres de la mañana',
  'The couple climbing by headlamp before dawn': 'La pareja subiendo con frontal antes del amanecer',
  'We carry the whole logistics of it so you do not have to think: the wake-up call, the timing worked backwards from the sunrise minute, the route we have already walked in daylight, spare layers for the cold hour before the sun. All you do is trust the alarm and turn up sleepy. And if none of that appeals &mdash; if you would rather a long lie-in and a glass of something at golden hour &mdash; a sunset elopement gives you the same empty, glowing light at a far more civilised time of day. There is no wrong answer, only the one that fits you.': 'Cargamos toda la logística para que no tengáis que pensar: la llamada de despertar, el horario calculado hacia atrás desde el minuto del amanecer, la ruta que ya hemos caminado de día, capas de repuesto para la hora fría antes del sol. Solo tenéis que fiaros del despertador y aparecer somnolientos. Y si nada de eso os atrae &mdash; si preferís dormir a gusto y una copa de algo a la hora dorada &mdash;, un elopement al atardecer os da la misma luz vacía y luminosa a una hora del día mucho más civilizada. No hay respuesta equivocada, solo la que encaja con vosotros.',
  'Protecting the moment': 'Proteger el momento',
  'Here is a small one that matters more than it sounds: write your vows in advance, and bring a printed copy. Phone screens die in the cold at exactly the wrong moment, and reading from paper you can actually hold, with shaking happy hands, is part of the memory anyway. Then guard the day a little. Do not post the exact location or the plan; silence the phones for the ceremony; ask any guests to stay present rather than filming. The fewer things pulling at your attention, the more the day belongs to you.': 'Una cosa pequeña que importa más de lo que suena: escribid vuestros votos de antemano y llevad una copia impresa. Las pantallas del móvil mueren con el frío justo en el peor momento, y leer de un papel que podéis sostener de verdad, con manos temblorosas de felicidad, es parte del recuerdo de todos modos. Luego proteged un poco el día. No publiquéis el lugar exacto ni el plan; silenciad los móviles para la ceremonia; pedid a los invitados que estén presentes en vez de grabar. Cuantas menos cosas tiren de vuestra atención, más os pertenece el día.',
  'The other half of protecting the moment is time. So many days feel rushed not because there was too little of it, but because nobody left any margin. We plan generous buffers into every hour &mdash; time to breathe on the ridge, time to fix a windblown strand of hair, time to just stand there and realise it happened. When a schedule has slack in it, the small disasters stop being disasters: a late cable car, a wrong turn, a sudden shower become footnotes instead of catastrophes. Space in the plan is the quiet luxury nobody tells you to ask for.': 'La otra mitad de proteger el momento es el tiempo. Tantos días se sienten apresurados no porque hubiera demasiado poco, sino porque nadie dejó margen. Planeamos generosos colchones en cada hora &mdash; tiempo para respirar en la cresta, tiempo para arreglar un mechón despeinado por el viento, tiempo para simplemente estar ahí y darse cuenta de que ocurrió. Cuando un horario tiene holgura, los pequeños desastres dejan de serlo: un teleférico perdido, un giro equivocado, un chubasco repentino se vuelven notas al pie en vez de catástrofes. El espacio en el plan es el lujo silencioso que nadie os dice que pidáis.',
  'The practical things nobody says': 'Las cosas prácticas que nadie dice',
  'A handful of unglamorous facts that save real headaches. Carry some cash &mdash; a few of the toll roads and car parks, the Tre Cime road and the Braies parking among them, are smoother with it, and some hut kitchens still prefer it. Check the last cable car down before you commit to a sunset up high, because being stranded at altitude in the dark is a story you do not want. Remember that Lago di Braies closes to traffic from mid-morning in summer, so we shoot it before or after that window. And pack one warm layer even in August: a summit at first light is genuinely cold, whatever the valley thermometer says.': 'Un puñado de datos poco glamurosos que ahorran verdaderos dolores de cabeza. Llevad algo de efectivo &mdash; algunas de las carreteras de peaje y aparcamientos, la carretera de las Tre Cime y el parking de Braies entre ellos, van más suaves con él, y algunas cocinas de refugio aún lo prefieren. Comprobad el último teleférico de bajada antes de comprometeros con un atardecer allá arriba, porque quedarse varado en altura y a oscuras es una historia que no queréis. Recordad que el Lago di Braies cierra al tráfico desde media mañana en verano, así que lo fotografiamos antes o después de esa ventana. Y meted una capa de abrigo incluso en agosto: una cumbre con la primera luz es de verdad fría, diga lo que diga el termómetro del valle.',
  'A skier passing in the background during a winter mountain ceremony': 'Un esquiador pasando al fondo durante una ceremonia de montaña en invierno',
  'And here is one nobody mentions at all: you are rarely the only people on the mountain. A hiker will wander through the background, a skier will cross the slope behind you, a cable car will hum overhead. It is not a problem &mdash; it is honest, and we know how to work with it: the right angle, the right minute, the quiet corner five steps off the main path. Part of what you are paying for is someone who knows exactly when the viewpoint empties and how to give you privacy in a public place. The mountain is shared; your moment does not have to feel like it.': 'Y aquí va una que nadie menciona en absoluto: rara vez sois los únicos en la montaña. Un excursionista cruzará el fondo, un esquiador atravesará la ladera tras vosotros, un teleférico zumbará por encima. No es un problema &mdash; es honesto, y sabemos cómo trabajar con ello: el ángulo correcto, el minuto correcto, el rincón tranquilo a cinco pasos del sendero principal. Parte de lo que pagáis es a alguien que sabe exactamente cuándo se vacía el mirador y cómo daros intimidad en un lugar público. La montaña es compartida; vuestro momento no tiene por qué sentirse así.',
  'The small print that saves you money': 'El pequeño detalle que os ahorra dinero',
  'A few early decisions quietly lower the bill. Book the mountain hut and, if you are marrying legally in Austria, the registrar months ahead &mdash; both are limited in summer and both get more expensive the later you leave them. Consider the shoulder season: late May and October are cheaper, far quieter and often more beautiful than high summer, with golden larches or a dusting of fresh snow on the peaks. And you rarely need both a toll road and a cable car on the same day &mdash; picking one keeps the budget and the schedule simple. We map all of this out with you so the money goes where it matters.': 'Unas pocas decisiones tempranas bajan la factura en silencio. Reservad el refugio de montaña y, si os casáis legalmente en Austria, al oficiante con meses de antelación &mdash; ambos son limitados en verano y ambos se encarecen cuanto más lo dejéis. Considerad la temporada baja: finales de mayo y octubre son más baratos, mucho más tranquilos y a menudo más bellos que el pleno verano, con alerces dorados o una capa de nieve fresca en las cumbres. Y rara vez necesitáis carretera de peaje y teleférico el mismo día &mdash; elegir uno mantiene el presupuesto y el horario simples. Trazamos todo esto con vosotros para que el dinero vaya donde importa.',
  'Build a real celebration into the day': 'Meted una verdadera celebración en el día',
  'An elopement is not a wedding with the joy removed &mdash; it is a wedding with the noise removed. So give the day something to celebrate with. Some of our favourite afternoons have ended with a portable pizza oven fired up on a mountain meadow, a bottle of something cold and shaken loose, a hut table groaning with local food. The vows are the heart of it, but the hours after are where the day loosens and becomes yours: the toast, the laughter, the meal with the peaks going pink. Plan for it. A celebration of two people is still a celebration.': 'Un elopement no es una boda a la que se le ha quitado la alegría &mdash; es una boda a la que se le ha quitado el ruido. Así que dad al día algo con que celebrar. Algunas de nuestras tardes favoritas terminaron con un horno de pizza portátil encendido en un prado de montaña, una botella de algo frío y bien agitado, una mesa de refugio repleta de comida local. Los votos son el corazón, pero las horas de después son donde el día se suelta y se vuelve vuestro: el brindis, las risas, la comida con las cumbres tornándose rosas. Planeadlo. Una celebración de dos personas sigue siendo una celebración.',
  'Setting up a portable pizza oven on a mountain meadow': 'Montando un horno de pizza portátil en un prado de montaña',
  'Fresh pizza straight from the oven at the celebration': 'Pizza recién salida del horno en la celebración',
  'A spray of champagne to celebrate on the mountain': 'Un chorro de champán para celebrar en la montaña',
  'Say yes to the odd idea': 'Decid sí a la idea rara',
  'The pictures couples treasure most are almost never the safe ones. They are the bride clicking into skis in her wedding dress, the groom sledging down a slope in his suit, the pair wading into a cold lake because the light was too good to resist. If you have a slightly ridiculous idea &mdash; a thing you have always secretly wanted to do &mdash; tell us. Nine times out of ten we can make it safe and make it happen, and it becomes the frame you hang on the wall and the story you tell for the rest of your lives. The mountain gives you permission to be a little wild.': 'Las fotos que las parejas más atesoran casi nunca son las seguras. Son la novia calzándose los esquís con su vestido de boda, el novio bajando una ladera en trineo con su traje, la pareja metiéndose en un lago frío porque la luz era demasiado buena para resistirse. Si tenéis una idea algo ridícula &mdash; algo que siempre quisisteis hacer en secreto &mdash;, decídnoslo. Nueve de cada diez veces podemos hacerlo seguro y hacerlo realidad, y se convierte en el cuadro que colgáis en la pared y la historia que contáis el resto de vuestras vidas. La montaña os da permiso para ser un poco salvajes.',
  'The bride on skis in her wedding dress': 'La novia sobre esquís con su vestido de boda',
  'The groom sledging down a slope in his suit': 'El novio bajando una ladera en trineo con su traje',
  'The one thing to remember': 'Lo único que recordar',
  'If you forget everything else on this page, keep this. It is your day, not a photo shoot. Every tip here &mdash; the snacks, the buffer time, the printed vows, the backup day &mdash; exists for one reason: to clear the small worries out of the way so you can simply be together. The best images we have ever made came in the moments the couple forgot we were there at all: a private joke on a ridge, a held breath before the vows, a quiet hand on a cold cheek. Plan well, then let go. We will take care of the rest.': 'Si olvidáis todo lo demás de esta página, quedaos con esto. Es vuestro día, no una sesión de fotos. Cada consejo aquí &mdash; los snacks, el tiempo de margen, los votos impresos, el día de reserva &mdash; existe por una razón: quitar de en medio las pequeñas preocupaciones para que podáis simplemente estar juntos. Las mejores fotos que hemos hecho llegaron en los momentos en que la pareja olvidó que estábamos allí: un chiste privado en una cresta, un aliento contenido antes de los votos, una mano quieta sobre una mejilla fría. Planead bien, luego soltad. Del resto nos encargamos nosotros.',
  'Comfort beats everything': 'El confort gana a todo',
  'The practical things': 'Las cosas prácticas',
  'The small print that saves money': 'El pequeño detalle que ahorra dinero',
  'Build in a celebration': 'Meted una celebración',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'What nobody tells you &mdash; FAQ': 'Lo que nadie te cuenta &mdash; preguntas frecuentes',
  'The big decisions &mdash; where, when, what it costs &mdash; are the easy part. It is the small, unglamorous details that quietly make or break a mountain wedding day, and no checklist ever mentions them. After years of eloping couples in the Alps, in rain and wind and three-in-the-morning darkness, these are the things we wish someone had told us first. None of it is scary. All of it is the difference between a day you endure and a day you never stop talking about.': 'Las grandes decisiones &mdash; dónde, cuándo, cuánto cuesta &mdash; son la parte fácil. Son los pequeños detalles poco glamurosos los que en silencio hacen o deshacen un día de boda en la montaña, y ninguna checklist los menciona. Tras años acompañando a parejas en los Alpes, bajo lluvia y viento y la oscuridad de las tres de la mañana, estas son las cosas que ojalá alguien nos hubiera contado primero. Nada de esto da miedo. Todo esto es la diferencia entre un día que soportáis y un día del que nunca dejáis de hablar.',
  'On this page': 'En esta página',
}
THINGS_IT = {
  'Comfort beats everything &mdash; and it shows': 'Il comfort batte tutto &mdash; e si vede',
  'If you take one thing from this whole guide, take this: cold, blisters and hunger always show in the photographs. Not in an obvious way &mdash; in the set of a jaw, a hunched shoulder, a smile that does not quite reach the eyes. The couples who look luminous all day are almost always the ones who packed a second pair of real shoes for the walk, warm layers to hide under a coat, water, a snack and hand warmers. The pretty shoes go in a bag and come out for the vows. Nobody ever regretted being warm and fed on their wedding day.': 'Se di tutta questa guida tenete una cosa sola, tenete questa: freddo, vesciche e fame si vedono sempre nelle foto. Non in modo ovvio &mdash; nella tensione di una mascella, una spalla incassata, un sorriso che non arriva del tutto agli occhi. Le coppie che appaiono luminose tutto il giorno sono quasi sempre quelle che hanno portato un secondo paio di scarpe vere per il cammino, strati caldi da nascondere sotto il cappotto, acqua, uno spuntino e scaldamani. Le scarpe belle vanno in una borsa ed escono per le promesse. Nessuno ha mai rimpianto di essere stato al caldo e sazio il giorno del proprio matrimonio.',
  'A partner changing into the ceremony outfit on a flat rock': 'Uno dei due che si cambia per la cerimonia su una roccia piatta',
  'Backpacks and gear laid out at the summit before the ceremony': 'Zaini e attrezzatura disposti in vetta prima della cerimonia',
  'This is also why we never rush you up a mountain. We scout the route in advance, carry the heavy things, and pace the walk so you arrive with breath to spare rather than red-faced and shaking. A little planning &mdash; the right shoes, a warm layer, a hut with a kitchen at the top &mdash; means the walk becomes part of the adventure instead of the thing you were dreading. And when you are comfortable, you forget the camera, and that is when the real pictures happen.': "È anche il motivo per cui non vi mettiamo mai fretta su per una montagna. Perlustriamo il percorso in anticipo, portiamo le cose pesanti e dosiamo la camminata così che arriviate con fiato d'avanzo invece che rossi e tremanti. Un po' di pianificazione &mdash; le scarpe giuste, uno strato caldo, un rifugio con cucina in cima &mdash; trasforma la camminata in parte dell'avventura invece che nella cosa che temevate. E quando siete a vostro agio, dimenticate la macchina fotografica, ed è allora che nascono le foto vere.",
  'A simple hut snack &mdash; bread, cheese and a warm drink after the ceremony': 'Una semplice merenda in rifugio &mdash; pane, formaggio e una bevanda calda dopo la cerimonia',
  'The weather is not the enemy': 'Il tempo non è il nemico',
  'Everyone plans for sunshine and dreads the grey. We would gently turn that around. Some of the most beautiful, most emotional pictures we have ever taken came out of rain, mist and wind &mdash; cloud pouring over a ridge, a veil caught mid-gust, two people laughing under a shared umbrella because there is nothing else to do. Bad weather strips a day down to what actually matters: the two of you, close, a little defiant, entirely present. We come prepared with clear umbrellas and dry cloths, and we are not afraid of a moody sky. Neither should you be.': "Tutti pianificano per il sole e temono il grigio. Noi lo ribalteremmo con delicatezza. Alcune delle foto più belle e più emozionanti che abbiamo mai scattato sono nate da pioggia, nebbia e vento &mdash; nuvole che si rovesciano su una cresta, un velo colto in una raffica, due persone che ridono sotto un ombrello condiviso perché non c'è altro da fare. Il brutto tempo riduce una giornata a ciò che conta davvero: voi due, vicini, un po' ostinati, del tutto presenti. Veniamo preparati con ombrelli trasparenti e panni asciutti, e non temiamo un cielo drammatico. Non dovreste temerlo neanche voi.",
  'The couple under an umbrella on a jetty in the rain': 'La coppia sotto un ombrello su un pontile sotto la pioggia',
  'A bride in a dirndl smiling through mountain rain': 'Una sposa in dirndl che sorride sotto la pioggia di montagna',
  'Wind is its own character. It lifts a veil and a dress into something alive, and a meadow in a stiff breeze photographs like a painting &mdash; but it is cold, and it steals words, so we pick sheltered spots for the vows and let the exposed ridges be for the portraits. The honest rule is this: we never cancel for weather, we move around it. A backup day, built into the bigger packages, means we can wait out a storm or chase a clearing. The forecast is a suggestion, not a verdict, and the mountain rarely reads it anyway.': 'Il vento è un personaggio a sé. Solleva un velo e un abito fino a renderli qualcosa di vivo, e un prato in una brezza decisa si fotografa come un dipinto &mdash; ma è freddo e ruba le parole, quindi scegliamo luoghi riparati per le promesse e lasciamo le creste esposte ai ritratti. La regola onesta è questa: non annulliamo mai per il tempo, gli giriamo intorno. Un giorno di riserva, incluso nei pacchetti più grandi, significa che possiamo aspettare che passi un temporale o inseguire uno schiarita. Le previsioni sono un suggerimento, non un verdetto, e la montagna raramente le legge comunque.',
  'Dress and veil caught by the wind on an open meadow': 'Abito e velo colti dal vento su un prato aperto',
  'The early-start truth': "La verità sulla partenza all'alba",
  'Nobody warns you quite how early a sunrise elopement begins. Hair and make-up can start at three or four in the morning; the walk up is often in the dark, by headlamp, with the valley asleep below you. It sounds punishing, and for about twenty minutes it is. Then the sky starts to move, you reach the spot, and the whole world is yours alone &mdash; no day-trippers, no queue at the viewpoint, just the first light climbing the rock while you say your words. By the time everyone else arrives, you are already coming down for breakfast, married.': "Nessuno vi avverte di quanto presto inizi un elopement all'alba. Trucco e acconciatura possono iniziare alle tre o alle quattro del mattino; la salita è spesso al buio, con la frontale, con la valle addormentata sotto di voi. Sembra durissimo, e per una ventina di minuti lo è. Poi il cielo comincia a muoversi, raggiungete il punto e il mondo intero è solo vostro &mdash; niente escursionisti, niente coda al punto panoramico, solo la prima luce che sale sulla roccia mentre dite le vostre parole. Quando arrivano tutti gli altri, state già scendendo per la colazione, sposati.",
  'Getting ready by lamplight at three in the morning': 'Prepararsi alla luce di una lampada alle tre del mattino',
  'The couple climbing by headlamp before dawn': "La coppia che sale con la frontale prima dell'alba",
  'We carry the whole logistics of it so you do not have to think: the wake-up call, the timing worked backwards from the sunrise minute, the route we have already walked in daylight, spare layers for the cold hour before the sun. All you do is trust the alarm and turn up sleepy. And if none of that appeals &mdash; if you would rather a long lie-in and a glass of something at golden hour &mdash; a sunset elopement gives you the same empty, glowing light at a far more civilised time of day. There is no wrong answer, only the one that fits you.': "Ci portiamo dietro tutta la logistica così che voi non dobbiate pensarci: la sveglia, i tempi calcolati a ritroso dal minuto dell'alba, il percorso che abbiamo già camminato di giorno, strati di scorta per l'ora fredda prima del sole. Voi dovete solo fidarvi della sveglia e presentarvi assonnati. E se niente di tutto ciò vi attira &mdash; se preferite una bella dormita e un bicchiere di qualcosa all'ora dorata &mdash;, un elopement al tramonto vi dà la stessa luce vuota e luminosa a un'ora del giorno molto più civile. Non c'è risposta sbagliata, solo quella che si adatta a voi.",
  'Protecting the moment': 'Proteggere il momento',
  'Here is a small one that matters more than it sounds: write your vows in advance, and bring a printed copy. Phone screens die in the cold at exactly the wrong moment, and reading from paper you can actually hold, with shaking happy hands, is part of the memory anyway. Then guard the day a little. Do not post the exact location or the plan; silence the phones for the ceremony; ask any guests to stay present rather than filming. The fewer things pulling at your attention, the more the day belongs to you.': "Una piccola cosa che conta più di quanto sembri: scrivete le promesse in anticipo e portatene una copia stampata. Gli schermi dei telefoni muoiono al freddo proprio nel momento peggiore, e leggere da un foglio che potete davvero tenere in mano, con mani tremanti di felicità, è comunque parte del ricordo. Poi proteggete un po' la giornata. Non pubblicate il punto esatto o il programma; silenziate i telefoni per la cerimonia; chiedete agli invitati di essere presenti invece di filmare. Meno cose tirano la vostra attenzione, più la giornata appartiene a voi.",
  'The other half of protecting the moment is time. So many days feel rushed not because there was too little of it, but because nobody left any margin. We plan generous buffers into every hour &mdash; time to breathe on the ridge, time to fix a windblown strand of hair, time to just stand there and realise it happened. When a schedule has slack in it, the small disasters stop being disasters: a late cable car, a wrong turn, a sudden shower become footnotes instead of catastrophes. Space in the plan is the quiet luxury nobody tells you to ask for.': "L'altra metà del proteggere il momento è il tempo. Tante giornate sembrano di fretta non perché ce ne fosse troppo poco, ma perché nessuno ha lasciato margine. Pianifichiamo generosi cuscinetti in ogni ora &mdash; tempo per respirare sulla cresta, tempo per sistemare una ciocca scompigliata dal vento, tempo per stare semplicemente lì e rendersi conto che è successo. Quando un programma ha gioco, i piccoli disastri smettono di esserlo: una funivia persa, una svolta sbagliata, un acquazzone improvviso diventano note a piè di pagina invece che catastrofi. Lo spazio nel piano è il lusso silenzioso che nessuno vi dice di chiedere.",
  'The practical things nobody says': 'Le cose pratiche che nessuno dice',
  'A handful of unglamorous facts that save real headaches. Carry some cash &mdash; a few of the toll roads and car parks, the Tre Cime road and the Braies parking among them, are smoother with it, and some hut kitchens still prefer it. Check the last cable car down before you commit to a sunset up high, because being stranded at altitude in the dark is a story you do not want. Remember that Lago di Braies closes to traffic from mid-morning in summer, so we shoot it before or after that window. And pack one warm layer even in August: a summit at first light is genuinely cold, whatever the valley thermometer says.': "Una manciata di fatti poco glamour che risparmiano veri grattacapi. Portate un po' di contanti &mdash; alcune strade a pedaggio e parcheggi, la strada delle Tre Cime e il parcheggio di Braies tra questi, sono più comodi con essi, e alcune cucine dei rifugi li preferiscono ancora. Controllate l'ultima funivia in discesa prima di puntare su un tramonto lassù, perché restare bloccati in quota al buio è una storia che non volete. Ricordate che il Lago di Braies chiude al traffico da metà mattina in estate, quindi lo fotografiamo prima o dopo quella finestra. E mettete in valigia uno strato caldo anche ad agosto: una vetta alla prima luce è davvero fredda, qualunque cosa dica il termometro a valle.",
  'A skier passing in the background during a winter mountain ceremony': 'Uno sciatore che passa sullo sfondo durante una cerimonia di montagna in inverno',
  'And here is one nobody mentions at all: you are rarely the only people on the mountain. A hiker will wander through the background, a skier will cross the slope behind you, a cable car will hum overhead. It is not a problem &mdash; it is honest, and we know how to work with it: the right angle, the right minute, the quiet corner five steps off the main path. Part of what you are paying for is someone who knows exactly when the viewpoint empties and how to give you privacy in a public place. The mountain is shared; your moment does not have to feel like it.': "Ed eccone una che nessuno menziona affatto: raramente siete gli unici sulla montagna. Un escursionista attraverserà lo sfondo, uno sciatore taglierà il pendio dietro di voi, una funivia ronzerà sopra. Non è un problema &mdash; è onesto, e sappiamo come lavorarci: l'angolo giusto, il minuto giusto, l'angolo tranquillo a cinque passi dal sentiero principale. Parte di ciò che pagate è qualcuno che sa esattamente quando il punto panoramico si svuota e come darvi intimità in un luogo pubblico. La montagna è condivisa; il vostro momento non deve sembrarlo.",
  'The small print that saves you money': 'Le clausole che vi fanno risparmiare',
  'A few early decisions quietly lower the bill. Book the mountain hut and, if you are marrying legally in Austria, the registrar months ahead &mdash; both are limited in summer and both get more expensive the later you leave them. Consider the shoulder season: late May and October are cheaper, far quieter and often more beautiful than high summer, with golden larches or a dusting of fresh snow on the peaks. And you rarely need both a toll road and a cable car on the same day &mdash; picking one keeps the budget and the schedule simple. We map all of this out with you so the money goes where it matters.': "Poche decisioni anticipate abbassano il conto in silenzio. Prenotate il rifugio e, se vi sposate legalmente in Austria, l'ufficiale di stato civile con mesi di anticipo &mdash; entrambi sono limitati in estate ed entrambi rincarano quanto più tardi ci pensate. Considerate la bassa stagione: fine maggio e ottobre sono più economici, molto più tranquilli e spesso più belli del pieno estate, con larici dorati o una spolverata di neve fresca sulle cime. E raramente servono strada a pedaggio e funivia lo stesso giorno &mdash; sceglierne una mantiene semplici budget e programma. Mappiamo tutto questo con voi così che il denaro vada dove conta.",
  'Build a real celebration into the day': 'Inserite una vera festa nella giornata',
  'An elopement is not a wedding with the joy removed &mdash; it is a wedding with the noise removed. So give the day something to celebrate with. Some of our favourite afternoons have ended with a portable pizza oven fired up on a mountain meadow, a bottle of something cold and shaken loose, a hut table groaning with local food. The vows are the heart of it, but the hours after are where the day loosens and becomes yours: the toast, the laughter, the meal with the peaks going pink. Plan for it. A celebration of two people is still a celebration.': 'Un elopement non è un matrimonio a cui è stata tolta la gioia &mdash; è un matrimonio a cui è stato tolto il rumore. Date quindi alla giornata qualcosa con cui festeggiare. Alcuni dei nostri pomeriggi preferiti si sono chiusi con un forno per pizza portatile acceso su un prato di montagna, una bottiglia di qualcosa di freddo e ben agitato, un tavolo di rifugio carico di cibo locale. Le promesse sono il cuore, ma le ore dopo sono dove la giornata si scioglie e diventa vostra: il brindisi, le risate, il pasto con le cime che si tingono di rosa. Pianificatelo. Una festa di due persone è pur sempre una festa.',
  'Setting up a portable pizza oven on a mountain meadow': 'Montaggio di un forno per pizza portatile su un prato di montagna',
  'Fresh pizza straight from the oven at the celebration': 'Pizza appena sfornata alla festa',
  'A spray of champagne to celebrate on the mountain': 'Uno spruzzo di champagne per festeggiare in montagna',
  'Say yes to the odd idea': "Dite sì all'idea strampalata",
  'The pictures couples treasure most are almost never the safe ones. They are the bride clicking into skis in her wedding dress, the groom sledging down a slope in his suit, the pair wading into a cold lake because the light was too good to resist. If you have a slightly ridiculous idea &mdash; a thing you have always secretly wanted to do &mdash; tell us. Nine times out of ten we can make it safe and make it happen, and it becomes the frame you hang on the wall and the story you tell for the rest of your lives. The mountain gives you permission to be a little wild.': "Le foto che le coppie custodiscono di più non sono quasi mai quelle sicure. Sono la sposa che si aggancia gli sci nel suo abito da sposa, lo sposo che scende un pendio in slittino nel suo completo, i due che entrano in un lago freddo perché la luce era troppo bella per resistere. Se avete un'idea un po' ridicola &mdash; una cosa che avete sempre segretamente voluto fare &mdash;, ditecelo. Nove volte su dieci possiamo renderla sicura e realizzarla, e diventa il quadro che appendete alla parete e la storia che raccontate per il resto della vita. La montagna vi dà il permesso di essere un po' selvaggi.",
  'The bride on skis in her wedding dress': 'La sposa sugli sci nel suo abito da sposa',
  'The groom sledging down a slope in his suit': 'Lo sposo che scende un pendio in slittino nel suo completo',
  'The one thing to remember': "L'unica cosa da ricordare",
  'If you forget everything else on this page, keep this. It is your day, not a photo shoot. Every tip here &mdash; the snacks, the buffer time, the printed vows, the backup day &mdash; exists for one reason: to clear the small worries out of the way so you can simply be together. The best images we have ever made came in the moments the couple forgot we were there at all: a private joke on a ridge, a held breath before the vows, a quiet hand on a cold cheek. Plan well, then let go. We will take care of the rest.': 'Se dimenticate tutto il resto di questa pagina, tenete questo. È la vostra giornata, non un servizio fotografico. Ogni consiglio qui &mdash; gli spuntini, il tempo di margine, le promesse stampate, il giorno di riserva &mdash; esiste per una ragione: togliere di mezzo le piccole preoccupazioni così che possiate semplicemente stare insieme. Le foto migliori che abbiamo mai fatto sono arrivate nei momenti in cui la coppia dimenticava del tutto che eravamo lì: una battuta privata su una cresta, un respiro trattenuto prima delle promesse, una mano quieta su una guancia fredda. Pianificate bene, poi lasciate andare. Al resto pensiamo noi.',
  'Comfort beats everything': 'Il comfort batte tutto',
  'The practical things': 'Le cose pratiche',
  'The small print that saves money': 'Le clausole che fanno risparmiare',
  'Build in a celebration': 'Inserite una festa',
  'FAQ': 'FAQ',
  'What nobody tells you &mdash; FAQ': 'Ciò che nessuno vi dice &mdash; domande frequenti',
  'The big decisions &mdash; where, when, what it costs &mdash; are the easy part. It is the small, unglamorous details that quietly make or break a mountain wedding day, and no checklist ever mentions them. After years of eloping couples in the Alps, in rain and wind and three-in-the-morning darkness, these are the things we wish someone had told us first. None of it is scary. All of it is the difference between a day you endure and a day you never stop talking about.': 'Le grandi decisioni &mdash; dove, quando, quanto costa &mdash; sono la parte facile. Sono i piccoli dettagli poco glamour a far riuscire o fallire in silenzio una giornata di matrimonio in montagna, e nessuna checklist li nomina. Dopo anni ad accompagnare coppie sulle Alpi, sotto pioggia e vento e il buio delle tre del mattino, queste sono le cose che avremmo voluto che qualcuno ci dicesse per primo. Niente di tutto ciò fa paura. Tutto ciò è la differenza tra una giornata che sopportate e una di cui non smettete mai di parlare.',
  'On this page': 'In questa pagina',
}
THINGS_FAQ_ES = {
  'What happens if it rains on our elopement day?': ('¿Qué pasa si llueve el día de nuestro elopement?', '¿Sinceramente? Puede ser lo mejor que ocurra. Algunas de nuestras fotos favoritas salen de cielos grises y lluvia &mdash; niebla derramándose por las crestas, un paraguas compartido, gotas sobre un velo, colores hondos y con carácter. Venimos preparados con paraguas transparentes y paños secos, y dejamos margen, normalmente un día entero de reserva en los paquetes más grandes, para que el tiempo nunca imponga el día. Vigilamos el pronóstico hora a hora y os movemos a la ventana que funciona. Una montaña que desaparece en la nube no es un día arruinado; es otro, más tranquilo y a menudo más bello.'),
  'Is a sunrise start really as early as it sounds?': ('¿Un comienzo al amanecer es de verdad tan temprano como suena?', 'Sí &mdash; y vale cada minuto. Una verdadera ceremonia al alba puede significar peinado y maquillaje a las tres o las cuatro de la mañana y subir a oscuras con frontal. Suena brutal y se siente como magia: tenéis los lugares más famosos enteramente para vosotros, la primera luz es irrepetible, y para cuando llegan los excursionistas ya estáis desayunando. Nosotros nos ocupamos de la logística &mdash; el despertar, los tiempos, la ruta a oscuras &mdash; para que solo tengáis que apareceros somnolientos e iros asombrados. ¿No sois de mañanas? Planeamos un atardecer.'),
  'What should we actually bring?': ('¿Qué deberíamos llevar de verdad?', 'Menos glamour y más confort de lo que pensáis. Imprimid vuestros votos &mdash; las pantallas del móvil mueren con el frío en el peor momento. Llevad capas de abrigo que podáis esconder bajo el abrigo, un segundo par de zapatos de verdad para caminar con los bonitos en una bolsa, snacks, agua y calientamanos. Llevad algo de efectivo: algunas carreteras de peaje, aparcamientos e incluso cocinas de refugio van más fáciles con él. El frío, las ampollas y el hambre siempre se ven en las fotos y en cómo os sentís &mdash; el equipo pequeño y poco glamuroso es lo que mantiene el día suave.'),
  'Are there hidden costs and permits we should know about?': ('¿Hay costes ocultos y permisos que deberíamos conocer?', 'Unos pocos pequeños, y los gestionamos todos por vosotros. Algunos lugares necesitan permiso de fotografía o ceremonia; la carretera de peaje de las Tre Cime cuesta unos 30&ndash;45&nbsp;&euro; por coche; el Lago di Braies tiene parking de pago y una ventana de acceso estival; los billetes de teleférico y una noche en un refugio también suman. Nada de esto es caro por sí solo &mdash; solo necesita a alguien que lo planee para que nada os sorprenda el día. Ese es nuestro trabajo: las reservas, los tiempos, los billetes y el efectivo que querréis en el bolsillo, todo resuelto de antemano.'),
  'How many guests can come to an elopement?': ('¿Cuántos invitados pueden venir a un elopement?', 'De nadie a un pequeño puñado &mdash; normalmente de cero a veinte. El sentido de fugarse es la intimidad, así que la mayoría de nuestras parejas vienen solo los dos, a veces con padres o uno o dos testigos. Cuanta más gente añadís, más logística necesita un día de montaña &mdash; el terreno, el ritmo, los tiempos, alguien que cuide los zapatos abajo &mdash;, así que lo mantenemos pequeño a propósito. Si queréis a un puñado de las personas que más amáis con vosotros en la montaña, funciona de maravilla; simplemente planeamos la caminata y los tiempos en torno a ellos.'),
  'Will the day feel like a photo shoot?': ('¿El día se sentirá como una sesión de fotos?', 'Eso es lo que más nos esforzamos por evitar. Es vuestra boda, no una sesión &mdash; y las mejores fotos, siempre, salen de los momentos en que os olvidáis de que estamos siquiera ahí. Nos mantenemos ligeros, guardamos distancia cuando importa y dirigimos solo lo justo para que estéis cómodos. La mayor parte del día simplemente estáis juntos: leyendo los votos, recobrando el aliento en una cresta, riendo del viento, compartiendo un almuerzo de refugio. Planeamos todo lo demás en torno a ese único objetivo, para que lo que recordéis sea el matrimonio, no la cámara.'),
}
THINGS_FAQ_IT = {
  'What happens if it rains on our elopement day?': ('Cosa succede se piove il giorno del nostro elopement?', "Onestamente? Potrebbe essere la cosa migliore che capiti. Alcune delle nostre foto preferite nascono da cieli grigi e pioggia &mdash; nebbia che cola dalle creste, un ombrello condiviso, gocce su un velo, colori profondi e intensi. Veniamo preparati con ombrelli trasparenti e panni asciutti, e lasciamo un margine, di solito un intero giorno di riserva nei pacchetti più grandi, così che il tempo non imponga mai la giornata. Seguiamo le previsioni ora per ora e vi spostiamo nella finestra che funziona. Una montagna che scompare nella nube non è una giornata rovinata; è un'altra, più quieta e spesso più bella."),
  'Is a sunrise start really as early as it sounds?': ("Una partenza all'alba è davvero presto come sembra?", "Sì &mdash; e vale ogni minuto. Una vera cerimonia all'alba può significare trucco e acconciatura alle tre o alle quattro del mattino e salire al buio con la frontale. Sembra brutale e sembra magia: avete i luoghi più famosi interamente per voi, la prima luce è irripetibile, e quando arrivano gli escursionisti state già facendo colazione. Noi gestiamo la logistica &mdash; la sveglia, i tempi, il percorso al buio &mdash; così che dobbiate solo presentarvi assonnati e andarvene stupiti. Non siete tipi da mattino? Pianifichiamo un tramonto."),
  'What should we actually bring?': ('Cosa dovremmo portare davvero?', "Meno glamour e più comfort di quanto pensiate. Stampate le promesse &mdash; gli schermi dei telefoni muoiono al freddo nel momento peggiore. Portate strati caldi da nascondere sotto il cappotto, un secondo paio di scarpe vere per il cammino con quelle belle in una borsa, spuntini, acqua e scaldamani. Portate un po' di contanti: alcune strade a pedaggio, parcheggi e persino cucine dei rifugi sono più comodi con essi. Freddo, vesciche e fame si vedono sempre nelle foto e in come vi sentite &mdash; il piccolo equipaggiamento poco glamour è ciò che mantiene morbida la giornata."),
  'Are there hidden costs and permits we should know about?': ('Ci sono costi nascosti e permessi da conoscere?', "Qualcuno piccolo, e li gestiamo tutti noi per voi. Alcune location richiedono un permesso foto o cerimonia; la strada a pedaggio delle Tre Cime costa circa 30&ndash;45&nbsp;&euro; ad auto; il Lago di Braies ha parcheggio a pagamento e una finestra d'accesso estiva; anche i biglietti della funivia e una notte in rifugio si sommano. Niente di tutto ciò è costoso di per sé &mdash; serve solo qualcuno che lo pianifichi così che nulla vi sorprenda il giorno stesso. È il nostro lavoro: le prenotazioni, i tempi, i biglietti e i contanti che vorrete in tasca, tutto sistemato in anticipo."),
  'How many guests can come to an elopement?': ('Quanti invitati possono venire a un elopement?', "Da nessuno a una piccola manciata &mdash; di solito da zero a venti. Il senso dell'elopement è l'intimità, quindi la maggior parte delle nostre coppie viene solo in due, a volte con i genitori o uno o due testimoni. Più persone aggiungete, più logistica richiede una giornata in montagna &mdash; il terreno, il ritmo, i tempi, qualcuno che badi alle scarpe a valle &mdash;, quindi la teniamo piccola di proposito. Se volete una manciata delle persone che amate di più con voi in montagna, funziona splendidamente; pianifichiamo semplicemente il cammino e i tempi intorno a loro."),
  'Will the day feel like a photo shoot?': ('La giornata sembrerà un servizio fotografico?', "È la cosa che ci sforziamo di più di evitare. È il vostro matrimonio, non un servizio &mdash; e le foto migliori, ogni volta, nascono dai momenti in cui dimenticate del tutto che siamo lì. Restiamo leggeri, teniamo le distanze quando conta e dirigiamo solo quanto basta a farvi stare a vostro agio. Per la maggior parte della giornata siete semplicemente insieme: a leggere le promesse, a riprendere fiato su una cresta, a ridere del vento, a condividere un pranzo in rifugio. Pianifichiamo tutto il resto attorno a quell'unico obiettivo, così che ciò che ricordate sia il matrimonio, non la macchina fotografica."),
}

THINGS_FAQ=[
 ("What happens if it rains on our elopement day?",
  "Honestly? It might be the best thing that happens. Some of our favourite photographs come from grey skies and rain &mdash; mist pouring off the ridges, a shared umbrella, drops on a veil, colours gone deep and moody. We come prepared with clear umbrellas and dry cloths, and we build in a buffer, usually a whole backup day on the bigger packages, so weather never forces the day. We watch the forecast hour by hour and move you to the window that works. A mountain that disappears into cloud is not a ruined day; it is a different, quieter, often more beautiful one.",
  "Was, wenn es an unserem Elopement-Tag regnet?",
  "Ehrlich? Vielleicht das Beste, was passieren kann. Einige unserer liebsten Bilder entstehen bei grauem Himmel und Regen &mdash; Nebel, der über die Grate quillt, ein geteilter Schirm, Tropfen auf dem Schleier, Farben tief und stimmungsvoll. Wir kommen vorbereitet mit durchsichtigen Schirmen und Tüchern, und wir bauen Puffer ein, bei den größeren Paketen meist einen ganzen Reservetag, damit das Wetter den Tag nie erzwingt. Wir verfolgen die Vorhersage Stunde um Stunde und legen euch in das Fenster, das passt. Ein Berg, der in Wolken verschwindet, ist kein ruinierter Tag; er ist ein anderer, stillerer, oft schönerer."),
 ("Is a sunrise start really as early as it sounds?",
  "Yes &mdash; and it is worth every minute. A true dawn ceremony can mean hair and make-up at three or four in the morning and walking up in the dark by headlamp. It sounds brutal and feels like magic: you have the most famous places entirely to yourselves, the first light is unrepeatable, and by the time the day-trippers arrive you are already having breakfast. We handle the logistics &mdash; the wake-up, the timing, the route in the dark &mdash; so all you have to do is show up sleepy and leave astonished. Not a morning person? We plan a sunset instead.",
  "Ist ein Sonnenaufgangs-Start wirklich so früh, wie er klingt?",
  "Ja &mdash; und jede Minute wert. Eine echte Zeremonie zur Morgendämmerung kann Haare und Make-up um drei oder vier Uhr früh und einen Aufstieg im Dunkeln mit Stirnlampe bedeuten. Es klingt brutal und fühlt sich wie Magie an: Ihr habt die berühmtesten Orte ganz für euch, das erste Licht ist unwiederholbar, und wenn die Tagesgäste kommen, frühstückt ihr längst. Wir übernehmen die Logistik &mdash; das Wecken, das Timing, die Route im Dunkeln &mdash;, ihr müsst nur verschlafen erscheinen und staunend gehen. Kein Morgenmensch? Dann planen wir einen Sonnenuntergang."),
 ("What should we actually bring?",
  "Less glamour, more comfort than you would think. Print your vows &mdash; phone screens die in the cold at the worst moment. Pack warm layers you can hide under a coat, a second pair of real shoes for the walk with the pretty ones in a bag, snacks, water, and hand warmers. Bring a little cash: some toll roads, car parks and even hut kitchens are easier with it. Cold, blisters and hunger always show in the photographs and in how you feel &mdash; the small, unglamorous kit is what keeps the day soft.",
  "Was sollten wir wirklich mitnehmen?",
  "Weniger Glamour, mehr Komfort, als ihr denkt. Druckt euer Gelübde &mdash; Handydisplays sterben in der Kälte im schlechtesten Moment. Packt warme Schichten für unter den Mantel, ein zweites Paar echte Schuhe für den Weg mit den schönen im Beutel, Snacks, Wasser und Handwärmer. Nehmt etwas Bargeld mit: manche Mautstraßen, Parkplätze und sogar Hüttenküchen sind damit einfacher. Kälte, Blasen und Hunger zeigen sich immer auf den Bildern und darin, wie ihr euch fühlt &mdash; das kleine, unglamouröse Gepäck hält den Tag weich."),
 ("Are there hidden costs and permits we should know about?",
  "A few small ones, and we handle them all for you. Some locations need a photography or ceremony permit; the Tre Cime toll road runs about &euro;30&ndash;45 per car; Lago di Braies has paid parking and a summer access window; cable-car tickets and a night in a mountain hut add up too. None of it is expensive on its own &mdash; it just needs someone to plan it so nothing surprises you on the day. That is our job: the reservations, the timings, the tickets and the cash you will want in your pocket, all sorted in advance.",
  "Gibt es versteckte Kosten und Genehmigungen, die wir kennen sollten?",
  "Ein paar kleine, und wir übernehmen sie alle für euch. Manche Orte brauchen eine Foto- oder Zeremonie-Genehmigung; die Drei-Zinnen-Mautstraße kostet rund 30&ndash;45&nbsp;&euro; pro Auto; der Pragser Wildsee hat kostenpflichtige Parkplätze und ein Sommer-Zufahrtsfenster; auch Bergbahn-Tickets und eine Hüttennacht summieren sich. Nichts davon ist für sich teuer &mdash; es braucht nur jemanden, der es plant, damit euch am Tag nichts überrascht. Genau das ist unsere Aufgabe: Reservierungen, Timing, Tickets und das Bargeld, das ihr in der Tasche wollt &mdash; alles vorab geregelt."),
 ("How many guests can come to an elopement?",
  "Anywhere from nobody to a small handful &mdash; usually zero to twenty. The whole point of eloping is intimacy, so most of our couples come as just the two of them, sometimes with parents or a witness or two. The more people you add, the more logistics a mountain day needs &mdash; footing, pace, timing, someone minding the shoes at the bottom &mdash; so we keep it small on purpose. If you want a handful of the people you love most on the mountain with you, that works beautifully; we simply plan the walk and the timing around them.",
  "Wie viele Gäste können zu einem Elopement kommen?",
  "Von niemandem bis zu einer kleinen Handvoll &mdash; meist null bis zwanzig. Der ganze Sinn eines Elopements ist Intimität, die meisten unserer Paare kommen also nur zu zweit, manchmal mit Eltern oder ein, zwei Trauzeugen. Je mehr Menschen ihr hinzufügt, desto mehr Logistik braucht ein Bergtag &mdash; Tritt, Tempo, Timing, jemand, der unten die Schuhe hütet &mdash;, wir halten es also bewusst klein. Wollt ihr eine Handvoll der liebsten Menschen mit am Berg, funktioniert das wunderbar; wir planen Weg und Timing einfach um sie herum."),
 ("Will the day feel like a photo shoot?",
  "That is the thing we work hardest to avoid. It is your wedding, not a shoot &mdash; and the best images, every time, come from the moments you forget we are there at all. We stay light, keep our distance when it matters, and direct only enough to keep you comfortable. Most of the day you are simply together: reading your vows, catching your breath on a ridge, laughing at the wind, sharing a hut lunch. We plan everything else around that one goal, so what you remember is the marriage, not the camera.",
  "Fühlt sich der Tag wie ein Fotoshooting an?",
  "Genau das vermeiden wir am hartnäckigsten. Es ist eure Hochzeit, kein Shooting &mdash; und die besten Bilder entstehen jedes Mal aus den Momenten, in denen ihr vergesst, dass wir überhaupt da sind. Wir bleiben zurückhaltend, halten Abstand, wo es zählt, und regen nur so viel an, dass ihr euch wohlfühlt. Den größten Teil des Tages seid ihr einfach zusammen: das Gelübde lesen, auf einem Grat verschnaufen, über den Wind lachen, ein Hüttenessen teilen. Alles andere planen wir um dieses eine Ziel, damit ihr euch an die Ehe erinnert, nicht an die Kamera."),
]

def build_things_guide(lang):
    slug='elopement-things-nobody-tells-you'
    g=next(x for x in GUIDES if x['slug']==slug); ex=GUIDE_EXTRA[slug]
    rel='how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/'+slug+'/'; P=prefix(lang,rel)
    DE=(lang=='de')
    def L(en,de):
        if lang=='de': return de
        if lang=='es': return THINGS_ES.get(en,en)
        if lang=='it': return THINGS_IT.get(en,en)
        return en
    def FQ(qen,aen,qde,ade):
        if lang=='de': return (qde,ade)
        if lang=='es': return THINGS_FAQ_ES.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        if lang=='it': return THINGS_FAQ_IT.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        return (qen,aen)
    GI=f'{P}img/guide-things-nobody-tells-you/'
    H2S='font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,3vw,36px);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:1.7em 0 .4em;scroll-margin-top:96px'
    def h2(i,en,de): return f'<h2 id="{i}" style="{H2S}">{L(en,de)}</h2>'
    def p(en,de): return f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2)">{L(en,de)}</p>'
    def fig(name,en,de): return f'<figure class="guide-fig"><img src="{GI}{name}" alt="{L(en,de)}" loading="lazy"></figure>'
    HERO_IMG='img/guide-things-nobody-tells-you/02-ehrlich-kuss-unter-dem-schirm.webp'
    toc=[('comfort',L('Comfort beats everything','Komfort schlägt alles')),('weather',L('The weather is not the enemy','Das Wetter ist nicht der Feind')),
         ('early',L('The early-start truth','Die Wahrheit über den frühen Start')),('moment',L('Protecting the moment','Den Moment schützen')),
         ('practical',L('The practical things','Die praktischen Dinge')),('smallprint',L('The small print that saves money','Das Kleingedruckte, das spart')),
         ('celebrate',L('Build in a celebration','Baut eine Feier ein')),('adventure',L('Say yes to the odd idea','Sagt Ja zur verrückten Idee')),
         ('remember',L('The one thing to remember','Das Eine, das bleibt')),('faq',L('FAQ','FAQ'))]
    toc_html=('<nav class="guide-toc" aria-label="'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'"><div class="cap">'+L('On this page','Auf dieser Seite')+'</div><ol>'
      +''.join(f'<li><a href="#{i}">{lbl}</a></li>' for i,lbl in toc)+'</ol></nav>')
    facts='<div class="facts">'+''.join(f'<div class="fct"><div class="fl">{LBL[k][lang]}</div><div class="fv">{val[lang]}</div></div>' for k,val in ex['facts'])+'</div>'
    C=[]
    C.append(f'<p class="lead">{L("The big decisions &mdash; where, when, what it costs &mdash; are the easy part. It is the small, unglamorous details that quietly make or break a mountain wedding day, and no checklist ever mentions them. After years of eloping couples in the Alps, in rain and wind and three-in-the-morning darkness, these are the things we wish someone had told us first. None of it is scary. All of it is the difference between a day you endure and a day you never stop talking about.","Die großen Entscheidungen &mdash; wo, wann, was es kostet &mdash; sind der leichte Teil. Es sind die kleinen, unglamourösen Details, die einen Berghochzeitstag still gelingen oder scheitern lassen, und keine Checkliste erwähnt sie. Nach Jahren, in denen wir Paare in den Alpen begleitet haben, in Regen und Wind und Drei-Uhr-früh-Dunkelheit, sind das die Dinge, die uns jemand zuerst hätte sagen sollen. Nichts davon ist beängstigend. Alles davon ist der Unterschied zwischen einem Tag, den ihr übersteht, und einem, von dem ihr nie aufhört zu erzählen.")}</p>')
    C.append(f'<div class="cap" style="margin:0 0 -14px">{t(lang,"quick_facts")}</div>{facts}')
    C.append(toc_html)

    C.append(h2('comfort','Comfort beats everything &mdash; and it shows','Komfort schlägt alles &mdash; und man sieht es'))
    C.append(p("If you take one thing from this whole guide, take this: cold, blisters and hunger always show in the photographs. Not in an obvious way &mdash; in the set of a jaw, a hunched shoulder, a smile that does not quite reach the eyes. The couples who look luminous all day are almost always the ones who packed a second pair of real shoes for the walk, warm layers to hide under a coat, water, a snack and hand warmers. The pretty shoes go in a bag and come out for the vows. Nobody ever regretted being warm and fed on their wedding day.","Wenn ihr aus diesem ganzen Guide eine Sache mitnehmt, dann diese: Kälte, Blasen und Hunger zeigen sich immer auf den Bildern. Nicht offensichtlich &mdash; im Zug eines Kiefers, einer hochgezogenen Schulter, einem Lächeln, das die Augen nicht ganz erreicht. Die Paare, die den ganzen Tag strahlen, sind fast immer die, die ein zweites Paar echte Schuhe für den Weg eingepackt haben, warme Schichten für unter den Mantel, Wasser, einen Snack und Handwärmer. Die schönen Schuhe wandern in den Beutel und kommen fürs Gelübde heraus. Niemand hat je bereut, an seinem Hochzeitstag warm und satt zu sein."))
    C.append(fig('08-ehrlich-umziehen-auf-dem-fels.webp',"A partner changing into the ceremony outfit on a flat rock","Umziehen ins Zeremonien-Outfit auf einem flachen Fels"))
    C.append(fig('09-ehrlich-ausruestung-am-gipfel.webp',"Backpacks and gear laid out at the summit before the ceremony","Rucksäcke und Ausrüstung am Gipfel vor der Zeremonie"))
    C.append(p("This is also why we never rush you up a mountain. We scout the route in advance, carry the heavy things, and pace the walk so you arrive with breath to spare rather than red-faced and shaking. A little planning &mdash; the right shoes, a warm layer, a hut with a kitchen at the top &mdash; means the walk becomes part of the adventure instead of the thing you were dreading. And when you are comfortable, you forget the camera, and that is when the real pictures happen.","Deshalb hetzen wir euch auch nie einen Berg hinauf. Wir erkunden die Route vorab, tragen das Schwere und dosieren den Weg so, dass ihr mit Atem übrig ankommt statt rot und zitternd. Ein wenig Planung &mdash; die richtigen Schuhe, eine warme Schicht, eine Hütte mit Küche oben &mdash; macht den Weg zum Teil des Abenteuers statt zu dem, wovor ihr euch gefürchtet habt. Und wenn ihr euch wohlfühlt, vergesst ihr die Kamera &mdash; und genau dann entstehen die echten Bilder."))
    C.append(fig('15-ehrlich-huettenjause.webp',"A simple hut snack &mdash; bread, cheese and a warm drink after the ceremony","Eine einfache Hüttenjause &mdash; Brot, Käse und ein warmes Getränk nach der Zeremonie"))

    C.append(h2('weather','The weather is not the enemy','Das Wetter ist nicht der Feind'))
    C.append(p("Everyone plans for sunshine and dreads the grey. We would gently turn that around. Some of the most beautiful, most emotional pictures we have ever taken came out of rain, mist and wind &mdash; cloud pouring over a ridge, a veil caught mid-gust, two people laughing under a shared umbrella because there is nothing else to do. Bad weather strips a day down to what actually matters: the two of you, close, a little defiant, entirely present. We come prepared with clear umbrellas and dry cloths, and we are not afraid of a moody sky. Neither should you be.","Alle planen für Sonne und fürchten das Grau. Wir würden das sanft umdrehen. Einige der schönsten, bewegendsten Bilder, die wir je gemacht haben, kamen aus Regen, Nebel und Wind &mdash; Wolken, die über einen Grat quellen, ein Schleier in der Böe, zwei Menschen, die unter einem geteilten Schirm lachen, weil es nichts anderes zu tun gibt. Schlechtwetter reduziert einen Tag auf das, was wirklich zählt: ihr zwei, nah, ein wenig trotzig, ganz da. Wir kommen vorbereitet mit durchsichtigen Schirmen und Tüchern und fürchten keinen stimmungsvollen Himmel. Ihr solltet es auch nicht."))
    C.append(fig('01-ehrlich-regenschirm-am-steg.webp',"The couple under an umbrella on a jetty in the rain","Das Paar unter einem Schirm auf einem Steg im Regen"))
    C.append(fig('10-ehrlich-regen-im-dirndl.webp',"A bride in a dirndl smiling through mountain rain","Eine Braut im Dirndl, die durch den Bergregen lächelt"))
    C.append(p("Wind is its own character. It lifts a veil and a dress into something alive, and a meadow in a stiff breeze photographs like a painting &mdash; but it is cold, and it steals words, so we pick sheltered spots for the vows and let the exposed ridges be for the portraits. The honest rule is this: we never cancel for weather, we move around it. A backup day, built into the bigger packages, means we can wait out a storm or chase a clearing. The forecast is a suggestion, not a verdict, and the mountain rarely reads it anyway.","Der Wind ist ein eigener Charakter. Er hebt Schleier und Kleid zu etwas Lebendigem, und eine Wiese in steifer Brise fotografiert sich wie ein Gemälde &mdash; aber er ist kalt und stiehlt Worte, wir wählen fürs Gelübde also geschützte Plätze und lassen die ausgesetzten Grate den Porträts. Die ehrliche Regel lautet: Wir sagen wegen Wetter nie ab, wir weichen ihm aus. Ein Reservetag, in den größeren Paketen eingebaut, heißt, wir können einen Sturm aussitzen oder eine Aufklarung jagen. Die Vorhersage ist ein Vorschlag, kein Urteil &mdash; und der Berg liest sie ohnehin selten."))
    C.append(fig('13-ehrlich-wind-auf-der-wiese.webp',"Dress and veil caught by the wind on an open meadow","Kleid und Schleier vom Wind erfasst auf offener Wiese"))

    C.append(h2('early','The early-start truth','Die Wahrheit über den frühen Start'))
    C.append(p("Nobody warns you quite how early a sunrise elopement begins. Hair and make-up can start at three or four in the morning; the walk up is often in the dark, by headlamp, with the valley asleep below you. It sounds punishing, and for about twenty minutes it is. Then the sky starts to move, you reach the spot, and the whole world is yours alone &mdash; no day-trippers, no queue at the viewpoint, just the first light climbing the rock while you say your words. By the time everyone else arrives, you are already coming down for breakfast, married.","Niemand warnt euch, wie früh ein Sonnenaufgangs-Elopement beginnt. Haare und Make-up können um drei oder vier Uhr früh starten; der Aufstieg ist oft im Dunkeln, mit Stirnlampe, das Tal schläft unter euch. Es klingt hart, und für etwa zwanzig Minuten ist es das. Dann beginnt der Himmel sich zu regen, ihr erreicht den Ort, und die ganze Welt gehört euch allein &mdash; keine Tagesgäste, keine Schlange am Aussichtspunkt, nur das erste Licht, das den Fels erklimmt, während ihr eure Worte sprecht. Wenn alle anderen kommen, steigt ihr längst zum Frühstück ab, verheiratet."))
    C.append(fig('06-ehrlich-start-um-drei-uhr.webp',"Getting ready by lamplight at three in the morning","Fertigmachen bei Lampenlicht um drei Uhr früh"))
    C.append(fig('07-ehrlich-aufstieg-im-dunkeln.webp',"The couple climbing by headlamp before dawn","Das Paar steigt vor der Dämmerung mit Stirnlampe auf"))
    C.append(p("We carry the whole logistics of it so you do not have to think: the wake-up call, the timing worked backwards from the sunrise minute, the route we have already walked in daylight, spare layers for the cold hour before the sun. All you do is trust the alarm and turn up sleepy. And if none of that appeals &mdash; if you would rather a long lie-in and a glass of something at golden hour &mdash; a sunset elopement gives you the same empty, glowing light at a far more civilised time of day. There is no wrong answer, only the one that fits you.","Wir tragen die ganze Logistik, damit ihr nicht denken müsst: den Weckruf, das rückwärts von der Sonnenaufgangs-Minute gerechnete Timing, die Route, die wir bei Tageslicht bereits gegangen sind, Ersatzschichten für die kalte Stunde vor der Sonne. Ihr müsst nur dem Wecker vertrauen und verschlafen erscheinen. Und wenn euch das gar nicht reizt &mdash; wenn ihr lieber ausschlaft und zur goldenen Stunde ein Glas hebt &mdash;, schenkt euch ein Sonnenuntergangs-Elopement dasselbe leere, glühende Licht zu einer weit zivileren Tageszeit. Es gibt keine falsche Antwort, nur die, die zu euch passt."))

    C.append(h2('moment','Protecting the moment','Den Moment schützen'))
    C.append(p("Here is a small one that matters more than it sounds: write your vows in advance, and bring a printed copy. Phone screens die in the cold at exactly the wrong moment, and reading from paper you can actually hold, with shaking happy hands, is part of the memory anyway. Then guard the day a little. Do not post the exact location or the plan; silence the phones for the ceremony; ask any guests to stay present rather than filming. The fewer things pulling at your attention, the more the day belongs to you.","Eine Kleinigkeit, die mehr zählt, als sie klingt: Schreibt euer Gelübde vorab und bringt eine gedruckte Kopie mit. Handydisplays sterben in der Kälte genau im falschen Moment, und von Papier zu lesen, das ihr wirklich in zitternden, glücklichen Händen halten könnt, ist ohnehin Teil der Erinnerung. Dann schützt den Tag ein wenig. Postet nicht den genauen Ort oder den Plan; stellt für die Zeremonie die Handys stumm; bittet Gäste, präsent zu sein statt zu filmen. Je weniger an eurer Aufmerksamkeit zerrt, desto mehr gehört der Tag euch."))
    C.append(p("The other half of protecting the moment is time. So many days feel rushed not because there was too little of it, but because nobody left any margin. We plan generous buffers into every hour &mdash; time to breathe on the ridge, time to fix a windblown strand of hair, time to just stand there and realise it happened. When a schedule has slack in it, the small disasters stop being disasters: a late cable car, a wrong turn, a sudden shower become footnotes instead of catastrophes. Space in the plan is the quiet luxury nobody tells you to ask for.","Die andere Hälfte, den Moment zu schützen, ist Zeit. So viele Tage wirken gehetzt, nicht weil zu wenig davon da war, sondern weil niemand Spielraum ließ. Wir planen großzügige Puffer in jede Stunde &mdash; Zeit zum Durchatmen am Grat, Zeit, eine vom Wind verwehte Haarsträhne zu richten, Zeit, einfach dazustehen und zu begreifen, dass es geschehen ist. Wenn ein Ablauf Luft hat, hören die kleinen Katastrophen auf, welche zu sein: eine verpasste Gondel, eine falsche Abzweigung, ein plötzlicher Schauer werden zu Fußnoten statt zu Dramen. Raum im Plan ist der stille Luxus, nach dem euch niemand zu fragen rät."))

    C.append(h2('practical','The practical things nobody says','Die praktischen Dinge, die keiner sagt'))
    C.append(p("A handful of unglamorous facts that save real headaches. Carry some cash &mdash; a few of the toll roads and car parks, the Tre Cime road and the Braies parking among them, are smoother with it, and some hut kitchens still prefer it. Check the last cable car down before you commit to a sunset up high, because being stranded at altitude in the dark is a story you do not want. Remember that Lago di Braies closes to traffic from mid-morning in summer, so we shoot it before or after that window. And pack one warm layer even in August: a summit at first light is genuinely cold, whatever the valley thermometer says.","Eine Handvoll unglamouröser Fakten, die echten Ärger sparen. Nehmt etwas Bargeld mit &mdash; einige der Mautstraßen und Parkplätze, die Drei-Zinnen-Straße und der Braies-Parkplatz darunter, sind damit reibungsloser, und manche Hüttenküchen bevorzugen es noch. Prüft die letzte Talfahrt der Gondel, ehe ihr euch für einen Sonnenuntergang hoch oben entscheidet, denn im Dunkeln in der Höhe zu stranden ist eine Geschichte, die ihr nicht wollt. Denkt daran, dass der Pragser Wildsee im Sommer ab dem späten Vormittag für den Verkehr schließt, wir fotografieren ihn also davor oder danach. Und packt selbst im August eine warme Schicht: Ein Gipfel im ersten Licht ist wirklich kalt, was auch immer das Talthermometer sagt."))
    C.append(fig('14-ehrlich-skifahrer-im-hintergrund.webp',"A skier passing in the background during a winter mountain ceremony","Ein Skifahrer, der im Hintergrund einer winterlichen Bergzeremonie vorbeizieht"))
    C.append(p("And here is one nobody mentions at all: you are rarely the only people on the mountain. A hiker will wander through the background, a skier will cross the slope behind you, a cable car will hum overhead. It is not a problem &mdash; it is honest, and we know how to work with it: the right angle, the right minute, the quiet corner five steps off the main path. Part of what you are paying for is someone who knows exactly when the viewpoint empties and how to give you privacy in a public place. The mountain is shared; your moment does not have to feel like it.","Und eine, die überhaupt niemand erwähnt: Ihr seid selten die Einzigen am Berg. Ein Wanderer streift durch den Hintergrund, ein Skifahrer quert den Hang hinter euch, eine Gondel summt über euch. Das ist kein Problem &mdash; es ist ehrlich, und wir wissen damit umzugehen: der richtige Winkel, die richtige Minute, die stille Ecke fünf Schritte neben dem Hauptweg. Ein Teil dessen, wofür ihr zahlt, ist jemand, der genau weiß, wann sich der Aussichtspunkt leert und wie man euch an einem öffentlichen Ort Privatheit gibt. Der Berg ist geteilt; euer Moment muss sich nicht so anfühlen."))

    C.append(h2('smallprint','The small print that saves you money','Das Kleingedruckte, das euch spart'))
    C.append(p("A few early decisions quietly lower the bill. Book the mountain hut and, if you are marrying legally in Austria, the registrar months ahead &mdash; both are limited in summer and both get more expensive the later you leave them. Consider the shoulder season: late May and October are cheaper, far quieter and often more beautiful than high summer, with golden larches or a dusting of fresh snow on the peaks. And you rarely need both a toll road and a cable car on the same day &mdash; picking one keeps the budget and the schedule simple. We map all of this out with you so the money goes where it matters.","Ein paar frühe Entscheidungen senken still die Rechnung. Bucht die Hütte und, wenn ihr in Österreich rechtsgültig heiratet, die Standesbeamtin Monate im Voraus &mdash; beides ist im Sommer begrenzt und beides wird teurer, je später ihr dran seid. Denkt an die Nebensaison: Ende Mai und Oktober sind günstiger, viel ruhiger und oft schöner als der Hochsommer, mit goldenen Lärchen oder frischem Schnee auf den Gipfeln. Und ihr braucht selten Mautstraße und Bergbahn am selben Tag &mdash; eines zu wählen hält Budget und Ablauf einfach. Wir kartieren das alles mit euch, damit das Geld dorthin geht, wo es zählt."))

    C.append(h2('celebrate','Build a real celebration into the day','Baut eine echte Feier in den Tag'))
    C.append(p("An elopement is not a wedding with the joy removed &mdash; it is a wedding with the noise removed. So give the day something to celebrate with. Some of our favourite afternoons have ended with a portable pizza oven fired up on a mountain meadow, a bottle of something cold and shaken loose, a hut table groaning with local food. The vows are the heart of it, but the hours after are where the day loosens and becomes yours: the toast, the laughter, the meal with the peaks going pink. Plan for it. A celebration of two people is still a celebration.","Ein Elopement ist keine Hochzeit ohne die Freude &mdash; es ist eine Hochzeit ohne den Lärm. Gebt dem Tag also etwas zum Feiern. Einige unserer liebsten Nachmittage endeten mit einem tragbaren Pizzaofen, der auf einer Bergwiese angefeuert wurde, einer Flasche von etwas Kaltem, kräftig geschüttelt, einem Hüttentisch, der sich unter regionalem Essen biegt. Das Gelübde ist das Herz, aber die Stunden danach sind, wo der Tag sich löst und euer wird: der Toast, das Lachen, das Essen, während die Gipfel rosa werden. Plant dafür. Eine Feier zweier Menschen ist immer noch eine Feier."))
    C.append(fig('03-ehrlich-pizzaofen-aufbau.webp',"Setting up a portable pizza oven on a mountain meadow","Aufbau eines tragbaren Pizzaofens auf einer Bergwiese"))
    C.append(fig('04-ehrlich-pizza-frisch-aus-dem-ofen.webp',"Fresh pizza straight from the oven at the celebration","Frische Pizza direkt aus dem Ofen bei der Feier"))
    C.append(fig('05-ehrlich-champagner-dusche.webp',"A spray of champagne to celebrate on the mountain","Eine Champagnerdusche zur Feier am Berg"))

    C.append(h2('adventure','Say yes to the odd idea','Sagt Ja zur verrückten Idee'))
    C.append(p("The pictures couples treasure most are almost never the safe ones. They are the bride clicking into skis in her wedding dress, the groom sledging down a slope in his suit, the pair wading into a cold lake because the light was too good to resist. If you have a slightly ridiculous idea &mdash; a thing you have always secretly wanted to do &mdash; tell us. Nine times out of ten we can make it safe and make it happen, and it becomes the frame you hang on the wall and the story you tell for the rest of your lives. The mountain gives you permission to be a little wild.","Die Bilder, die Paare am meisten schätzen, sind fast nie die sicheren. Es sind die Braut, die im Hochzeitskleid in die Ski steigt, der Bräutigam, der im Anzug einen Hang hinunterrodelt, das Paar, das in einen kalten See watet, weil das Licht zu gut war, um zu widerstehen. Wenn ihr eine leicht absurde Idee habt &mdash; etwas, das ihr insgeheim immer tun wolltet &mdash;, sagt es uns. Neun von zehn Mal machen wir es sicher und machen es möglich, und es wird zum Bild, das ihr an die Wand hängt, und zur Geschichte, die ihr euer Leben lang erzählt. Der Berg gibt euch die Erlaubnis, ein wenig wild zu sein."))
    C.append(fig('11-ehrlich-ski-im-brautkleid.webp',"The bride on skis in her wedding dress","Die Braut auf Ski im Brautkleid"))
    C.append(fig('12-ehrlich-rodeln-im-anzug.webp',"The groom sledging down a slope in his suit","Der Bräutigam rodelt im Anzug einen Hang hinab"))

    C.append(h2('remember','The one thing to remember','Das Eine, das bleibt'))
    C.append(p("If you forget everything else on this page, keep this. It is your day, not a photo shoot. Every tip here &mdash; the snacks, the buffer time, the printed vows, the backup day &mdash; exists for one reason: to clear the small worries out of the way so you can simply be together. The best images we have ever made came in the moments the couple forgot we were there at all: a private joke on a ridge, a held breath before the vows, a quiet hand on a cold cheek. Plan well, then let go. We will take care of the rest.","Wenn ihr alles andere auf dieser Seite vergesst, behaltet dies. Es ist euer Tag, kein Fotoshooting. Jeder Tipp hier &mdash; die Snacks, die Pufferzeit, das gedruckte Gelübde, der Reservetag &mdash; existiert aus einem Grund: die kleinen Sorgen aus dem Weg zu räumen, damit ihr einfach zusammen sein könnt. Die besten Bilder, die wir je gemacht haben, kamen in den Momenten, in denen das Paar vergaß, dass wir überhaupt da waren: ein privater Scherz am Grat, ein angehaltener Atem vor dem Gelübde, eine stille Hand auf einer kalten Wange. Plant gut, dann lasst los. Um den Rest kümmern wir uns."))

    faq_html='<h2 id="faq" style="'+H2S+'">'+L('What nobody tells you &mdash; FAQ','Was dir niemand sagt &mdash; FAQ')+'</h2>'
    FAQL=[FQ(*x) for x in THINGS_FAQ]
    faq_html+=''.join('<div style="margin:1.3em 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:1.1em">'
      f'<h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:20px;margin:0 0 .3em">{q}</h3>'
      f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2);margin:0">{a}</p></div>' for q,a in FAQL)
    faq_ld={"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
      {"@type":"Question","name":_plain(q),"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":_plain(a)}} for q,a in FAQL]}
    related=''.join(story_card(lang,P,STORYBY[sl]) for sl in ex['stories'])
    more=''.join(guide_card(lang,P,x) for x in GUIDES if x['slug']!=slug)
    body=(nav(lang,rel,'howto')+
      f'<section class="page-hero" style="padding:0">{herobg(P,HERO_IMG,g["title"][lang])}'
      f'<div class="content"><div class="wrap"><div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"guide_kick")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h1>{g["title"][lang]}</h1></div></div></section>'
      '<section><div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">'+''.join(C)+faq_html+
      f'<p style="margin-top:2.4em"><a href="{u(P,lang,"how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/")}" class="arrow-link">&larr; {T["nav"]["howto"][lang]}</a></p></div></section>'
      '<section style="padding-top:0"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"related_stories")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"related_stories")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{related}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="stories" style="padding-top:clamp(40px,6vw,80px)"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"more_guides")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{t(lang,"more_guides")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{more}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="cta"><div class="wrap row reveal"><div>'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{t(lang,"cta_k")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2 style="margin-top:20px">{t(lang,"cta_h")}</h2></div>'
      f'<a href="{u(P,lang,"get-in-touch/")}" class="btn light">{t(lang,"start_planning")}</a></div></section>'
      +footer(lang,rel))
    write(lang,rel,head(lang,rel,g['title'][lang]+' — Mountain Elopement',g['excerpt'][lang],ld_extra=faq_ld,pre=herolink(P,HERO_IMG))+body+scripts(P))

TYROL_REGION_FAQ=[
 ("Can we legally get married in Tyrol?",
  "Yes &mdash; and it is the single best reason to choose Tyrol. Austria allows a legally binding civil ceremony, and several Tyrolean registry offices will marry you at an approved outdoor location, not just inside the office &mdash; a lakeshore, a viewpoint, a mountain terrace. That means the ceremony that counts on paper can happen with the peaks right behind you. In Italy, by contrast, a binding wedding can only take place inside a town hall. We coordinate the office, the date and the paperwork for you.",
  "Können wir in Tirol rechtsgültig heiraten?",
  "Ja &mdash; und es ist der beste einzelne Grund, Tirol zu wählen. Österreich erlaubt eine rechtsgültige standesamtliche Trauung, und mehrere Tiroler Standesämter trauen euch an einem genehmigten Ort im Freien, nicht nur im Amt &mdash; einem Seeufer, einem Aussichtspunkt, einer Bergterrasse. Die Zeremonie, die auf dem Papier zählt, kann also mit den Gipfeln direkt im Rücken stattfinden. In Italien dagegen kann eine bindende Hochzeit nur im Rathaus stattfinden. Wir koordinieren Amt, Termin und Papiere für euch."),
 ("Where can we elope in Tyrol?",
  "From the Nordkette ridges right above Innsbruck to hidden turquoise lakes and high toll roads that open bare-rock views without a hike. Our shortlist: the Hafelekar and the ridges over Innsbruck, the protected Obernberger See near the Brenner, the emerald Schlegeisspeicher in the Zillertal, and the quiet high tarns above K&uuml;htai. All sit close to Innsbruck yet feel a world away, and each is calmest at first light.",
  "Wo können wir in Tirol heiraten?",
  "Von den Nordketten-Graten direkt über Innsbruck bis zu versteckten türkisen Seen und Höhen-Mautstraßen, die Felsblicke ohne Wanderung öffnen. Unsere Auswahl: das Hafelekar und die Grate über Innsbruck, der geschützte Obernberger See nahe dem Brenner, der smaragdgrüne Schlegeisspeicher im Zillertal und die stillen Hochseen über K&uuml;htai. Alle liegen nah an Innsbruck und fühlen sich doch wie eine andere Welt an, und jeder ist im ersten Licht am ruhigsten."),
 ("Do we have to hike?",
  "Only as far as you want to. Innsbruck is the only city in the Alps with a high mountain on its doorstep &mdash; the Nordkette lifts carry you from the old town to 2,256&thinsp;m in about twenty minutes, no walking required. Several of our favourite Tyrolean lakes sit right at the end of a road. And if you want the day to feel earned, a short ridge walk puts you somewhere that looks impossible. We match the effort to you and never oversell what a spot costs to reach.",
  "Müssen wir wandern?",
  "Nur so weit ihr wollt. Innsbruck ist die einzige Stadt der Alpen mit einem Hochgebirge direkt vor der Tür &mdash; die Nordkettenbahnen bringen euch in rund zwanzig Minuten von der Altstadt auf 2.256&thinsp;m, ganz ohne Fußweg. Mehrere unserer liebsten Tiroler Seen liegen direkt am Ende einer Straße. Und wenn sich der Tag verdient anfühlen soll, bringt euch ein kurzer Gratweg irgendwohin, das unmöglich aussieht. Wir passen die Anstrengung an euch an und beschönigen nie, was ein Ort an Aufstieg kostet."),
 ("When is the best time to elope in Tyrol?",
  "May to October is the reliable window: the lifts run, the high roads are open and the meadows are green. July and August give the warmest, most settled weather; late September brings golden larches and thinner crowds and is our quiet favourite. The shoulder weeks can hand you fresh snow on the peaks and empty trails in the same morning. Winter is spectacular and silent but needs a close eye on which roads and lifts are open.",
  "Wann ist die beste Zeit für ein Elopement in Tirol?",
  "Mai bis Oktober ist das verlässliche Fenster: Die Bahnen fahren, die Höhenstraßen sind offen und die Wiesen grün. Juli und August bringen das wärmste, beständigste Wetter; der späte September schenkt goldene Lärchen und weniger Andrang und ist unser stiller Favorit. Die Randwochen können euch frischen Schnee auf den Gipfeln und leere Wege am selben Morgen bescheren. Der Winter ist spektakulär und still, verlangt aber einen wachen Blick darauf, welche Straßen und Bahnen offen sind."),
 ("How do we get to Tyrol?",
  "Easily &mdash; it is one of the most accessible Alpine regions. Innsbruck has its own airport minutes from the old town, and Munich and Venice are each a straightforward drive or train away, so most couples are under a mountain within an hour or two of landing. From an Innsbruck base you can reach the Nordkette, the Zillertal lakes and the high roads without a long transfer, and the crossing south into the Dolomites is a simple, scenic drive.",
  "Wie kommen wir nach Tirol?",
  "Leicht &mdash; es ist eine der am besten erreichbaren Alpenregionen. Innsbruck hat einen eigenen Flughafen wenige Minuten von der Altstadt, und München und Venedig sind jeweils eine unkomplizierte Fahrt oder Zugverbindung entfernt, die meisten Paare stehen also ein bis zwei Stunden nach der Landung unter einem Berg. Von einer Basis in Innsbruck erreicht ihr die Nordkette, die Zillertaler Seen und die Höhenstraßen ohne langen Transfer, und der Übertritt nach Süden in die Dolomiten ist eine einfache, landschaftlich schöne Fahrt."),
 ("What does an elopement in Tyrol cost?",
  "Our elopement packages start at &euro;6,000 and cover photography, location scouting, a planning call and your private online gallery. The middle package adds hair and make-up, flowers and full coordination; the largest covers the whole day including accommodation, reception and transfers. We handle the registry appointment, the timings, the huts and the backup plan, so the only thing you think about on the day is each other.",
  "Was kostet ein Elopement in Tirol?",
  "Unsere Elopement-Pakete beginnen bei 6.000&nbsp;&euro; und umfassen Fotografie, Location-Scouting, ein Planungsgespräch und eure private Online-Galerie. Das mittlere Paket ergänzt Hair &amp; Make-up, Blumen und volle Koordination; das größte deckt den ganzen Tag inklusive Unterkunft, Feier und Transfers. Wir übernehmen den Standesamt-Termin, das Timing, die Hütten und den Plan B, damit ihr am Tag nur an eines denkt: aneinander."),
 ("How far in advance should we book?",
  "For a summer date, six to twelve months is comfortable. If you want the legal ceremony in Austria, book the registrar and the mountain hut months ahead &mdash; both are limited in summer and both fill early. Off-season we have occasionally made something beautiful happen in a few weeks. Tell us your dates and we will tell you honestly what is still possible.",
  "Wie früh sollten wir buchen?",
  "Für einen Sommertermin sind sechs bis zwölf Monate komfortabel. Wollt ihr die rechtsgültige Zeremonie in Österreich, bucht Standesbeamtin und Berghütte Monate im Voraus &mdash; beides ist im Sommer begrenzt und beides ist früh vergeben. In der Nebensaison haben wir gelegentlich in wenigen Wochen etwas Schönes möglich gemacht. Sagt uns eure Daten, und wir sagen euch ehrlich, was noch geht."),
]

# --- elopement-tyrol region ES/IT (auto-generated, keyed by exact EN string) ---
TYROL_ES = {
  'Questions couples ask us': 'Preguntas que nos hacen las parejas',
  'Real elopements': 'Elopements reales',
  'Real Tyrol elopements': 'Elopements reales en el Tirol',
  'Your day': 'Vuestro día',
  'Tell us what you&rsquo;re imagining': 'Contadnos lo que imagináis',
  'All planning guides': 'Todas las guías de planificación',
  'Our elopement packages start at <strong>&euro;6,000</strong> and cover photography, location scouting, a planning call and your private online gallery. The middle package adds hair and make-up, flowers and full coordination; the largest covers the whole day including accommodation, reception and transfers. What we handle for you in Tyrol: the registry appointment and paperwork, the hut booking, the timing so your mornings stay calm, and a backup plan for the day the weather turns.': 'Nuestros paquetes de elopement empiezan en <strong>6.000&nbsp;&euro;</strong> e incluyen fotografía, scouting de localizaciones, una llamada de planificación y vuestra galería online privada. El paquete intermedio añade peluquería y maquillaje, flores y coordinación completa; el mayor cubre el día entero, incluidos alojamiento, celebración y traslados. Lo que gestionamos por vosotros en el Tirol: la cita del registro y el papeleo, la reserva del refugio, los tiempos para que vuestras mañanas estén tranquilas, y un plan B para el día en que cambia el tiempo.',
  'What it costs, and what&rsquo;s included': 'Qué cuesta y qué incluye',
  'See the full price list': 'Ver la lista de precios completa',
  'Innsbruck has its own airport minutes from the old town, and Munich and Venice are each a simple drive or train away, so most couples are under a mountain within an hour or two of landing. Innsbruck makes the ideal base &mdash; the Nordkette above you, the Zillertal and its lakes a short drive east, the high roads west, and the Dolomites two to three hours south for couples who want to fold both countries into one trip. For a dawn ceremony we often book a mountain hut, so you sleep up high and wake already there.': 'Innsbruck tiene su propio aeropuerto a minutos del casco antiguo, y Múnich y Venecia están cada uno a un sencillo trayecto en coche o tren, así que la mayoría de las parejas está bajo una montaña una o dos horas tras aterrizar. Innsbruck es la base ideal &mdash; la Nordkette sobre vosotros, el Zillertal y sus lagos a un corto trayecto al este, las carreteras de altura al oeste, y los Dolomitas dos o tres horas al sur para parejas que quieren juntar los dos países en un viaje. Para una ceremonia al alba solemos reservar un refugio de montaña, para que durmáis arriba y despertéis ya allí.',
  'Getting here &amp; where to stay': 'Cómo llegar y dónde alojarse',
  'May through October is the dependable season: the lifts run, the high roads are open and the meadows are green. July and August bring the warmest, most settled weather; late September brings golden larches and thinner crowds and is our quiet favourite. The shoulder weeks can hand you fresh snow on the peaks and empty trails in a single morning &mdash; often the best pictures of the year. Winter turns Tyrol spectacular and silent, with a close eye needed on which roads and lifts stay open.': 'De mayo a octubre es la temporada fiable: los remontes funcionan, las carreteras de altura están abiertas y los prados verdes. Julio y agosto traen el tiempo más cálido y estable; finales de septiembre trae alerces dorados y menos gente, y es nuestro favorito tranquilo. Las semanas de transición pueden regalaros nieve fresca en las cumbres y senderos vacíos en una misma mañana &mdash; a menudo las mejores fotos del año. El invierno vuelve el Tirol espectacular y silencioso, con un ojo atento a qué carreteras y remontes siguen abiertos.',
  'When to come': 'Cuándo venir',
  'For a civil marriage you will generally need valid passports, birth certificates and a certificate of no impediment, usually with certified translations and, depending on your home country, an apostille. Each office sets its own lead times and the summer slots fill early, so start a few months ahead. Prefer to keep it simple? Sign the short legal act at home and hold a symbolic ceremony on the mountain &mdash; both carry all of the feeling, and we will tell you honestly which fits your timeline.': 'Para un matrimonio civil necesitaréis por lo general pasaportes válidos, certificados de nacimiento y un certificado de no impedimento, normalmente con traducciones juradas y, según vuestro país, una apostilla. Cada oficina fija sus propios plazos y las citas de verano se llenan pronto, así que empezad unos meses antes. ¿Preferís que sea sencillo? Firmad el breve acto legal en casa y celebrad una ceremonia simbólica en la montaña &mdash; ambas llevan todo el sentimiento, y os diremos con honestidad cuál encaja con vuestro calendario.',
  'This is the heart of why couples choose Tyrol. A civil marriage in Austria is straightforward for foreign couples, and several Tyrolean registry offices conduct the legal ceremony at an approved outdoor location &mdash; not only inside the office. The act that actually changes your legal status can happen with a lake or a summit right there.': 'Este es el corazón de por qué las parejas eligen el Tirol. Un matrimonio civil en Austria es sencillo para parejas extranjeras, y varios registros civiles tiroleses celebran la ceremonia legal en un lugar autorizado al aire libre &mdash; no solo dentro de la oficina. El acto que de verdad cambia vuestro estado legal puede ocurrir con un lago o una cumbre justo ahí.',
  'Making it legal in Austria': 'Casarse legalmente en Austria',
  '<strong>The high roads.</strong> Two alpine toll roads open big scenery with almost no walking: the Schlegeis Alpine Road in the Zillertal (roughly &euro;13 per car) climbs to a milk-blue reservoir, and the K&uuml;htai and Timmelsjoch high roads lift you well past the treeline. You step out of the car already at altitude, in a dress or a suit, with the peaks right there.': '<strong>Las carreteras de altura.</strong> Dos carreteras de peaje alpinas abren gran escenario casi sin caminar: la Schlegeis Alpenstraße en el Zillertal (unos 13&nbsp;&euro; por coche) sube a un embalse azul lechoso, y las carreteras de altura de K&uuml;htai y del Timmelsjoch os elevan mucho más allá del bosque. Salís del coche ya en altura, en vestido o en traje, con las cumbres justo ahí.',
  '<strong>The Tyrolean lakes.</strong> Quieter than the famous Dolomite icons: the protected Obernberger See near the Brenner, the emerald Schlegeisspeicher deep in the Zillertal, and the small high tarns above K&uuml;htai. Mirror-still water, larch and grey rock, and almost nobody around at first light.': '<strong>Los lagos tiroleses.</strong> Más tranquilos que los famosos iconos dolomíticos: el protegido Obernberger See junto al Brennero, el esmeralda Schlegeisspeicher en lo hondo del Zillertal, y las pequeñas lagunas de altura sobre K&uuml;htai. Agua espejada, alerces y roca gris, y casi nadie alrededor con la primera luz.',
  'Read the full Tyrol &amp; Austria location guide': 'Leer la guía completa de lugares del Tirol y Austria',
  '<strong>Innsbruck &amp; the Nordkette.</strong> The only city in the Alps with a high mountain on its doorstep. The Hungerburg funicular and Nordkette cable cars lift you from the old town to Hafelekar at 2,256&thinsp;m in about twenty minutes &mdash; genuine high-alpine exposure with no climb, and a dramatic finish to a day that started at a lake.': '<strong>Innsbruck y la Nordkette.</strong> La única ciudad de los Alpes con una alta montaña a la puerta. El funicular de la Hungerburg y los teleféricos de la Nordkette os suben del casco antiguo al Hafelekar, a 2.256&thinsp;m, en unos veinte minutos &mdash; exposición alpina de verdad sin subida, y un final dramático para un día que empezó en un lago.',
  'Where to say your vows in Tyrol': 'Dónde dar el sí en el Tirol',
  'Innsbruck airport': 'Aeropuerto de Innsbruck',
  'Getting here': 'Cómo llegar',
  'Yes &middot; on the mountain': 'Sí &middot; en la montaña',
  'Legal wedding': 'Boda legal',
  'May&ndash;Oct': 'May&ndash;Oct',
  'Season': 'Temporada',
  'It is also home ground for us. We grew up under these ridges; we know which lake is still glass at six in the morning and which registry office will marry you outdoors. That local knowledge is the difference between a good day and a flawless one &mdash; the sheltered alternative when the weather turns, the quiet twin when a lake is mobbed, the exact minute a viewpoint empties out.': 'También es terreno de casa para nosotros. Crecimos bajo estas crestas; sabemos qué lago sigue siendo un cristal a las seis de la mañana y qué registro civil os casa al aire libre. Ese conocimiento local es la diferencia entre un buen día y uno impecable &mdash; la alternativa resguardada cuando cambia el tiempo, el gemelo tranquilo cuando un lago está abarrotado, el minuto exacto en que se vacía un mirador.',
  'Most couples dreaming of an Alpine elopement look first at the Italian Dolomites &mdash; and they are extraordinary. But there is one thing Tyrol does that Italy cannot: it lets you be legally married on the mountain. In Italy a binding wedding happens only inside a town hall, so a Dolomite ceremony is always symbolic. In Austria the legal act itself can move to a lakeshore or a summit terrace. If you want the day that counts to be the day on the mountain, Tyrol is the answer &mdash; and it is every bit as beautiful, with a fraction of the crowds.': 'La mayoría de las parejas que sueñan con un elopement alpino miran primero a los Dolomitas italianos &mdash; y son extraordinarios. Pero hay una cosa que el Tirol hace y que Italia no puede: os permite casaros legalmente en la montaña. En Italia una boda vinculante ocurre solo dentro de un ayuntamiento, así que una ceremonia dolomítica es siempre simbólica. En Austria el propio acto legal puede trasladarse a una orilla o a una terraza de cumbre. Si queréis que el día que cuenta sea el día en la montaña, el Tirol es la respuesta &mdash; y es igual de bello, con una fracción de la gente.',
  'Why marry in Tyrol': 'Por qué casarse en el Tirol',
  'The Region': 'La región',
  'Tyrol Elopement': 'Elopement en el Tirol',
  'Tyrol is our home &mdash; and one of the few places in the Alps where your wedding can be both breathtaking and legally binding on the same mountain. From the ridges above Innsbruck to hidden turquoise lakes, the Austrian Alps make eloping simple: real peaks, a real certificate, and a photographer who grew up under these mountains.': 'El Tirol es nuestro hogar &mdash; y uno de los pocos lugares de los Alpes donde vuestra boda puede ser a la vez sobrecogedora y legalmente vinculante en la misma montaña. Desde las crestas sobre Innsbruck hasta lagos turquesa escondidos, los Alpes austriacos hacen que fugarse sea sencillo: cumbres de verdad, un certificado de verdad y un fotógrafo que creció bajo estas montañas.',
  'Tyrol elopement region': 'Región de elopement del Tirol',
  'Tyrol Elopement 2027 — Elope in the Austrian Alps': 'Elopement en el Tirol 2027 — casarse en los Alpes austriacos',
  'Planning a Tyrol elopement for 2027? Get legally married on an Austrian mountain, near Innsbruck &mdash; locations, the legal route, costs and the best light, from Tyrolean photographers.': '¿Planeáis un elopement en el Tirol para 2027? Casaos legalmente en una montaña austriaca, cerca de Innsbruck &mdash; lugares, la vía legal, costes y la mejor luz, de fotógrafos tiroleses.',
}
TYROL_IT = {
  'Questions couples ask us': 'Domande che le coppie ci fanno',
  'Real elopements': 'Elopement reali',
  'Real Tyrol elopements': 'Elopement reali in Tirolo',
  'Your day': 'La vostra giornata',
  'Tell us what you&rsquo;re imagining': 'Raccontateci cosa immaginate',
  'All planning guides': 'Tutte le guide di pianificazione',
  'Our elopement packages start at <strong>&euro;6,000</strong> and cover photography, location scouting, a planning call and your private online gallery. The middle package adds hair and make-up, flowers and full coordination; the largest covers the whole day including accommodation, reception and transfers. What we handle for you in Tyrol: the registry appointment and paperwork, the hut booking, the timing so your mornings stay calm, and a backup plan for the day the weather turns.': "I nostri pacchetti elopement partono da <strong>6.000&nbsp;&euro;</strong> e comprendono fotografia, sopralluoghi, una call di pianificazione e la vostra galleria online privata. Il pacchetto intermedio aggiunge trucco e acconciatura, fiori e coordinamento completo; il più grande copre l'intera giornata inclusi alloggio, festa e transfer. Ciò che gestiamo per voi in Tirolo: l'appuntamento in comune e le pratiche, la prenotazione del rifugio, i tempi così che le vostre mattine restino serene, e un piano B per il giorno in cui il tempo cambia.",
  'What it costs, and what&rsquo;s included': 'Quanto costa e cosa è incluso',
  'See the full price list': 'Vedi il listino completo',
  'Innsbruck has its own airport minutes from the old town, and Munich and Venice are each a simple drive or train away, so most couples are under a mountain within an hour or two of landing. Innsbruck makes the ideal base &mdash; the Nordkette above you, the Zillertal and its lakes a short drive east, the high roads west, and the Dolomites two to three hours south for couples who want to fold both countries into one trip. For a dawn ceremony we often book a mountain hut, so you sleep up high and wake already there.': "Innsbruck ha un proprio aeroporto a pochi minuti dal centro storico, e Monaco e Venezia sono ciascuna a una semplice guida o a un treno, quindi la maggior parte delle coppie è sotto una montagna un'ora o due dopo l'atterraggio. Innsbruck è la base ideale &mdash; la Nordkette sopra di voi, la Zillertal e i suoi laghi a breve distanza a est, le strade d'alta quota a ovest, e le Dolomiti due o tre ore a sud per le coppie che vogliono unire i due Paesi in un solo viaggio. Per una cerimonia all'alba prenotiamo spesso un rifugio, così dormite in alta quota e vi svegliate già lì.",
  'Getting here &amp; where to stay': 'Come arrivare e dove alloggiare',
  'May through October is the dependable season: the lifts run, the high roads are open and the meadows are green. July and August bring the warmest, most settled weather; late September brings golden larches and thinner crowds and is our quiet favourite. The shoulder weeks can hand you fresh snow on the peaks and empty trails in a single morning &mdash; often the best pictures of the year. Winter turns Tyrol spectacular and silent, with a close eye needed on which roads and lifts stay open.': "Da maggio a ottobre è la stagione affidabile: gli impianti funzionano, le strade d'alta quota sono aperte e i prati verdi. Luglio e agosto portano il tempo più caldo e stabile; fine settembre porta larici dorati e meno folla ed è il nostro preferito tranquillo. Le settimane di transizione possono regalarvi neve fresca sulle cime e sentieri vuoti in un solo mattino &mdash; spesso le foto migliori dell'anno. L'inverno rende il Tirolo spettacolare e silenzioso, con un occhio attento a quali strade e impianti restano aperti.",
  'When to come': 'Quando venire',
  'For a civil marriage you will generally need valid passports, birth certificates and a certificate of no impediment, usually with certified translations and, depending on your home country, an apostille. Each office sets its own lead times and the summer slots fill early, so start a few months ahead. Prefer to keep it simple? Sign the short legal act at home and hold a symbolic ceremony on the mountain &mdash; both carry all of the feeling, and we will tell you honestly which fits your timeline.': "Per un matrimonio civile servono di norma passaporti validi, certificati di nascita e un certificato di nulla osta, di solito con traduzioni giurate e, a seconda del vostro Paese, un'apostille. Ogni ufficio fissa i propri tempi e gli appuntamenti estivi si riempiono presto, quindi iniziate qualche mese prima. Preferite fare semplice? Firmate il breve atto legale a casa e tenete una cerimonia simbolica in montagna &mdash; entrambe portano tutta l'emozione, e vi diremo onestamente quale si adatta ai vostri tempi.",
  'This is the heart of why couples choose Tyrol. A civil marriage in Austria is straightforward for foreign couples, and several Tyrolean registry offices conduct the legal ceremony at an approved outdoor location &mdash; not only inside the office. The act that actually changes your legal status can happen with a lake or a summit right there.': "È questo il cuore del perché le coppie scelgono il Tirolo. Un matrimonio civile in Austria è semplice per le coppie straniere, e diversi uffici di stato civile tirolesi celebrano la cerimonia legale in una location autorizzata all'aperto &mdash; non solo dentro l'ufficio. L'atto che cambia davvero il vostro stato legale può avvenire con un lago o una vetta proprio lì.",
  'Making it legal in Austria': 'Sposarsi legalmente in Austria',
  '<strong>The high roads.</strong> Two alpine toll roads open big scenery with almost no walking: the Schlegeis Alpine Road in the Zillertal (roughly &euro;13 per car) climbs to a milk-blue reservoir, and the K&uuml;htai and Timmelsjoch high roads lift you well past the treeline. You step out of the car already at altitude, in a dress or a suit, with the peaks right there.': "<strong>Le strade d'alta quota.</strong> Due strade a pedaggio alpine aprono grande scenario quasi senza camminare: la Schlegeis Alpenstraße in Zillertal (circa 13&nbsp;&euro; ad auto) sale a un bacino azzurro latte, e le strade d'alta quota di K&uuml;htai e del Timmelsjoch vi sollevano ben oltre il limite del bosco. Scendete dall'auto già in quota, in abito o in completo, con le cime proprio lì.",
  '<strong>The Tyrolean lakes.</strong> Quieter than the famous Dolomite icons: the protected Obernberger See near the Brenner, the emerald Schlegeisspeicher deep in the Zillertal, and the small high tarns above K&uuml;htai. Mirror-still water, larch and grey rock, and almost nobody around at first light.': "<strong>I laghi tirolesi.</strong> Più tranquilli delle famose icone dolomitiche: il protetto Obernberger See presso il Brennero, lo smeraldo Schlegeisspeicher in fondo alla Zillertal, e i piccoli laghetti d'alta quota sopra K&uuml;htai. Acqua a specchio, larici e roccia grigia, e quasi nessuno intorno alla prima luce.",
  'Read the full Tyrol &amp; Austria location guide': 'Leggi la guida completa ai luoghi di Tirolo e Austria',
  '<strong>Innsbruck &amp; the Nordkette.</strong> The only city in the Alps with a high mountain on its doorstep. The Hungerburg funicular and Nordkette cable cars lift you from the old town to Hafelekar at 2,256&thinsp;m in about twenty minutes &mdash; genuine high-alpine exposure with no climb, and a dramatic finish to a day that started at a lake.': "<strong>Innsbruck e la Nordkette.</strong> L'unica città delle Alpi con un'alta montagna alla porta. La funicolare dell'Hungerburg e le funivie della Nordkette vi portano dal centro storico all'Hafelekar, a 2.256&thinsp;m, in circa venti minuti &mdash; vera esposizione d'alta quota senza salita, e un finale drammatico per una giornata iniziata a un lago.",
  'Where to say your vows in Tyrol': 'Dove dire il sì in Tirolo',
  'Innsbruck airport': 'Aeroporto di Innsbruck',
  'Getting here': 'Come arrivare',
  'Yes &middot; on the mountain': 'Sì &middot; in montagna',
  'Legal wedding': 'Matrimonio legale',
  'May&ndash;Oct': 'Mag&ndash;Ott',
  'Season': 'Stagione',
  'It is also home ground for us. We grew up under these ridges; we know which lake is still glass at six in the morning and which registry office will marry you outdoors. That local knowledge is the difference between a good day and a flawless one &mdash; the sheltered alternative when the weather turns, the quiet twin when a lake is mobbed, the exact minute a viewpoint empties out.': "È anche il nostro campo di casa. Siamo cresciuti sotto queste creste; sappiamo quale lago è ancora uno specchio alle sei del mattino e quale ufficio di stato civile vi sposa all'aperto. Questa conoscenza del posto è la differenza tra una bella giornata e una impeccabile &mdash; l'alternativa riparata quando il tempo cambia, il gemello tranquillo quando un lago è preso d'assalto, il minuto esatto in cui un punto panoramico si svuota.",
  'Most couples dreaming of an Alpine elopement look first at the Italian Dolomites &mdash; and they are extraordinary. But there is one thing Tyrol does that Italy cannot: it lets you be legally married on the mountain. In Italy a binding wedding happens only inside a town hall, so a Dolomite ceremony is always symbolic. In Austria the legal act itself can move to a lakeshore or a summit terrace. If you want the day that counts to be the day on the mountain, Tyrol is the answer &mdash; and it is every bit as beautiful, with a fraction of the crowds.': "La maggior parte delle coppie che sognano un elopement alpino guarda prima alle Dolomiti italiane &mdash; e sono straordinarie. Ma c'è una cosa che il Tirolo fa e che l'Italia non può: vi permette di sposarvi legalmente in montagna. In Italia un matrimonio vincolante avviene solo dentro un municipio, quindi una cerimonia dolomitica è sempre simbolica. In Austria l'atto legale stesso può spostarsi su una riva o una terrazza di vetta. Se volete che il giorno che conta sia il giorno in montagna, il Tirolo è la risposta &mdash; ed è altrettanto bello, con una frazione della folla.",
  'Why marry in Tyrol': 'Perché sposarsi in Tirolo',
  'The Region': 'La regione',
  'Tyrol Elopement': 'Elopement in Tirolo',
  'Tyrol is our home &mdash; and one of the few places in the Alps where your wedding can be both breathtaking and legally binding on the same mountain. From the ridges above Innsbruck to hidden turquoise lakes, the Austrian Alps make eloping simple: real peaks, a real certificate, and a photographer who grew up under these mountains.': "Il Tirolo è casa nostra &mdash; e uno dei pochi luoghi delle Alpi dove il vostro matrimonio può essere insieme mozzafiato e legalmente valido sulla stessa montagna. Dalle creste sopra Innsbruck ai laghi turchesi nascosti, le Alpi austriache rendono l'elopement semplice: cime vere, un certificato vero, e un fotografo cresciuto sotto queste montagne.",
  'Tyrol elopement region': 'Regione elopement del Tirolo',
  'Tyrol Elopement 2027 — Elope in the Austrian Alps': 'Elopement in Tirolo 2027 — sposarsi nelle Alpi austriache',
  'Planning a Tyrol elopement for 2027? Get legally married on an Austrian mountain, near Innsbruck &mdash; locations, the legal route, costs and the best light, from Tyrolean photographers.': 'Pianificate un elopement in Tirolo per il 2027? Sposatevi legalmente su una montagna austriaca, vicino a Innsbruck &mdash; luoghi, la via legale, costi e la luce migliore, da fotografi tirolesi.',
}
TYROL_FAQ_ES = {
  'Can we legally get married in Tyrol?': ('¿Podemos casarnos legalmente en el Tirol?', 'Sí &mdash; y es la mejor razón para elegir el Tirol. Austria permite una ceremonia civil legalmente vinculante, y varios registros civiles tiroleses os casan en un lugar autorizado al aire libre, no solo dentro de la oficina &mdash; una orilla, un mirador, una terraza de montaña. Eso significa que la ceremonia que cuenta sobre el papel puede ocurrir con las cumbres justo detrás. En Italia, en cambio, una boda vinculante solo puede celebrarse dentro de un ayuntamiento. Coordinamos la oficina, la fecha y el papeleo por vosotros.'),
  'Where can we elope in Tyrol?': ('¿Dónde podemos fugarnos en el Tirol?', 'Desde las crestas de la Nordkette justo sobre Innsbruck hasta lagos turquesa escondidos y carreteras de altura que abren vistas de roca sin caminata. Nuestra lista: el Hafelekar y las crestas sobre Innsbruck, el protegido Obernberger See junto al Brennero, el esmeralda Schlegeisspeicher en el Zillertal, y las tranquilas lagunas de altura sobre K&uuml;htai. Todos cerca de Innsbruck y a la vez en otro mundo, y cada uno más tranquilo con la primera luz.'),
  'Do we have to hike?': ('¿Tenemos que caminar?', 'Solo lo que queráis. Innsbruck es la única ciudad de los Alpes con una alta montaña a la puerta &mdash; los teleféricos de la Nordkette os suben del casco antiguo a 2.256&thinsp;m en unos veinte minutos, sin caminar. Varios de nuestros lagos tiroleses favoritos están justo al final de una carretera. Y si queréis que el día se sienta ganado, una corta subida por una cresta os pone en un sitio que parece imposible. Ajustamos el esfuerzo a vosotros y nunca exageramos lo que cuesta llegar a un lugar.'),
  'When is the best time to elope in Tyrol?': ('¿Cuál es la mejor época para un elopement en el Tirol?', 'De mayo a octubre es la ventana fiable: los remontes funcionan, las carreteras de altura están abiertas y los prados verdes. Julio y agosto dan el tiempo más cálido y estable; finales de septiembre trae alerces dorados y menos gente, y es nuestro favorito tranquilo. Las semanas de transición pueden regalaros nieve fresca en las cumbres y senderos vacíos en la misma mañana. El invierno es espectacular y silencioso pero pide un ojo atento a qué carreteras y remontes están abiertos.'),
  'How do we get to Tyrol?': ('¿Cómo llegamos al Tirol?', 'Fácil &mdash; es una de las regiones alpinas más accesibles. Innsbruck tiene su propio aeropuerto a minutos del casco antiguo, y Múnich y Venecia están cada uno a un sencillo trayecto en coche o tren, así que la mayoría de las parejas está bajo una montaña una o dos horas tras aterrizar. Desde una base en Innsbruck alcanzáis la Nordkette, los lagos del Zillertal y las carreteras de altura sin un largo traslado, y el cruce al sur hacia los Dolomitas es un trayecto sencillo y bello.'),
  'What does an elopement in Tyrol cost?': ('¿Cuánto cuesta un elopement en el Tirol?', 'Nuestros paquetes de elopement empiezan en 6.000&nbsp;&euro; e incluyen fotografía, scouting de localizaciones, una llamada de planificación y vuestra galería online privada. El paquete intermedio añade peluquería y maquillaje, flores y coordinación completa; el mayor cubre el día entero, incluidos alojamiento, celebración y traslados. Nos ocupamos de la cita del registro, los tiempos, los refugios y el plan B, para que lo único en que penséis el día sea el uno en el otro.'),
  'How far in advance should we book?': ('¿Con cuánta antelación deberíamos reservar?', 'Para una fecha de verano, de seis a doce meses es cómodo. Si queréis la ceremonia legal en Austria, reservad al oficiante y el refugio de montaña con meses de antelación &mdash; ambos son limitados en verano y ambos se llenan pronto. En temporada baja a veces hemos hecho algo bello en pocas semanas. Decidnos vuestras fechas y os diremos con honestidad qué sigue siendo posible.'),
}
TYROL_FAQ_IT = {
  'Can we legally get married in Tyrol?': ('Possiamo sposarci legalmente in Tirolo?', "Sì &mdash; ed è la ragione migliore per scegliere il Tirolo. L'Austria consente una cerimonia civile con valore legale, e diversi uffici di stato civile tirolesi vi sposano in una location autorizzata all'aperto, non solo dentro l'ufficio &mdash; una riva, un punto panoramico, una terrazza di montagna. Significa che la cerimonia che conta sulla carta può avvenire con le cime proprio dietro. In Italia, invece, un matrimonio vincolante può avvenire solo dentro un municipio. Coordiniamo ufficio, data e pratiche per voi."),
  'Where can we elope in Tyrol?': ("Dove possiamo fare l'elopement in Tirolo?", "Dalle creste della Nordkette proprio sopra Innsbruck a laghi turchesi nascosti e strade d'alta quota che aprono vedute di roccia senza camminata. La nostra rosa: l'Hafelekar e le creste sopra Innsbruck, il protetto Obernberger See presso il Brennero, lo smeraldo Schlegeisspeicher in Zillertal, e i quieti laghetti d'alta quota sopra K&uuml;htai. Tutti vicini a Innsbruck eppure in un altro mondo, e ognuno più calmo alla prima luce."),
  'Do we have to hike?': ('Dobbiamo camminare?', "Solo quanto volete. Innsbruck è l'unica città delle Alpi con un'alta montagna alla porta &mdash; le funivie della Nordkette vi portano dal centro storico a 2.256&thinsp;m in circa venti minuti, senza camminare. Diversi dei nostri laghi tirolesi preferiti stanno proprio alla fine di una strada. E se volete che la giornata si senta guadagnata, una breve salita in cresta vi mette in un posto che sembra impossibile. Adattiamo la fatica a voi e non esageriamo mai quanto costa raggiungere un luogo."),
  'When is the best time to elope in Tyrol?': ('Qual è il periodo migliore per un elopement in Tirolo?', "Da maggio a ottobre è la finestra affidabile: gli impianti funzionano, le strade d'alta quota sono aperte e i prati verdi. Luglio e agosto danno il tempo più caldo e stabile; fine settembre porta larici dorati e meno folla ed è il nostro preferito tranquillo. Le settimane di transizione possono regalarvi neve fresca sulle cime e sentieri vuoti nello stesso mattino. L'inverno è spettacolare e silenzioso ma chiede un occhio attento a quali strade e impianti sono aperti."),
  'How do we get to Tyrol?': ('Come arriviamo in Tirolo?', "Facilmente &mdash; è una delle regioni alpine più accessibili. Innsbruck ha un proprio aeroporto a pochi minuti dal centro storico, e Monaco e Venezia sono ciascuna a una semplice guida o a un treno, quindi la maggior parte delle coppie è sotto una montagna un'ora o due dopo l'atterraggio. Da una base a Innsbruck raggiungete la Nordkette, i laghi della Zillertal e le strade d'alta quota senza un lungo trasferimento, e il passaggio a sud verso le Dolomiti è una guida semplice e panoramica."),
  'What does an elopement in Tyrol cost?': ('Quanto costa un elopement in Tirolo?', "I nostri pacchetti elopement partono da 6.000&nbsp;&euro; e comprendono fotografia, sopralluoghi, una call di pianificazione e la vostra galleria online privata. Il pacchetto intermedio aggiunge trucco e acconciatura, fiori e coordinamento completo; il più grande copre l'intera giornata inclusi alloggio, festa e transfer. Gestiamo l'appuntamento in comune, i tempi, i rifugi e il piano B, così che l'unica cosa a cui pensate il giorno stesso siate l'un l'altra."),
  'How far in advance should we book?': ('Con quanto anticipo dovremmo prenotare?', "Per una data estiva, da sei a dodici mesi è comodo. Se volete la cerimonia legale in Austria, prenotate l'ufficiale di stato civile e il rifugio con mesi di anticipo &mdash; entrambi sono limitati in estate ed entrambi si riempiono presto. In bassa stagione a volte abbiamo reso possibile qualcosa di bello in poche settimane. Diteci le vostre date e vi diremo onestamente cosa è ancora possibile."),
}

def build_tyrol_region(lang):
    # Commercial region landing page for Tyrol / the Austrian Alps.
    # EN+DE fully translated; ES/IT fall back to EN until TYROL_ES/TYROL_IT land (mirrors build_region behaviour).
    rel='elopement-tyrol/'; P=prefix(lang,rel)
    DE=(lang=='de')
    def L(en,de):
        if lang=='de': return de
        if lang=='es': return TYROL_ES.get(en,en)
        if lang=='it': return TYROL_IT.get(en,en)
        return en
    def FQ(qen,aen,qde,ade):
        if lang=='de': return (qde,ade)
        if lang=='es': return TYROL_FAQ_ES.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        if lang=='it': return TYROL_FAQ_IT.get(qen,(qen,aen))
        return (qen,aen)
    H2S='font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:clamp(25px,3vw,36px);letter-spacing:-.01em;margin:1.6em 0 .4em'
    def h2(en,de): return f'<h2 style="{H2S}">{L(en,de)}</h2>'
    def p(en,de): return f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2)">{L(en,de)}</p>'
    HERO_IMG='img/guide-elope-in-austria/11-oesterreich-sonnenuntergang-tirol.webp'
    faqs=[FQ(*x) for x in TYROL_REGION_FAQ]
    faq_html=''.join(
      f'<div style="margin:1.3em 0 0;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:1.1em">'
      f'<h3 style="font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:400;font-size:20px;margin:0 0 .3em">{q}</h3>'
      f'<p style="color:var(--ink-2);margin:0">{a}</p></div>' for q,a in faqs)
    faq_ld={"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[
        {"@type":"Question","name":_plain(q),"acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":_plain(a)}} for q,a in faqs]}
    stories=['official-married-in-the-alps','lake-elopement-tyrol-mountains','sunset-elopement-tyrol']
    cards=''.join(story_card(lang,P,STORYBY[s]) for s in stories)
    guidelink=u(P,lang,'how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/elope-in-austria/')
    title=L(f'Tyrol Elopement {SEO_YEAR} — Elope in the Austrian Alps',f'Elopement in Tirol {SEO_YEAR} — in den österreichischen Alpen heiraten')
    desc=L(f'Planning a Tyrol elopement for {SEO_YEAR}? Get legally married on an Austrian mountain, near Innsbruck &mdash; locations, the legal route, costs and the best light, from Tyrolean photographers.',f'Elopement in Tirol {SEO_YEAR}? Heiratet rechtsgültig auf einem österreichischen Berg, nahe Innsbruck &mdash; Orte, der Rechtsweg, Kosten und das beste Licht, von Tiroler Fotografen.')
    body=(nav(lang,rel,'')+
      f'<section class="page-hero" style="padding:0">{herobg(P,HERO_IMG,L("Tyrol elopement region","Elopement-Region Tirol"))}'
      f'<div class="content"><div class="wrap"><div class="kicker" data-n="{L("The Region","Die Region")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h1>{L("Tyrol Elopement","Elopement in Tirol")}</h1></div></div></section>'
      '<section><div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">'
      f'<p class="lead">{L("Tyrol is our home &mdash; and one of the few places in the Alps where your wedding can be both breathtaking and legally binding on the same mountain. From the ridges above Innsbruck to hidden turquoise lakes, the Austrian Alps make eloping simple: real peaks, a real certificate, and a photographer who grew up under these mountains.","Tirol ist unsere Heimat &mdash; und einer der wenigen Orte der Alpen, an dem eure Hochzeit am selben Berg zugleich atemberaubend und rechtsgültig sein kann. Von den Graten über Innsbruck bis zu versteckten türkisen Seen macht Österreich ein Elopement einfach: echte Gipfel, ein echtes Zertifikat und ein Fotograf, der unter diesen Bergen aufgewachsen ist.")}</p>'
      +h2('Why marry in Tyrol','Warum in Tirol heiraten')
      +p("Most couples dreaming of an Alpine elopement look first at the Italian Dolomites &mdash; and they are extraordinary. But there is one thing Tyrol does that Italy cannot: it lets you be legally married on the mountain. In Italy a binding wedding happens only inside a town hall, so a Dolomite ceremony is always symbolic. In Austria the legal act itself can move to a lakeshore or a summit terrace. If you want the day that counts to be the day on the mountain, Tyrol is the answer &mdash; and it is every bit as beautiful, with a fraction of the crowds.","Die meisten Paare, die von einem alpinen Elopement träumen, schauen zuerst auf die italienischen Dolomiten &mdash; und die sind außergewöhnlich. Doch eines kann Tirol, was Italien nicht kann: euch rechtsgültig am Berg trauen lassen. In Italien findet eine bindende Hochzeit nur im Rathaus statt, eine Dolomiten-Zeremonie ist also immer symbolisch. In Österreich kann der Rechtsakt selbst an ein Seeufer oder eine Gipfelterrasse wandern. Wollt ihr, dass der Tag, der zählt, der Tag am Berg ist, ist Tirol die Antwort &mdash; und mindestens ebenso schön, mit einem Bruchteil des Andrangs.")
      +p("It is also home ground for us. We grew up under these ridges; we know which lake is still glass at six in the morning and which registry office will marry you outdoors. That local knowledge is the difference between a good day and a flawless one &mdash; the sheltered alternative when the weather turns, the quiet twin when a lake is mobbed, the exact minute a viewpoint empties out.","Es ist für uns auch Heimspiel. Wir sind unter diesen Graten aufgewachsen; wir wissen, welcher See um sechs Uhr früh noch spiegelglatt ist und welches Standesamt euch im Freien traut. Dieses lokale Wissen ist der Unterschied zwischen einem guten und einem makellosen Tag &mdash; die geschützte Alternative, wenn das Wetter kippt, der stille Zwilling, wenn ein See überlaufen ist, die genaue Minute, in der sich ein Aussichtspunkt leert.")
      +'<div class="facts" style="margin:2.2em 0 0"><div class="fct"><div class="fl">'+L('Season','Beste Zeit')+'</div><div class="fv">'+L('May&ndash;Oct','Mai&ndash;Okt')+'</div></div>'
      +'<div class="fct"><div class="fl">'+L('Legal wedding','Trauung')+'</div><div class="fv">'+L('Yes &middot; on the mountain','Ja &middot; am Berg')+'</div></div>'
      +'<div class="fct"><div class="fl">'+L('Getting here','Anreise')+'</div><div class="fv">'+L('Innsbruck airport','Flughafen Innsbruck')+'</div></div></div>'
      +h2('Where to say your vows in Tyrol','Wo ihr in Tirol das Ja sagt')
      +p("<strong>Innsbruck &amp; the Nordkette.</strong> The only city in the Alps with a high mountain on its doorstep. The Hungerburg funicular and Nordkette cable cars lift you from the old town to Hafelekar at 2,256&thinsp;m in about twenty minutes &mdash; genuine high-alpine exposure with no climb, and a dramatic finish to a day that started at a lake.","<strong>Innsbruck &amp; die Nordkette.</strong> Die einzige Stadt der Alpen mit einem Hochgebirge direkt vor der Tür. Die Hungerburgbahn und die Nordkettenbahnen bringen euch in rund zwanzig Minuten von der Altstadt aufs Hafelekar auf 2.256&thinsp;m &mdash; echte hochalpine Ausgesetztheit ohne Aufstieg und ein dramatischer Abschluss für einen Tag, der am See begann.")
      +p("<strong>The Tyrolean lakes.</strong> Quieter than the famous Dolomite icons: the protected Obernberger See near the Brenner, the emerald Schlegeisspeicher deep in the Zillertal, and the small high tarns above K&uuml;htai. Mirror-still water, larch and grey rock, and almost nobody around at first light.","<strong>Die Tiroler Seen.</strong> Stiller als die berühmten Dolomiten-Ikonen: der geschützte Obernberger See nahe dem Brenner, der smaragdgrüne Schlegeisspeicher tief im Zillertal und die kleinen Hochseen über K&uuml;htai. Spiegelglattes Wasser, Lärchen und grauer Fels &mdash; und im ersten Licht fast niemand.")
      +p("<strong>The high roads.</strong> Two alpine toll roads open big scenery with almost no walking: the Schlegeis Alpine Road in the Zillertal (roughly &euro;13 per car) climbs to a milk-blue reservoir, and the K&uuml;htai and Timmelsjoch high roads lift you well past the treeline. You step out of the car already at altitude, in a dress or a suit, with the peaks right there.","<strong>Die Höhenstraßen.</strong> Zwei alpine Mautstraßen öffnen große Kulisse mit fast keinem Fußweg: Die Schlegeis Alpenstraße im Zillertal (rund 13&nbsp;&euro; pro Auto) steigt zu einem milchblauen Stausee, und die Höhenstraßen von K&uuml;htai und Timmelsjoch heben euch weit über die Baumgrenze. Ihr steigt bereits in der Höhe aus dem Auto, in Kleid oder Anzug, die Gipfel direkt daneben.")
      +f'<p style="margin:.2em 0 0"><a href="{guidelink}" class="arrow-link">{L("Read the full Tyrol &amp; Austria location guide","Zum ausführlichen Tirol- &amp; Österreich-Ortsguide")} &rarr;</a></p>'
      +h2('Making it legal in Austria','Rechtsgültig heiraten in Österreich')
      +p("This is the heart of why couples choose Tyrol. A civil marriage in Austria is straightforward for foreign couples, and several Tyrolean registry offices conduct the legal ceremony at an approved outdoor location &mdash; not only inside the office. The act that actually changes your legal status can happen with a lake or a summit right there.","Das ist der Kern, warum Paare Tirol wählen. Eine standesamtliche Trauung in Österreich ist für ausländische Paare unkompliziert, und mehrere Tiroler Standesämter vollziehen den Rechtsakt an einem genehmigten Ort im Freien &mdash; nicht nur im Amt. Der Akt, der euren rechtlichen Status wirklich ändert, kann mit einem See oder einem Gipfel direkt daneben geschehen.")
      +p("For a civil marriage you will generally need valid passports, birth certificates and a certificate of no impediment, usually with certified translations and, depending on your home country, an apostille. Each office sets its own lead times and the summer slots fill early, so start a few months ahead. Prefer to keep it simple? Sign the short legal act at home and hold a symbolic ceremony on the mountain &mdash; both carry all of the feeling, and we will tell you honestly which fits your timeline.","Für eine standesamtliche Trauung braucht ihr in der Regel gültige Reisepässe, Geburtsurkunden und ein Ehefähigkeitszeugnis, meist mit beglaubigten Übersetzungen und &mdash; je nach Heimatland &mdash; einer Apostille. Jedes Amt setzt eigene Vorlaufzeiten, und die Sommertermine sind früh vergeben, beginnt also ein paar Monate vorher. Lieber einfach? Unterschreibt den kurzen Rechtsakt zu Hause und feiert eine symbolische Zeremonie am Berg &mdash; beide tragen das ganze Gefühl, und wir sagen euch ehrlich, welcher zu eurem Zeitplan passt.")
      +h2('When to come','Die beste Zeit')
      +p("May through October is the dependable season: the lifts run, the high roads are open and the meadows are green. July and August bring the warmest, most settled weather; late September brings golden larches and thinner crowds and is our quiet favourite. The shoulder weeks can hand you fresh snow on the peaks and empty trails in a single morning &mdash; often the best pictures of the year. Winter turns Tyrol spectacular and silent, with a close eye needed on which roads and lifts stay open.","Mai bis Oktober ist die verlässliche Saison: Die Bahnen fahren, die Höhenstraßen sind offen und die Wiesen grün. Juli und August bringen das wärmste, beständigste Wetter; der späte September schenkt goldene Lärchen und weniger Andrang und ist unser stiller Favorit. Die Randwochen können euch frischen Schnee auf den Gipfeln und leere Wege an einem Morgen bescheren &mdash; oft die besten Bilder des Jahres. Der Winter macht Tirol spektakulär und still, mit wachem Blick darauf, welche Straßen und Bahnen offen bleiben.")
      +h2('Getting here &amp; where to stay','Anreise &amp; wo ihr wohnt')
      +p("Innsbruck has its own airport minutes from the old town, and Munich and Venice are each a simple drive or train away, so most couples are under a mountain within an hour or two of landing. Innsbruck makes the ideal base &mdash; the Nordkette above you, the Zillertal and its lakes a short drive east, the high roads west, and the Dolomites two to three hours south for couples who want to fold both countries into one trip. For a dawn ceremony we often book a mountain hut, so you sleep up high and wake already there.","Innsbruck hat einen eigenen Flughafen wenige Minuten von der Altstadt, und München und Venedig sind jeweils eine einfache Fahrt oder Zugverbindung entfernt, die meisten Paare stehen also ein bis zwei Stunden nach der Landung unter einem Berg. Innsbruck ist die ideale Basis &mdash; die Nordkette über euch, das Zillertal und seine Seen eine kurze Fahrt östlich, die Höhenstraßen westlich, und die Dolomiten zwei bis drei Stunden südlich für Paare, die beide Länder in eine Reise fassen wollen. Für eine Zeremonie zur Morgendämmerung buchen wir oft eine Berghütte, damit ihr oben schlaft und schon dort aufwacht.")
      +h2('What it costs, and what&rsquo;s included','Was es kostet und was dabei ist')
      +p("Our elopement packages start at <strong>&euro;6,000</strong> and cover photography, location scouting, a planning call and your private online gallery. The middle package adds hair and make-up, flowers and full coordination; the largest covers the whole day including accommodation, reception and transfers. What we handle for you in Tyrol: the registry appointment and paperwork, the hut booking, the timing so your mornings stay calm, and a backup plan for the day the weather turns.","Unsere Elopement-Pakete beginnen bei <strong>6.000&nbsp;&euro;</strong> und umfassen Fotografie, Location-Scouting, ein Planungsgespräch und eure private Online-Galerie. Das mittlere Paket ergänzt Hair &amp; Make-up, Blumen und volle Koordination; das größte deckt den ganzen Tag inklusive Unterkunft, Feier und Transfers. Was wir in Tirol für euch übernehmen: den Standesamt-Termin und die Papiere, die Hüttenbuchung, das Timing, damit eure Morgen ruhig bleiben, und einen Plan B für den Tag, an dem das Wetter kippt.")
      +f'<p style="margin-top:1.7em"><a href="{u(P,lang,"our-packages/")}" class="btn">{L("See the full price list","Zur vollständigen Preisliste")}</a></p>'
      +h2('Questions couples ask us','Fragen, die Paare uns stellen')+faq_html+
      '</div></section>'
      '<section style="padding-top:clamp(30px,5vw,64px)"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head reveal">'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{L("Real elopements","Echte Elopements")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2>{L("Real Tyrol elopements","Echte Tiroler Elopements")}</h2></div>'
      f'<div class="story-grid">{cards}</div></div></section>'
      '<section class="cta"><div class="wrap row reveal"><div>'
      f'<div class="kicker" data-n="{L("Your day","Euer Tag")}"><span class="line"></span></div><h2 style="margin-top:20px">{L("Tell us what you&rsquo;re imagining","Erzählt uns, was ihr euch vorstellt")}</h2></div>'
      f'<a href="{u(P,lang,"get-in-touch/")}" class="btn light">{t(lang,"start_planning")}</a></div></section>'
      f'<section style="padding:clamp(28px,4vw,48px) 0"><div class="wrap"><a href="{u(P,lang,"how-to-elope-in-the-europe-mountains/")}" class="arrow-link">&larr; {L("All planning guides","Alle Planungs-Guides")}</a></div></section>'
      +footer(lang,rel))
    write(lang,rel,head(lang,rel,title,desc,ld_extra=[faq_ld,prof_service_ld()],pre=herolink(P,HERO_IMG))+body+scripts(P))

PROPOSAL_LP_FAQ=[
 ("How do you photograph a proposal without my partner noticing?",
  "It is what we do best. We plan every detail with you by message beforehand &mdash; the spot, the timing, a small signal for the moment you are about to kneel. On the day we arrive early, blend in with the other hikers and shoot from a distance with a long lens, so your partner has no idea until the ring is out. Only after the yes do we step in, introduce ourselves and turn it into a relaxed couples session. The surprise stays a surprise.",
  "Wie fotografiert ihr einen Antrag, ohne dass mein Gegenüber es merkt?",
  "Das ist unsere Spezialität. Wir planen jedes Detail vorab mit euch per Nachricht &mdash; den Ort, das Timing, ein kleines Zeichen für den Moment, in dem ihr euch hinkniet. Am Tag kommen wir früh, mischen uns unter die anderen Wanderer und fotografieren aus der Ferne mit dem Teleobjektiv, sodass euer Gegenüber nichts ahnt, bis der Ring draußen ist. Erst nach dem Ja treten wir hinzu, stellen uns vor und machen ein entspanntes Paar-Shooting daraus. Die Überraschung bleibt eine Überraschung."),
 ("Where is the best place to propose in the Dolomites?",
  "The best proposal spots give you a natural reason to pause and little effort &mdash; a long, sweaty hike tends to give the game away. Roadside lakes are perfect: the Lago di Braies boardwalk or little Lago d&rsquo;Antorno, where at first light you have the railing to yourselves. Cable-car viewpoints like the Sass Pordoi terrace or the Nordkette minutes above Innsbruck are just as easy. We match the spot to your fitness and the surprise you have in mind.",
  "Wo ist der beste Ort für einen Antrag in den Dolomiten?",
  "Die besten Antragsorte bieten einen natürlichen Grund zum Innehalten und wenig Aufwand &mdash; eine lange, verschwitzte Wanderung verrät den Plan meist. Seen an der Straße sind perfekt: der Steg am Pragser Wildsee oder der kleine Lago d&rsquo;Antorno, wo ihr im ersten Licht das Geländer für euch habt. Bergbahn-Aussichtspunkte wie die Sass-Pordoi-Terrasse oder die Nordkette Minuten über Innsbruck sind ebenso leicht. Wir stimmen den Ort auf eure Fitness und die geplante Überraschung ab."),
 ("What if it rains, or the weather turns?",
  "We plan around it. First light gives you empty trails and soft colour, but mountain weather changes fast, so we always hold a backup spot and, where we can, a spare morning. Grey skies and mist are not a problem &mdash; some of the most emotional proposal pictures we have ever taken came out of soft rain and low cloud. We watch the forecast closely in the days before and pick the window that works.",
  "Was, wenn es regnet oder das Wetter umschlägt?",
  "Wir planen darum herum. Das erste Licht schenkt leere Wege und weiche Farben, aber das Bergwetter wechselt schnell, deshalb halten wir immer einen Ausweichort und, wo möglich, einen Reservemorgen bereit. Grauer Himmel und Nebel sind kein Problem &mdash; einige der bewegendsten Antragsbilder, die wir je gemacht haben, entstanden bei sanftem Regen und tiefen Wolken. Wir verfolgen die Vorhersage in den Tagen davor genau und wählen das Fenster, das passt."),
 ("Do we get a proper couples session after the proposal?",
  "Yes &mdash; and it is one of the best parts. Once the yes is out and the nerves have melted, we keep shooting for a relaxed engagement session while you are still glowing. You get the surprise itself and a proper set of portraits from the same morning, and we can usually turn a few images around the same day so you have something to share with family straight away.",
  "Bekommen wir nach dem Antrag ein richtiges Paar-Shooting?",
  "Ja &mdash; und es ist einer der schönsten Teile. Sobald das Ja heraus ist und die Nervosität geschmolzen, fotografieren wir weiter für ein entspanntes Verlobungs-Shooting, solange ihr noch strahlt. Ihr bekommt die Überraschung selbst und dazu eine richtige Porträtserie vom selben Morgen, und meist können wir noch am selben Tag ein paar Bilder liefern, damit ihr sofort etwas mit der Familie teilen könnt."),
 ("When is the best time for a proposal shoot?",
  "All year round, and always at first light. Sunrise gives you the quietest trails, the softest colour and the fewest strangers in the background &mdash; the perfect cover for a surprise. Summer and early autumn are the easiest for access; winter turns the peaks monochrome and magical and hands you near-total solitude. Tell us your travel dates and we will find the best morning within them.",
  "Wann ist die beste Zeit für ein Antrags-Shooting?",
  "Das ganze Jahr über &mdash; und immer im ersten Licht. Der Sonnenaufgang schenkt die ruhigsten Wege, die weichsten Farben und die wenigsten Fremden im Hintergrund &mdash; die perfekte Tarnung für eine Überraschung. Sommer und Frühherbst sind am leichtesten für den Zugang; der Winter macht die Gipfel monochrom und magisch und schenkt fast völlige Einsamkeit. Sagt uns eure Reisedaten, und wir finden den besten Morgen darin."),
 ("What does a proposal shoot cost?",
  "A proposal shoot is a shorter, simpler booking than a full elopement, so it sits below our elopement packages. Because every proposal is different &mdash; the location, the travel, the length of the couples session after &mdash; we send tailored pricing rather than a fixed number. Tell us your date and what you are imagining and we will come straight back with a clear quote.",
  "Was kostet ein Antrags-Shooting?",
  "Ein Antrags-Shooting ist eine kürzere, einfachere Buchung als ein ganzes Elopement und liegt daher unter unseren Elopement-Paketen. Weil jeder Antrag anders ist &mdash; der Ort, die Anreise, die Länge des Paar-Shootings danach &mdash;, schicken wir ein maßgeschneidertes Angebot statt einer festen Zahl. Sagt uns euren Termin und was ihr euch vorstellt, und wir kommen umgehend mit einem klaren Angebot zurück."),
]

